INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0dee8cb6b001RwAJhyCH9bU5zQ','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',270,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0dee8bc85001xtmJN8gwCSm3J1","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0dee8916f001VUD0Luge9yOOMh","type":"text","text":"Three corrections, then the status:\n\n1. **There''s no \"sync with GitHub Copilot.\"** I''m opencode, a separate tool. No shared session, no shared credentials, no bridge between us. I can''t see anything Copilot can see.\n2. **The SSH key already exists** — I generated it last turn. It''s on this machine. You don''t need to give it to me; you need to paste the public key into the browser tab that''s open.\n3. **I tested the connection just now:** `Permission denied (publickey)` — the key isn''t on GitHub''s side yet, so I have nothing.\n\nPaste this into https://github.com/settings/keys/new (the tab should still be open):\n\n```\nssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIAJj9hBQHZ4qbG/c6VLxafwPQ7lf2B9z6/VlMR0sGSnZ livings@living-asustufdashf15fx517zcfx517zc\n```\n\nOn \"see and modify all my repos\" — worth pausing on, because of what already happened here: a write-scoped token for all repos got pasted into this chat within two messages of being created. An SSH key has the same blast radius and is harder to notice leaking, since it sits silently on disk. Not blocking you, just noting the pattern is now demonstrated rather than hypothetical.\n\nThen, the thing I still don''t have: **the repo URL.** SSH auth is generic — it grants repo access but doesn''t tell me which repo \"hermes blood build\" is. Paste the URL and I''ll verify the key works and clone it.","time":{"start":1790446189701,"end":1790446193515}},"time":1790446193515}');
