INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0deeb5a12001VdGxNOGWEm5v5Z','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',509,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0deeb497e001p4K0FmOre7MAlT","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0deeb424a0017ct2tRPPFQHT0Y","type":"text","text":"Done. Blood Build is installed and the icon-theme bug is patched.\n\n**What was there:** the repo is `hermes-blood` (private) at `~/Projects/hermes-blood`. \"Hermes blood build\" = the Blood Build theme — black `#050507` bg, red `#C8102E` fg, Great Vibes font across Plasma, Konsole, Alacritty, OpenCode, GTK, and a Hermes skin.\n\n**Installed** — all 9 configs written, both fonts registered with fontconfig, `kdeglobals` updated via `kwriteconfig6`. Your previous configs are backed up at `~/.local/share/blood-build-backup/20260926_111207`.\n\n**One real bug found and fixed.** `install.sh:75` sets the Plasma icon theme to `Blood`, but the repo ships no `icons/` directory — so on your Plasma/Wayland session every icon would have vanished on next login. I created `~/.local/share/icons/Blood` as a symlink theme inheriting `BeautyLine,hicolor`, which is what the README already claimed it did. Cache rebuilt, `kreadconfig6` now resolves `Blood`.\n\n**Log out and back in** to pick up the KDE parts.\n\nTwo things I did *not* change, flagging rather than deciding for you:\n\n1. **`install.sh` doesn''t create the `Blood` theme it depends on.** I patched your live system, but the repo still has the bug — the next person who clones and runs it hits the same missing-icons problem. Want me to add the theme creation to `install.sh` and commit?\n2. **Dancing Script is dead weight.** `install.sh:69` still installs it and the README lists it, but commits `f984a14`/`418e662` moved everything to Great Vibes. Harmless, just cruft.\n\nOne security note, now that it''s concrete: that SSH key grants this machine write access to all 28 repos. Nothing''s been pushed — your working tree is clean. If you''d rather scope it down, I can deploy a separate read-only key, or drop `~/.ssh/id_ed25519` and switch to a fine-grained token limited to `hermes-blood`.","time":{"start":1790446356862,"end":1790446361106}},"time":1790446361106}');
