INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0deec76ac0010xCaGC9I2SViCa','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',592,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0deec6e57001Va1xHorSTemcDZ","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0deec697b001yOZFPWzoy1pLE1","type":"reasoning","text":"More findings:\n\n1. **Great Vibes has ONLY Regular.** No bold, no italic. `fc-match \"Great Vibes:bold\"` returns Regular — so fontconfig silently returns Regular rather than synthesizing. Alacritty requests Bold/Italic and will get Regular. Effect: no visual bold/italic distinction in alacritty. Not a crash, but a real fidelity issue. Minor.\n\n2. **`Garuda.profile` sets `Command=/usr/bin/fish`** — the Konsole default profile launches fish. Is fish installed? If not, Konsole opens and immediately closes/fails → **this IS a lockout-shaped risk.** Let me check fish.\n\n3. Konsole is installed. Garuda.profile references ColorScheme=BlackRed, which exists. Parent=FALLBACK/ is normal.\n\nLet me check fish, and also check the GTK settings for validity, and the blood.yaml.\n\nCritical checks remaining:\n- fish installed? (lockout risk — konsole dies)\n- gtk settings.ini validity\n- blood.yaml validity (it''s a \"hermes skin\" but hermes doesn''t exist — dead config)\n- KDE global font = Great Vibes 14 — readability/brick risk\n\nLet me check fish and the rest.","time":{"start":1790446431831,"end":1790446433963}},"time":1790446433963}');
