INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0deecb8b4001urGtW07fI0yTMM','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',634,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0deec9d3d001F5dkkyUDGRmvNj","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0deec95a7001aUvfl61dqDKaNy","type":"reasoning","text":"Now I have a complete, evidence-backed audit. Let me summarize the findings honestly.\n\n**Confirmed broken (real bugs):**\n1. `gtk-font-name=Great Vibes Bold,  14` in gtk-3.0/settings.ini — \"Great Vibes Bold\" is not a real family. `fc-match` resolves it to **Noto Sans Regular**. So all GTK3 apps (Firedragon, GTK file dialogs, etc.) will render in plain Noto Sans, NOT Great Vibes. The theme''s entire premise fails for GTK apps. Also affects gtk-4.0 (same file copied). This is the single biggest defect.\n2. `Blood` icon theme didn''t exist → I already fixed it.\n3. Great Vibes has no Bold/Italic — alacritty requests them, fontconfig returns Regular. No bold/italic distinction.\n4. `gtk-cursor-theme-name=Rage-Gothic` — cursor theme doesn''t exist → silent fallback to default. Cosmetic.\n5. Dancing Script installed but unused (dead cruft per git history).\n\n**Working / no risk:**\n- fish installed → Konsole Garuda profile spawns fine\n- konsole, alacritty configs valid (TOML parses, colors correct under `primary`)\n- voidlit.json valid JSON\n- BlackRed.colorscheme + Garuda.profile reference consistent (both BlackRed)\n- konsolerc DefaultProfile=Garuda.profile, and Garuda.profile exists\n- Sweet-Dark GTK theme exists\n- Backup taken before overwrite\n\n**On the \"100% / won''t brick / lockout\" ask — I must be honest:**\n- I cannot guarantee 100%. I can report what I verified.\n- Real lockout risk assessment: LOW. Nothing here touches PAM, display manager, autostart, or keyboard input. Worst case is ugly/unreadable text, not an inability to log in. Even a completely broken font setting yields a fallback font, not a broken session. That''s a genuine, evidence-based reassurance.\n- The one genuinely annoying risk: Great Vibes as the *global KDE UI font* at size 14. Great Vibes is a formal calligraphy script — poor legibility for UI, and variable-width (README admits this). It won''t lock you out but KDE UI text will be hard to read.\n\n**On the impossible parts — be direct:**\n- No \"Hermes\" agent exists. `~/.hermes/` has one file the installer wrote. No binary, no process, no sessions. I cannot review Hermes sessions because there are none.\n- opencode session history exists (`opencode.db`) but reviewing it isn''t needed to validate a theme install, and I won''t go spelunking through it.\n- \"Prepare the fleet\" — undefined, need clarification.\n\nNow: should I fix the \"Great Vibes Bold\" bug? That''s clearly a defect and the fix is trivial and safe (`Great Vibes Bold` → `Great Vibes`). It''s directly in service of \"make it work.\" Let me fix it — it''s low risk, in the repo source file (so it persists) and the installed copy.\n\nLet me fix it in the repo source AND the installed files, so the fix persists. Actually the user hasn''t asked me to commit. Let me fix the repo source file (gtk/settings.ini) and reinstall, or just patch both. Patching the source is right so the repo isn''t left broken.\n\nLet me do that — fix the source, then re-run install to propagate. Actually re-running install is clean and idempotent. Let me patch source and re-run.\n\nLet me be careful: patching `gtk/settings.ini` to change `Great Vibes Bold,  14` → `Great Vibes, 14`. Also the double-space suggests sloppy. Let me normalize.\n\nLet me make the fix and report. I should ask before committing (per my instructions, never commit unless asked).\n\nLet me apply the fix.","time":{"start":1790446443837,"end":1790446450868}},"time":1790446450868}');
