INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0deee14b3001kB4iuiVrJCw9Zw','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',726,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0deee0196001fLS5DWesoiO5G5","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0deedfb27001HjV0TNlEzLXHGj","type":"reasoning","text":"The user is asking me to check \"previous sessions from the last 3 weeks for the fleet tool we made\" and \"also check from 2 days ago\" and \"rebuild everything that was broken.\"\n\nLet me think about what''s actually available:\n\n1. opencode session history: `~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db` (SQLite, ~843KB + 4MB WAL). This session started today (Sep 26, 2026). The DB is 843KB with a 4MB WAL — so there IS prior content. Files in ~/.local/share/opencode dated Sep 26 11:00-11:13. So opencode was first installed/used around Sep 26 11:00 today. That means session history likely does NOT go back 3 weeks — the tool appears to be ~13 minutes old on this machine.\n\nLet me verify by checking the actual earliest session timestamps in the DB. That''s the honest, verifiable thing to do.\n\n2. \"the fleet tool we made\" — I should check if anything named \"fleet\" exists. Earlier repo list had no \"fleet\". Let me check the DB and the filesystem.\n\n3. Note: the `hermes-blood` repo''s most recent commit is Sep 4, 2026 (`soh-masterquest-build` was Sep 4, but hermes-blood commits were around Sep 21-22 based on other repos). Actually the git log of hermes-blood showed commits but I didn''t get dates. Let me check.\n\nLet me actually investigate the DB — this is a legitimate request and the data is the user''s own. Let me query session/message timestamps to determine the real history depth.\n\nThis is genuinely useful: if the history only goes back to today, I should tell them that plainly rather than pretending to find 3 weeks of sessions.\n\nLet me query the SQLite DB read-only. Important: must open read-only to avoid modifying, and there''s a WAL. Let me use `file:...?mode=ro` and immutable maybe. Actually mode=ro is fine.\n\nLet me explore the schema first.\n\nLet me be careful not to modify the DB — the user is actively using opencode right now, so writing could corrupt. Read-only mode.\n\nLet me do it.","time":{"start":1790446535062,"end":1790446539955}},"time":1790446539955}');
