INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0deee73f2001ehWzamueU4eqan','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',801,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0deee63df001uCIAWDs92Q474u","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0deee5d7a001tMVNmbfmnsBcRg","type":"reasoning","text":"Now the picture is clear and I need to correct my earlier claim:\n\n**Everything happened TODAY (Sep 26, 2026), between 10:53 and 11:04.** Not 3 weeks ago, not 2 days ago. The machine was set up today.\n\n- 10:53 — paru cloned hermes-agent AUR, downloaded 75MB tarball\n- 11:00 — opencode-bin, python311, electron34 also in paru cache\n- 11:02 — tarball downloaded\n- 11:04 — src/ extracted, .git present\n\nSo: the user was installing `hermes-agent` from the AUR **today**, ~1 hour before this session. It was NOT successfully installed (`pacman -Q hermes-agent` → not found). The `pkg/` dir is `d--x--x--x` (execute-only, no read) — that''s paru''s staging dir, and the permissions are odd. That suggests a build was attempted.\n\nAlso notable: `electron34` is in the cache — hermes-agent has a desktop Electron app, hence 75MB tarball and electron dependency.\n\nSo \"the fleet tool we made\" = the fleet subsystem in hermes-agent, and \"rebuild everything that was broken\" = the AUR build of hermes-agent failed / was never completed.\n\nNow, critical honesty points:\n1. There are NO previous sessions. Not 3 weeks, not 2 days. One session, today. I verified this in the DB.\n2. The \"fleet tool\" is not something \"we made\" in a prior session — it''s part of the upstream hermes-agent 2026.9.24 source tree. Though notably there''s `contributors/emails/hermes-fleet-fix@localhost` which hints at local fleet patches. Let me check the git log of that source tree to see if there were local commits — that would tell whether they/we modified fleet code.\n3. hermes-agent is NOT installed. The AUR build is incomplete.\n\nLet me check the git state of the hermes-agent clone and the PKGBUILD to understand what broke. That''s the actual \"rebuild everything that was broken\" work.\n\nLet me investigate the git log and PKGBUILD.\n\nThis is the real work. Let me dig.\n\nLet me be efficient and check: git log in the hermes-agent clone, and the PKGBUILD contents.","time":{"start":1790446560223,"end":1790446564338}},"time":1790446564338}');
