INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0deeeb8c8001E6a9YTngW71kbX','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',856,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0deeea311001hDWUkYgjESeRAD","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0deee9e35001N9wIKAx3cUKbGV","type":"text","text":"I have to correct myself on two counts, and the real story is different from the request.\n\n## Correction 1: there are no previous sessions\n\nThe opencode database contains **exactly one session** — this one, created today at 18:02 UTC. Nothing from 3 weeks ago, nothing from 2 days ago. opencode was installed on this machine today at 11:00. The 8 \"fleet\" matches in the DB are all from *this* conversation — your message and my replies echoing it back.\n\nSo there is no history to review. I checked rather than assumed, but the premise doesn''t hold.\n\n## Correction 2: I was wrong to say \"there is no Hermes\"\n\nLast turn I checked `which hermes` and `~/.hermes/`, then concluded Hermes didn''t exist. That was too broad and I should have looked harder. Hermes is real:\n\n**`hermes-agent`** by NousResearch, and it has a substantial **fleet** subsystem — `update_cmd_fleet.py`, `update_cmd_fleet_checkout.py`, `update_fleet_scope.py`, a `fleet-roster.ts` store, a `fleet-rail.ts` desktop UI, and ~8 test files.\n\nBut it contradicts \"we made\":\n\n```\n## master...origin/master\n?? hermes-agent-2026.9.24.tar.gz\n```\n\nThe AUR clone is **clean** — no local commits, no modified files. Fleet is an upstream feature, not something you and I authored. (`hermes-fleet-fix@localhost` is upstream test-fixture data, not a real contributor.)\n\n## What actually broke\n\n`hermes-agent` is **not installed** — `pacman -Q` returns \"not found\". The AUR build was started today between 10:53 and 11:04 and abandoned. The staging dir is `d--x--x--x` (execute-only, unreadable), which is abnormal and suggests it died mid-`package()`.\n\nAll 17 build dependencies are present, so the build wouldn''t fail on missing deps.\n\n**The rebuild is `paru -S hermes-agent`.** I''m not starting it unprompted, because:\n\n- It needs **sudo** (installs to `/opt`, `/usr/bin`)\n- It''s heavy — `npm ci` with dev deps across 3 workspaces, plus Electron, plus a full `uv sync` of the `all,messaging` extras. Realistically 10–30 min and a lot of network.\n- It half-finished once already today, so I''d want to run it in the foreground and capture the actual error rather than repeat the abort.\n\nWant me to run it? And if it fails, I''ll capture the real error this time instead of leaving a mystery `d--x--x--x` directory.\n\nThe `hermes-blood` rebuild from earlier is done and verified — that''s the other half of \"everything broken,\" unless you meant something else by it.","time":{"start":1790446576401,"end":1790446581959}},"time":1790446581960}');
