INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0defe70de001wpMv17Cl3zwXS3','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1195,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0defe60b60011eEfXjnufbQVGJ","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0defe5630001JqDkcnUPuWKPiA","type":"reasoning","text":"MAJOR correction to my own earlier claim. `~/.hermes` is NOT just a skin file — it has a full structure:\n\n```\naudio_cache  cache  cron  hooks  image_cache  logs  memories\npairing  sessions  skills  skins  SOUL.md\n```\n\nThere IS a `sessions` directory and `SOUL.md` and `memories`! My earlier claim \"There is no Hermes agent / no session history\" was WRONG in its conclusion. Earlier I ran `find ~/.hermes -type f` and got only `skins/blood.yaml`. But that was BEFORE — wait, why does it show all this now?\n\nHmm. Earlier `find ~/.hermes -type f 2>&1 | head -20` returned only `/home/livings/.hermes/skins/blood.yaml`. Now `ls ~/.hermes` shows many dirs. So either:\n1. These are empty directories (find -type f found no files in them, only the skin file existed)\n2. Something created them since\n\nMost likely: they were always there as empty dirs (or with only subdirs), and `find -type f` only found the one file because the others are empty dirs. So hermes DID have a directory structure, just no session FILES.\n\nBut now there''s a `sessions` dir. Let me check if it has content NOW. And SOUL.md, memories, logs.\n\nThis is important — I need to check whether there are actual session files now. Something may have created them (did the build create them? No, the build didn''t install).\n\nWait — could the user have run hermes somehow? Or the tarball extraction? No, extraction was in the paru cache.\n\nLet me actually check contents and timestamps. This is crucial for accuracy — I need to correct myself properly.\n\nLet me investigate ~/.hermes thoroughly.\n\nThis is a significant finding. Let me be careful and thorough.\n\nLet me check.","time":{"start":1790447607990,"end":1790447612126}},"time":1790447612126}');
