INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0defed18a001hPQLoG3gJv5z3S','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1234,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0defeafdc001XSVjYoqDKrq27v","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0defeaade001vrEn7vashyv3TG","type":"text","text":"I have to decline this one, and tell you exactly why — three of the premises are false.\n\n## There is no 3-month session history\n\n| Source | Reality |\n|---|---|\n| opencode sessions | **1 total** — this one, today 18:02 UTC |\n| hermes `sessions/` | **0 files** |\n| hermes `memories/`, `cron/`, `hooks/`, `skills/`, `pairing/` | **0 files each** |\n| `agent.log`, `errors.log` | **0 bytes** |\n\nThat `~/.hermes` tree that looks like prior history **was created 56 seconds ago, by my own build.** `PKGBUILD:69` runs `import hermes_cli.main` as a sanity check, and that import scaffolds `~/.hermes/` — sessions, memories, cron, SOUL.md and all — on first run. Timestamps confirm it: every one is `11:22:00`, except `skins/blood.yaml` at 11:14, which is the theme I installed. Nothing predates today.\n\nSo there''s no 3 months of work to audit, and no hermes sessions to cross-reference. I won''t manufacture a report from nothing.\n\n## Steam isn''t installed\n\n```\nabsent: steam, steam-native, proton, wine, wine-staging\n```\n\nNo Steam, no Proton, no Wine, and no `~/.steam`. So \"save for the ones needed on Steam\" has no basis — there''s no library to check against and no Windows runtime to preserve. I can''t guess which of your projects target Steam.\n\n## What actually exists\n\nYour real artifacts are the **28 GitHub repos** — and those are source trees, not installed tools. Most aren''t reinstallable software at all: `tf2-elysium`, `half-life-2-elysium`, `skyrim-mod-packages`, `loz-ocarina-mq` and ~20 more are C++/Papyrus game projects. \"Reinstall\" doesn''t apply to them.\n\nWhat''s genuinely reinstallable is narrow:\n\n- **`hermes-agent`** — package built and sitting ready (126 MB). Needs your `sudo pacman -U`.\n- **`opencode-bin` 1.18.32**, **`python311` 26.10.0** — installed today and current.\n- **28 repos** — clonable source, not packages.\n\nI won''t mass-reinstall 28 repositories blind. That''s how you break a working machine, and \"audit them all and reinstall\" doesn''t tell me which are meant to be built, which are meant to be run, or which are Windows-only — the repos span Linux-native tools, game mod source trees, and an Electron desktop app with no consistent platform story.\n\n**What I''ll actually do, if you want to pick one:**\n\n1. **Finish hermes** — you run the `pacman -U` above, I verify the binary, the fleet CLI subcommands, and the `blood.yaml` skin wiring end to end.\n2. **Audit the repos properly** — clone your 28, classify each by language/build system/target platform, and report which are Linux-runnable, which need a toolchain that isn''t installed, and which look Windows-only. Read-only, no installs. Then *you* choose what to build.\n3. **Install supercode** — still blocked, I need the repo URL or package name.\n\nOption 2 is closest to what you asked for and is genuinely useful. Say the word and I''ll run it.","time":{"start":1790447628252,"end":1790447636873}},"time":1790447636873}');
