INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0deffcc01001CtqS5Rcng75xhm','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1268,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0deffbc26001chrGduW4fMBeoI","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0deffb542001up4c85NEHoORM2","type":"reasoning","text":"No Link header at all, which means there''s no \"last\" page — i.e., the listing isn''t paginated beyond the first page. With per_page=100 and 28 results returned and no Link header, 28 is the complete public count.\n\nSo confirmed: 28 public, and ~92 private (120 - 28 = 92) that I cannot see.\n\nThe root cause: I authenticated via **SSH** (good for clone/push) but SSH keys cannot authenticate to the REST API. The API needs a token. So the repo listing I did was anonymous.\n\nNow, the fix. I need a way to enumerate private repos. Options:\n1. `gh` (github-cli) with device-flow login — browser-based, no secret in chat. Best option. Needs `sudo pacman -S github-cli`.\n2. A fine-grained PAT stored via git credential helper — but the API needs it in a header, and I won''t handle it in chat.\n\nLet me verify github-cli is available in the repos.\n\nLet me check and present the clear path.\n\nLet me also be honest: this is the cost of choosing SSH. I should own that I could have flagged this earlier when I listed the 28 — I presented it as \"your repos\" when it was only public ones. That''s a real imprecision on my part. Let me acknowledge it.\n\nActually, let me re-read what I said: \"Public side shows 28 repos — nothing named hermes or blood.\" I did say \"Public side.\" So I was somewhat clear. But later I said \"Your real artifacts are the 28 GitHub repos\" which overclaimed. Let me acknowledge the imprecision.\n\nLet me check github-cli availability and give the path forward.","time":{"start":1790447696935,"end":1790447700993}},"time":1790447700993}');
