INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df020ff5001hlGTz3zb5YoSUL','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1413,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df020737001wI4mNCo8BeMemk","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df020299001f8tofPY3i0vmkD","type":"text","text":"Tested and working. Run this — it works from fish, bash, anything:\n\n```bash\nbash -c ''read -rs -p \"token: \" T && printf \"%s\" \"$T\" > ~/.config/gh/token && chmod 600 ~/.config/gh/token && echo saved''\n```\n\nPaste the token at the prompt, press Enter, and you''ll see `saved`. Then tell me and I''ll read it from there.\n\nIf you''d rather stay in fish, the native equivalent is:\n\n```fish\nread -s -P \"token: \" T; printf ''%s'' \"$T\" > ~/.config/gh/token; chmod 600 ~/.config/gh/token; echo saved\n```\n\nNote the difference: fish uses `-P` for a literal prompt string (`-p` expects a command substitution), and `;` instead of `&&`. That mismatch is exactly what tripped up the original command.\n\nTwo other things still open, both needing your terminal:\n\n```bash\nsudo pacman -U /home/livings/.cache/paru/clone/hermes-agent/hermes-agent-0.21.5-1-x86_64.pkg.tar.zst\n```\n\n**And supercode** — I still have no way to find it. Not in the AUR, not in `extra`, not on disk, no binary. I need a repo URL or package name. If it''s a GitHub project, `owner/repo` is enough; I''ll confirm the remote before cloning rather than fetching something arbitrary onto this machine.","time":{"start":1790447847223,"end":1790447849461}},"time":1790447849461}');
