INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df0258b2001EXxLK3x4B8R3JJ','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1456,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df024cbb0016IFR8rjneUK0hN","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df02412a001Ykrf36DDrPBXeq","type":"text","text":"I pre-created the file for you at **`~/.config/gh/token.md`** — mode 600, and outside the Desktop so Baloo won''t index it.\n\nPaste the token there, save, then say \"saved\" and I''ll:\n\n1. Read it from that path\n2. Enumerate all 120 repos (this is the actual goal — the 28-repo list was public-only)\n3. Audit them: language, build system, target platform, whether Linux-runnable\n4. **Delete the file and `shred` it** when done\n\nA `.md` extension isn''t a security measure — it''s just avoiding the Baloo index and any accidental `git add`. The real protections are the 600 perms and the fact that it never touches chat or shell history.\n\nTwo notes on the token itself:\n\n- **30 days** is longer than the 7 I suggested. Fine, but nothing here will warn you when it lapses — put a calendar reminder, or revoke manually at [github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens](https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens).\n- If you set it to **read-only** (`Contents: Read-only`), that''s all the audit needs. The SSH key already grants full git write, so a token doesn''t need to add that. If you accidentally granted write, say so and I''ll tell you what to change.\n\nStill outstanding: **hermes** needs `sudo pacman -U` on the 126 MB package that''s built and waiting, and **supercode** still has no lead I can find — repo URL or package name, or I can''t install it.","time":{"start":1790447865019,"end":1790447868082}},"time":1790447868082}');
