INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df040f0c0025fA9ryH75iKBcg','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1506,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df0402ac001rUo6bcG8hAJlbA","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df03f337001Ue0FKgYCOfUzoF","type":"reasoning","text":"Now it''s clear:\n\n- `~/.config/gh/token` — **186 chars, no trailing newline** (wc -l = 0 means no newline). 186 = 93 × 2. So the token was pasted **TWICE** into the `read` prompt. Actually, `read` reads one line... but if they pasted twice with a newline, read would take the first line. Hmm, but there''s 0 newlines and 186 chars.\n\nActually what likely happened: they ran the `bash -c ''read...''` command, pasted the token, and something caused duplication. Or they pasted the token twice. Either way, `~/.config/gh/token` contains the token duplicated (93+93=186), same ending \"vkZJ\".\n\n- `~/Desktop/token.txt` — **93 chars, ends with newline** (wc -l = 1). This is the correct single token. 93 chars matches a fine-grained PAT length.\n\nBoth end in `vkZJ` so same token, just the config/gh one is doubled.\n\nSo: use the Desktop one (93 chars), strip the newline. Or fix the config/gh one.\n\nLet me:\n1. Fix perms on Desktop file (644 → 600)\n2. Copy the correct 93-char token to ~/.config/gh/token with 600\n3. Verify it works against the API\n4. Then enumerate repos\n\nImportant: I should NOT print the token. Let me do the copy programmatically.\n\nAlso need to exclude from Baloo and later delete.\n\nLet me do the API test first to confirm the token works and get the repo count.\n\nLet me be careful: use the token in a curl header, don''t echo it.\n\nLet me set it up and test.\n\nNote: rate limit was 58/60 unauthenticated. With a token it''s 5000/hour.\n\nLet me do it.","time":{"start":1790447977132,"end":1790447980300}},"time":1790447980300}');
