INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df06a2d9001e7yEhnpKl2DfbN','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1691,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df068784001fkI7hgeSVHvoU1","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df067d8f001SINntCOGQFWopb","type":"text","text":"Inventory confirmed: **120 repos, 470 MB, 92 private.** All 120 were touched within 90 days, so the staleness filter is useless here — this is all recent work.\n\nThe shape is completely different from what I could see before. The 28 public repos were C++ game projects; the 92 private ones are overwhelmingly **Python (53) and Shell (16)** — automation, tooling, bots. Those are the reinstallable things you were asking about. `work-automation`, `himalaya-bot`, `lia-cli`, `business-health-monitor`, `non-steam-games`.\n\nBefore I go further, two corrections to keep on the record, since I was wrong twice:\n\n- I said Hermes had no session history. `~/.hermes` looked like proof otherwise, but every file there was created at 11:22 by the AUR package''s `check()` step importing `hermes_cli.main`. Zero real sessions, confirmed.\n- I reported \"28 repos\" as your inventory twice. That was a token-scoping artifact, not your actual count.\n\nNow — **I''m going to stop and ask rather than clone 470 MB across 120 repos.** Reasons:\n\n`Contents: Read-only` is enough to *read* repo contents via the API, so I can audit without cloning anything at all. That''s cheaper and leaves no trace. Let me do that.\n\nBut \"reinstall them all, excluding Windows tools\" needs judgment calls I can''t make blind. Concretely, `non-steam-games` and the Elysium C++ repos look like Windows/Steam game projects; `zen-suite-iso` and `once-human-linux-fixes` are empty; and I don''t know which of the 53 Python repos are meant to be run versus libraries. Mass-cloning and building 120 repos on a machine whose toolchain I haven''t verified is how you break a working system.\n\nSo, three questions:\n\n1. **Audit method** — read-only via API (no clones, nothing written), or clone locally so you can inspect the files yourself?\n2. **Scope** — all 120, or just the 92 private ones? The 28 public C++ game repos are a different category from your Python tooling.\n3. **\"Reinstall\" means what** — `pip install -e` from each Python repo? Run `install.sh`? Build the C++ ones? I need one concrete example of what you consider \"installed\" for a given repo, or I''ll guess wrong 120 times.\n\nAnd **supercode** — I still have no way to find it. Not in the AUR, not in `extra`, no binary on disk. If it''s one of these 120, tell me which and I''ll treat it normally. If it''s external, I need a URL.\n\nAlso still pending on your side: `sudo pacman -U ~/.cache/paru/clone/hermes-agent/hermes-agent-0.21.5-1-x86_64.pkg.tar.zst`.","time":{"start":1790448142212,"end":1790448149209}},"time":1790448149209}');
