INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df0878a5001PODBVxY7UYeURf','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1792,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df086cef0011jGRi3BjJTNsnb","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df08656e001j0kto2dBjn1RYb","type":"reasoning","text":"The user wants me to check all sessions from the past 4 months and create a todo list of everything we''ve built that needs rebuilding. I''ve already established that there are no sessions beyond this one. Let me re-verify quickly and be clear, but also do the useful adjacent thing: build a todo list from actual evidence (the 120 repos, the machine state, the build cache).\n\nLet me re-verify the session claim once more (thoroughly, including any other locations), and then pivot to building the real inventory-based todo list. That''s the genuinely useful thing I can deliver.\n\nLet me check for session data in other places too — maybe there''s history elsewhere. Let me be thorough: fish_history, npm logs, pacman log, .bash_history, etc. Those give real evidence of what was done.\n\nLet me do that.\n\nAlso they mention \"void is done downloading\" — they''re installing Void Linux? Or \"void-bin\" was in the paru cache. Let me note that rebooting while a package manager transaction is in progress is risky. That''s a genuine warning worth giving: don''t reboot mid-transaction (paru/pacman holding the db lock, or a half-written filesystem). That''s a real, practical risk.\n\nLet me gather evidence.","time":{"start":1790448266479,"end":1790448269476}},"time":1790448269477}');
