INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df0914cd00177vhgi6LfHCY6l','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1885,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df08fd0a001uvth83vOjkPqPY","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df08f2ee0018NDqsoCl98hmOl","type":"text","text":"Two corrections before the list.\n\n**There are no 4-month-old sessions.** One session — this one, today. Zero hermes sessions. The `openai_gpt-5.6-*.jsonl` files I found are hermes''s own bundled *test fixtures*, not your history.\n\n**supercode isn''t real.** Your history shows four attempts, all failures:\n\n| Attempt | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `npm i -g @kirmad/supercode@latest` | **404 Not Found** |\n| `cargo install supercode-cli` | failed |\n| `npm i -g supercode@latest` | **404 Not Found** |\n| `curl cdn.supercode.sh/claude/install.sh \\| bash` | failed |\n\nNeither package exists on npm. The `curl | bash` is worth flagging: piping a remote script straight to a shell is how people get owned, and that domain may not be what you think. **What did you install it for?** If it was meant to replace opencode, `void-bin` — which paru is downloading right now — is literally *\"The open-source Cursor alternative\"*, an Electron editor with a built-in agent. That may be the thing you actually wanted.\n\nAlso: **don''t reboot yet.** `paru -S void-bin` is still live (pid 27643) and holds the pacman lock. Interrupting a package transaction mid-write is how you get a half-installed system. Wait for it to finish, then reboot.\n\nThe todo list, built from your actual history and the 120-repo inventory:","time":{"start":1790448303370,"end":1790448309453}},"time":1790448309453}');
