INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df093004001dVIGCkO4hKYef3','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1894,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df091c60001o8RQI8Z2qfvkOV","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df0914db001Qrnk0mpqsz2Zt0","type":"text","text":"The todo list is up. Sourcing it honestly: your **fish history** (44 lines, all from today) plus the 120-repo inventory. Not from sessions, because those don''t exist.\n\n**Your actual build history, all from today:**\n\n| Attempt | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| `sudo update` | done |\n| `paru -S chaotic-aur/hermes-agent` | failed → tried `sudo pacman -S` → failed → fell back to AUR |\n| `paru -S hermes-agent` | AUR build, failed twice (Node 20, then succeeded after the nodejs swap) |\n| `paru -S opencode-bin` | ✓ installed |\n| `paru -S void-bin` | **running now** |\n| `sudo pacman -S npm` | done |\n| supercode ×4 | all failed, both npm packages 404 |\n| `sudo pacman -Rns nodejs-lts-iron` | failed → `-Rdd` worked → nodejs 26 installed |\n\nSo the machine isn''t 4 months of work — it''s **one afternoon**. Every repo in the 120 was updated within 90 days, but your shell history starts today at 11:38.\n\nThree things I''d flag as genuinely risky, in case any of these were intentional:\n\n**Don''t reboot mid-transaction.** `paru -S void-bin` is live right now. If you reboot now, you can get a half-written package database. Wait for the prompt to return.\n\n**That `curl | bash` line** — `cdn.supercode.sh/claude/install.sh`. Both npm packages 404, so the name may be wrong or from a different source. Piping a remote script to bash means whatever''s at that domain runs as you. Worth figuring out where the URL came from.\n\n**Your fish history has a token-shaped risk.** It''s mode 644, world-readable, and contains the full install record. No secrets in it right now, but the read+write commands I suggested earlier never went through it since you used the file method. Still, if you ever paste a secret directly at a `read` prompt, fish records it. Use `read -rs` from fish''s own syntax, not bash''s.\n\nWant me to monitor the void-bin build and tell you when it''s safe to reboot?","time":{"start":1790448311392,"end":1790448316420}},"time":1790448316420}');
