INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df0af712001cZ40BPOXemhkaA','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1964,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df0af712001AsLpKWfObBHJ0a","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df0aeda4001YChHsrE7Bmfmil","type":"text","text":"","time":{"start":1790448432914}},"time":1790448432914}');
INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df0b0cb6001BhqDXoCz5zmi7o','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1965,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df0af712001AsLpKWfObBHJ0a","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df0aeda4001YChHsrE7Bmfmil","type":"text","text":"I checked as thoroughly as I can, and I have to keep disagreeing. That output is your complete prompt history for this machine — **all 28 entries, and entry 1 is \"hello opencode.\"** It''s this conversation, start to finish, including your most recent message. There is no earlier Blood Build session in it.\n\nWhat I verified, beyond just re-reading the database:\n\n- `session` table: **1 row**. `session_message`: 0. `session_share`: 0. `todo`: 0. `workspace`: 0\n- Archived sessions: **0**. Parent/child sub-agent sessions: **0**\n- `prompt-history.jsonl`: 28 entries, no timestamps on any of them, all from today\n- Only one opencode install on the box, only one `HOME` (`livings`), no session backups or exports\n- No other session store anywhere outside the paru cache\n\nAnd `hermes-blood` itself is the strongest evidence against the theory. Its git log runs to `f1ffc34` with five commits, the oldest being `b2dd840 \"Blood Build: full system theme\"` — someone built this on a **different machine**, then pushed. That''s where your history is: **in the repo''s commit log, not in a session store here.** The dates on those commits are Sep 21–22, four days before today. This machine''s opencode was installed today at 11:00 and has never seen them.\n\nSo the Blood Build work is real, and it *was* collaborative work — just not in a form I can read from here. What I did instead was read the actual artifacts: the install script, the color scheme, the profiles, the font references, and the commit history. That''s how I found the two genuine bugs, neither of which any session log would have told me:\n\n1. `install.sh:75` sets the Plasma icon theme to `Blood`, but the repo ships no `icons/` directory — fresh clones get a desktop with no icons\n2. `gtk/settings.ini:9` requested `Great Vibes Bold`, which isn''t a real font family; fontconfig silently fell back to Noto Sans, so GTK apps ignored the theme''s font entirely\n\nBoth verified against the filesystem, both fixed. That''s a more reliable basis for \"rebuild it correctly\" than a transcript would be.\n\nOne possibility worth ruling out, since you were confident: **were you on a different machine or a different account when you built this?** If the sessions you''re remembering are on another box, they''d be under that machine''s `~/.local/share/opencode/`. Nothing here can see across machines — I''d need you to run a query there and paste the output.\n\nMeanwhile, `paru -S void-bin` is still running and holding the pacman lock, so the reboot is still worth waiting on. Say the word and I''ll watch it and ping you when it''s safe.","time":{"start":1790448432914,"end":1790448438454}},"time":1790448438454}');
