INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df1480c70011HC3ZjA0yB7Wtn','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',2761,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df146d70001bsQ33oxqlMZWnj","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df146206001UoeQyUgI00u88k","type":"text","text":"16pt applied everywhere and committed to `hermes-blood` (`a38327d`), so it survives a re-install. Backup at `~/.local/share/blood-build-backup/20260926_115711`.\n\n| Location | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `kdeglobals` font/fixed | 14 | **16** |\n| `gtk-3.0` / `gtk-4.0` | 14 | **16** |\n| `.gtkrc-2.0` | 10 | **16** |\n| `Garuda.profile` (Konsole) | 12 | **16** |\n| `alacritty.toml` | 11 | **16** |\n\nRepo sources and `install.sh:76-77` updated too, so re-running the installer won''t revert it.\n\n**Bold did not work, and I want to be straight about that.** Great Vibes ships exactly one weight — I confirmed with `fc-list` that only `GreatVibes-Regular.ttf` exists. I added a synthetic-emboldening rule at `~/.config/fontconfig/conf.d/99-greatvibes-bold.conf`, and it still reports `Great Vibes Regular` for `weight=bold`. Fontconfig''s `embolden` isn''t taking effect through `fc-match`, and I don''t want to claim bold is working when the tooling says otherwise.\n\nReal bold needs a font with a bold weight. **Dancing Script** is already installed and is a variable font with a genuine weight axis — it would give you true bold. But commits `f984a14`/`418e662` moved you *off* Dancing Script deliberately, so I''m not swapping it without you saying so.\n\nOptions: leave it regular at 16pt, switch to Dancing Script for real bold, or point me at a Great Vibes bold file if you have one. I can also try the embolden rule differently — it may need to be an `<edit>` on the font element rather than a pattern match.\n\n**Two things still open, and one correction:**\n\n`paru` has now been running over an hour on the Chromium clone and still holds the pacman lock. Steam and the emulators can''t install until it''s done or killed.\n\nI''d also correct my earlier lockout theory. I claimed no-bold was part of the risk, but that''s wrong — apps fall back to regular cleanly, they don''t break. The real risk was always just legibility of a script face at small sizes. Going to 16pt genuinely helps, which is a point in this change''s favour.\n\nAnd **supercode** still has no lead: both npm packages 404, and `void-bin` is the open-source Cursor alternative paru is currently building. If that''s what you were after, say so and I''ll wire it up once the lock clears.","time":{"start":1790449053040,"end":1790449057990}},"time":1790449057991}');
