INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df15394b00132y2UiqcU1DJU4','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',2945,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df1530af001Q2wvR5TxF4ZMOZ","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df152570001cpR380iQxDehVJ","type":"reasoning","text":"My test harness has a bug — the `$schema` in the f-string is being interpolated. And case a/c \"correctly refused\" is wrong; they should succeed. Let me look: the issue is `cfg.get(''$schema'')` inside a bash heredoc with ''PY'' quoted... actually PY is quoted so no interpolation. But the f-string `f\"{p.split(''/'')[-1]}: theme=... schema={cfg.get(''$schema'',''(none)'')}\"` — inside an f-string, `$schema` is fine. Hmm.\n\nWait, why did a.jsonc fail to parse? a.jsonc is valid JSON. The regex `(?m)(^\\s*|[:,{}\\[\\]])//.*$` — the issue is `https://opencode.ai/...` — the `//` in `https://` is preceded by `:` which IS in the character class `[:,{}\\[\\]]`. So `://opencode.ai/config.json` gets stripped! That''s exactly the bug I identified earlier in my test but the real script still has it.\n\nSo the comment stripper is broken for URLs. I need to fix that in the actual script. Let me use a proper approach: only strip // comments when the line, before //, doesn''t look like part of a URL. Better: use a simple state machine, or just require that // is not preceded by `:`.\n\nLet me fix it properly.","time":{"start":1790449103023,"end":1790449105227}},"time":1790449105227}');
