INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df15b5fd001V6dgsnlzZdMyU8','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',3050,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df15b5fc001MX4C8npgaXyf4d","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df15b5fb001OZSS7Gdx1qa2t0","type":"text","text":"and then after reinstall all of my toolsets and reenable my BDE patrols and my Lin-antimalware systems"},"time":1790449137149}');
INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df15b5ff001qG1Jt1jyLz71ND','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',3051,'session.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","info":{"id":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","slug":"glowing-wolf","projectID":"global","directory":"/home/livings","path":"home/livings","summary":{"additions":0,"deletions":0,"files":0},"cost":0,"tokens":{"input":45841,"output":48379,"reasoning":30708,"cache":{"read":12933929,"write":0}},"title":"New session - 2026-09-26T18:02:29.035Z","agent":"build","model":{"id":"big-pickle","providerID":"opencode"},"version":"1.18.32","time":{"created":1790445749035,"updated":1790449137150}}}');
INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df15c6b6001gs7UP12JZOW5FL','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',3052,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df15aa5a001xrZtlDYI5wXUZ3","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df15a32f0015EfC7zU86RF5ip","type":"text","text":"I''m stopping here rather than installing this, and the reason is concrete.\n\n**`healer.py` runs 7 distinct `sudo` commands as a background daemon every 5 minutes, on a timer:**\n\n| Line | Command | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| 35 | `sudo snapper create -c root` | root snapshot |\n| 41 | `sudo snapper rollback -c root` | **rolls back root filesystem** |\n| 96 | `sudo pacman -Sc` | clears package cache |\n| 98 | `sudo journalctl --vacuum-size=50M` | deletes logs |\n| 103 | `sudo systemctl restart {svc}` | **restarts arbitrary services** |\n| 107 | `sudo auditctl -l` | reads audit rules |\n\nPlus `shell=True` with string interpolation on `svc` at lines 68 and 103 — a service name containing shell metacharacters is command injection. And `run()` at line 27 uses `shell=True` throughout.\n\n**Three concrete blockers:**\n\n**1. It was built for a machine that no longer exists.** The service hardcodes `User=sin` and `/home/sin/zen/ai-healer/healer.py`. You''re `livings` with a home at `/home/livings`. The rebuild changed both. As written it cannot start.\n\n**2. `sudo` inside a systemd timer needs a rule that doesn''t exist.** Timer units have no TTY, so `sudo` would either hang or fail. This needs a `visudo` entry — the same passwordless-sudo step you haven''t done yet.\n\n**3. A daemon that can roll back root and restart services, unattended, every 5 minutes, is exactly the shape of thing that locks you out of a machine.** You already rebuilt this device once. I''m not installing that on autopilot, and I''d want you to have read `healer.py` in full first — 167 lines, and I''ve only seen the lines matching my grep.\n\n**What I''d suggest instead**, in order:\n\n1. **Read it with me, line by line.** 167 lines is short. I''ll show you every `sudo` and destructive call and explain what each does before anything runs.\n2. **Fix the hardcoded paths** for `livings`, install the units, but **leave the timer disabled** (`systemctl --user enable --now` not run). Install it, verify by hand, enable later.\n3. **Strip the risky calls** — the snapper rollback and the journal vacuum are the ones that can bite you. A healer that reports and alerts without mutating root is much safer.\n\nThe `business-debug-wrappers` and `business-health-monitor` repos are far tamer — wrappers, scans, and a daily report. `business-health-monitor` is already referenced in your fish history and its installer is a straightforward wrapper-plus-cron. Happy to install that one now.\n\nOne thing worth noting: your fish history shows `sudo update` as the very first command on the rebuild, and `hermes` was never successfully run. The healer is the tool you''d have used to catch that, which may be why it feels urgent — but it''s also the tool most capable of making things worse unattended.\n\nWhich of the three do you want? And has `paru` finished, incidentally? It''s been over an hour holding the pacman lock.","time":{"start":1790449134170,"end":1790449141430}},"time":1790449141430}');
