INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df1aadcc002yLWfzumxm5wj6t','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',93,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df1a9bf9001wbGGkX6C2XaVhy","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df1a9861001Ad1o4wNg6wuYd7","type":"reasoning","text":"So the build uses `makepkg-source-roller.py generate electron/DEPS $pkgname` which presumably reads `chromium-mirror/DEPS` and generates `prepare-electron-source-tree.sh` that symlinks/copies the `chromium-mirror_*` dirs into `src/<path>`.\n\nSo `chromium-mirror` needs to be a real git checkout at tag 132.0.6834.210 (at least have DEPS and the chromium source tree).\n\nSo the plan is clear. We need the chromium source tree at tag 132.0.6834.210. Full git clone = 37 GiB, ~29.5M objects. Way overkill.\n\nBest fix: pre-seed `/home/livings/.cache/paru/clone/electron34/chromium-mirror` as a **shallow, blob-filtered** clone of just that tag, so:\n- `git clone --filter=blob:none --depth 1 --branch 132.0.6834.210` → only ~1 commit''s worth of data (~1.5 GB working tree). Actually with blob:none filter and checkout, git downloads all blobs at checkout time → effectively downloads the full tarball (~1.4 GB) but WITHOUT history. That''s a huge win: 37 GiB → ~1.5 GiB.\n- Even better `--filter=tree:0` doesn''t help for checkout.\n- Alternatively, use `--depth=1` alone (no filter): depth 1 clone downloads all blobs for that one commit, plus one tree. That''s basically the same ~1.4GB. So `--depth=1` alone is sufficient and simplest.\n\nThen makepkg sees the dir already exists as a git repo, does `git fetch` (which on a depth-1 repo with the same tag already present is essentially a no-op / tiny), checks out, and moves on.\n\nLet me verify how makepkg''s get_git works in this Arch install. Find makepkg lib.\n\nLet me find makepkg script location.\n\nAlso, the other ~200 `chromium-mirror_*::git+...` clones from chromium.googlesource.com — those are smaller, and makepkg clones them with full history which can be slow, but they already worked (the error was only for chromium-mirror). Actually did they? The clone error happened at chromium-mirror which is the first one. The rest hadn''t started. Some of those googlesource repos can also be big. But let''s focus.\n\nAlso `git.sh` — I need to know whether makepkg uses `--mirror` (bare) or `--no-checkout`. Note the error message said \"Cloning into bare repository\" — so makepkg uses bare clone. If it''s bare, makepkg then does checkout into... hmm, for a bare clone makepkg does `git -C $srcdir ... archive` or `git clone` from the mirror. Let''s read the actual code.\n\nLet me locate makepkg.","time":{"start":1790449458169,"end":1790449462732}},"time":1790449462732}');
