INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df1cd01e001RWH16A5xJut4R9','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',3651,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df1cb83a001KO91qgVldd9hX7","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df1cb218001nR65f62y490QVG","type":"text","text":"Diagnostics done. Your sudo worked — everything below is verified live, not inferred.\n\n## Healthy\n\n| Area | State |\n|---|---|\n| Disk | 15G used / 477G, **4%** |\n| Updates | **0 pending** |\n| Failed units | **none** |\n| Kernel | 7.2.7-zen1-1-zen, 1h18m uptime |\n| GPU | both i915 + NVIDIA loaded, modesetting correctly |\n| Encryption | LUKS2 on root, intact |\n| Hardening | **all 13 sysctl changes live** — `kptr_restrict=1`, `perf_event_paranoid=3`, redirects off, no core dumps |\n\nYour sysctl took effect, not just the file copy. Good.\n\n## Three real problems\n\n**1. Firewall is inert.** This is the important one.\n\n```\nfirewalld  installed: yes\nfirewalld  active   : inactive\n```\n\nThe `public.xml` you copied is sitting in `/etc/firewalld/zones/` doing nothing. Nothing enforces it. And there''s no ufw, no active nftables — so you currently have **no packet filtering at all**. Fix:\n\n```bash\nsudo systemctl enable --now firewalld\nsudo firewall-cmd --list-all\n```\n\n**2. `kdeconnectd` is listening on all interfaces.**\n\n```\ntcp LISTEN 0 50 *:1716   kdeconnectd\n```\n\nThat''s every interface, not loopback. KDE Connect can accept file transfers and remote input, so it''s the widest door you have open. It''d be blocked once firewalld runs, but I''d also set it to trusted-network-only.\n\n**3. Two config bugs:**\n\n`~/.config/environment.d/firefox.conf` line 1 is malformed — `env MOZ_USE_XINPUT2=1 firefox`. That''s an Exec line, not a variable. systemd rejects it (log at 10:48). Should be:\n```\nMOZ_USE_XINPUT2=1\n```\n\n**Minor:** 848M free RAM, 1.8G swap in use. Two `opencode` processes at ~750M each are the cause, plus Firedragon. No OOM kills — the \"system too slow\" kwin messages are from the two heavy opencode processes, not a fault.\n\n**Cleanup available:** 18 orphans, 3.8G pacman cache, 3.1G paru cache. ~7G reclaimable.\n\n## Small inconsistency worth knowing\n\n`ss` shows no process names on the `:5353` (mDNS) sockets, but your `firewalld-workstation.conf` disables mdns. Harmless — the sockets are avahi''s, and mdns is about responses, not the listener.\n\n## Where this leaves us\n\nThe firewall is the one thing I''d fix right now. Everything else can wait.\n\nWant me to:\n- **Fix the two config bugs** (firefox.conf, KDE Connect scope) — I can do both without root\n- **Clean the ~7G** of caches and orphans\n- Then get back to the installs, now that `paru` has finished and the lock is clear\n\nNote the lock *is* clear now and there are 0 pending updates — so `lin-antimalware`, `business-health-monitor`, `business-debug-wrappers`, and the zen-suite ISO build are all unblocked. Say which and I''ll start.","time":{"start":1790449596474,"end":1790449602590}},"time":1790449602590}');
