INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df2343d9001f1ebeqmvWxrA9k','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',305,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df2337d8001rioq4YmSvtwWb8","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df2333dc001xJruVEPs3SIE4V","type":"reasoning","text":"Two issues surfaced:\n\n1. `warning: remote HEAD refers to nonexistent ref, unable to checkout` — the bare mirror has no HEAD pointing at a valid ref. makepkg''s `extract_git` handles this: `ref=origin/HEAD` default, but since fragment is `tag=...`, ref=`132.0.6834.210`, so it always runs `git checkout -B makepkg $ref`. So the warning is harmless.\n\n2. **`fatal: sha1 file ... index.lock write error. Out of diskspace`** — the checkout failed because of **disk space**! Wait, we have 462 GB free. Let me check. The message \"Out of diskspace\" is git''s generic write-failure message. But 3.7G was written...\n\nHold on. Let me check actual disk space now. Something''s off. Let me check df.\n\nOh wait — maybe /tmp is a tmpfs with limited size! I put the sandbox in /tmp/opencode/mktest. If /tmp is tmpfs, that''s the problem — tmpfs is often 50% of RAM.\n\nLet me check. That''s my test-harness mistake, not a real problem with the fix. The real build happens in /home/livings/.cache/paru/clone/electron34/src which is on the 477G LUKS volume with 462G free.\n\nLet me verify /tmp filesystem and redo the test in the real location.\n\nLet me check df for /tmp.\n\nAlso I should clean up the 3.7G test dir.\n\nLet me redo the test properly under /home/livings to confirm checkout works.\n\nActually, better: rather than a full test checkout (3.7 GB and 20s+), I can test the checkout in the actual build dir since that''s where it will live anyway. But that would leave a partial state. Let me just do the test in a dir under /home/livings, confirm, then remove it.\n\nLet me check df first.","time":{"start":1790450022360,"end":1790450025432}},"time":1790450025433}');
