INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df25d03f001sH4Xf5B5fAMyBJ','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',449,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df25c241001MAAOPm82M2u3zh","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df25bda2001MHFzLk0a55fVLm","type":"reasoning","text":"The user says: \"lets do that check hermes and reapply the fleet systems to hermes and opencode on my system\"\n\nThis is quite vague and references \"hermes\" (from the handoff message) and \"fleet systems\". The previous message was a handoff from \"Hermes\" which I was told to acknowledge only. Now the user wants to \"do that check hermes\" and \"reapply the fleet systems to hermes and opencode on my system.\"\n\nKey issues:\n1. \"that check hermes\" — ambiguous. Do they mean read /tmp/hermes-handoff.md? Or run some check?\n2. \"fleet systems\" — I have no idea what this means. There''s no established term in our conversation.\n3. \"reapply the fleet systems to hermes and opencode on my system\" — no established meaning.\n\nI need to be careful here. This is exactly the kind of ambiguous request where I should not guess and start modifying system configuration. The user said \"on my system\" — this could involve installing things, changing configs, applying dotfiles.\n\nI have no context on what \"fleet systems\" means. It could be:\n- Some systemd units?\n- A set of configuration files?\n- Fleet management (like Ansible/Fleet)?\n- Something from the hermes project?\n\nLet me first check what exists. I could look at ~/Projects/hermes-blood and see if there''s something called \"fleet\". Let me investigate before asking — that''s the proactive approach. But I must not install/change anything yet.\n\nLet me search for \"fleet\" in the projects.\n\nActually, let me be careful and efficient. Let me look for what \"fleet\" refers to. Let me check the hermes projects.\n\nLet me do read-only investigation first, then ask if still ambiguous.\n\nThe user did NOT repeat the \"do not act\" instruction — that was specifically \"in response to\" the handoff message. Now they''re giving a new instruction. So I can act, but I need clarity on what \"fleet systems\" means before making system changes.\n\nLet me investigate first.","time":{"start":1790450188865,"end":1790450192447}},"time":1790450192447}');
