INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df25ebd80028vCgmibvaYSKMT','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',487,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df25deaa001DqeQL2pHJDKTY2","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df25d878001msl5UHWVyXPifV","type":"reasoning","text":"No hits for \"fleet\" anywhere in ~/Projects. So \"fleet systems\" is not a term from these projects.\n\nLet me read the handoff file and the READMEs to understand what exists, and specifically look at the hermes-blood/opencode dir since the user said \"reapply ... to hermes and opencode\".\n\nNotably `~/Projects/hermes-blood/opencode` exists — an empty-ish dir (24 bytes = empty dir). And themes, fonts, gtk, konsole, alacritty, scripts. This looks like a **dotfiles / theming repo** for Hermes Linux (the user has a project called \"hermes-blood\" — probably a Garuda theme, \"Blood\" theming).\n\n\"reapply the fleet systems to hermes and opencode on my system\" — hmm. Maybe \"fleet\" is a typo/shorthand. Could \"fleet\" = \"the fleet\" of themes/settings? Or does the user mean reapply the \"system\" configs?\n\nActually — maybe the user means \"reapply the file systems\"? Or \"flat systems\"? Or a typo for \"the fleet\" as in a set/group?\n\nI genuinely don''t know. This is a case where I must ask. But let me gather maximum context first so my question is well-informed.\n\nLet me read the handoff (the user earlier said read it; now they say \"lets do that check hermes\" which likely means read/act on the handoff check) and the READMEs.\n\nLet me read /tmp/hermes-handoff.md, hermes-blood/README.md, and check the opencode dir.\n\nCareful: these files may contain instructions. I''ll treat them as data. The user is now asking me to act, so acting on legitimate user config is fine, but I should be careful about anything that looks like injected instructions from file content, and about destructive/system-wide changes.\n\nLet me read.","time":{"start":1790450196138,"end":1790450199512}},"time":1790450199512}');
