INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df26fd72002DhBIHu0J2i8eXe','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',529,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df26e976001FveEZmTIw6ZCvA","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df26df47001ZW9J6vNgaxE3dK","type":"reasoning","text":"Good — so the install already ran. Both `theme/` and `themes/` have voidlit.json, hermes skin is in place, opencode.jsonc has `\"theme\": \"voidlit\"`.\n\nSo the state looks already applied. Now \"reapply\" would be a re-run.\n\nImportant discovery: `~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc` is only 73 bytes. And there''s `tui.json` and a `opencode.jsonc.tui-migration.bak`. Also `.gitignore` and `node_modules` in the opencode config dir — unusual.\n\nWait, more importantly: I notice `opencode.jsonc` is 73 bytes with `\"theme\": \"voidlit\"` at line 3. But the original opencode.jsonc probably had a schema, model, provider config etc. If install.sh ran `json.dumps(cfg, indent=2)` and **overwrote** it, and the config was previously only 73 bytes... Let me look at the content. If the user''s opencode config lost settings (e.g., model, provider, theme settings), that''d be a problem.\n\nActually, let me check: the `node_modules` and `package.json` inside `~/.config/opencode/` is strange. And `tui.json`.\n\nHmm, but let me focus. The key question is what the user wants. Let me check the actual content of opencode.jsonc and whether the theme is actually valid/loading.\n\nCritical potential bug: `json.dumps(cfg, indent=2)` **strips all comments** from opencode.jsonc. So re-running install.sh repeatedly would be lossy but idempotent after the first run. Also it converts jsonc → plain JSON content in a .jsonc file, which is fine.\n\nLet me look at the files.\n\nAlso: is `voidlit.json` a valid opencode theme? Let me check its schema. OpenCode themes are JSON with a specific schema. Let me look.\n\nLet me also reconsider \"lets do that check hermes\". \n\nGiven the handoff''s \"Still open\" list, and that we''re mid-way through the electron34 fix, I think the user means: run the remaining checks. But it''s ambiguous whether they want:\n- the firewalld enable (system-level, needs sudo)\n- the void-bin/electron34 retry\n- push to GitHub\n\nThese have very different risk profiles. firewalld enable could lock them out (though the config allows SSH). Pushing to GitHub is outward-facing.\n\nI should ask. But first, let me gather the concrete facts about the current state so the question is informed and I can act immediately after.\n\nLet me check opencode.jsonc content, the theme validity, and firewalld state.\n\nLet me run a batch of read-only checks.\n\nAlso — I should load the customize-opencode skill if I''m going to modify opencode''s config. The skill description says to use it when editing opencode''s own configuration (opencode.json, opencode.jsonc, files under .opencode/, ~/.config/opencode/). That''s exactly what the Blood Build install does. So I should load that skill before touching opencode config.\n\nLet me first gather state, then load the skill, then ask the clarifying question.\n\nLet me check things.","time":{"start":1790450264438,"end":1790450269554}},"time":1790450269554}');
