INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df27290c001iSeA7ZQgnEkR9y','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',559,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df2708a8001qB6s2wjqDpV7Sv","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df27046f001id49WMVVQojkz6","type":"reasoning","text":"Now the user says: \"rebuild the global agent system i had in place before\"\n\nThis is another vague request. \"global agent system\" — what does this mean? Let me think about what I know:\n\n- There''s a `~/.hermes` tree (Hermes Agent), hermes-agent 0.21.5 package\n- There''s opencode with a global config at `~/.config/opencode/`\n- The handoff mentions \"Hermes sessions: exactly 1\", \"OpenCode sessions: 2\"\n- There were \"healer daemon / BDE patrols / antivirus / hardening daemons: not installed\" in \"Deliberately not done\"\n\n\"the global agent system i had in place before\" — the user claims they had one before. The handoff says session history before the machine rebuild is gone: \"Session history before the machine rebuild is gone; provenance lives in the git logs of the repos above, not in transcripts.\"\n\nSo there WAS a previous system, but there''s no record of what it was beyond the git logs. The handoff explicitly notes the \"healer daemon\" was deliberately not installed and specifically flags it as dangerous: \"The healer runs `sudo snapper rollback -c root` on a 5-minute timer with `shell=True` interpolation.\"\n\nThis is a critical situation. The user is asking me to rebuild something whose definition I don''t have, referencing a prior state that:\n1. Was never documented in the handoff\n2. Included components explicitly flagged as dangerous (auto-rollback daemon on a timer, antivirus, hardening daemons, BDE patrols)\n3. Has no surviving record\n\nI genuinely cannot \"rebuild\" something I have no specification for. If I guess, I could easily install a daemon that runs `sudo snapper rollback` on a timer — that would be destructive to the user''s system (auto-reverting the root filesystem every 5 minutes).\n\nThis is exactly the case where I should NOT guess and act. I must ask for clarification / state what I know and what''s missing.\n\nLet me be honest and concrete:\n- I have no record of the previous \"global agent system.\" The handoff explicitly says pre-rebuild session history is gone.\n- The only surviving trace is 4 local git repos, none pushed to GitHub.\n- The handoff lists components \"deliberately not done,\" some of which are risky (healer daemon = `sudo snapper rollback -c root` every 5 min via `shell=True`).\n\nSo I should:\n1. Tell them I can''t reconstruct it from nothing.\n2. Point to what evidence survives (the git repos, buildlog, the backup dir).\n3. Check whether the git history actually contains a prior version of such a system — that''s the legitimate place to look. Let me search the git logs for anything agent-system-like.\n4. Flag the dangerous component and not install it without explicit confirmation.\n\nLet me actually investigate the git history across all 4 repos for evidence of a prior \"agent system\" — commits, deleted files, stashes, other branches. That''s the right move: find the actual provenance rather than invent.\n\nLet me do that investigation, then report and ask.\n\nLet me check:\n- git log --all, reflog, stash, dangling objects in each repo\n- any files ever tracked named *agent*, *hermes*, *daemon*, *service*, systemd units\n- the buildlog journal (which the handoff says is \"the durable build journal built after the lockout\" — \"worth using for anything that should survive the next rebuild\"). buildlog might contain the history of what was installed!\n\nThat''s the key lead: `~/Projects/buildlog` with `buildlog build|fix|env|push` and a `logs/` dir. The handoff says it''s \"the durable build journal built after the lockout\". If it records installs, it may document the previous agent system.\n\nLet me investigate all of this.\n\nLet me run the searches.\n\nThis is genuinely the right approach: recover the spec from surviving evidence rather than invent it.","time":{"start":1790450272424,"end":1790450280716}},"time":1790450280716}');
