INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df2768a5002w67A854EoOe4If','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',596,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df273f750014jXjrhzVjLYL95","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df273a5c00144YxdlQnvpdOse","type":"reasoning","text":"Now I have real evidence. Key findings:\n\n1. **Line 39**: `void-bin: paru stuck 55min cloning all of Chromium (code.sh source redirects to chromium mirror); 0 bytes in 15s - AUR packaging bug`\n\nSo `void-bin` is an AUR package whose `code.sh` source redirects to the chromium mirror. That''s why the user said \"it was a void install i need void\" — they meant the **`void-bin` AUR package**, not a Void Linux installation! Now the earlier confusion is fully resolved. My correction (\"this box is not Void\") was technically true but missed the actual intent: they wanted the `void-bin` AUR package built via paru.\n\nWait — but the chromium-mirror I pre-seeded is for `electron34`, not `void-bin`. The handoff line 35-38 says \"void-bin never installed. The chromium mirror is now pre-seeded as a 1.3 GB shallow bare mirror at ~/.cache/paru/clone/electron34/chromium-mirror (tag 132.0.6834.210, 1 ref) instead of the 37 GB full-history clone that died. Retry should work.\"\n\nHmm, so the handoff conflates: the pre-seeded mirror is in the `electron34` directory, but the package that needed it is `void-bin`. That''s a discrepancy! `void-bin` would have its own clone dir `~/.cache/paru/clone/void-bin/...`. So the pre-seed I did (in electron34/) does NOT help void-bin.\n\nLet me verify what void-bin''s sources actually are.\n\n2. **Line 47**: \"machine was rebuilt after a lockout; prior session history lost. 120 repos intact via git remote. Prime lockout suspect: Great Vibes as global KDE UI font (calligraphy, size 14, no bold/italic) reaching lock screen + dialogs\"\n\nThis is critical context. The user''s machine was REBUILT after a LOCKOUT, and the prime suspect was Great Vibes as the global KDE UI font. And the Blood Build theme **sets Great Vibes as the global KDE UI font** (kdeglobals General font + fixed). And line 51 says they bumped it 10/12/14 → 16pt to mitigate.\n\nSo: **reapplying the Blood Build theme = re-applying Great Vibes as the global UI font, which is the documented cause of a previous system lockout.** That''s a serious warning I must raise before \"reapplying.\"\n\n3. **Line 35**: `supercode: 4 install attempts, all failed - npm @kirmad/supercode and supercode both 404 Not Found`\n\nSo there was a \"supercode\" agent component that failed.\n\n4. There''s no mention of a \"global agent system\" as a distinct thing. The agents present: hermes (0.21.5), opencode (1.18.32), supercode (failed).\n\nSo \"rebuild the global agent system i had in place before\" most plausibly means: get hermes + opencode working again as the global agents. But there''s no recorded \"global agent system\" — and the one dangerous extra (the healer daemon with `sudo snapper rollback` timer) was explicitly \"deliberately not done.\"\n\nNow, what should I do? The user has now asked three times for vaguely-specified things, and I''ve been investigating. I have real, decision-relevant findings. I should:\n\n1. Report the key discoveries, especially:\n   - `void-bin` is an AUR package — that''s what \"void\" meant. My earlier correction was wrong in spirit. I should own that.\n   - The pre-seeded mirror is in the WRONG directory for void-bin (electron34/ vs void-bin/).\n   - **The Great Vibes lockout risk** — reapplying Blood Build re-applies the font that was blamed for a lockout.\n   - There''s no surviving spec for a \"global agent system\"; the only agents recorded are hermes + opencode (+ supercode which 404''d).\n   - Nothing is pushed to GitHub, so the \"120 repos intact via git remote\" claim needs checking — the handoff says nothing was pushed, so those remotes may be unreachable/unpushed. Actually \"120 repos intact via git remote\" suggests they HAVE remotes. But \"Nothing has been pushed to GitHub\" for these 4 repos. Contradiction worth noting.\n\n2. Ask the user what they actually want, with concrete options.\n\nLet me quickly check void-bin and the fontconfig/lockout state to be maximally useful. Let me verify:\n- Is there a void-bin in paru cache? What''s its PKGBUILD source?\n- Current KDE font setting (is Great Vibes currently applied?)\n\nLet me do that, then report + ask.\n\nI should be careful not to over-run. Let me do one focused batch.\n\nLet me check void-bin sources and current font state.\n\nThis is genuinely important: if the user re-runs install.sh, it sets Great Vibes as global UI font at 16pt, which is the documented lockout suspect. I must flag it. The user did already bump to 16pt and added a synthetic bold rule, so they were mitigating. Still worth flagging.\n\nLet me check.","time":{"start":1790450286453,"end":1790450296997}},"time":1790450296997}');
