INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df27c640001DasCtSY880XhyP','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',651,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df279974001YwYYijHsRYSLtv","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df279530001sxmmrdDGz2z5m6","type":"reasoning","text":"Now I have the complete picture. Let me summarize the decisive findings:\n\n**1. Correction I owe the user: \"void\" = `void-bin` AUR package = the Void *editor* (a Cursor alternative), NOT Void Linux.**\n- `void-bin` provides `void`, \"The open-source Cursor alternative\", from github.com/voideditor.\n- My earlier \"this machine is not Void, there''s no Void install\" was factually true about the OS but completely missed the intent. I should own this clearly.\n\n**2. The dependency chain is now proven:**\n`void-bin` depends on `electron34` (`_elnum=34`, `depends=(electron${_elnum} ...)`).\nSo building `void-bin` REQUIRES building `electron34`, which is the package whose 37 GiB chromium clone died. **My pre-seeded shallow mirror at `~/.cache/paru/clone/electron34/chromium-mirror` is exactly the right fix, in exactly the right directory.** The handoff''s line 35-38 was correct after all — I misread it as a discrepancy.\n\nWait, let me re-read the handoff: \"void-bin never installed. The chromium mirror is now pre-seeded as a 1.3 GB shallow bare mirror at ~/.cache/paru/clone/electron34/chromium-mirror (tag 132.0.6834.210, 1 ref) instead of the 37 GB full-history clone that died. Retry should work.\"\n\nYes — correct. void-bin → electron34 → chromium mirror. My pre-seed unblocks it. Good, so the work I did is directly on the critical path for the thing the user actually wants.\n\n**3. Great Vibes lockout risk is CURRENTLY ACTIVE.**\n`~/.config/kdeglobals` currently has:\n```\nfont=Great Vibes,16,-1,5,75,0,0,0,0,0\nfixed=Great Vibes,16,-1,5,4,75,0,0,0,0,0\n```\nGreat Vibes is the global KDE UI font RIGHT NOW. The buildlog (line 47) says: \"machine was rebuilt after a lockout; prior session history lost... Prime lockout suspect: Great Vibes as global KDE UI font (calligraphy, size 14, no bold/italic) reaching lock screen + dialogs.\"\nAnd fc-list confirms Great Vibes has only Regular weight.\n\nSo the user has already been locked out once by this, and the font is currently re-applied. Re-running install.sh re-applies it (same 16pt). This is a genuine, documented risk of another lockout.\n\n**4. No \"global agent system\" is recorded anywhere.** The surviving agents are:\n- hermes 0.21.5 (built via makepkg, 126MB)\n- opencode 1.18.32\n- supercode — FAILED, npm 404 both `@kirmad/supercode` and `supercode`\nThe \"healer daemon / BDE patrols / antivirus / hardening daemons\" were \"deliberately not done\" and the healer is described as running `sudo snapper rollback -c root` on a 5-min timer with `shell=True`.\n\n**5. Durability gap:** 3 of 4 repos have NO remote. Only hermes-blood has one. The buildlog README''s whole premise is \"Code survives because it was pushed\" — but nothing is pushed. So a rebuild would lose zen-hardening, nyan-gfsf-alert, and buildlog entirely, including the very journal meant to survive rebuilds.\n\nNow, what does the user want? \"rebuild the global agent system i had in place before.\"\n\nHonestly: there is no evidence of a \"global agent system\" beyond hermes + opencode (+ failed supercode). The most likely intent: get the agent tooling working — i.e., finish `void-bin` (the editor the agents use?) and have hermes + opencode operational.\n\nBut I''ve been asked three times now with vague scope. I should:\n- Report the correction about void-bin (important, I was wrong).\n- Report the Great Vibes lockout risk (important safety issue).\n- Report that no \"global agent system\" spec survives.\n- Ask what to prioritize, with concrete options.\n\nLet me also note: I''ve been doing a lot of investigation without acting. The user''s original concrete ask (\"fix that please\" = the clone) IS now genuinely fixed and verified. I should state that clearly as the one completed thing.\n\nLet me now ask a focused question. Options for \"global agent system\":\n\nA. Finish void-bin (unblocks: electron34 build, hours) — the one thing clearly on the critical path\nB. Re-apply Blood Build theme (but flag lockout risk; offer to exclude the KDE font)\nC. Fix the durability gap (add git remotes / push)\nD. Re-create the deliberately-not-done daemons (I should push back — healer daemon auto-rollback is dangerous)\n\nLet me ask with the question tool. And be concise in the text.\n\nLet me structure the response tightly.\n\nI''ll present findings then ask.\n\nRegarding \"lets do that check hermes\" from before — the hermes agent: let me quickly note hermes is installed as 0.21.5-1. I didn''t verify if it''s currently working. I could check `hermes --version`. Let me include that in a final quick check? I have enough. Let me just ask, but mention I can verify hermes runs.\n\nActually, let me do one quick check on hermes + opencode actually running, since \"do that check hermes\" may mean that, and it makes my report complete. Quick and cheap.\n\nLet me combine: run the check AND then ask. I''ll run the check first.\n\nLet me be efficient — one command, then the question.","time":{"start":1790450309492,"end":1790450320960}},"time":1790450320960}');
