INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df27f17f001rapbmac9txn5nA','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',676,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df27e90c001WibcS6gEl6m0J0","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df27cdcc001sriEhSRZUHRCVd","type":"tool","callID":"call_function_kowp0zz9gwby_1","tool":"question","state":{"status":"running","input":{"questions":[{"header":"What to build first","options":[{"description":"electron34 build then paru -S void-bin. Clone already fixed; still needs ~165 DEPS git sources fetched + multi-hour Chromium compile.","label":"Finish void-bin (recommended)"},{"description":"Re-run install.sh for Hermes + OpenCode only, skipping the kdeglobals Great Vibes lines so the lockout suspect stays off the lock screen.","label":"Reapply theme, but skip the KDE font"},{"description":"Re-run install.sh as-is, re-applying Great Vibes globally at 16pt. Accepts lockout risk.","label":"Reapply full Blood Build as-is"},{"description":"Add git remotes to zen-hardening, nyan-gfsf-alert, buildlog so they survive the next rebuild.","label":"Close the durability gap first"},{"description":"Enable firewalld (installed but inactive/disabled) so the zen-hardening zone config actually enforces. Needs sudo.","label":"Enable firewalld"}],"question":"Which piece of the agent system do you want me to do first?","multiple":true}]},"time":{"start":1790450332030}}},"time":1790450332030}');
INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df27f18600110btqjzCKFSCmw','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',677,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df27d90e001MjQb3BpBR77JlH","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df27cdcc001sriEhSRZUHRCVd","type":"text","text":"I owe you a correction, and I found one thing you should know before any reapply.\n\n**You''re right that I had the wrong model of \"void.\"** `void-bin` is an AUR package for the **Void editor** (a Cursor alternative, `github.com/voideditor`) — not Void Linux. My earlier \"this box isn''t Void\" was true about the OS and useless about your actual goal. And `void-bin` PKGBUILD:11 has `depends=(electron34 ...)`, so `void` → `electron34` → the chromium clone. **The shallow mirror I seeded and verified is precisely what unblocks `void-bin`.** That fix is done and on the critical path.\n\n**The safety issue:** `~/.config/kdeglobals` right now has\n```\nfont=Great Vibes,16,...    fixed=Great Vibes,16,...\n```\nand `fc-list` confirms Great Vibes ships **only Regular** — no bold/italic. Your buildlog:47 records that this machine was **rebuilt after a lockout** with *\"Prime lockout suspect: Great Vibes as global KDE UI font (calligraphy, size 14, no bold/italic) reaching lock screen + dialogs.\"* Re-running `install.sh` re-applies exactly that font (lines 125-127). The 16pt bump + synthetic-embolden rule mitigates it; it doesn''t remove it.\n\n**On \"the global agent system\":** no spec for one survives. What''s actually recorded is:\n\n| Agent | State |\n|---|---|\n| hermes 0.21.5 | installed, working |\n| opencode 1.18.32 | installed, working, `voidlit` active |\n| supercode | **dead** — `@kirmad/supercode` and `supercode` both 404 on npm (4 attempts) |\n| void (editor) | not installed, blocked on the electron34 build |\n\nThe \"global agent system\" extras (healer daemon, BDE patrols, antivirus) were listed as *deliberately not done*, and the healer ran `sudo snapper rollback -c root` on a 5-minute timer via `shell=True`. I won''t recreate that without you explicitly asking.\n\nAlso worth knowing: 3 of your 4 repos have **no git remote** (only `hermes-blood` does). buildlog''s entire premise is \"code survives because it was pushed\" — right now a rebuild loses `zen-hardening`, `nyan-gfsf-alert`, and the journal itself.","time":{"start":1790450325774,"end":1790450332038}},"time":1790450332038}');
