INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df2beb0d001T2WhVD5oSClvAa','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',4835,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df2bdea80010ergM0sRQ9535D","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df2bd9ec001KIJ7OaL1I2XSm7","type":"reasoning","text":"The 4.3G paru clone cache is all from the failed void-bin/electron34 build. Let me check what''s in it and whether any are needed. `paccache -r` keeps 3 versions of installed packages by default — safe.\n\nFor orphans, I should be careful: `pacman -Rns` on orphans. But note `electron` and `electron39` are orphans — these are big. But wait, are they truly orphans? `pacman -Qdtq` = packages required by nothing. Careful: removing `python-requests` could break AUR tools (paru needs python-requests? actually paru is Rust now). Let me not remove orphans aggressively without asking — but the user said \"those two\" which includes the 7G cleanup. Let me do the cache part (safe, reversible-ish) and be careful with orphans.\n\nActually, let me check: is the paru clone cache needed? It''s build sources, safe to delete. 4.3G.\n\npaccache for /var/cache/pacman/pkg — keeps last 3 versions, safe.\n\nFor orphans, let me present the list and let them decide, but note that removing orphans requires sudo (pacman -Rns needs root). So I can''t do it. Cache cleanup of /var/cache/pacman/pkg also needs root.\n\nSo: I can clean ~/.cache/paru (user-owned). The rest needs sudo. Let me do what I can and give the commands.\n\nLet me first install the watcher service (enable --now), then clean paru cache.\n\nLet me do the service install first.","time":{"start":1790450589352,"end":1790450592525}},"time":1790450592525}');
