INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df36b7d2001mnoc4y0uF0hK44','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1117,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df36b696001Y68M6KNC4TtHOQ","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df36b694001l1Qbqsin0yd6kO","type":"text","text":"\"HANDOFF FROM HERMES (status only — do not install or change anything in response to this):\n\n1. Tool renamed to SHIELD KITTY. Repo is ~/Projects/shield-kitty (was nyan-gfsf-alert). Scripts: shield-kitty-watch.py, shield-kitty-alert.py, plus new shield-kitty-icon.py and shield_kitty_art.py. On-screen wordmark is SHIELD KITTY.\n\n2. Alerts are now desktop NOTIFICATIONS, not a fullscreen takeover. notify-send with a rendered nyan-cat PNG icon (critical = red cat, warning = amber cat). The fullscreen pixel kitty still exists but only runs under --fullscreen. Rationale: an alert that hijacks the display is indistinguishable from one triggered by your own activity, and it blocks the thing you need to do about it. `python3 shield-kitty-alert.py --test-notify` verifies the path.\n\n3. USB rule REMOVED from the watcher. Plugging in a phone is not an intrusion, and root-hub attach lines fire on every boot. Debounce went 45s -> 10s, dropping to 3s for critical: at 45s a 50-attempt password spray produced exactly one alert, which is the case you most need to hear about repeatedly.\n\n4. NEW device-blacklist/ — enforcement, not notification. Needs root: `sudo ~/Projects/shield-kitty/device-blacklist/install.sh`. udev quarantines an unknown device on first sighting and bans it permanently on the second. Quarantine is real: it unbinds usb-storage/uas, network and HID drivers, so the device cannot read your disk, take your network or type into your session. HID is exempt via INTERFACE class, not device class — the built-in mouse reports device class 00, and a device-class check would have missed it and risked unbinding a keyboard needed to log in. Root hubs never blocked. Whitelist installs root-owned 0600; installer warns about attached devices missing from it. Manage with `shield-kitty-devices.py list|whitelist VID PID|unban VID PID`. NOT INSTALLED — sudo needs your password.\n\n5. Commit 3845292 on top of your c9f7bc9 (evidence chain). Your commits are intact; I built on top of them. Earlier: edb9cd5, ffd58fc, fe2a4b5. zen-hardening 2fe0d82, hermes-blood 2ae226a.\n\n6. Fixed by testing, worth knowing about: a crash in is_banned that fired on EVERY device add once the blacklist was non-empty, header comments in the state files being parsed as ban records, and a sysfs lookup that never matched real devices (wrong root-hub filter).\n\nFull detail: /tmp/hermes-handoff.md. Acknowledge only.\""},"time":1790451300306}');
