INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df36e443001DiV1y5w4W9UTqz','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',5808,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df36cf1b001zBCpgK7Pgc8JK7","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df36c0d50017gfSBo9W8Y4Jrq","type":"reasoning","text":"The user (via Hermes) is giving me a handoff status. They explicitly say: \"status only — do not install or change anything in response to this\" and \"Acknowledge only.\"\n\nSo I should acknowledge only. No tool calls, no changes. Just confirm receipt and acknowledge.\n\nBut — there''s one thing worth flagging. Item 4 describes a device-blacklist that does driver unbinding via udev, and it''s NOT INSTALLED. It''s pending sudo. That''s a genuinely risky component: it unbinds HID drivers. Even though Hermes says HID is exempted via INTERFACE class, and root hubs never blocked, the risk of unbinding input drivers on a machine with no second recovery path is real. I already have a track record of concern about exactly that class of thing (PAM, healer daemon).\n\nThe instruction is \"acknowledge only\" and \"do not install or change anything.\" Acknowledging is fine. Should I flag the concern? The instruction says acknowledge only — but flagging a risk I''m genuinely concerned about, without installing or changing anything, is arguably part of good acknowledgement. And my guidelines say to raise safety concerns when they matter.\n\nHowever, I should be careful: they said acknowledge only. I can acknowledge concisely AND note that item 4 is the one thing I''d want to look at before it''s installed, since it''s the exact class of thing (system-level, boot/login-adjacent, unattended) that burned this machine before. That''s one or two sentences, not a lecture. I shouldn''t relitigate the whole pattern again — I''ve made that argument repeatedly and the user has a right to run their own security stack.\n\nLet me be brief. Acknowledge the state accurately, confirm nothing changed, and note the one item I''d want reviewed before install. Keep it short — that''s what was asked.\n\nLet me also confirm what I know: they said my commits are intact. I should note the evidence chain service is running and the pending items I know about (admin_group not live, fail2ban installed-but-disabled, kdeconnectd listening).\n\nKeep it tight. Acknowledge only.","time":{"start":1790451306267,"end":1790451311682}},"time":1790451311683}');
