ces\n# (keyboards/mice/gamepads) — see ALLOWED_CLASSES in shield-kitty-devices.py.\n","title":"cd ~/Projects/shield-kitty\necho \"=== claim 6: the HID/root-hub fixes — inspect, do NOT install ===\"\ngrep -nE \"INTERFACE|03FF|09|root.?hub|is_banned\" device-blacklist/shield-kitty-devices.py | head -20\necho; echo \"=== whitelist ownership (must be 0600 root once installed) ===\"\nhead -12 device-blacklist/whitelist.conf","metadata":{"output":"=== claim 6: the HID/root-hub fixes — inspect, do NOT install ===\n55:    (\"1d6b\", \"0001\"), (\"1d6b\", \"0002\"), (\"1d6b\", \"0003\"),  # root hubs\n63:# class 00, NOT 09 — so the exemption has to look at the INTERFACE class of\n65:HID_CLASSES = {\"03\", \"09\"}  # keyboard, mouse / HID\n154:      \"usb3\"     a root hub                      <- never a target\n155:      \"3-0:1.0\"  a root hub interface            <- never a target\n164:            continue          # interface or root hub\n325:def is_banned(vid, pid, serial):\n349:    if is_banned(vid, pid, serial):\n426:        (\"root hub 1d6b:0002 is never-blocked\", (\"1d6b\", \"0002\") in NEVER_BLOCK),\n\n=== whitelist ownership (must be 0600 root once installed) ===\n# Shield Kitty device whitelist\n#\n# Format:  <VID>:<PID>  # description\n# Case-insensitive. Comments and blank lines ignored.\n#\n# Devices NOT listed here are treated as unknown. An unknown device gets one\n# chance: it is logged, you get a notification, and it is quarantined (its\n# driver is unbound so it cannot read or write anything). A second attempt by\n# the same device is a permanent ban, written to the blacklist.\n#\n# Built-in always-allowed: root hubs (1d6b:*), and HID-class devices\n# (keyboards/mice/gamepads) — see ALLOWED_CLASSES in shield-kitty-devices.py.\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1790451313020,"end":1790451313039}}},"time":1790451313039}');
