INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df36f45f001GsV6kW027Fkbo0','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',5810,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df36e447001Op0xmvA0ajlM2C","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df36c0d50017gfSBo9W8Y4Jrq","type":"text","text":"Acknowledged. No changes made.\n\nTracked state from your handoff:\n\n1. `~/Projects/shield-kitty` — renamed, 4 scripts, SHIELD KITTY wordmark\n2. Desktop notifications via `notify-send` + rendered PNG icon; fullscreen only under `--fullscreen`. Agreed with the rationale — a display hijack is unactionable and self-triggering.\n3. USB rule removed, debounce 45s → 10s (3s critical). The 45s figure was mine; 10s is the right call.\n4. `device-blacklist/` built, **not installed** — awaiting sudo\n5. `3845292` on top of my `c9f7bc9`; evidence chain untouched and still `INTACT`\n6. Three bugs fixed by testing, including the `is_banned` crash on every device add\n\nMy side, unchanged: `shield-kitty-watch.service` active, `evidence-seal.timer` hourly, `business-health.timer` daily 07:00, firewalld active on `wlo1`.\n\nOpen items I still have noted: `admin_group = wheel` was **not** written to `/etc/security/faillock.conf` (live is `deny=10, unlock_time=30, audit=silent`), fail2ban 1.1.1 installed but disabled/inactive, and `kdeconnectd` still on `*:1716`.\n\nOne flag before item 4 gets installed, then I''ll leave it alone: driver-unbinding enforcement is the same class of change as the PAM module and the healer daemon — system-level, boot-adjacent, and wrong on a machine with no second recovery path. The INTERFACE-class HID exemption is the right design and the root-hub filter fix is the right instinct. If you want, I''ll read the udev rules and the class-matching logic line by line before it goes near root, and leave it disabled until that''s done. Otherwise noted and I''ll stay out of it.","time":{"start":1790451311687,"end":1790451315807}},"time":1790451315807}');
