INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df370310001oFw7XuddL7CrhP','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1170,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df36f1df001nUW2hXql5zHL6I","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df36e99d001Q4DNRhDKZNyiSa","type":"text","text":"Acknowledged, and nothing installed or changed.\n\n**Verified:**\n- Notifications, not fullscreen — `shield-kitty-alert.py:234` marks fullscreen as opt-in only; `notify-send` is the default with a terminal fallback.\n- USB rule removed; `DEBOUNCE = 10` / `DEBOUNCE_MIN = 3` confirmed.\n- Not installed — no `/etc/udev/rules.d/*shield*`, no `/var/lib/shield-kitty`. Correct, given sudo needs your password.\n- The three claim-6 bugs look genuinely fixed: root hubs in `NEVER_BLOCK` (line 55), `HID_CLASSES = {\"03\", \"09\"}` with the comment explaining why INTERFACE class is required rather than device class (line 65), and a comment-stripping guard for state files.\n\n**One correction, as flagged:** `c9f7bc9` is authored by `opencode <opencode@localhost>`. It is not mine — I never ran `git commit` this session. My edits were uncommitted working-tree changes, and the tree is now clean. The USB fix I made did land and is subsumed by the rule''s removal, but the display-gate edits were overwritten before commit. The net outcome you wanted is achieved anyway, just not by work I committed.\n\n**One risk worth your attention on the un-installed blacklist**, since it''s the part that *blocks* rather than notifies: a wrong `is_banned` or sysfs lookup fails **closed** — it unbinds `usb-storage`, network, and HID drivers. That means an unrecognized device can lose network, and if the HID exemption is ever wrong, your input devices stop working. Worth testing on a USB stick you don''t need before letting it near your daily driver.\n\nOutstanding from earlier, unchanged: `sudo` needs your password (blocks firewalld, `gh`, the blacklist installer); `shield-kitty-watch.service` installed unit still points at the deleted `nyan-gfsf-alert/` path; and `void-bin` still needs the `electron34` build.","time":{"start":1790451315167,"end":1790451319568}},"time":1790451319568}');
