INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df3e16bf001MVTE4uMlMc4uTN','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',6512,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df3df9f3001Weexb6FEYCu8Xr","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df3df2dd001X4enJVbvdIvMFd","type":"reasoning","text":"`hermes-security-scripts` is an excellent host: it has `config/` and `scripts/` with security hardening scripts. Perfect fit for:\n- `zen-hardening` configs → `config/`\n- `shield-kitty` (watcher/alert/device-blacklist) → `scripts/` or a subdir\n\nBut `shield-kitty` is a Python project with its own structure. Mixing it into a shell scripts repo is a bit awkward but the user asked for consolidation.\n\n`security-audit-2026` was pushed 2026-09-21 (recent, 5 days ago) — more active, has `findings/`, `logs/`, `reports/`. It''s an audit repo, not a code repo. `shield-kitty-forensics` (evidence chain) could fit there conceptually, but that repo seems to be reports/findings.\n\nLet me propose a concrete mapping and get confirmation before writing to existing repos, because:\n1. Pushing into an existing repo with history is a write to something that already exists\n2. The mapping is a judgment call\n\nProposed mapping:\n- `zen-hardening` → `hermes-security-scripts/config/zen-hardening/` (sysctl, faillock, firewalld, fail2ban configs — exactly what `config/` is for)\n- `shield-kitty` → `hermes-security-scripts/scripts/shield-kitty/` (the intrusion watcher)\n- `shield-kitty-forensics` → `hermes-security-scripts/scripts/shield-kitty/forensics/` (evidence chain, companion tool)\n- `buildlog` → hmm. `garuda-tools-fresh` is a public repo — probably not appropriate. `rocket-build-system`? Let me think. buildlog is a personal build journal. Could go in `hermes-security-scripts`? Not really a fit.\n\nFor buildlog, options: `rocket-build-system` (Python) or `garuda-tools-fresh` (public, Shell). Since the user said \"my already built repos\" and buildlog is a Garuda/system tool, `garuda-tools-fresh` is thematically right but it''s PUBLIC — pushing a personal journal log there would leak personal data. That''s a real concern. Better: keep buildlog local, or put it in a private repo.\n\nLet me flag that: garuda-tools-fresh is PUBLIC, so buildlog (which contains personal build history with package lists, hostnames, etc.) should NOT go there.\n\nLet me verify what buildlog''s log contains for sensitive info. Actually I know from the summary it has logs/buildlog.md with session events, package versions, hostnames. That''s personal. Should not be pushed to a public repo.\n\nLet me propose and ask for confirmation on the mapping, especially the public-repo concern.\n\nActually, the user has said \"push as needed as we go\" and \"add them to my already built repos if needed\" — they want autonomy. But pushing to a public repo is irreversible-ish (git history on a public repo is cached by forks/scrapers). That''s a genuine irreversible action, so I should confirm that specific one.\n\nLet me:\n1. Push the 3 ready repos now (unambiguous)\n2. Propose the mapping for the 4, flag the public repo issue\n3. Do the consolidation for the 3 that fit hermes-security-scripts\n\nLet me start with the 3 pushes since those are unambiguous, then handle consolidation.\n\nLet me push the 3 repos.","time":{"start":1790451775987,"end":1790451783359}},"time":1790451783359}');
