INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df3e7b8e001V95Qqd5Zyb4xSt','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',6565,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df3e6471001oZc81p5ZQOtp1m","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df3e57b8001JrAHJ1KMpdBL0C","type":"reasoning","text":"`garuda-tools-fresh` is PUBLIC — confirmed. So buildlog must NOT go there.\n\nNow let me do the consolidation for the three that fit `hermes-security-scripts`:\n- `zen-hardening` → `config/zen-hardening/`\n- `shield-kitty` → `scripts/shield-kitty/`\n- `shield-kitty-forensics` → `scripts/shield-kitty/forensics/`\n\nApproach: clone hermes-security-scripts, copy the trees in, commit, push.\n\nFor buildlog: it''s a personal journal. Options:\n- Put it in a private repo. `security-audit-2026` is private and has `logs/` — that''s a decent thematic fit (build/audit journal). It''s private, so safe.\n- Actually `security-audit-2026` has `logs/` dir already. And it''s private. buildlog is a journal of builds/audits/fixes. That fits reasonably.\n\nBut security-audit-2026 was pushed 5 days ago (active). Mixing a build journal into an audit repo is a bit odd but defensible.\n\nAlternatively `rocket-build-system` (private, Python) — buildlog is a build journal. Hmm.\n\nLet me just ask about buildlog specifically since it''s the ambiguous one, and do the other three now. Actually — the user said \"add them to my already built repos if needed\" and wants autonomy. Let me make a sensible call for buildlog: `security-audit-2026` is private and has a `logs/` directory, and buildlog is a durable journal of builds/audits. That''s the best fit among private repos. But I should flag it.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The cleanest thing: put buildlog in `hermes-security-scripts` too? No, it''s not security.\n\nLet me be decisive but transparent: do the three security ones now, propose `security-audit-2026/logs/buildlog/` for buildlog and flag the choice. Actually the user wants me to proceed. Let me do all four and clearly report what I chose, since they can always move it.\n\nHmm — but pushing buildlog into security-audit-2026 means pushing personal hostname data into a shared repo. It''s private, so acceptable. Let me do it and report.\n\nActually, let me reconsider once more: is it better to just ask? The user has said \"push as needed as we go\" — they want me to act. I''ll act and report clearly. The action is reversible (a commit can be reverted) as long as I don''t push to a public repo. So: proceed with private repos only, report the mapping.\n\nLet me do the consolidation.\n\nSteps for each:\n1. Clone hermes-security-scripts to /tmp\n2. Copy zen-hardening → config/zen-hardening/\n3. Copy shield-kitty → scripts/shield-kitty/\n4. Copy shield-kitty-forensics → scripts/shield-kitty/forensics/\n5. Exclude .bak files, venv, __pycache__, .git\n6. Commit + push\n\nAnd buildlog → security-audit-2026/logs/buildlog/\n\nLet me be careful with .gitignore for the bak files and venv.\n\nLet me do it.","time":{"start":1790451803249,"end":1790451809166}},"time":1790451809166}');
