INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df406590001804X06piZKJES4','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',6615,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df3ec52a0011luRnvGTF5sTyW","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df3eac31001JqZnMkrKVwS6gR","type":"reasoning","text":"We need produce exact structured summary, same language conversation English. Need combine prior + entire recent conversation, capture current state, contradictions corrected. Need terse but comprehensive enough next agent continue. Need not continue work. We need identify current immediate work: fail2ban config failed; diagnose filename extension and stock recidive issue; need fix config/install as .conf and ensure recidive bootstrap. Also perhaps faillock admin group confusion/live state. Need carry objectives earlier theme, tools etc but finished drop. Need preserve pending broader work. We need synthesize.\n\nLet''s parse chronology/state carefully to ensure accurate facts.\n\nEnvironment:\n- Garuda Linux, Plasma Wayland, user livings, wheel, sudo with password.\n- LUKS2 root, 477G, kernel 7.2.7 zen, 12 cores, 7.4 GiB etc perhaps relevant.\n- Firewalld active enabled public wlo1. only ssh + dhcpv6. KDE Connect listening *:1716 but blocked inbound. sshd disabled, no remote login surfaces.\n- Hardening configs installed:\n `/etc/sysctl.d/99-hardening.conf`, live 24 settings, 13 changes; specifics.\n `/etc/security/faillock.conf`: recent checked live = deny=10 unlock_time=30 audit=silent, no admin_group. Project copy at `~/Projects/zen-hardening/faillock.conf` includes admin_group=wheel and unlock=30, audit silent. User seemingly ran earlier copy before admin_group, so live no admin_group. Important: `admin_group` is real supported directive. The assistant initially incorrectly said nonexistent. It exempts wheel from faillock according docs (handled like root; default root not locked). User wants it, but would weaken brute force protection. They might later copy correct file? The most recent verification says not live. Need preserve.\n `/etc/firewalld/zones/public.xml` from staged file; firewalld active. But XML has potentially questionable entries: `<masquerade/>` in public zone; allows SSH even sshd disabled. Could note.\n- fail2ban 1.1.1 installed, enabled but failed inactive. Config copied to `/etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty-fail2ban.local` (hyphen) and not loaded because only `*.conf` auto-included. Despite not loaded, stock jail.conf `[recidive]` maybe enabled? Why stock recidive attempted if base jail has enabled? Need inspect; error says recidive. Probably stock recidive section has `enabled = true` in later lines. The project corrected `recidive` to false but copied installed remains old enabled true. Correct file extension needed likely `/etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty.conf` or `.local`? Need be accurate. The assistant asserted only `*.conf` loaded; config docs say files in jail.d ending `.conf` likely indeed. Need next move rename/copy to `.conf`, set recidive false, test and start. But also potential issue multiple `logpath` lines in config: `logpath = /var/log/auth.log` and indented `journalctl ...` means configparser multi-value? In fail2ban syntax, multiple `logpath` may be allowed if separate logpath directives, but indentation doesn''t matter. However `/var/log/auth.log` likely absent; plus journal target. `backend=auto` should fall back? Fail2ban may error \"Have not found any log file\" if one absent. Need next agent inspect. We should state known potential: `/var/log/auth.log` may not exist in systemd journal setup; fail2ban supports multiple logpath but likely chooses one. We shouldn''t invent unless relevant. Current blocker immediate. Need preserve exact error: `Failed to access socket path: /var/run/fail2ban/fail2ban.sock. Is fail2ban running?`; service failure error `Have not found any log file for ''recidive'' jail.` The local corrected file isn''t installed, installed extension ignored, and stock recidive points at missing `/var/log/fail2ban.log`. Need fix sequence.\n- Fail2ban config location source `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/shield-kitty-fail2ban.local`, corrected project version recidive enabled=false, all jails permanent bantime=-1, sddm/sudo use pam-generic, sshd, recidive. It still includes private IP ignore, etc. But not installed correctly. Need mention permanent bans self-lockout risk.\n- Hermes handoff state: Tool renamed to Shield Kitty, repo `~/Projects/shield-kitty`, scripts watcher, alert, icon, art; notifications default, fullscreen under flag; USB removed, debounce 10 sec, critical 3 sec. Device-blacklist built, not installed, requires sudo. Need preserve because user gave handoff and says Hermes did it. User clarified renames by Hermes. New evidence chain integration maybe Hermes commit `3845292` on top `c9f7bc9`. Forensics repo. Current service path updated to shield-kitty. Need capture uncommitted states? Prior diagnostics said shield-kitty 3 uncommitted, then commits. Hermes says commit 3845292, likely now clean? Need not assert. Full handoff says commit. Device blacklist not installed. Need perhaps mention no changes due user status-only. Current watcher active, evidence chain intact at last diagnostics. But after Hermes modifications? Service was updated before handoff; handoff says still active. Need preserve.\n- Evidence tool:\n `~/Projects/shield-kitty-forensics/evidence.py`: HMAC-SHA256 chained log at `~/.local/share/shield-kitty/evidence/chain.jsonl`; key `~/.config/shield-kitty/evidence.key`; anchor; commands. Hourly user timer `evidence-seal.timer`, service. Auto integrated into watcher. Bundle/report. It is tamper-evident not tamper-proof, auto authority reporting deliberately not implemented. Need maybe include in completed.\n- System diagnostics current:\n no failed system units before fail2ban; now fail2ban failed.\n disk after cache cleanup 13G/477G, mem tight 5.2Gi used 595Mi free 2.1Gi avail; no OOM; two opencode processes. no pending updates, package integrity no altered. Orphans 1 (earlier 18; Hermes cleaned). `pacman -Q hermes-agent` says 0.21.5-1. fish PATH includes local bin. `~/.config/environment.d/firefox.conf` fixed to `MOZ_USE_XINPUT2=1`, backup moved to `~/.config/environment.d-backups/firefox.conf.20260926_120708.bak`. Need preserve completed. System health: SSH, FTP, RDP none installed/enabled; only KDE Connect listening, firewall blocks. Firewalld allows SSH despite no daemon. `kdeconnectd` bind all interface.\n- Business tools:\n cloned and installed `lin-antimalware`, `business-health-monitor`, `business-debug-wrappers`.\n Paths fixed from hardcoded `/home/sin` and `~/Projects/security`; commits:\n lin `4d304c3`; debug `7301a28`; business `e1562d4`. But later repos commit counts changed due Hermes? Maybe commits remained. `business-health` wrapper runs, daily timer 07:00. `business-debug` runs, no `--status` flag. `lin-antimalware` venv and deps click requests pyyaml, scan works. Business health scan reported 66 low/medium missing license files, 0 critical/high. Need preserve maybe not central but objective.\n- Tools in PATH via fish config, okay.\n- Zen hardening project and configs. `faillock` weird config validity: `audit = silent` is valid syntax? In pam_faillock man page, audit and silent are standalone flags? The file with `audit = silent` maybe config parser accepts? Installed and service? We need not question.\n- `admin_group=wheel` should be supported and in binary; project copy. Earlier user asked permanent lockout attackers. Assistant explained faillock cannot source-IP / permanent and created fail2ban. Need state current config source has admin group but not live. This is important: user''s desired \"only local host admin / outside force locked out\" not correctly achieved. Need next agent correct misunderstanding if continuing.\n- User had asked `unlock_time=30`, copied to live. Yes.\n- User asked permanent lockout; fail2ban config. Need not conflate account lockout and source ban.\n- Void installation:\n Prior summary had active `paru void-bin/electron34` build. Conversation later established process gone, no lock, package not installed, paru cache clone 4.3G. Assistant''s assertion \"AUR broken at source because upstream repo 404\" is not necessarily accurate: AUR `void-bin` fetched from `voideditor/binaries`, not `void-oss/void-bin`; they tested wrong GitHub repo. The source release might or might not be 404; likely assistant falsely concluded. We need correct fact based observed: `void-bin` not installed; cached AUR clone existed and source is `https://github.com/voideditor/binaries/releases/download/1.99.30044/...`; no successful build happened. `~/.cache/paru/clone` deleted during cleanup, so build state lost. `void-oss/void-bin` 404 is irrelevant/wrong repo. The prior active build blocker is resolved (process ended; lock clear), but installation unresolved. Need not retain PID. We should state build no longer running, cache purged; package absent; any install needs fresh `paru -S void-bin` and correct upstream verification, not claim broken. The user later asked \"install void from this instance\" and said \"those two next\" meaning alert + cache, not void? They accepted skip. Current objective broader. Need mention pending Void maybe active. They asked \"full diagnostics once everything rebuilt and installed oh and install void\"; assistant said no. User then chose two next (watcher + cache). Void not installed. Need active/blocker.\n- BDE, zen-healer, local emergency patrol, full zen suite, kali dual boot, 21-layer encryption:\n Prior conversation assessed. Need carry unresolved user requests maybe:\n  - `bde-security-biometrics` installs PAM modules and daemons; not installed, needs review/approval. Lockout risk.\n  - `lin-antimalware-tools`, local emergency patrol etc not installed. Only lin antimalware installed.\n  - `zen-healer` unsafe, not installed, hardcoded user `sin`, shell=True, root daemon, snapper. Need preserve.\n  - 21-layer encryption not found; disk already LUKS2, no repo; don''t reformat.\n  - full Zen suite: system is Garuda, no Kali partition/dual boot. Repos exist: `zen-suite`, `kali-zen-suite`, `linux-zen-suite`, `zen-suite-iso`, `zen-suite-release`; not installed. `zen-suite` scripts build ISO via pacstrap, not disk. User wanted \"Kali left arm, Arch right arm\"; no second OS.\n  - hardening scripts `security-audit-2026`, secure tactical etc unreviewed. We wrote baseline.\n  - \"all hardening scripts\" not blanket run.\n- Blood Build theme work: prior summary says completed mostly, but pending dedicated repo and uncommitted changes. Conversation didn''t revisit. Need carry Active:\n  - `/home/livings/Projects/hermes-blood` local modifications, need commit perhaps.\n  - dedicated OpenCode Blood Build repo requested not created.\n  - Great Vibes bold unverified.\n  - buildlog local no remote, one uncommitted? Later diagnostics said buildlog 1 uncommitted.\n Could include these as Active. But current task is security. Template says combine. We should retain pending.\n- Hermes package now verified `hermes-agent 0.21.5-1`, resolves old blocker. Node update completed. Buildlog present. Could move to completed, not dwell.\n- Steam/emulators: no need perhaps pending original objective. Prior summary says confirmed absent. User asked full toolsets maybe not directly resolved. We can mention in Active/Blocked if still relevant. But exact summary should be terse, not overlong. Desired oververbosity 3 but summary needs sufficient.\n- Password/faillock: PAM stack already wired system-auth and sddm-autologin. `deny=10`, `unlock=30`, audit silent live. `livings` in wheel and sudo. User''s project copy includes admin group, but they think it''s installed. Need immediate next perhaps after fail2ban fix, decide whether to copy admin_group. But note their actual goal is attackers permanently blocked, and admin group would exempt their own username, directly counterproductive. We should not automatically install it; next agent should clarify. In summary mark project copy ready but not live. It may be a risk.\n- Fail2ban config extension:\n Installed filename is `shield-kitty-fail2ban.local`, not loaded. Yet service failure from stock recidive. Correct source currently project file ends `.local`; fail2ban only includes `*.conf`. Need either copy as `/etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty.conf`. Remove old ignored file optional. Then `fail2ban-client -t`. Corrected project has recidive false. But if source copy name differs, no matter. `sudo install -m 0644 ... /etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty.conf`; test; start. Then after log created, can enable recidive in a second `.conf` or update section. But note fail2ban config includes `[DEFAULT]` and multiple jails in one file. Fine.\n Potential config issue: `sddm` section''s name `[sddm]` with `filter=pam-generic`; fail2ban will call it jail sddm, okay. `sudo` same. `logpath` includes `/var/log/auth.log` which likely missing, and journal command. If backend auto sees missing file but journal exists, fail2ban can support both. Need test after corrected config.\n The old file in `/etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty-fail2ban.local` should be removed/ignored. It is ignored anyway. The stock recidive is apparently enabled (maybe jail.conf''s recidive has `enabled = true` in base; error). Once our `.conf` sets recidive false, override should disable. Config include order? jail.d files included after jail.conf, so yes.\n- The user last message was error; immediate next action fix, not ask. Summary should say that.\n- Need include `shield-kitty` service and device blacklist status, because recent handoff.\n- Evidence chain had test fake events and perhaps later chain reset empty. At final diagnostics, chain intact, likely no list output because reset and a logger did not produce? Let''s trace: after restoring:\n```\nrm chain\nlogger synthetic\nsleep 8\nseal -> count 0\nverify intact\n```\nSo watcher didn''t record synthetic within 8 sec? It may have cursor advanced past event? Actually service likely cursor and polling; maybe not. But chain was empty. Then no further. At final diagnostics, evidence verify intact, no list. It''s intact but empty possibly. Do not claim event currently stored. It had test events earlier. Service active.\n- Device-blacklist not installed, requires root. Need preserve.\n- Shield Kitty notification scripts. Current `shield-kitty-watch.service` active. Last service path repointed. Hermes handoff says commit and modifications. Need perhaps say full detail `/tmp/hermes-handoff.md`.\n- Alert service hardening: originally `ProtectSystem=strict` caused 226, removed, uses ProtectKernelTunables etc. Current service.\n- Evidence chain auto report to authorities not built; human reports only. User asked proper authorities. Completed as deliberate limitation. Next move maybe no.\n- System hardening firewall config `firewalld-workstation.conf` may use `<service name=\"samba-client\" enable=\"no\"/>` invalid firewalld schema? It was accepted? firewalld active. Not necessary.\n- User asked \"all attack surfaces no outside attack\" impossible; assistant stated no guarantee. Current remote surface none.\n- Need note `void-bin` prior source/cache cleanup: `/home/livings/.cache/paru` reduced 4.3G to 544K, `/var/cache/pacman/pkg` 3.8G earlier but `paccache -rk2` returned no candidates oddly; maybe package cache was already 3.8G but output says no candidate. Later disk 13G. No need.\n- Full diagnostics showed package integrity `pacman -Qkk` 0 altered. Great.\n- GitHub token still exists and should shred after audit. Prior says token read-only at path mode600, but commands used it for private repo API. It might be token with access. Need preserve security constraint. The token should be shredded eventually. It is sensitive. Relevant file list.\n- GitHub SSH broad access; avoid exposing.\n- `pacman` lock now clear, no `paru`. Update old active blocker.\n- Node/Hermes etc completed. Need maybe not list all theme details? But carry objective and pending. The template wants all relevant.\n- User''s overall objective evolved: restore/rebuild security stack and tools, full diagnostics, safe system hardening, reinstall low-risk tools, alert/forensics, and possibly Void. We need one-two sentence objective.\n- Important details should include no blanket unattended root, no claims zero attack surface, distinction between faillock and fail2ban, user wants live admin exemption/permanent source bans but current state differs. Also user clarified Hermes is parallel agent making renames.\n- Work State Completed should be terse bullets maybe group.\n- Active: immediate fail2ban failed; project config corrected but not installed as .conf. Also void, pending high-risk repos, uncommitted projects, device blacklist, admin group project copy.\n- Blocked: root commands need user sudo; faillock cannot source IP/permanent; no remote services; `void` maybe no blocker except sudo and fresh build. BDE/zen healer.\n- Next Move:\n  1. Fix fail2ban: install corrected source as `.conf`, remove/ignore old, run `fail2ban-client -t`, start, status. Then enable recidive second phase after `/var/log/fail2ban.log` exists. Need ensure no permanent sddm self-ban or adjust. This is immediate.\n  2. Recheck live faillock and decide admin_group. Also full diagnostics after fail2ban; then optional Shield Kitty device blacklist review/install. The user asked fail2ban, so next two.\n Maybe include void after. Template only 2 numbered items but can bundle.\n- Relevant Files list all key paths. Need not include every prior theme file? User asked preserve exact paths from prior. We should carry relevant pending ones. Could list:\n  - `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/shield-kitty-fail2ban.local`\n  - `/etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty-fail2ban.local`\n  - `/etc/fail2ban/jail.conf`\n  - `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/faillock.conf`, backups, `/etc/security/faillock.conf`\n  - `/home/livings/Projects/shield-kitty/...`\n  - forensics\n  - systemd units\n  - hardening configs\n  - firefox\n  - business repos and tools maybe.\n  - theme active files.\n  - token and inventory.\n Could be long but okay.\n\nLet''s ensure no contradictions:\n- System says fail2ban package installed and enabled but failed. `systemctl is-enabled` enabled. Good.\n- Installed config path is `/etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty-fail2ban.local`; ignored extension. The source project config same basename. To fix, copy to `/etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty.conf`. Project file was updated to recidive false. The actual source includes comment with `sudo sed -i ''s/^enabled  = false/enabled  = true/'' /etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty.local` (it refers .local incorrectly in comment; if copied to .conf, sed path wrong). Important next agent should correct documentation path. Also all jails permanent. Need note.\n- The source config''s `ignoreip` multiline indentation may be parsed? ConfigParser allows continuation lines if indented, yes. It spans two lines. Fine.\n- `logpath` lines: `logpath = /var/log/auth.log` followed indented `journalctl...`; config parser treats continuation as same value `/var/log/auth.log\\n journalctl...`, likely this is invalid. Wait important! In INI syntax, indented continuation line without \"=\" is appended to previous value, meaning `logpath` value becomes two lines, not two separate logpath options. The assistant claimed journal fallback but this is likely wrong. Need flag active potential. Let''s inspect fail2ban syntax: multiple logpath can be specified in jail.local? In fail2ban, `logpath` may be space/newline separated? Man says \"Set log file which is monitored. Standard substitutions applied. Multiple log files can be specified (when using python module, you may use space separated string).\" There is `logpath = /var/log/auth.log /var/log/secure` maybe. Here continuation could be whitespace, likely accepted as path list, perhaps. But `journalctl -f -u...` command as second logpath with backend auto may be supported. The configuration tester will tell. Summary need not add.\n- Fail2ban recidive stock issue: corrected file false should override. Need not create log manually root? Could `sudo install -o root -g root -m 0644 /dev/null /var/log/fail2ban.log` but fail2ban config can start with recidive false. Then enable later.\n- User asked \"permanent lock out any system.\" Permanent ban config is risky; note current wlo1 private 10.245.106.176 covered by `10.0.0.0/8` at check, but dynamic/public risk. This is important.\n- Faillock `admin_group=wheel` behavior: Source copy now includes it. But user ran command perhaps before addition. Later check confirms live lacks it. Their current intent? They want it, then realize? Assistant corrected that it does opposite. Then user still asked permanent attackers. Next agent should not install admin group without clarification because it would exempt brute force target. But the user explicitly said \"perfect\" before misunderstanding, but last direct ask was fail2ban. Still project copy prepared. Summary can state \"Do not silently install; it conflicts with latest anti-bruteforce goal.\" That is a decision? We should phrase constraint.\n- Full diagnostics: before fail2ban, no failed system units; after, one failed. The user wanted full diagnostics once everything installed. Need rerun after fixing.\n- Business health scan missing license issues may be false positives. Not urgent.\n- `shield-kitty` device-blacklist potentially risky and not installed. Need mention status only. Handoff says unknown device quarantine on second, HID interface exemption, root hub safe. User asked status only, no install. The current next move shouldn''t install without review.\n- `shield-kitty` on-screen wordmark changed to SHIELD KITTY (not GFSF). User originally wanted GFSF. Hermes changed. Since user explicitly says Hermes, likely accepted. Mention.\n- Alerts now desktop notifications by default, fullscreen only flag. This is a design change.\n- No USB rule; debounce.\n- Full-screen art scripts.\n- Evidence chain commit c9f7bc9 + 3845292. `shield-kitty-forensics` separate commit 7d9894e. Need exact.\n- `zen-hardening` commit 2fe0d82; may have uncommitted fail2ban changes now. Earlier diagnostics showed clean before fail2ban. New file likely untracked and faillock modified. Need say working tree likely dirty. We can check from transcript: `zen-hardening` initialized and commit 2fe0d82. After adding fail2ban source, no commit. `faillock.conf` changed to 30/admin group, backup files likely untracked. So active.\n- Prior `hermes-blood` uncommitted. `buildlog` one uncommitted. Keep.\n- No dedicated OpenCode repo.\n- Void: current no lock, cache purged. Need mention fresh build likely huge (electron34 32GB source) and package needs sudo; user asked. But assistant wrongly said source 404 from wrong repo. Summary should state corrected: AUR remote is `https://aur.archlinux.org/void-bin`; upstream code URL `https://github.com/voideditor/void`; source binary release URL. Do not trust 404 claim. The source cache was deleted, so build must restart. Is there perhaps a prebuilt package? `void-bin` source uses .deb and electron34; `void-electron-latest-bin` likely uses electron latest. The package requires `electron34` from Arch? On current date maybe electron34 no longer repo. Could fail. But no need.\n- User originally asked Steam/emulators, not addressed. Could include in Active if objective broad, but maybe not immediate.\n- \"21 layer encryption\" not real. We should carry decision: LUKS2 already active; no repo; do not reformat. Blocked/Completed fact.\n- \"Kali left arm Arch right\" not present. Full zen suite ISO could be built but not installed. Keep.\n- BDE patrols: `bde-security-biometrics` PAM not installed, `local-emergency-patrol` unreviewed, `lin-antimalware-tools` not installed. The user says reinstall all security; only safe subset. Keep.\n- `zen-healer` unsafe. Keep.\n- `security-audit-2026` and `secure-tactical-systems` unreviewed. Keep perhaps.\n- Root firewalld active despite config; no SSH daemon. We can remove SSH service from firewall to minimize, but perhaps future use. Not current next.\n- `kdeconnectd` disable decision pending. User never answered. Include.\n- `admin_group=wheel` source copy has backups `faillock.conf.1800s.bak`, `faillock.conf.pre-admin.bak`.\n- Full hardening config `99-hardening.conf`: 24 settings, 13 differed. Live values verified. Include maybe.\n- Firewalld zone file `firewalld-workstation.conf` and live.\n- `faillock.conf` project has comments perhaps incorrectly calls `/etc/security/faillock.conf` proposed replacement. Fine.\n- `firefox.conf` fix completed.\n- `business-health` cron replaced systemd timer. Good.\n- Tools installed no broad autoheal? `business-health --heal` exists but not run.\n- `lin-antimalware` scanner produced many medium SUID findings normal. Could mention no quarantine used.\n- No automatic authority reporting. Good.\n- User wants \"full proof\": evidence chain is not court-defensible, only tamper-evident local evidence. Summary should accurately state. The assistant called court-defensible in comment but recognized limitations. Need avoid overclaim.\n- \"proper authorities\" not automated due false positives. Completed decision.\n- User wants attackers not recognized admin. Need state admin rights are `wheel`; if attacker authenticates as `livings`, inherits admin. `faillock admin_group` doesn''t change authorization. This is crucial context.\n- Fail2ban installed by user. It was not active.\n- User ran `sudo cp` faillock; live `unlock=30`. Did they run admin group copy? no.\n- Did user run `sudo cp` of fail2ban file with `.local`; yes.\n- Did fail2ban service create symlink? enabled, then failed.\n- Current stock recidive error may persist even after installing corrected `.conf` due source extension ignored. Next action.\n- Need mention no root password available to agent; user executes commands.\n- The prior token read-only claim perhaps not necessarily read-only. It was used bearer. We can say temporary token path, shred after audit. Keep exact.\n- \"all security measures\" likely could involve malicious? No, defensive. Fine.\n\nWe need output exact Markdown structure, terse bullets. Need not overdo paragraphs. Let''s formulate.\n\nObjective 1-2 bullets:\n- Restore/audit/reinstall user''s Garuda security/tool stack and finish hardening, diagnostics, Shield Kitty alerting/evidence, and optionally Void.\n- Avoid lockout/destructive changes; preserve provenance.\n\nImportant Details bullets:\n- system, user, sudo.\n- firewall, ssh, KDE.\n- faillock semantics and current desired conflicts.\n- fail2ban permanent ban risk.\n- Hermes parallel changes.\n- no guarantee no attack surface/dark web scanning.\n- tool repos status maybe.\n- package state / no lock.\n- admin rights distinction.\nCould be 10 bullets.\n\nCompleted:\nGroup:\n1 hardening configs installed and live.\n2 low risk security tools installed/fixed.\n3 Shield Kitty + forensics.\n4 system diagnostics.\n5 environment/theme from prior.\n6 disk encryption and dual boot facts maybe.\n7 Void build process no longer active? This is not completed installation. Put active.\n8 GitHub theme etc.\n\nNeed avoid listing every old completed thing if not needed but prior says don''t lose. The prior completed state is important but can summarize.\n- Blood Build theme and OpenCode activation.\n- Hermes installed.\n- buildlog.\n- environment.\n- disk and system.\n- Tools.\n\nActive:\n- fail2ban immediate.\n- Faillock admin copy.\n- Void not installed/cache cleared.\n- device blacklist not installed.\n- uncommitted changes.\n- high risk security repos.\n- zen suite and dual boot.\n- dedicated OpenCode repo/Great Vibes bold.\n- KDE connect.\nMaybe too many, but necessary.\n\nBlocked:\n- root.\n- faillock limitation.\n- no remote service / permanent source ban.\n- `void` fresh build + sudo.\n- BDE/zen.\n- no 21-layer.\n- dark web.\nCould overlap Active. Keep terse.\n\nNext moves:\n1 fix fail2ban config.\n2 verify live config and rerun full diagnostics; then review pending. Maybe mention don''t enable admin_group silently.\nCould maybe include commands in Next Move:\n```\nsudo install -m 0644 ... /etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty.conf\nsudo fail2ban-client -t\nsudo systemctl restart fail2ban\nsudo fail2ban-client status\n```\nBut source file corrected recidive false. Then create log/enable recidive. Need root. We can state exact.\n- Remove/ignore `/etc/...local`. It is ignored, no urgent.\n- Since service enabled but failed, `restart` after config.\n- Test status.\n- Only then enable recidive; note first start creates log. Could include in same item.\n- Full diagnostics after.\n\nRelevant files: Need list. We can list many in one bullet? Template says path: why. Terse bullets.\n\nLet''s ensure \"Objective one or two brief sentences\" exactly perhaps two bullets. Fine.\n\nPotential concern: Prior summary says `hermes-blood` origin f1ffc34, local commit a38327d; conversation found uncommitted. No need exact all. But relevant.\n- Great Vibes synthetic bold still unverified. Good.\n- `buildlog` no remote. Good.\n- Steam/emulators maybe not central, but original objective includes all tools. Put Active one bullet.\n- Supercode unavailable. Not necessary? Prior says blocked and user had asked. Could retain one bullet: \"`supercode` unresolved; historical npm names 404.\" But current work security. The instruction says carry forward user directives and blockers unless finished. Include maybe Active/Blocked.\n- Xbox etc. Probably not needed to current continuation, but must not lose? \"Carry forward objectives constraints user directives decisions and parallel workstreams.\" We should include a compact \"Entertainment/toolchain requests remain...\" bullet. It can mention Steam/emulators absent, no native Xbox. Good.\n- Void no longer active. Good.\n\nLet''s be precise about theme:\n- `~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc` `\"theme\": \"voidlit\"`, files.\n- Hermes package 0.21.5-1 now verified.\n- Buildlog tool on fish PATH. Good.\n- `~/.config/environment.d/firefox.conf` corrected.\n- Business tools.\n\nPotential mistake: In prior summary, `void-bin` build \"electron34 from 32GB mirror\" was active. Conversation said no process and cache 4.3G partial, not necessarily completed. Then cache deleted. So blocker resolved process, not package.\n- `paru` cache currently 544K after purge; root disk 13G.\n- `pacman cache` maybe 3.8G but paccache said no candidates. We can simply say 4.3G paru clone cache purged. Good.\n\nPotential issue: \"all toolsets reinstalled\" not done. State active.\n\nLet''s inspect recent fail2ban comments. The source config currently says recidive disabled. The file remains `.local` in project. To install, rename to `.conf`. Good.\n- Existing `/etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty-fail2ban.local` can remain ignored; better remove to avoid confusion. The user must sudo.\n- Stock recidive section in `/etc/fail2ban/jail.conf` apparently enabled and points `/var/log/fail2ban.log`. Need confirm no explicit `enabled` output because grep only section and values not displayed. But error proves. Our config false override should disable.\n- `fail2ban-client -t` after install should pass. The source uses `logpath` with `/var/log/auth.log`, which may not exist. If tester fails, need change to only journal commands or ensure auth log. Mention as next debugging if still fails.\n- `banaction=firewallcmd-rich-rules` exists.\n- `ignoreip` includes private ranges; current address 10.245.106.176.\n- Permanent sddm ban can self-lock if public IP. Mention.\n\nEvidence:\n- On Btrfs, chattr +i unavailable. HMAC chain. Key user-owned. This is tamper-evident, not tamper-proof or legal proof. Need state.\n- Seal anchor was 0644 for re-sealing. It can be altered by owner. Fine.\n- `evidence-seal.timer` hourly.\n- Automatic reporting omitted. Good.\n- At final verify chain intact but likely empty. State \"verified intact\" not \"contains events.\"\n\nShield Kitty:\n- Hermes handoff says new scripts. The current service `ExecStart` path might still point `~/Projects/shield-kitty/shield-kitty-watch.py`. It was repointed. The service active.\n- On-screen wordmark now SHIELD KITTY, not GFSF. Important because user initially asked GFSF. They accepted? Handoff says.\n- Notifications default, full screen opt-in.\n- Device blacklist built not installed. Needs review because root/udev.\n- Commit chain. Good.\n\nSystem diagnostics:\n- firewalld allowed SSH service though sshd not installed? `pacman -Q openssh` says installed, `systemctl is-enabled` disabled. Assistant later said not installed erroneously in summary: command `for s` checks systemctl only and labels \"not installed\" because disabled, but package is installed. Need correct: openssh installed, sshd disabled. In our summary say no enabled remote login daemon. Good.\n- Only TCP 1716; UDP mDNS 5353, KDE Connect UDP 1716 maybe `ss` grep only LISTEN omitted UDP. In final diagnostics command only grep LISTEN, not all sockets. Earlier showed UDP 5353, 1716. Should mention KDE Connect listening TCP/UDP 1716, mDNS 5353. Firewall blocks inbound. This is accurate.\n- Firewall zone public. Good.\n- No failed units prior to fail2ban. Current fail2ban failed. Mention current.\n- Package integrity 0 altered, no updates.\n- Memory pressure. Maybe not necessary but diagnostics. Include in completed.\n- Hermes cleaned orphans to 1. Good.\n- LUKS2. Good.\n- `fstrim.timer` disabled from initial, not addressed. Is that an attack surface? no. Could omit.\n- AppArmor inactive, no fail2ban before. Fail2ban now installed but failed. No need.\n- `ssh` service firewalld allowed despite no daemon. This could be tightened by removing. Active decision.\n- KDE Connect can be disabled. Active.\n\nBDE:\n- `bde-security-biometrics` install script writes separate PAM file but not integrate. It installs daemon under `/opt/bde`, helpers. Not installed. Need explicit.\n- `local-emergency-patrol` unreviewed. `lin-antimalware-tools` not installed.\n- `zen-healer` unsafe. Good.\n- \"full Zen suite\" not installed; scripts only build ISO. Kali no partition. Good.\n- 21-layer no repo. Good.\n- Security audit repos unreviewed. Good.\n\nNo passwordless sudo. The user can run commands. Good.\n\nOne question: The user had asked \"set faillock to permanently lock out any system\" and assistant did not directly ask clarification, wrote config. Current next should be fix fail2ban. No need ask.\n\nLet''s compose summary with enough detail. Need exactly section headers. \"Completed\" bullets can be grouped but not paragraphs. Use semicolons.\n\nLet''s draft:\n\n## Objective\n- Restore user’s post-rebuild Garuda security/tool stack, apply reviewed hardening, install safe utilities, and produce repeatable diagnostics without auth/boot lockout.\n- Finish Shield Kitty notification/evidence enforcement and, if desired, Void, while keeping dangerous PAM/root daemons reviewed/disabled.\n\n## Important Details\n- `livings`... etc.\n- No blanket NOPASSWD. User executes sudo.\n- `admin_group=wheel` is real; makes wheel treated like root, exempt from faillock by default; it does not stop attackers becoming admin. If attacker logs in as livings, inherits wheel.\n- Current live faillock lacks admin group.\n- Faillock per username, no IP/permanent. Fail2ban source IP/permanent.\n- Permanent bans risk.\n- firewalld etc.\n- Hermes.\n- no dark web.\n- GitHub token.\nMaybe 8 bullets.\n\nCompleted:\n- Low risk tools.\n- hardening.\n- alert/evidence.\n- diagnostics.\n- environment/theme.\n- system facts.\nNeed not list `firefox` maybe.\n- Void process resolved? Not completed install.\n- no automatic authority reporting.\n- Business health scan.\n\nActive:\n- fail2ban.\n- project config admin group.\n- void.\n- device blacklist.\n- high risk.\n- theme/uncommitted.\n- entertainment.\n- KDE.\n- maybe dedicated repo.\n- fail2ban immediate.\n\nBlocked:\n- sudo.\n- faillock limitation.\n- no dual boot/21 layer.\n- void build.\n- no absolute\nsurface guarantee.\n- supercode.\nCould overlap.\n\nNext:\n1. `sudo install ... .conf`, test, restart, status, then recidive.\n2. Rerun diagnostics and review live faillock. Mention do not install admin_group unless reaffirm after tradeoff. Then perhaps review device blacklist.\nMaybe two items.\n\nRelevant Files:\n- fail2ban source/live.\n- faillock source/live/backups.\n- hardening.\n- Shield Kitty repo and service/evidence.\n- business tools.\n- theme.\n- token/inventory.\n- GitHub repos high risk maybe.\nCould list 15 bullets. Terse.\n\nNeed be careful not to say \"current source config recidive disabled\" if commit maybe uncommitted. Yes current file. \"Corrected but not installed.\" Good.\n- Installed file path is `.local`, ignored. We should note no need to remove but recommended.\n- `fail2ban.service` failed due stock recidive, exact error.\n- The next command source copy with `.conf`.\n- Might need to create `/var/log/fail2ban.log` before enabling recidive; first start with false creates it. Good.\n- After first start, enabling recidive requires modifying `.conf`, not project `.local` path. Good.\n\nPotential root cause nuance: Assistant''s assertion `.local` ignored may be based config comments. Fail2ban''s `jail.conf` includes `.conf`; yes. Good.\n- Source corrected file uses `recidive enabled=false`; if copied as `.conf`, override stock. Then start. Good.\n\nCheck prior theme repository:\n- `hermes-blood` commit local `a38327d`; handoff says `hermes-blood 2ae226a` in handoff, so origin advanced. Conversation says \"zen-hardening 2fe0d82, hermes-blood 2ae226a.\" The prior summary said a38327d. Need combine corrected latest: `hermes-blood` at `2ae226a` according handoff. It has uncommitted? Earlier diagnostics after handoff said 0 uncommitted, but prior said additional uncommitted before. By full diagnostics it showed 0. We should state current handoff identifies `2ae226a`; working tree last observed clean. `buildlog` 1 uncommitted. `zen-hardening` now likely dirty due new configs. The Hermes handoff says zen-hardening 2fe0d82. Good.\n- `shield-kitty` commit `3845292`; last diagnostics before handoff? The handoff is latest. likely clean? Not stated. Could say commit exists; device changes.\n- `shield-kitty-forensics` commit 7d9894e. Handoff says evidence chain untouched.\n- Hermes rename is expected, not suspicious.\n\nMaybe don''t include all theme details in Important, but in Completed.\n\nLet''s ensure summary doesn''t mention conversation process. Fine.\n\nNo questions or answers. Just summary.\n\nWe can be a little more detailed due complex state. Need exact Markdown.\n\nLet''s formulate polished summary:\n\nObjective 2 bullets.\n\nImportant details:\n- Garuda etc.\n- sudo and system auth.\n- current security surfaces.\n- semantics.\n- Hermes.\n- scope limitations.\n- token.\n\nCompleted:\n- System hardening.\n- firewall.\n- faillock live.\n- tools.\n- shield kitty.\n- environment/theme.\n- diagnostics.\n- package/cache.\n- disk facts.\nCould separate.\n\nActive:\n- fail2ban.\n- `admin_group` staging.\n- device blacklist.\n- Void.\n- high-risk security repos.\n- Zen suite.\n- remaining local work.\n- KDE.\n- dedicated repo etc.\n\nBlocked:\n- root.\n- faillock limitations.\n- no 21 layer/Kali.\n- no native Xbox etc.\n- supercode.\n- package Void maybe.\n- impossible dark web.\nNeed not duplicate.\n\nNext Move exact commands:\n```\nsudo install -m 0644 ~/Projects/zen-hardening/shield-kitty-fail2ban.local /etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty.conf\nsudo fail2ban-client -t\nsudo systemctl restart fail2ban\nsudo fail2ban-client status\n```\nThen check jails. If pass, `sudo sed -i ... /etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty.conf`, test/restart. But `sed` line in source uses `enabled  = false`; section has exact. Good.\n- Also remove old `.local` optional.\n- Then full diagnostic.\n- Do not silently install admin_group.\n\nRelevant files exact:\n`/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/shield-kitty-fail2ban.local`\n`/etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty-fail2ban.local`\n`/etc/fail2ban/jail.conf`\n`/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/faillock.conf`\n`/etc/security/faillock.conf`\n`/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/99-hardening.conf`\n`/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/firewalld-workstation.conf`\n`/home/livings/Projects/shield-kitty/...`\n`~/.config/systemd/user/...`\n`/home/livings/Projects/shield-kitty-forensics/evidence.py`\n`~/.local/share...`\n`business...`\n`lin...`\n`hermes...`\n`opencode...`\n`firefox...`\n`token`, inventory.\nMaybe too many but okay.\n\nNeed mention `/tmp/hermes-handoff.md` full detail. Good.\n\nLet''s think whether `admin_group=wheel` in source copy was after adding comments, but live current no. Backups. Good.\n\nPotential statement \"fail2ban installed and enabled but failed\" exact.\n- Source config permanent bans, recidive disabled. Good.\n- Installed ignored file still has recidive true. The stock config caused error. Good.\n- The source file''s install instructions comments still mention `.local`, which is wrong. Need next agent fix comment. Mention Active maybe.\n- The current service enabled symlink exists. Good.\n\nPotential statement \"OpenSSH installed but disabled\" in Completed or Important. Good.\n\nEvidence chain:\n- It was local user HMAC key, tamper-evident only. Don''t call full proof. Good.\n- It bundles context. Good.\n- No auto reporting. Good.\n\nBusiness health:\n- `business-health.timer` daily. Good.\n- `business-debug` runs. Good.\n- `lin-antimalware` not scheduled as daemon? Only CLI/venv, no service. Don''t imply patrol active. It is installed and tested, but not running. Good.\n- The user asked antivirus. State no continuous antimalware service. Active perhaps.\n- `lin-antimalware`