INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df4589fe001QGBhGCdRwEhX7B','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',6757,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df457c1e001WUn5cggzKkiRiY","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df4576ba001ESgiik4X0wj0K9","type":"reasoning","text":"Now the real issue is clear: the socket is mode `srwx------` owned by root:root. So only root can query it. The user ran `sudo fail2ban-client status` — and that should work. But I ran `fail2ban-client status` without sudo, hence permission denied.\n\nSo the user''s error was... wait, the user ran WITH sudo:\n```\nsudo fail2ban-client status\n[sudo] password for livings:\nactive\n2026-09-26 12:50:41,545 fail2ban [202188]: ERROR Failed to access socket path: ...\n```\n\nHmm, the ERROR at 12:50:41 came from PID 202188, which is close to the server PID 202181. Actually the log prefix `[202188]` is the client PID. So it was a sudo''d client at 12:50:41 that failed with \"Failed to access socket path\".\n\nBut the socket was created at 12:50 (directory timestamp 12:50). So at 12:50:41 the socket may not have existed yet. The restart happened at 12:50:xx and the client ran immediately after.\n\nSo: timing race. The server takes a few seconds to create the socket. `systemctl restart` returned \"active\" before the socket existed.\n\nNow the socket exists and works (my unprivileged call got \"Permission denied\", which proves the socket is live and answering — a missing socket gives a different error).\n\nSo the fix: add a small wait. Let me verify with sudo... I can''t use sudo. But I can prove the socket works because the permission-denied response came FROM the socket (fail2ban-server responded with a proper error). That''s conclusive.\n\nLet me confirm the jails another way — read the log, or check the process. Actually let me just show the user the command with a wait built in.\n\nLet me verify the socket is functional by checking that fail2ban-server is responding — the \"Permission denied to socket\" error IS a response from the server. Good.\n\nLet me give them the correct command sequence with a wait, and confirm jails.\n\nLet me also check the journal to confirm all 3 jails loaded successfully (no errors).","time":{"start":1790452268062,"end":1790452271614}},"time":1790452271614}');
