INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df46f998001y6dtckxPPSb4S9','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',6831,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df46e3cd001obYeQrJtXJRRvD","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df46df5d001zgELE3s1QovyMT","type":"reasoning","text":"The sed worked: `enabled = true` at line 105 in the recidive section. And `/var/log/fail2ban.log` exists (9844 bytes, created 12:52).\n\nSo the config is correct. The problem was purely the RACE — the `until` loop failed in fish, so the client queried at 12:52:13, exactly when \"Server ready\" printed. Jails are added asynchronously after that.\n\nNow let me check if recidive exists NOW. I can''t sudo. But I can infer: the socket is root-only. Hmm.\n\nWait — I could check via the log file or via a different means. Let me see if there''s any way to list jails without root.\n\nOptions:\n- Read /var/run/fail2ban/fail2ban.pid — no\n- The socket is srwx------ root only\n\nI can''t query as non-root. So I need the user to run the query.\n\nBut let me think about whether recidive would actually load. The config looks right. `/var/log/fail2ban.log` exists. `backend = polling`, `logpath` set. Should work.\n\nThe most likely explanation for the NOK: race condition — queried before the jail finished being added.\n\nLet me give the user a fish-compatible readiness wait and have them re-query.\n\nFish syntax for waiting:\n```fish\nwhile not sudo fail2ban-client ping >/dev/null 2>&1\n    sleep 0.3\nend\n```\n\nOr simpler: just `sleep 2` then query. Or use `sudo fail2ban-client status` after a moment.\n\nActually the cleanest fish-compatible approach:\n```fish\nsleep 2; sudo fail2ban-client status\n```\n\nOr use fish''s `until` equivalent. Fish has `while` and `begin...end`, no `until`. So:\n```fish\nwhile not sudo fail2ban-client ping >/dev/null 2>&1\n    sleep 0.3\nend\n```\n\nBut actually, a better readiness check that also waits for jails: poll until the jail list is non-empty.\n\nLet me give them the fish version and a simple sleep fallback.\n\nAlso — I should note: the errors in the transcript show the `until` line produced fish errors but the rest still ran. So `sudo fail2ban-client status recidive` ran immediately.\n\nLet me give a clean fish command. And I should verify my own mistake clearly.\n\nLet me also double check: is there a way for me to verify? I could check the fail2ban log for jail starts.\n\nLet me look at the fail2ban log for \"Added jail\" lines — but it''s mode 600 root, so I can''t read it. Let me try.\n\nActually let me just try reading it to see if I can confirm jails.","time":{"start":1790452360142,"end":1790452365719}},"time":1790452365720}');
