INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df4ec6ce001Zmd0HzFrWJNzSA','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',7341,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df4eb6a3001945jsEI9olqoal","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df4eadf7001KqsisYutjNw8UY","type":"reasoning","text":"Two errors:\n1. `RUNNING_BUT_FAILED` — firewalld is in FAILED state (from the earlier fail2ban failures? or from the reload). Permanent config changes not allowed.\n2. `PARSE_ERROR: service: Unexpected attribute disable` — this is from the `sudo cp` + `firewall-cmd --reload` trying to parse the new public.xml. The `disable=\"yes\"` attribute on `<service name=\"mdns\" disable=\"yes\"/>` is NOT valid in firewalld zone XML!\n\nSo the original file had TWO bugs:\n- `--` in XML comments\n- `disable=\"yes\"` on a service element — invalid schema. In firewalld, to disable an inherited service you use `<service name=\"mdns\" enable=\"no\"/>` NOT `disable=\"yes\"`.\n\nSo my \"fix\" made the XML well-formed but the SCHEMA is still invalid. And now the live /etc/firewalld/zones/public.xml has been overwritten with this invalid file, and firewalld is in FAILED state.\n\nThis is worse than before — the original was malformed XML but firewalld tolerated it. Now it''s well-formed XML but schema-invalid, and firewalld''s reload failed, putting it in FAILED state.\n\nI need to:\n1. Fix the schema: `disable=\"yes\"` → `enable=\"no\"`\n2. Also `samba-client enable=\"no\"` is correct syntax\n3. Fix firewalld FAILED state\n\nLet me first check the current state — is the firewall still enforcing? In FAILED state, firewalld may have stopped managing rules, which could mean the firewall is down (bad!) or the previous rules still loaded.\n\nThis is urgent — let me check whether we''re still protected.\n\nLet me diagnose.\n\nAlso: `firewall-offline-cmd --check-config` to check the offline config.\n\nLet me be careful and methodical. First: is the firewall still enforcing?\n\nLet me check.\n\nAlso note: the user has already overwritten /etc/firewalld/zones/public.xml with the invalid file. So I need to fix and re-copy.\n\nLet me check current state.","time":{"start":1790452872867,"end":1790452877006}},"time":1790452877006}');
