INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df516005002HsedxEpQ616Yv0','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',7469,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df5150e4001NYJeE3QPtzkA3F","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df512bbf001jabZf1GNTTM8GH","type":"reasoning","text":"Another PARSE_ERROR: \"service: Unexpected attribute enable\"\n\nSo `enable=\"no\"` is ALSO not valid! And the original `samba-client enable=\"no\"` was also invalid.\n\nHmm. So what IS the correct way to disable an inherited service in a firewalld zone XML?\n\nLet me think about the firewalld zone XML schema. A `<service>` element in a zone has only a `name` attribute. The way to REMOVE an inherited service is:\n1. Use `<remove-service name=\"mdns\"/>` — this is a separate element!\n2. Or just don''t include it\n\nYes! The firewalld zone XML has:\n- `<service name=\"foo\"/>` — add\n- `<remove-service name=\"foo\"/>` — remove an inherited one\n\nSo the correct syntax is `<remove-service name=\"mdns\"/>`.\n\nI got it wrong twice. Let me verify by checking the firewalld documentation or an existing zone file on the system that uses remove-service.\n\nLet me check /usr/lib/firewalld/zones/ for examples.\n\nThis is the right approach — check the shipped zone files for the actual schema.\n\nLet me look.\n\nAlso note: the original file had BOTH `disable=\"yes\"` (invalid) and `enable=\"no\"` (invalid). So the file was always broken. The live one was tolerated... hmm, but actually maybe the live one WAS failing silently and the tolerance was for the comment issue.\n\nWait — actually the live zone showed `dhcpv6-client ssh` and mdns disabled didn''t error. So firewalld loaded it. Confusing. But regardless, let me get the schema right.\n\nLet me check the shipped zones.","time":{"start":1790453043428,"end":1790453047301}},"time":1790453047301}');
