INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df527ad3001Diett5oMCZVI3N','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',7686,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df526d25001mNIJgcYJ5iJrSC","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df525f4b001npkBujv3U07sMR","type":"reasoning","text":"A brand-new `Zone()` has:\n- services = [] (empty, denies everything)\n- icmp_blocks = [] (nothing blocked → PMTU + NDP pass)\n- masquerade = False\n\nSo a custom zone is exactly what I want: deny all inbound by default, nothing added, and critical ICMP unblocked by default.\n\nSo the plan:\n1. Create a custom zone `workstation` in /etc/firewalld/zones/workstation.xml\n2. Add only `dhcpv6-client` service\n3. Explicitly allow icmp + ipv6-icmp protocols (for clarity, though default is fine)\n4. Set as default zone\n5. Bind wlo1 to it\n6. Remove the broken public.xml override (so built-in public is used again as the fallback)\n\nLet me write the zone file and validate it with the real parser.\n\nLet me write it.\n\nNote: no masquerade needed for a workstation — masquerade on a client zone is actually wrong/pointless (it''s for NAT-ing a network behind). Let me drop it. Actually the original had `<masquerade/>` which would NAT traffic. On a client laptop that''s unnecessary and could interfere. Let me remove it.\n\nLet me write the corrected file.","time":{"start":1790453116197,"end":1790453119699}},"time":1790453119699}');
