INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df5523a1001mlbigX0I5ai2e0','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',7831,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df5523a1001g1M291X32g3tJX","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df551c89001cItBQu3pf2Av9k","type":"reasoning","text":"","time":{"start":1790453293985}},"time":1790453293985}');
INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df5532d3001D9kMo44Yg7VJs1','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',7832,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df5523a1001g1M291X32g3tJX","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df551c89001cItBQu3pf2Av9k","type":"reasoning","text":"Now I have the complete picture. Let me summarize accurately:\n\n1. **It did not work.** firewalld is \"running\" but has 0 rules loaded. Default zone fell back to `public` because `workstation` never existed. The `cp` of workstation.xml apparently didn''t execute (or the user skipped it).\n\n2. **My errors:**\n   - Told them `wlo0`, actual interface is `wlo1`\n   - Said `firewall-cmd --reload` when firewalld explicitly required `systemctl restart firewalld`\n\n3. **What DID work:** `set-anon-identity.sh` — hostname is now `zero`, /etc/hosts updated.\n\n4. **Concerning:** those `INVALID_ICMPTYPE` errors at 12:57 — someone attempted `--add-icmp-block` on v6-neighbour-solicit etc. All failed as invalid, so likely nothing blocked. But I should verify ICMP state after restart.\n\nSo the corrected recovery:\n```bash\nsudo cp ~/Projects/zen-hardening/workstation.xml /etc/firewalld/zones/workstation.xml\nsudo firewall-offline-cmd --check-config\nsudo systemctl restart firewalld        # RESTART, not reload\nsudo firewall-cmd --set-default-zone=workstation\nsudo nmcli con mod \"USL - Public\" connection.zone workstation\nsudo nmcli con up \"USL - Public\"\n```\n\nThen verify with nft tables count.\n\nLet me be honest and concise. The user asked \"what''s next\" so let me lead with the correction and the fix.\n\nLet me also flag the ICMP block attempt as a question — who ran it? Probably the user experimenting. I should verify it''s not in effect. Let me include a check.\n\nLet me write the response.\n\nKey message: it did NOT work; firewall still unenforced; two of my instructions were wrong; here''s the corrected sequence.\n\nLet me be direct about the severity.","time":{"start":1790453293985,"end":1790453297875}},"time":1790453297875}');
INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df5532d7001I3ChSnHFGvrTKG','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',7833,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df5532d7001WSqRxDvuhy5LDK","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df551c89001cItBQu3pf2Av9k","type":"text","text":"","time":{"start":1790453297879}},"time":1790453297879}');
INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df554575001wk8yHPD4Uo3Sfj','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',7834,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df5532d7001WSqRxDvuhy5LDK","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df551c89001cItBQu3pf2Av9k","type":"text","text":"It did not work, and I need to correct myself before you go further.\n\n## Status\n\n**Firewall is still not enforcing.** `firewalld` reports `running` but has **0 rules loaded** and no zone bound to `wlo1`. The journal tells the story:\n\n```\n13:07:18  Default zone ''workstation'' is not valid. Using ''public''.\n13:07:46  INVALID_ZONE: workstation\n```\n\nThe `workstation.xml` copy never landed — `/etc/firewalld/zones/` is empty. So `--set-default-zone=workstation` silently fell back to `public`, and `wlo1` is bound to no zone at all.\n\n## Two mistakes in what I gave you\n\n1. **I wrote `wlo0`.** Your interface is **`wlo1`**.\n2. **I said `firewall-cmd --reload`.** firewalld explicitly told you otherwise at 13:01:03 — a failed config requires `systemctl restart firewalld`. A reload just re-reads the same broken state and leaves it unenforced.\n\n## Corrected sequence\n\n```bash\nsudo cp ~/Projects/zen-hardening/workstation.xml /etc/firewalld/zones/workstation.xml\nsudo firewall-offline-cmd --check-config\nsudo systemctl restart firewalld            # restart, NOT reload\nsudo firewall-cmd --set-default-zone=workstation\nsudo nmcli con mod \"USL - Public\" connection.zone workstation\nsudo nmcli con up \"USL - Public\"\n```\n\nThen the check that actually matters — **not** `--state`, which lies:\n\n```bash\nsudo nft list tables | grep firewalld\nfirewall-cmd --get-zone-of-interface=wlo1\nfirewall-cmd --zone=workstation --list-services\n```\n\nI want to see actual `firewalld` table names in the nft output. `running` alone is not evidence.\n\n## What did succeed\n\n`set-anon-identity.sh` worked:\n\n```\nhostname now: zero\n127.0.1.1\tzero\n```\n\n## One thing I want to check with you\n\nThe journal shows these at 12:57, before any of my zone work:\n\n```\n12:57:16  ERROR: INVALID_ICMPTYPE: v6-neighbour-solicit\n12:57:18  ERROR: INVALID_ICMPTYPE: v6-neighbour-advert\n12:57:20  ERROR: INVALID_ICMPTYPE: v6-redirect\n```\n\nSomething tried to **block** those three. They''re exactly the IPv6 neighbour discovery types that must stay open. All three calls failed, so nothing should be blocked — but I want to confirm after the restart, because if PMTU or NDP is blocked your IPv6 will break in ways that look like a network fault.\n\nDid you run an `--add-icmp-block` command around 12:57?","time":{"start":1790453297879,"end":1790453302645}},"time":1790453302645}');
