INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df571da4001p1S1uGWu37l1lN','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',7892,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df570ada001gG03g550OhMJ6W","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df56b010001ji8FRmTK1tKiDw","type":"text","text":"Good news: **no ICMP types are blocked.** All three calls were rejected, so nothing took effect. Your IPv6 and PMTU are fine — the mystery is harmless.\n\nOn the source: those were three interactive `sudo` prompts, so a command typed in a terminal, not a background service. My scripts contain no `icmp` references and I never gave you an `--add-icmp-block` command. Most likely a stray paste or shell history recall. Nothing to chase.\n\n## The one thing that matters now\n\nYour firewall is still down. `wlo1: no zone`, zero rules loaded. Run:\n\n```bash\nsudo cp ~/Projects/zen-hardening/workstation.xml /etc/firewalld/zones/workstation.xml\nsudo firewall-offline-cmd --check-config\nsudo systemctl restart firewalld\nsudo firewall-cmd --set-default-zone=workstation\nsudo nmcli con mod \"USL - Public\" connection.zone workstation\nsudo nmcli con up \"USL - Public\"\n```\n\n`systemctl restart`, not `firewall-cmd --reload` — firewalld told you that itself at 13:01:03, and I should have said it the first time.\n\n**Verify:**\n```bash\nsudo nft list tables | grep firewalld\nfirewall-cmd --get-zone-of-interface=wlo1\nfirewall-cmd --zone=workstation --list-services\n```\n\nPaste that output. The first command is the only real proof — `--state` said `running` while zero rules were loaded, so it can''t be trusted on its own.\n\n## Where we actually are\n\n| | Status |\n|---|---|\n| Firewall rules | **DOWN** — needs the block above |\n| Hostname | `zero` ✓ |\n| `/etc/hosts` | `zero` ✓ |\n| ICMP | open, correct ✓ |\n| fail2ban | active, jail list still unverified |\n| Anon script | ran, MAC randomization unconfirmed |\n\nAfter the firewall is confirmed up, the remaining items are: verify fail2ban''s four jails, confirm `wlo1` MAC randomization actually took, and push the corrected zone file — which I still haven''t pushed, since I won''t commit a config I haven''t watched pass `--check-config` on your machine.","time":{"start":1790453418714,"end":1790453423523}},"time":1790453423524}');
