INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df58c377001BA4U77bsFhMqKm','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',7943,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df58b2f30018pOqZG1y22nRIG","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df588afd001gE2tIMdhRdg3dX","type":"text","text":"`/etc/firewalld/zones/` is still empty — the `cp` never executed. The source file is fine at `~/Projects/zen-hardening/workstation.xml` (1760 bytes).\n\nLet''s do this one step at a time so nothing gets lost in a paste. Absolute paths, no `~`:\n\n**Step 1 — install the file:**\n```bash\nsudo cp /home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/workstation.xml /etc/firewalld/zones/workstation.xml\n```\n\n**Step 2 — confirm it actually landed:**\n```bash\nsudo ls -la /etc/firewalld/zones/\n```\n\nThat second one is the check that matters. If the file is there, run:\n\n**Step 3:**\n```bash\nsudo firewall-offline-cmd --check-config\n```\n\nThen paste what steps 2 and 3 print. I expect `workstation.xml` in the listing and `ok` from step 3.\n\nOnce those pass:\n```bash\nsudo systemctl restart firewalld\nsudo firewall-cmd --set-default-zone=workstation\nsudo nmcli con mod \"USL - Public\" connection.zone workstation\nsudo nmcli con up \"USL - Public\"\n```\n\nA note on the error you saw: `Default zone ''workstation'' is not valid` is not a problem with the file. Your earlier attempt at 13:07 already wrote `DefaultZone=workstation` into `/etc/firewalld/firewalld.conf`, but the zone file it points to was never installed. So the reference is dangling. Installing the file resolves it.","time":{"start":1790453527283,"end":1790453531511}},"time":1790453531511}');
