INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df62ee8b001rc6yv1iap6mo1d','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',8386,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df62e69c001A14rCQtOWI2NA7","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df62da15001vFM0Vw4JKD2noh","type":"text","text":"That''s a self-inflicted problem, and I should have anticipated it.\n\nPasting a multi-line `while` loop into an interactive fish shell is a bad idea. Fish executes each line as you paste it, so the loop got fed to the terminal line by line and the terminal — not fish — tried to interpret pieces of it. That killed Konsole.\n\n**Don''t paste that block.** The helper is already installed and verified, so all you need is one line:\n\n```fish\nsource ~/.config/fish/config.fish\n```\n\nThen:\n\n```fish\nf2bready\n```\n\nIf you''d rather not source anything, single-line form, safe to paste:\n\n```fish\nsudo fail2ban-client status\n```\n\nfail2ban has been up for several minutes now, so the readiness race is long gone — a plain query will answer instantly. The wait loop only mattered in the seconds right after a restart.\n\nPaste that one line and tell me the jail count. If Konsole is being difficult, a terminal emulator is trivially replaceable and nothing of yours was at risk in losing it.","time":{"start":1790454195868,"end":1790454197898}},"time":1790454197898}');
