INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df641ce8001hjiwLt6pmoXpyn','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',8494,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df640f4f001FK2tzFE1WHaVRL","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df64085b001u9rFSlqUmrMu2h","type":"text","text":"Verified. Your 2 jails are up and clean, but install this fix:\n\n```bash\nsudo cp /home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/shield-kitty-fail2ban.local /etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty.conf\nsudo fail2ban-client -t\n```\n\nThen apply it:\n\n```fish\nsource ~/.config/fish/config.fish\n```\n```bash\nsudo systemctl stop fail2ban\nsudo systemctl restart fail2ban\nf2bready\n```\n\n## What I verified\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Service / process | active, PID 228983 |\n| Errors since 13:21 | none |\n| `recidive` enabled on disk | `true` ✓ |\n| Jails | 2 — `recidive`, `sshd` ✓ |\n| `/var/log/fail2ban.log` | exists, 21.8 KB ✓ |\n| `bantime` | `86400` everywhere, no `-1` ✓ |\n\n## The bug worth knowing about\n\n`firewallcmd-common.conf:37` hardcodes `zone = public`. Changing your default zone to `workstation` silently broke every ban — fail2ban would have written rich rules to a zone that isn''t bound to your interface, logged `SUCCESS`, and blocked nothing.\n\nThat''s the failure mode you can''t detect by checking whether fail2ban is running. It only shows up if you test an actual ban end-to-end.\n\nIf you want proof rather than my word, after applying:\n\n```bash\nsudo fail2ban-client set sshd banip 192.0.2.66\nfirewall-cmd --zone=workstation --list-rich-rules\nsudo fail2ban-client set sshd unbanip 192.0.2.66\n```\n\n`192.0.2.0/24` is TEST-NET-1, reserved and unroutable, so it''s safe to ban as a test. The rich rule should appear in the `workstation` zone, confirming bans land where they take effect.\n\nWant me to push everything once that''s confirmed?","time":{"start":1790454271823,"end":1790454275304}},"time":1790454275304}');
