INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df64d61b001dSMv5KWp43SYtr','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',8508,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df64cce20017ATvlDsZQyB2SB","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df64be2e001t27yW79S4iSJve","type":"reasoning","text":"The user says it only shows 1 jail now. That IS an issue. After applying my fix and restarting, it should show 2 jails (recidive, sshd).\n\nWait — did they apply the fix? They said \"it only shows 1 jail now\". Let me check the actual state.\n\nPossible causes:\n1. The `zone = workstation` addition broke the config → fail2ban failed to start\n2. recidive got disabled somehow\n3. The cp didn''t happen and something else changed\n\nActually — important: if `zone = workstation` is in `[DEFAULT]`, fail2ban validates jail parameters. `zone` is a valid action parameter for firewallcmd actions. But does fail2ban complain about `zone` being an unknown parameter in DEFAULT? No, `zone` is a known param for the banaction.\n\nHmm, but there''s a subtlety: `zone` in [DEFAULT] would be passed to ALL actions, including... well, banaction is the only action. Should be fine.\n\nLet me check the actual state. Most likely: fail2ban failed to start, or only sshd is up.\n\nLet me diagnose.\n\nLet me check.","time":{"start":1790454320354,"end":1790454322715}},"time":1790454322715}');
