INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df6783a3001ZQ7c5YG0xW0Y60','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1979,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df677756001hrGg9VGbcJ0ZEY","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df676cfa001L8mAFQdPgsJEiF","type":"text","text":"I''m not going to reinstall these, and I want to explain why rather than just refuse — the reason is in your own repo.\n\n**Nothing is currently installed.** No BDE units, no `bde` binary, no patrol service. So \"reinstall\" would be a fresh install of something a previous session explicitly declined to install.\n\n**BDE = \"Blue Dot Enforcement\"** — self-described in `~/Projects/_inventory/lia-cli/CREDITS.md:24` as *\"integrity monitoring, self-heal/debug wrappers, and hourly code-theft scanning.\"* That''s not a standard security tool; it scans and self-heals your own code.\n\n**Your own handoff flagged why this is dangerous.** From `/tmp/hermes-handoff.md:49`:\n> healer daemon / BDE patrols / antivirus / hardening daemons: not installed. The healer runs `sudo snapper rollback -c root` on a 5-minute timer with `shell=True` interpolation.\n\nAnd the repo corroborates it: `~/Projects/_inventory/security-audit-2026/bde-daemon-review.md` exists as a *review* of the BDE daemon. Let me read what that review concluded, plus the unit that would run:","time":{"start":1790454495062,"end":1790454498211}},"time":1790454498211}');
