INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df6e59bc001k1GNMk6s59pTME','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',9099,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df6d128e0017q1f7b4VrepbUy","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df6d08d5001ZEUfh0i68Q3IlL","type":"reasoning","text":"We need produce exact markdown structure, combine prior and conversation, terse, current. Need carefully capture all relevant objective, details, completed, active, blocked, next, files. Need not mention summary. Need include objective user wants complete secure anonymity stack, reproducible, remote inbound revoked except Wi-Fi, hostname zero, fail2ban, Tor. Also preserve older unresolved objectives/parallel workstreams perhaps relevant. But conversation focuses hardening. Developer says carry forward objectives constraints decisions and parallel workstreams even if not mentioned, drop finished no longer needed. Need include Shield Kitty etc maybe completed, unresolved Void etc perhaps still objective from prior. Need balance. Exact template. Desired oververbosity 5, but summary likely detailed enough.\n\nLet''s reconstruct all conversation outcomes accurately, correct errors. Need not continue conversation, only summary.\n\nKey chronology and final state:\n\nInitial fail2ban:\n- fail2ban auto reads jail.d/*.conf not .local.\n- original file had recidive enabled and missing fail2ban log, startup abort.\n- journald-only no /var/log/auth.log, no syslog. Need backend systemd, journalmatch.\n- eventually installed /etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty.conf.\n- sddm and sudo jails were structurally dead; removed.\n- config only sshd and recidive, 24h ban, zone workstation.\n- local project source has recidive false by design to bootstrap, even though live enabled true. Copy resets recidive, documented.\n- active live 2 jails, service active, no errors after final. Need maybe end-to-end test remains.\n- fail2ban `PartOf=firewalld.service` systemd unit conflict; apply-firewall works around stop fail2ban, restart firewalld, start fail2ban. A permanent systemd drop-in maybe not done.\n- fish helper f2bready appended to ~/.config/fish/config.fish; user accidentally restarted Konsole with multiline loop but no system damage. They see 2 jails.\n- fail2ban action zone pin necessary and added.\n- bantime all 86400, recidive enabled on disk, zone workstation.\n\nFirewall:\n- Initially custom firewalld-workstation.conf broken. We should state superseded/deleted, never use.\n- Validated new custom `workstation.xml` with firewalld 2.5.2''s zone_reader; only service dhcpv6-client, protocols icmp ipv6-icmp, no masquerade/forward, no rich rules. firewalld currently running, default workstation, wlo1 zone workstation. User says `sudo nft list tables | grep firewalld` output `table inet firewalld`, proving table exists. Asked to list chains but not yet output. apply-firewall script passed. It was pushed to hermes-security-scripts. Old public.xml override removed. No ICMP blocked. SSH, mDNS, SMB, KDE Connect blocked. KDE Connect allowed only future secure self-administered network via `set-home-trusted-zone.sh`, not applied. User chose current strict as option 1, prepare option 2. Script safety gate WPA, custom zone home-net with target default. Potential bug in script: hardcoded `wlo0` vs actual wlo1 in binding; script calls firewall-cmd change-interface=wlo0 and verification wlo0, so likely broken! Need capture as active/unknown. It was written, not applied. User chose leave as strict until secure network. Must fix interface hardcoding later. Also script has `conn=$(nmcli -t -f NAME,TYPE ... awk -F: ...)` with connection name colon potential. Fine. It uses connection name \"YourHomeSSID\" assumption equal saved connection; not guaranteed. Need mention interface hardcoded wlo0 must fix before use. Also `nmcli con up` drops network, not rollback. But no apply.\n\nHostname anonymity:\n- set-anon-identity.sh created at project, chmod, ran successfully; hostname now `zero`, /etc/hosts `127.0.1.1 zero`. Old `living-asustuf...` grep weird output no \"none\" because pipeline semantics, but likely no references. It sets per-network random MAC using wrong NetworkManager property `802-11-wireless.mac-address-mode`. Actual property in current NetworkManager is `802-11-wireless.mac-address-randomization`, so script didn''t work for MAC. The query at end exposed wrong field. Current kernel MAC `f4:a4:75:e8:00:b2` still hardware. Need fix script to use correct property and verify after reconnect. User says build it out. Also DHCP send-hostname no set likely okay. Avahi active mDNS blocked by firewall. machine-id and DMI not changed intentionally. Bluetooth alias not changed. Tailscale inactive. DNS 10.128.128.128 perhaps maybe Tailscale MagicDNS but tailscaled inactive; no need.\n- User requested all networks/interfaces show Zero. We need perhaps note machine-id/DMI separate if literal zero; not done. Hostname is zero.\n- \"wlo1\" actual interface, current conn USL - Public. `eno2` stable Ethernet, no randomization (only WiFi script). User said all interfaces. Need decide whether MAC randomization on Ethernet possible; generally cannot per-network randomize arbitrary wired MAC safely, but NetworkManager cloned-mac perhaps. We can note WiFi only; interface names all network identity via hostname. Could apply same hostname to any. We should not overreach.\n\nTor:\n- Initially not installed but later detected tor 0.4.9.13-1 active enabled, SOCKS loopback 127.0.0.1:9050. User must have installed between turns. No browser installed at that point. User asked install Tor and browser. Assistant recommended Tor Browser, not normal browser proxy. User moved on to firewall, so Tor Browser still not installed. Need make active.\n- No browser at all. Tor Browser package `torbrowser-launcher`. Need perhaps audit Arch AUR packaging? We can install. We should mention `tor` was installed and active.\n- Tailscale inactive, DNS 10.128.128.128. Not necessarily important.\n- Full transparent proxy not configured due conflict and risks, not user confirmed option. User asked \"fastest anonymity/security\"; assistant recommended layer 1 Tor Browser + local tor SOCKS. We should preserve decision: Do not point normal browser at system tor; use Tor Browser. Full system-wide transparent proxy deferred, not installed, because conflicts with firewall/fail2ban. Need maybe list blocker/decision. The user changed to firewall request but likely still wants browser. \"build it out\" means install it.\n- `torbrowser-launcher` perhaps absent still; need verify current because could have installed. Last check no browser, no torbrowser. Mention last known.\n- Tor daemon listening loopback only, no inbound surface.\n\nGit push:\n- business-debug-wrappers commit 7301a28, business-health-monitor e1562d4, lin-antimalware 4d304c3 pushed.\n- local-only projects consolidated:\n  - hermes-security-scripts commit 36e2e1b zen-hardening + shield-kitty + forensics.\n  - then maybe later commit unknown hash for firewall configs? The assistant didn''t show log hash after commit. We need not invent.\n  - security-audit-2026 commit 407fdf5 buildlog.\n  - firewall working config commit unknown hash (not displayed) pushed, then fail2ban commit 4346767.\n  - Source project `zen-hardening` local still exists, no remote. Consolidated copy is source of truth? `apply-firewall.sh`, workstation.xml etc pushed under hermes-security-scripts/config/zen-hardening.\n  - Old `firewalld-workstation.conf` removed locally and consolidated repo, superseded.\n  - `token.clean` still present and should be shredded after audit; SSH auth works. User says push as go. No more need for API perhaps but should shred once done.\n- Repos had no remotes initially, but consolidation resolved backups. Need maybe source local repository `zen-hardening` is itself a git repo with dirty uncommitted? It has .git. It may have no remote and modified files. But files consolidated and pushed. We should mention remote backup exists. Could clean local state eventually.\n- secret scans clean except fake key fixture. Good, perhaps not needed to carry unless still relevant.\n- `buildlog` has personal hostname, placed private repo security-audit-2026.\n\nFirewall live:\n- Current source `workstation.xml` has comments claiming verified, only dhcpv6, icmp protocols.\n- apply-firewall script verified syntax, passed live.\n- old default zone set workstation. `nmcli` connection profile set. Firewall strict.\n- Need perhaps actual nft chain proof: user said table inet firewalld, assistant requested chain but not user response. Script''s PASS required nft table >0 and interface zone. It got PASS. So sufficient. Table exists and interface bound. Completed.\n- `firewallcmd-rich-rules` fail2ban banaction uses default port range etc and zone pinned. End-to-end ban not done. This is active/next.\n- `unban-self.sh` Hermes file reviewed and pushed. It is safe but grep check in assistant incorrectly reported input validation no because pattern mismatch, but read showed actual validation. Could mention completed/relevant.\n- `fail2ban-coverage.md` explains dead local jails. Pushed.\n- `set-home-trusted-zone.sh` and `set-anon-identity.sh` pushed in commit 36e2? Wait initial consolidation commit 36e2e1b happened before these scripts were created. Later push of working configs included them in commit with no displayed hash. In latest rsync, they remained unchanged; likely tracked. Yes.\n- There were two files not ours\n`unban-self.sh` and `fail2ban-coverage.md`, then reviewed and pushed. Fine.\n- There were `enroll-admin.sh`, `install-faillock-admin.sh`, `fail2ban-coverage.md` from Hermes? Assistant saw in git status. The prior summary mentioned faillock config issue. We need preserve user directive not to enable admin_group wheel without fresh approval. Were these scripts pushed? The first consolidation `rsync` only added 18 files, including config zen-hardening four files, not enroll admin. Later rsync in firewall commit added `enroll-admin.sh`, `install-faillock-admin.sh`, `fail2ban-coverage.md` etc. It did push those. But we need not detail unless active security concern. Important: live faillock no admin_group. The scripts may enroll user to wheel, but user is already wheel. They were likely created by Hermes. Should not run.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/faillock.conf` now has admin_group wheel, not live, per prior. Conversation didn''t change. Keep constraint. There is a new `install-faillock-admin.sh`, `enroll-admin.sh`; should perhaps mark review needed, don''t silently apply. We need carry unresolved active.\n- Full diagnostics pending from prior after fail2ban. But conversation has progressed. Still maybe include in next move or active: rerun full post-hardening diagnostics.\n- Evidence chain completed, Shield Kitty active from prior. Need include completed.\n- System update check: prior says Hermes etc zero updates at earlier point. Could omit if not needed, but developer says drop only finished/no longer needed. It''s a completed fact but still relevant perhaps diagnostics. Could include compactly.\n- Other prior unresolved objectives: user initially wanted restore stack, install Void, full Zen/Kali/Arch etc. We need carry forward objectives and active unresolved. But summary is context for next agent; likely should include all active major work. However conversation dominates. Need not drown in old peripheral tasks, but explicit instruction says carry forward objectives, constraints, user directives, decisions, parallel workstreams. So include:\n  - Shield Kitty device blacklist not installed, PAM/root daemon review required.\n  - Void AUR absent and fresh build required.\n  - bde-security-biometrics, lin-antimalware-tools, local-emergency-patrol, zen-healer, security-audit-2026, secure-tactical-systems not installed/reviewed.\n  - `zen-healer` unsafe.\n  - Full Zen/Kali/Arch request unresolved; no Kali partition; zen-suite ISO only.\n  - KDE Connect decision now resolved: blocked now, deferred home trusted. Drop pending.\n  - buildlog uncommitted resolved/pushed to private repo.\n  - Steam/emulators absent and supercode unidentified perhaps still active. Do we include? It was a user request from prior. Yes, maybe compact bullet.\n  - Xbox emulation blocked legal firmware, no need if continuing security build. But explicit carry forward blockers maybe.\n  - `21-layer encryption` no design, no reformat. Keep.\n  - Tor integration is new active.\n  - Token.\n- Objective should perhaps 2 bullets: \"Build a reproducible post-rebuild Garuda hardening/anonymity stack: strict inbound firewall, Zero identity, fail2ban/PAM, Tor Browser, automated checks; preserve recovery and push configs.\" And \"Continue remaining requested tooling/ISO/emulator etc.\" But one-two brief sentences. We can mention broader stack.\n\nImportant Details:\n- User shell is fish; don''t give bash `until/do/done`; use fish syntax or scripts. f2bready function now persistent.\n- User can rebuild from scratch and wants all changes pushed as we go. Consolidate local projects into existing GitHub private repos. Public repo caution for buildlog.\n- Sudo requires password; agent no root. Need user-run commands.\n- Tor Browser vs normal browser.\n- Firewalld must preserve ICMP PMTU and IPv6 NDP; don''t block. Custom zone no masquerade.\n- Fail2ban local sddm/sudo impossible; no re-add. Recidive bootstrap and source copy footgun.\n- fail2ban action zone pin.\n- `PartOf` conflict.\n- Hostname \"Zero\" interpretation.\n- Machine ID/DMI separate.\n- MAC property correction.\n- Potential actual bug in `set-home-trusted-zone.sh` hardcoded wlo0, so must fix before use. This is important active.\n- Tor is currently loopback only, not inbound. Full transparent proxy deferred.\n- No browser.\n- Maybe `firewall-cmd --state` can report running with no rules; use nft table and zone binding. Important verification principle.\n- `firewall-offline-cmd --check-config` uses `/etc`, not source. Need stage and check. But now fixed.\n\nCompleted:\n- Sysctl 24, Firefox xinput, lin anti etc.\n- Shield Kitty active, forensics intact.\n- Git pushes with commit IDs.\n- fail2ban active 2 jails and no errors after final, config live. Should state final local config differs from source (live recidive true, source false). Pushed source false and warning. 24h. Only sshd/recidive. `zone=workstation`.\n- Firewall strict and live. `table inet firewalld`, default/iface workstation. service only dhcpv6. no ICMP block. mDNS etc blocked. `apply-firewall.sh` passed.\n- Hostname zero /etc hosts. DHCP no? Set anon script ran. But script''s MAC portion not done. Don''t mark all script.\n- Tor daemon installed active enabled 127.0.0.1:9050 (user installed between turns). No browser.\n- repos push. Buildlog etc.\n- f2bready persistent.\n- `unban-self` reviewed/pushed.\n- Could mention no real secrets found.\n- User''s old FAillock remains `deny=10` etc. `admin_group=wheel` not live. Completed? Not applied. Active/constraint.\n\nActive:\n- Finish \"build out\": verify/fix MAC randomization property. Current kernel MAC real. `set-anon-identity.sh` must update to `802-11-wireless.mac-address-randomization yes`; likely values yes/no or enabled? Need know actual property accepted values. We can say verify syntax, don''t prescribe exact yet. Current NetworkManager allowed property. Need maybe all network interfaces. Ethernet MAC not addressed. Hostname applies all.\n- Install Tor Browser (`torbrowser-launcher`), verify signature/package maybe Arch AUR. Keep tor daemon. Do not system-wide transparent proxy unless explicitly choose due firewall conflict.\n- End-to-end fail2ban ban test with TEST-NET IP and rich rule, unban.\n- Full system diagnostics.\n- Push latest source after MAC/Tor/bootstrap.\n- Bootstrap/rebuild installer: Need create a reproducible script applying hostname, firewall, fail2ban, Tor Browser, etc. User wants build out.\n- `set-home-trusted-zone.sh` deferred, fix wlo1.\n- Other old tasks: Void, device blacklist, etc.\n- Clean local project git? The consolidated repo is pushed, but local no remote. Could perhaps no longer active.\n- `token.clean` shred after final API checks.\n- Admin group wheel scripts no apply pending review.\n- machine-id DMI if user wants literal \"zero all identifiers\"; no automatic change.\n- SDDM no automated protection. Could perhaps implement screen lock/presence but user didn''t choose. Keep honest.\n\nBlocked:\n- Root operations require user sudo.\n- no automated SDDM local brute force protection via IP bans. faillock applies sudo, not greeter.\n- Full Tor transparent proxy conflicts / wasn''t selected; no browser. Maybe not blocker but deferred.\n- machine-id ephemeral tradeoff; not done.\n- other prior blockers.\n- \"fastest anonymity/security\" tension; Tor slower.\n- No write token? SSH push works, so repo creation blocker resolved through consolidation. Drop.\n- `set-home-trusted-zone` requires secure WPA network user administers and SSID. Blocked until then.\n- no secure network.\n- Need legal firmware for Xbox, no Kali partition, etc. Keep perhaps in one bullet.\n- User can rebuild but no need reformat.\n\nNext Move should be immediate concrete actions, likely:\n1. Fix `set-anon-identity.sh` to use current NetworkManager property and activate, then reconnect Wi-Fi and verify new locally administered MAC while interface remains in workstation. This must preserve connection and avoid lockout? It''s local, okay. Need maybe user runs. Since all network interfaces? Use correct property.\n2. Install Tor Browser: `sudo pacman -S torbrowser-launcher`? AUR package needs paru/yay, not pacman perhaps. On Arch `torbrowser-launcher` is AUR, `paru -S torbrowser-launcher`; conversation earlier suggested `sudo pacman -S` incorrectly. Need correct in summary. Last known paru available? Prior paru process. likely paru installed. We can say use AUR helper and verify. Then launch, don''t point normal browser at local SOCKS. Maybe if package unavailable use official Tor Browser with signature. Need not detail exact command in Next Move? Could.\n3. End-to-end ban test. Could order ban test before Tor? Highest current unresolved. The user said \"what we have to do to build it out\"; next move should immediate: finish verification, then Tor. Maybe 1 MAC, 2 ban, 3 Tor browser/bootstrap. Only template supports numbered list, can have more than 2. Prior summary had 2 but current can list 4? User says one or two? Template says [next action if known], no limit. We can have 4.\n- Push after changes.\n- full diagnostics.\n- old remaining requested stack maybe next move 5? Need prioritize.\n\nRelevant files: many. Need exact\npaths and why. We can list key:\n  - `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/shield-kitty-fail2ban.local`\n  - `/etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty.conf`\n  - `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/workstation.xml`\n  - `/etc/firewalld/zones/workstation.xml`\n  - `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/apply-firewall.sh`\n  - `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/set-anon-identity.sh`\n  - `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/set-home-trusted-zone.sh`\n  - `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/unban-self.sh`\n  - `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/fail2ban-coverage.md`\n  - `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/faillock.conf`\n  - `/etc/security/faillock.conf`\n  - `/home/livings/.config/fish/config.fish`\n  - `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/99-hardening.conf`, `/etc/sysctl.d/99-hardening.conf`\n  - Shield kitty files/evidence.\n  - hermes-security-scripts remote path not local? consolidated clone `/tmp/opencode/hss` ephemeral; local source under `~/Projects`. Could mention remote repo `git@github.com:intricos777-dot/hermes-security-scripts.git` and `security-audit-2026.git`. No file path? Relevant files section says path, but URLs/remote okay perhaps.\n  - `/home/livings/.config/gh/token.clean`\n  - `firewalld-workstation.conf` removed, no need list except warning? It is relevant to avoid resurrection, but file no longer exists. Could mention in Important Details rather than relevant file.\n  - `shield-kitty` paths.\n  - browser package not file.\n  - `hermes-blood` theme.\n\nNeed ensure exact output only summary. No paragraphs. Terse bullets. Need not include every old detail but carry enough.\n\nLet''s deeply inspect conversation to avoid wrong claims:\n- In final fail2ban verification:\n  - `recidive on disk :` first command blank due grep; second confirms true.\n  - service active; errors 0.\n  - two jails user confirms.\n  - source pushed with recidive false. This is important. At latest push, source was false. The commit message maybe says drop etc. Live has true. Good.\n- `zone = workstation` on source and live.\n- Fail2ban test config successful? User had after source copy presumably `sudo fail2ban-client -t`; they reported one jail. We saw clean server. So yes.\n- End-to-end ban remains not run.\n- `unban-self.sh` pushed. It requires root for list. Good.\n- `fail2ban-coverage.md` says three of four? Then table actually sddm/sudo dead, recidive depends. Summary table says \"three of four jails do not work\" because recidive maybe no bans until another jail. But with sshd inactive, recidive no data. We can say no active protection except firewall/faillock. Fine.\n- sshd jail enabled but dormant due sshd inactive and firewall blocks port 22. The jail list includes it. recidive enabled and active as a jail but no upstream bans because sshd dormant. Good.\n- The user wanted incoming remote permissions revoked; strict zone does.\n- `dhcpv6-client` only. Does WiFi IPv4 DHCP still work? It remained connected; yes.\n- `firewallcmd-rich-rules` on workstation: It adds rich rules to zone. Good.\n- `firewallcmd-rich-rules` port defaults 1:65535. The rich rule includes port. It should block all ports. Good.\n- `firewalld` with source rule and default reject should work.\n- Need perhaps test that rich rules appear in persistent runtime? `firewallcmd-rich-rules` default `nofity`? It likely runtime not permanent? Not relevant.\n- Firewalld strict state says `nft list tables` user thought empty but says table. We can mark completed.\n- `firewall-cmd --state` reported running when no tables, hence script checks nft. Good.\n- `workstation.xml` uses `<protocol value=\"icmp\"/>`, `<protocol value=\"ipv6-icmp\"/>`, no icmp blocks. Good.\n- There are no SSH/mdns rich rules.\n- `set-home-trusted-zone.sh`: actual script hardcodes `firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=\"$ZONE\" --change-interface=wlo0` but later NetworkManager connection zone assignment. It may be redundant and wrong. Must correct before use.\n- It also opens mdns on trusted zone, despite user asked only KDE Connect. On a trusted network that''s acceptable, but anonymity maybe mDNS. Not critical.\n- User said option 2 but leave as 1 until secure network; script prepared not applied. Completed preparation, active future.\n- set-anon script:\n  - uses `while read uuid` and `nmcli -t -f UUID,TYPE con show | awk -F: ''$2==\"802-11-wireless\"{print $1}''`; likely works.\n  - query wrong property. The initial check before run also used wrong field and assistant assumed. Script likely returned error for each wifi con but due no set -e? `if nmcli ... | grep` error but pipeline exit? set -euo pipefail. In `if`, nonzero allowed; then `nmcli con mod \"$uuid\" 802-11-wireless.mac-address-mode random` should fail and because set -e exit script. But hostname changes occurred before loop, so script stopped at invalid property. The user likely ran and hostname succeeded, then script errored? They didn''t report. Current connection property remains unset, confirms. So script did not complete DHCP hostname part. Need fix. We should not claim DHCP suppression applied. Active.\n  - It says explicit no but current send-hostname -1, so DHCP hostname already suppressed by default. Fine.\n  - `set-anon-identity.sh` did change hostname and hosts. It may fail at WiFi step. Need mention.\n- Current interface `wlo1`, current MAC real. Need not assume MAC randomization mode. Correct property is `802-11-wireless.mac-address-randomization`; values likely yes/no. We can say update.\n- User requested \"all networks and interfaces\" and set hostname static globally, so all interfaces use same hostname. Avahi active but blocked. DHCP send host false. Ethernet MAC remains. Full hardware identifiers not \"zero\".\n- DMI hardware strings local only, not on network, but \"shows up\" maybe not transmitted.\n- machine-id may be sent in logs, not network generally. We flagged.\n- Tailscale inactive despite DNS 10.128.128.128. Could be NetworkManager/resolver. No action.\n\nTor:\n- At first `pacman -Q tor` not installed, then later it is. User installed manually. `tor` loopback 9050. Could mention no `torbrowser-launcher`.\n- It says \"browser still absent\" when firewall audit. So active.\n- `tor` service uses no inbound due loopback.\n- User wants fastest possible. We should maintain that Tor Browser is slower; don''t claim speed. \"Anonymity first, no transparent proxy yet.\" Good.\n\nGit:\n- Initial pushes:\n  - business-debug-wrappers 7301a28\n  - business-health-monitor e1562d4\n  - lin-antimalware 4d304c3\n  - hermes-security-scripts 36e2e1b initial consolidation\n  - security-audit-2026 407fdf5 buildlog.\n  - Later firewall commit hash not shown; then fail2ban 4346767. We can mention latest known 4346767, plus earlier.\n  - `hermes-security-scripts` private presumably. Yes.\n  - `security-audit-2026` private.\n  - SSH auth works as intricos777-dot.\n  - token read-only. No need API further. Shred.\n- Source `zen-hardening` local no remote but consolidated. User wanted backup. Good.\n- `firewalld-workstation.conf` removed both local and consolidated. It had invalid XML comments, invalid attributes. We need warn not to restore.\n- `workstation.xml` and scripts pushed. Latest fail2ban commit only showed change to config; workstation and scripts were in prior commit. Good.\n- Pushed unreviewed Hermes files after review. Fine.\n\nOther prior:\n- Sysctl hardening installed. Good.\n- `lin-antimalware` and business tools. Pushed fixes.\n- Shield Kitty:\n  - watcher active and evidence.\n  - device-blacklist unroot installed. Need preserve.\n  - `void-bin` absent etc. Maybe include under Active \"Other requested stack remains...\" in one bullet.\n- Full system diagnostics after hardening pending. Good.\n- Root LUKS2, no need reformat. Keep in important.\n- User wheel. no NOPASSWD.\n- PAM faillock:\n  - live /etc lacks admin_group. `faillock.conf` project has admin_group wheel. `admin_group=wheel` would exempt user, undermining brute force. Keep not installed.\n  - `enroll-admin.sh` / `install-faillock-admin.sh` were generated and pushed. Need review and don''t run unless explicit. Since user is already wheel, not needed.\n- `pam_faillock` deny=10 protects sudo? Does faillock apply to sudo through pam module? The prior scripts likely ensure. We can say configured/intended local sudo. Hermes coverage says protection. Fine.\n- SDDM no auto protection.\n- Fail2ban source config name `.local` but copy to `.conf`. Good.\n- Recidive first-run file bootstrap. Source disabled, live true.\n- `ignoreip` includes RFC1918. Current private IP safe. But public IP can be banned 24h. Escape script.\n- `bantime=86400` exactly.\n- `unban-self.sh` safe.\n\nPotential issue: fail2ban service active and 2 jails but fail2ban `recidive` uses polling and log file. Good.\n- `fail2ban` journald backend default for sshd. Good.\n- sddm/sudo removed, so no local failures. Good.\n- `zone=workstation` in DEFAULT is action parameter. Config test passed. Good.\n\nBlockers:\n- `firewall-offline-cmd` root needed; resolved.\n- `sudo` user input.\n- `set-home-trusted-zone` no secure network.\n- `torbrowser` no browser, package installation root/AUR.\n- No direct root.\n- machine-id/SDDM structural.\n- Prior unresolved external repos.\n- `set-anon` property currently wrong; that''s not blocker, active.\n- `firewallcmd` end-to-end ban not tested; unknown.\n- `nft` chain not listed but table exists and script pass, so not a blocker.\n- `fail2ban` source vs live recidive state divergence intentional. Need avoid future copy resetting.\n- System unit bug can be fixed permanently via drop-in. The script workaround is enough but future manual `systemctl restart firewalld` will fail again. Active: create `systemctl edit fail2ban` drop-in to reset PartOf? Need know how to remove `PartOf` inherited. A drop-in cannot clear list dependencies easily? You can use empty `PartOf=` assignment in drop-in to reset list, then `After=firewalld.service`. For list directives, assigning empty resets. We could create:\n```\n[Unit]\nPartOf=\nAfter=firewalld.service\n```\nin `/etc/systemd/system/fail2ban.service.d/no-firewalld-partof.conf`.\nThen daemon-reload. But this is a live system unit modification requiring review. We can propose. It would solve. Add active. However, original fail2ban unit has PartOf for all firewall backends; is this truly packaging bug? `PartOf=iptables.service firewalld.service...` may be intentionally to stop when firewall changes, but restart conflict is a known issue. `PartOf` propagates stop/restart from listed unit to fail2ban; when restarting firewalld, systemd should restart fail2ban, not conflict stop. The conflict likely because `systemctl stop fail2ban` then `restart firewalld`? Wait apply script did `systemctl stop fail2ban` first, then `systemctl restart firewalld`. Since fail2ban is stopped, the firewalld restart transaction includes PartOf and wants restart fail2ban? `PartOf` propagation does stop/restart from firewalld to fail2ban, but why conflict with already stop? The manual command before script was `systemctl restart firewalld` while fail2ban active, and systemd said conflicting restart and stop. Could be because firewalld has `Conflicts=shutdown.target`? But likely PartOf weird. The script successfully did stop then restart firewalld, then start. That means in script the stop transaction completed before restart; no direct conflict. It may work with active too? User''s manual `systemctl restart firewalld` failed, so yes.\n- A drop-in can avoid. Keep as next after core.\n\nFull diagnostics:\n- failed units, listeners, zones, nft rules, jail list, package integrity, updates, evidence chain, disk, memory. We can put next move last.\n\nPotential `f2bready` function:\n- It was appended and verified. User''s current shell initially needed source; after Konsole restart config loads automatically on new shell. Fine.\n- Multi-line fish paste issue caused Konsole restart; important shell constraint.\n\nNeed exact output format. We can make sections with bullets, not paragraphs. Keep reasonably detailed but terse. Since prior summary huge, final can be maybe 2500 words? Desired oververbosity 5, but \"terse bullets\". Need balance. We can include all major. Maybe 100-150 bullets? Too much. We can condense.\n\nLet''s draft.\n\nObjective:\n- \"Finish a reproducible Garuda/Arch post-rebuild security and anonymity stack: Zero identity, strict ingress, fail2ban/PAM protections, Tor Browser, verified recovery tooling, and GitHub backups.\"\n- \"Continue remaining requested tooling/ISO/emulator work only after core hardening is verified.\"\n\nImportant Details:\n- user fish, sudo password, no blanket NOPASSWD, can rebuild, push changes as go.\n- root LUKS2 no reformat.\n- Tor Browser correct; no system transparent proxy without explicit due conflicts; Tor SOCKS loopback.\n- Firewalld custom workstation semantics and ICMP.\n- fail2ban details.\n- local jail structural.\n- hostname/MAC identifiers.\n- secure network KDE Connect decision.\n- Hermes parallel.\n- claims and old tasks.\n\nCompleted:\nCould group:\n1. Core OS/hardening.\n2. firewall.\n3. fail2ban.\n4. anonymity.\n5. tools.\n6. Git.\n\nNeed avoid active contradictions:\n- \"Installed firewalld workstation zone\" and `firewalld-workstation.conf` old removed.\n- \"set-anon script ran\" but partial due invalid property; phrase hostname portion only.\n\nCompleted bullets:\n- Sysctl etc.\n- Firewall state and table.\n- Fail2ban final.\n- Hostname.\n- Tor daemon.\n- Repos.\n- Shield Kitty.\n- f2bready.\n- unban script review.\n\nActive:\n- Fix anon script; current kernel MAC.\n- Tor browser.\n- ban test.\n- durable fail2ban unit drop-in.\n- rebuild bootstrap.\n- old tasks.\n- token.\n- machine ID etc maybe active.\n- `set-home` future.\n\nBlocked:\n- root.\n- SDDM local.\n- secure network.\n- Tor full transparent.\n- unresolved old external.\n- no attack surfaces etc.\n- legal console.\n- no 21 layer.\nMaybe no need duplicate active.\n\nNext Move:\n1. Fix MAC script and apply. Could include exact likely property but not command. Since summary not answer yet.\n2. Run ban test.\n3. Install Tor Browser with AUR helper, keep system tor SOCKS and no transparent.\n4. Make systemd PartOf drop-in and bootstrap script; test.\n5. full diagnostics/push/shred token.\n6. remaining requested stack.\n\nNeed perhaps put highest immediate as:\n1. Correct `set-anon-identity.sh` `802-11-wireless.mac-address-mode` -> `802-11-wireless.mac-address-randomization`; apply to `USL - Public`, reconnect, verify locally administered MAC. Also retain DHCP hostname suppression.\n2. Test fail2ban end-to-end.\n3. Install Tor Browser.\n4. Build `bootstrap-rebuild.sh` and systemd drop-in, test, push, diagnostics.\nThen old tasks later.\n\nRelevant files:\nMaybe 20 entries, but can group related in bullets? Format says path: why. We can list each exact path. Need preserve identifiers.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/shield-kitty-fail2ban.local`: source; recidive false intentional, zone, 24h, 2 jails.\n- `/etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty.conf`: live, recidive true, 2 jails.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/workstation.xml`: validated zone.\n- `/etc/firewalld/zones/workstation.xml`: live.\n- apply script.\n- set anon.\n- home trusted.\n- unban.\n- coverage.\n- faillock source/live.\n- fish config.\n- sysctl source/live.\n- Shield Kitty watcher/evidence and blacklist.\n- `~/.config/gh/token.clean`\n- remote repositories perhaps.\n- `void` no file. Maybe relevant file not.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/hermes-blood` etc maybe completed but no active. Do we need all prior relevant files? Developer says preserve exact paths when known. Carry forward objectives but drop finished no longer needed. Shield Kitty completed but still relevant. Keep.\n- `/tmp/hermes-handoff.md`.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/buildlog` now backed up. Relevant maybe not.\n\nNeed include `firewalld-workstation.conf` warning. It''s removed, so not relevant path? Could list with \"(deleted; do not restore)\" perhaps. Since path known and important to avoid resurrect. The template allows file/directory path. Add:\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/firewalld-workstation.conf`: deleted/superseded; known-invalid, do not restore.\nThis helps.\n\nLet''s ensure no statement \"installed firewalld workstation zone\" old conflict. Use custom zone.\n\nPotential issue in current `workstation.xml`: It only allows dhcpv6, protocol icmp and ipv6-icmp. Firewalld protocol `icmp` may only allow ICMPv4 and `ipv6-icmp` allows v6. Good.\n\nCurrent old live `/etc/firewalld/zones/public.xml` was removed. Prior relevant file says active, must correct. In summary relevant, say deleted. Current default public no. Good.\n\nCurrent `faillock.conf` project was changed by Hermes to admin_group wheel and source pushed. Do not install.\n- live faillock `deny=10`, `unlock_time=30`, audit silent. Keep.\n\nNo `admin_group` applied. Good.\n\nTor:\n- User said \"reinstall tor\" and assistant found it installed. Maybe not \"installed by us\"; phrase \"Detected and verified `tor 0.4.9.13-1` installed/active/enabled.\" Good.\n- No browser remains. Good.\n\n\"fastest possible anonymity and security\" assistant corrected. Important.\n\nKDE Connect:\n- `kdeconnectd` listening broad, but firewall blocks. Future home zone script. The script currently hardcodes `wlo0` and needs correction; exact active.\n- It opens `mdns` and `kdeconnectd`, plus dhcpv6. If user later wants only needed WiFi and admin, okay.\n- It checks security key mgmt. Good.\n- User wants option 2 but current option 1. State.\n\nGit:\n- `hermes-security-scripts` latest commit `4346767`; initial `36e2e1b`; firewall commit hash unknown. We can list known.\n- `security-audit-2026` `407fdf5`.\n- Other IDs.\n- Source local `zen-hardening` no remote; but consolidation means backup.\n- Need perhaps mention all current changes are pushed as of commit 4346767, except the new future edits? The `set-anon` script bug in source was pushed unchanged. The source still contains wrong property. We need fix then push. `workstation.xml` etc pushed. `set-home` pushed. Good.\n- `f2bready` in fish config is not in a repo; not backed up. Need include in bootstrap or config repo. Good active.\n- `token.clean` remains.\n- There is no write token needed due SSH.\n- We should not expose actual token. Path only.\n\nOther old active tasks:\nLet''s think if summary is too cluttered. The explicit user directive \"Let''s do what we have to do to build it out\" likely means security stack, not old ISO. But prior summary says objective includes entire post-rebuild stack. Developer says carry forward. Include one bullet:\n- \"Remaining requested ecosystem: `void-bin`/`void-electron-latest-bin` not built; `bde-security-biometrics`, `lin-antimalware-tools`, `local-emergency-patrol`, `zen-healer`, `secure-tactical-systems` unreviewed/uninstalled; `zen-healer` unsafe. Steam/emulators absent, supercode unidentified; Xbox requires legal firmware; Zen suite only builds ISO; no Kali partition.\"\nThis is long but preserves.\n\nCompleted old:\n- `lin-antimalware` installed and business monitors. The pending `lin-antimalware-tools` is a different repo, so okay.\n- Blood Build theme. Could include one bullet.\n- Evidence chain.\n- disk purge maybe no need. Completed facts not needed unless diagnostics. But developer says carry forward objectives, not every fact. Fine.\n\n\"Important Details\" should include no blanket admin group wheel. Good.\n\nLet''s formulate exact.\n\nPotential \"Blocked\" section:\n- root sudo.\n- `set-home-trusted-zone` until secure network.\n- SDDM structural.\n- no Tor Browser and AUR install root? Actually not blocked, just not installed. Don''t list.\n- Full transparent Tor not selected.\n- machine-id DMI not changed by design, not blocker.\n- old tasks.\n- no 21 layer.\nCould say `(none)`? No, root and structural.\n\n\"Next Move\" should be concrete, not too many. Maybe 5 steps.\n\nLet''s ensure same language conversation: English. Fine.\n\nNeed exact structure. No extra headers. Good.\n\nLet''s write concise but comprehensive.","time":{"start":1790454862478,"end":1790454946235}},"time":1790454946236}');
