INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df6f6e6e001wqXDuv3Feg3fp6','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',9239,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df6f592a001yXnuvz8qfVusFW","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df6f5418001zpU4LWwyYkxFbl","type":"text","text":"`79ecc5e` pushed.\n\n## Correction: your \"all green\" was not all green\n\n`bootstrap.sh` reported `0 checks failed` but MAC randomization had never worked. The firewall, fail2ban and hostname are genuinely correct; the identity check simply wasn''t in the verification table. Two bugs, both mine, both silent by construction:\n\n| Attempt | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `mac-address-mode random` | Property doesn''t exist in NM 1.58 → `set -e` abort, prints success anyway |\n| `mac-address-randomization 1` | Accepted — but `1` is the enum value for **NEVER**, so it *disabled* randomization |\n\nNM 1.58.1 accepts exactly `default`, `never`, `always`. `yes` and `random` are both rejected. Fixed to `always`.\n\nThe pattern worth noting: both bugs were settings that were *accepted* and *reported* a plausible value while doing the opposite of what was asked. That is why I verified against the interface rather than the exit code.\n\n## One command left\n\n```bash\nsudo bash /home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/set-anon-identity.sh\n```\n\nWiFi will drop for a few seconds. Then confirm it actually took:\n\n```bash\ncat /sys/class/net/wlo1/address\n```\n\nExpect a **different** address than `f4:a4:75:e8:00:b2`, with a locally-administered first octet — one of `2x`, `6x`, `ax`, `ex`. The MAC changes on reconnect, not on the setting itself, so read it *after* you''re back online.\n\nIf it still shows the hardware MAC, tell me and I''ll dig further rather than assume.\n\n## Final state\n\n- `hermes-security-scripts` @ `79ecc5e` — private, contains bootstrap, firewall zone, fail2ban config, anonymisation, Shield Kitty tools\n- Firewall: strict, only `dhcpv6-client` inbound, `wlo1` in `workstation`\n- fail2ban: 2 jails, 24h, zone-pinned, 0 errors\n- Hostname `zero`, DHCP hostname suppressed\n- Tor bootstrapped, loopback-only — but **still no browser**, so it does nothing for anonymity yet\n\nTwo things I''d still flag: `~/.config/gh/token.clean` is on disk and should be shredded, and the SDDM greeter has no automated brute-force protection (structural — documented in `fail2ban-coverage.md`, not fixable with config).","time":{"start":1790455011626,"end":1790455017070}},"time":1790455017070}');
