INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df71d48c001ugV1ycJj6wm7Y2','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',2462,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df71cbc0001q4xoWDXslplkRB","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df71aee8001M6iamKHvZPbUss","type":"tool","callID":"call_function_0y2qnpaheq1l_1","tool":"question","state":{"status":"running","input":{"questions":[{"header":"Deployment scope","options":[{"description":"You run the exact sudo commands I print, in order: create shield-admin, enrol livings, set enroll.lock, install the corrected faillock.conf, verify. I write and verify the commands but never touch /etc myself.","label":"Deploy admin exemption, skip permanent lock (Recommended)"},{"description":"Same sequence, plus dir= off tmpfs and unlock_time=0 so non-admin accounts stay locked across reboots. You acknowledge the DoS risk and that recovery needs a root console.","label":"Also enable permanent lockout for others"},{"description":"I only fix the malformed ''audit = silent'' line and add the missing enroll.lock guidance to the repo docs. No /etc changes, no group creation.","label":"Fix repo files only, deploy nothing"},{"description":"Point me at how to reach the other machines and I''ll audit each one for other users before proposing anything.","label":"Tell me about the other machines first"}],"question":"There are no other users on this machine, so the ''lock out and ban'' half has no targets. How should I proceed?","multiple":false}]},"time":{"start":1790455174284}}},"time":1790455174284}');
INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df71d491001cPnhfnZqZH63so','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',2463,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df71b629001Y4ISP27dTcsch6","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df71aee8001M6iamKHvZPbUss","type":"text","text":"I''ve stopped short of changing anything, because what I found contradicts the premise of the request. Here''s the situation.\n\n**There are no other users.** `livings` (uid 1000) is the only login-capable account; `root` is the only uid-0 account. Every entry in your login history is you. So there is nothing to lock out, nothing to flag as a guest, and nothing to ban — on this machine.\n\n**I can''t act \"on any other machines\"** — I only have shell access here. Nothing in this repo or these scripts can reach another host, and I''d have no way to verify such a change.\n\n**The admin exemption you want is not active, and can''t be safely turned on as-is.** The whole design is correct in the repo, but none of it is live:\n\n- `/etc/security/faillock.conf` has **no `admin_group`** — so you are not exempt, and `pam_faillock` will lock `livings` like anyone else after 10 failures.\n- The `shield-admin` **group does not exist**.\n- `/etc/shield-kitty/enroll.lock` is **missing**, so `enroll-admin.sh` reports enrollment **OPEN** — it would let any account be enrolled.\n- The live config has drifted from the repo (`unlock_time = 30` vs the repo''s `admin_group` line, and `audit = silent` is malformed — `audit` and `silent` are bare flags, so that line likely sets neither the way you intend).\n\n**On \"permanently\":** `unlock_time = 0` is what you''d want for real permanent lockout, but the man page is explicit that it''s *\"usually undesirable... easily a target of denial of service attack.\"* And it only becomes truly permanent if you also set `dir=` off tmpfs — right now tallies live in `/var/run/faillock`, which **vanishes on reboot**. So `unlock_time = 0` as-is would be permanent only until the next reboot, which is the worst of both: strict enough to hurt you, leaky enough to not work.\n\nCritically, **`unlock_time = 0` and the admin exemption must be enabled together, in that order** — group created, `livings` enrolled, `admin_group` set and verified *before* permanent lockout goes on. If I set `unlock_time = 0` first and the exemption silently doesn''t work, you''re locked out of your own machine with no recovery except a root console.\n\n**And I can''t apply any of it** — every step needs your sudo password, which I don''t have.\n\nSo the honest summary: the config for \"only `livings` is admin\" is already written and well-reasoned (`enroll-admin.sh` even refuses to enroll anyone else), but it''s **entirely undeployed**, and the \"lock out and ban other users\" half has no targets here.","time":{"start":1790455166505,"end":1790455174288}},"time":1790455174289}');
