INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df76e7cf002Rby4crEkkybwSp','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',2583,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df76dbd7001Pb7qwQKj0GM0wv","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df76d7ac001PrvaKMAw4AZXRp","type":"reasoning","text":"Part 1 fails because `tr '','' ''\\n''` doesn''t split — the group output uses `:` as the separator for the member list, not `,`! \n\n`getent group shield-admin` returns: `shield-admin:x:991:livings` — the members are after the LAST colon, and multiple members are comma-separated. So `shield-admin:x:991:livings,other` would be the format for multiple members.\n\nSo I need to strip the `shield-admin:x:991:` prefix first, THEN split on commas. `tr '','' ''\\n''` on `shield-admin:x:991:livings` gives one line `shield-admin:x:991:livings`, which does not match `-x livings`.\n\nThis is the same bug class as the earlier source-name parsing bug. Let me fix it properly using cut or parameter expansion.\n\nThe robust way: `getent group \"$GROUP\" | cut -d: -f4 | tr '','' ''\\n''`\n\nLet me fix both the script and the test. This is a real bug I introduced — good thing I tested.\n\nNote: `enroll-admin.sh` also has this pattern? Let me check... In enroll-admin.sh cmd_status it just does `getent group \"$GROUP\"`. And the config comment says:\n```\ngetent group shield-admin | tr '','' ''\\n'' | grep -v ''^shield-admin'' | grep -v livings\n```\nThat''s in the faillock.conf comment — which has the SAME BUG. It would not work correctly either. Let me fix that comment too.\n\nLet me fix the script first.","time":{"start":1790455503831,"end":1790455506895}},"time":1790455506895}');
