INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df7711d2001SHFBzKrXkIOhBf','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',2628,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df770dd2001OIqZCZ6Q81CnyG","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df770605001mhXwZLNRgld9yX","type":"reasoning","text":"Now the predicate is correct: only the genuinely-exempt states proceed, and it correctly handles a multi-member list with livings not first.\n\nNote the important case: \"group has a DIFFERENT member\" -> ABORT. Good, that''s the safety property.\n\nNow, the same bug exists in the faillock.conf comment verification instructions. Let me fix that too.\n\nLet me check the comment in faillock.conf:\n```\n# Verify the membership is still just you:\n#   getent group shield-admin\n# Expected: shield-admin:x:<gid>:livings\n#   getent group shield-admin | tr '','' ''\\n'' | grep -v ''^shield-admin'' | grep -v livings\n# Expected: no output.\n```\n\nThat `tr '','' ''\\n'' | grep -v ''^shield-admin''` is wrong. Let me fix it.\n\nLet me read and fix.","time":{"start":1790455516626,"end":1790455517649}},"time":1790455517650}');
