ave passed unconditionally -- or failed, depending on\n  which direction it was read. Fixed with cut -d: -f4 in both the script and\n  the instructions in faillock.conf.\n\nVerified the step-4 predicate against six states: it proceeds only when\nlivings is genuinely a member AND the config names the group, and aborts\nwhen the group is absent, empty, holds a different member, or the config\nis missing. unlock_time stays 30s -- permanent lockout (unlock_time=0) is\ndeliberately not enabled, since with a broken exemption it is unrecoverable.\"\ngit log --oneline | head -2","metadata":{"output":"819c363 faillock: add ordered deploy script, fix malformed audit/silent flags\n207f22e chore: ignore __pycache__\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1790455528198,"end":1790455528216}}},"time":1790455528216}');
