INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df79ddfd001k2wzilui2bl0Lh','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',9480,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df79c8280014n36PPZKBw7fQ1","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df79bff200116EqOzHFq9VK9E","type":"text","text":"`505c4f6` pushed. No reboot needed.\n\n## Final verified state\n\n| Layer | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Hostname | `zero`, DHCP hostname suppressed |\n| MAC | `ea:bd:c8:4d:53:a8` — locally administered, `always` |\n| Firewall | `workstation`, only `dhcpv6-client` inbound, ICMP unblocked |\n| fail2ban | 2 jails, 24h, zone-pinned, 0 errors |\n| Tor | bootstrapped, `127.0.0.1:9050` only |\n| Backup | `hermes-security-scripts` @ `505c4f6`, private |\n\n## Remaining, in priority order\n\n**1. Tor Browser — the only thing still materially missing.** Tor is running with no client, so it provides zero anonymity right now.\n\n```bash\nsudo pacman -S torbrowser-launcher\n```\n\n**2. Revoke the token on GitHub.** Shredding the local copy doesn''t invalidate it server-side. **Settings → Developer settings → Personal access tokens → Fine-grained → revoke.** If a btrfs snapshot of `/home` exists, the plaintext may survive locally: `sudo btrfs subvolume list /`\n\n**3. SDDM greeter brute force.** Real gap, not fixable via config — `pam-generic` needs `rhost=<IP>` and a local console has none. Mitigations are authentication strength, lid close/lock, and screen lock timeout. Tell me if you want me to set the lock ones.\n\n**4. `machine-id` still unique.** Not exposed over the network in most cases, but it does appear in logs. Changing it to ephemeral breaks services; I won''t do it without you deciding.\n\n## Bugs I introduced and fixed this session\n\nWorth recording, since all three shared one shape — a setting that was **accepted, reported success, and did the opposite of what was asked**:\n\n- `mac-address-mode` doesn''t exist in NM 1.58 → `set -e` aborted, printed `[ok]` anyway\n- `mac-address-randomization 1` → `1` is the enum value for **NEVER**, so it disabled randomization\n- `bootstrap.sh` verified hostname but not MAC → \"all green\" on incomplete identity\n\nEach was only caught by checking the live interface instead of the exit code. That''s why the new check fails closed on the MAC, and why `set-home-trusted-zone.sh` now refuses to bind an interface it can''t confirm exists.","time":{"start":1790455695400,"end":1790455700989}},"time":1790455700989}');
