INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df7aac96002N99h7PJR3LpueL','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',2824,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df7a9b660012xR2vnaKy1LBip","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df7a95db001Gch8ea9AMTtr0u","type":"reasoning","text":"The only difference is `enabled = false` (repo) vs `enabled = true` (live) for the `recidive` jail. Everything else is identical, including all three `bantime = 86400`.\n\nSo the 1-day lockout is ALREADY live and active. The `recidive` jail is enabled live (which the repo says should be false until manually enabled — and the comment says it''s enabled by `sudo sed -i`).\n\nSo the current state:\n- bantime = 86400 (1 day) — already live on sshd, sudo, sddm-ish jails\n- recidive jail enabled live: repeat offenders get another 24h\n- `unban-self.sh` documentation says bantime = -1 (permanent) — that''s WRONG/stale documentation\n\nSo the \"1 day lockout\" request is already satisfied for the network-intrusion jails (sshd, sudo, and one more).\n\nBUT: the user asked for two things:\n1. \"anything spoofing my system\" — system spoofing. Is there any jail for that? fail2ban doesn''t do spoofing detection. There is NO jail for ARP/DHCP/hostname spoofing. That''s not fail2ban''s job.\n2. \"trying to access my system from another system thru any connection device\" — network access attempts. Partially covered by sshd/sudo jails, but what about ALL connection devices? sshd is INACTIVE on this machine (established earlier). So the sshd jail matches nothing.\n\nKey gaps to report:\n- sshd is not running → its jail bans nothing. And even if enabled, nothing listens on port 22.\n- No spoofing detection at all (no arpwatch, no DHCP snooping, no mDNS/hostname collision guard).\n- `unban-self.sh` docs are stale/wrong (say permanent, actually 86400).\n- The `recidive` jail is enabled live but the repo says false — a drift, though arguably intentional (someone enabled it deliberately).\n- The device blacklist (USB HID) — not installed.\n\nLet me verify the full jail list and which are actually live/active. Need root for fail2ban-client. Let me parse the config instead to determine enabled jails.\n\nLet me read the full repo config to understand the jail structure, and determine what''s actually enabled and covering.\n\nLet me also check what \"connection device\" attack surfaces exist and are listening.\n\nLet me read the full file.","time":{"start":1790455749478,"end":1790455753878}},"time":1790455753878}');
