INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df7acbca001WTnc6zOUiCvIwI','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',2838,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df7ab50c001C3tEp9syUrG6o3","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df7aae300011BP0WeLW51fA6w","type":"reasoning","text":"Now I have the full picture. Let me verify the actual live state and identify the gaps.\n\nCurrent state:\n- `bantime = 86400` (1 day) is ALREADY live for sshd and recidive. The user already has what they asked for on the network-intrusion side.\n- The comment at line 52 says \"must list 2 jails\" — so DEFAULT + sshd + recidive.\n- `zone = workstation` — but firewalld is INACTIVE/disabled! So `firewallcmd-rich-rules` banaction will fail or do nothing. This is a critical gap: bans would be logged but block nothing, OR fail2ban errors out.\n\nThat''s a big finding: firewalld is inactive (established earlier), so the `banaction = firewallcmd-rich-rules` cannot apply bans. Let me verify that.\n\n- sshd is inactive → sshd jail matches nothing.\n- No `sudo` jail in the live file! The user has fail2ban for sshd and recidive only. `unban-self.sh` mentions sddm and sudo jails. But the live file has only sshd + recidive. So sudo attempts aren''t fail2ban-covered (though pam_faillock covers sudo via faillock).\n\nLet me verify what jails are actually running — needs root. I can''t. But I can check the config and whether fail2ban is actually functional.\n\nKey gaps for the user''s request:\n1. **1-day bantime: already live.** ✓\n2. **firewalld inactive** → the ban action can''t actually block anything. This is the critical failure: bans would be recorded but not enforced.\n3. **No spoofing detection at all.** fail2ban is a log-parsing brute-force tool; it has no capability for ARP/DHCP/hostname/MAC spoofing. That needs something else entirely (arpwatch, dnsmasq DHCP fingerprinting, systemd hostname collision, TPM attestation).\n4. **sshd inactive** → remote-access jail matches nothing.\n5. **`unban-self.sh` docs are stale** — say bantime=-1 permanent, actually 86400.\n6. **Device (USB HID) blacklist not installed** — that''s the \"connection device\" local ban path.\n\nLet me verify the firewalld issue since it''s the most important — if bans can''t be enforced, \"1 day lockout\" is theater.\n\nLet me check.\n\nLet me test whether the banaction would work. I can check if firewallcmd is functional.\n\nLet me verify these gaps concretely.","time":{"start":1790455756044,"end":1790455761865}},"time":1790455761866}');
