INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df7b385c0025JFqUL6moNklTE','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',2904,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df7b2943001BqjiPbqovGzZsv","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df7b1e24001v0Z8fUupButEMV","type":"reasoning","text":"Key finding: the machine''s address is 10.197.250.246/8, which is inside 10.0.0.0/8 — so it''s covered by `ignoreip = 10.0.0.0/8`. That means the whole LAN is ignored by fail2ban, which is intentional per the config (never ban your own LAN).\n\nBut that also means: an attacker on the same LAN (10.x) would NEVER be banned, because ignoreip covers all of 10.0.0.0/8. That''s a significant gap given the machine is on a 10.x network — likely a campus/enterprise network where \"another system\" could be on the same /8.\n\nThis is a really important finding: the ignoreip is so broad that on a 10.x network, fail2ban effectively never bans anyone. And 10.197.250.246/8 — the /8 means the whole 10/8 is ignored, which is a huge range.\n\nWait, let me re-read: `ip -4 addr show scope global` gave `10.197.250.246/8`. So the interface has a /8 mask. That means the machine considers 10.0.0.0/8 to be \"on-link\" (local). So a huge number of hosts are on the same L2/L3 broadcast domain potentially.\n\nSo fail2ban''s ignoreip = 10.0.0.0/8 would exempt all of them from banning. This directly undermines \"1 day lockout for anything trying to access my system from another system.\"\n\nThis is worth flagging prominently.\n\nAlso: kdeconnectd on *:1716 is LAN-exposed and has no jail.\n\nLet me now:\n1. Fix the stale unban-self.sh doc.\n2. Report these findings clearly.\n\nLet me check the actual subnet more carefully — is the /8 real or just how it was reported?\n\nLet me verify and also check the fail2ban effective config for ignoreip.\n\nLet me do the doc fix and then report comprehensively. Let me not over-engineer; the user needs to know:\n- 1 day is already live ✓\n- but it can''t ban anyone on 10/8, and the machine IS on 10/8 → effectively no enforcement for \"another system on the network\"\n- sshd jail is inert (sshd off)\n- kdeconnectd is LAN-exposed with no jail\n- spoofing detection: entirely absent, and fail2ban can''t do it\n\nLet me verify the subnet claim.","time":{"start":1790455785795,"end":1790455789660}},"time":1790455789660}');
