INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df7ed5a1001sJ5qWM843uG9Pc','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',3206,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df7ec3d10012d6YyOT2GWt51M","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df7ebac600150MzJI5BWpNLk3","type":"text","text":"Repo updated and committed (`c897508`). The two are now byte-identical on every functional line.\n\n**What changed:** `recidive` is now `enabled = true` in `shield-kitty-fail2ban.local`, recorded as deliberate rather than drift. All three jails (`DEFAULT`, `sshd`, `recidive`) are `bantime = 86400` — your 1-day lockout.\n\n**I didn''t just take your word for it that enabling it was safe** — I checked the preconditions, because `recidive` has a dependency that fails silently:\n\n- `/var/log/fail2ban.log` present (root:root `0600`, 34K) — the file it reads\n- `loglevel = INFO` in `fail2ban.conf` — **this is the one that matters.** Below `INFO`, recidive never observes the Ban events it exists to count, and gives no error. It would have looked enabled while doing nothing.\n- `backend = polling` + `logpath` set, since the systemd journal doesn''t carry fail2ban''s own log\n- `fail2ban-client -t` → `OK: configuration test is successful` with recidive on\n\nI kept the bootstrap-order warning and split it into \"done here on 2026-09-26\" versus \"still required on a fresh machine\" — because it''s still true for a new deploy: where fail2ban has never run, that log is missing and fail2ban **aborts the entire startup**, taking every other jail down with it. Flipping the repo to `true` unconditionally would have broken any future install.\n\nOne honest limit: I couldn''t read the log to confirm recidive is actively seeing bans — it''s `0600 root`. I verified the mechanism is configured correctly, not its runtime output. `sudo fail2ban-client status recidive` would confirm that.\n\n**Still open, unchanged by this commit** — all need your decision and root:\n\n1. `ignoreip` covers `10.0.0.0/8` and you''re on `10.197.250.246/8`, so **16.7M addresses on your own network are exempt from any ban**. This is the biggest gap versus \"ban anything reaching me from another system.\"\n2. `kdeconnectd` is LAN-exposed on `*:1716` with no jail — your only real remote surface, unmonitored.\n3. `sshd` jail is inert (sshd inactive, nothing on :22).\n4. System spoofing remains uncovered — fail2ban structurally cannot detect ARP/DHCP/hostname/MAC spoofing.\n\nWant me to draft the `ignoreip` narrowing and a `kdeconnectd` jail? Both are the kind of change that can lock you out of your own machine, so I''d want them written with a dry-run and a revert path before anything is applied.","time":{"start":1790456021969,"end":1790456026529}},"time":1790456026529}');
