INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df8150a200178Y1ZBUVCZUJ3D','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',9805,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df8141d0001IkJqgnYbn3Tk0B","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df8110b8001ekEm41XpjtW94M","type":"tool","callID":"call_function_6xn73c2wk8wj_1","tool":"question","state":{"status":"running","input":{"questions":[{"header":"Wait for agents?","question":"Several of these processes are persistent infrastructure (`hermes_cli.main gateway`, the bare `opencode` TUI sessions) that will never exit, so I can''t use process count alone. Repos are still being written to, though. How should I proceed?","options":[{"label":"Wait for repo activity to go quiet (Recommended)","description":"I poll until no repo has been committed to for ~5 minutes, then fix the Shield Kitty units and the recidive regression. Safest — avoids conflicting with in-flight writes."},{"label":"Proceed now, only touching other agents'' repos","description":"I fix Shield Kitty unit installation now but leave zen-hardening alone until it goes quiet, since that repo is actively being written."},{"label":"Proceed now with everything","description":"I fix both issues immediately. Risk: overwriting an agent''s in-flight commit to zen-hardening, which is where the recidive regression lives."}]},{"header":"Root-only checks","question":"Several diagnostics need root (nft rule dump, NVMe SMART, btrfs scrub status, dmesg). I cannot authenticate. How do you want to handle these?","options":[{"label":"Give me a command list to run (Recommended)","description":"I write out the exact read-only commands; you paste the output back and I interpret it. Nothing is changed."},{"label":"Skip root-only checks","description":"Rely on the unprivileged results only. Boot readiness is already strongly evidenced without them."},{"label":"Add NOPASSWD for specific read-only commands","description":"I create a tightly scoped sudoers drop-in for only these audit commands. Note this adds a sudo surface, which cuts against the current hardening."}]}]},"time":{"start":1790456189090}}},"time":1790456189090}');
INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df8150a40011v3wYDDQ2oog1W','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',9806,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df812f0d001JwajgkzQrPc5pA","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df8110b8001ekEm41XpjtW94M","type":"text","text":"Agents are **still writing** — `zen-hardening` committed 67s ago, 17 agent processes live. I won''t edit files they''re writing.\n\n## Audit findings so far (read-only, safe to run concurrently)\n\n**Boot readiness — clean**\n- No `pacman` db lock, **fully up to date**, no held-back packages → no partial-upgrade boot-breaker\n- No queued systemd jobs; no failed units\n- ESP mounted, `fsck` passed at boot; all `fstab` devices resolve\n- `dracut 111` is the initramfs generator (not `mkinitcpio`) — normal for current Garuda; initramfs newer than kernel\n- Boot 49.5s total, graphical target 2.8s into userspace\n- No `.pacnew`/`.pacsave` config drift\n\n**Real issues found**\n\n1. **Shield Kitty will not survive your reboot.** It''s running as a bare process (PID 287282) with *no systemd unit installed anywhere* — the units exist only in the repo. A Hermes handoff also confirms the device-blacklist is `NOT INSTALLED`. Earlier in this session it was reported \"active\"; that was the process, not a unit. Needs installing.\n\n2. **`zen-hardening` recidive regression — just introduced by another agent.** A commit 67s ago set `recidive enabled=true` in the *repo*. My `bootstrap.sh` only ever *enables* it when `/var/log/fail2ban.log` exists; it never disables it. A fresh install would therefore copy `enabled = true` with no log file — and a missing log aborts **every** jail at startup. That breaks fail2ban on a clean rebuild.\n\n3. **Memory pressure:** 5.5Gi of 7.4Gi used, 2.9Gi in zram swap. Expected with 17 agents; should drop once they exit, but worth re-checking before you reboot.\n\n**Clean / by design**\n- `kdeconnectd` and mDNS bind all interfaces, but `workstation` is `target: default` with only `dhcpv6-client` + ICMP allowed → rejected. Matches the earlier decision to block KDE Connect.\n- 3 coredumps were `alert.py --demo` test runs, not the watcher\n- `bch-faucet` `.env` missing, but its unit is `not-found` → not a boot issue\n- `dmesg` unreadable because our own `kernel.dmesg_restrict=1` is active — expected, but it means SMART/dmesg checks need root\n\nI need a decision before touching anything, because \"finished\" is ambiguous here:","time":{"start":1790456180493,"end":1790456189092}},"time":1790456189092}');
