INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df83c8390011JL5SSykv4eTFt','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',3612,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df83bd70001j8VDuIU28X2Rsu","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df83b7f6001OTv9KQmHoGINtD","type":"reasoning","text":"The schema is:\n```json\n{\n  \"severity\": \"critical\",\n  \"events\": [{\"label\": \"...\", \"count\": 1}, ...],\n  \"timestamp\": \"...\"\n}\n```\n\nAnd the headline is auto-generated: \"SHIELD KITTY\" or \"SHIELD KITTY (warning)\". So I should NOT be putting my own headline in the first event''s label — the label is the event description.\n\nSo my payload should be:\n```json\n{\n  \"severity\": \"critical\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"...\",\n  \"events\": [\n    {\"label\": \"ARP spoof: 10.0.0.5 was aa:..:01, now aa:..:02\", \"count\": 1}\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nThat gives notification: head=\"SHIELD KITTY\", body=\"ARP spoof: 10.0.0.5 was ... x1\".\n\nLet me fix the hook''s notify() to build the correct schema. I need to be careful with JSON escaping — use python to build the JSON safely rather than printf, since MAC addresses and IPs are safe but let me be robust.\n\nLet me rewrite notify() in the hook to use python3 for JSON encoding.\n\nAlso the fullscreen path (line 139, 210) uses `self.payload.get(\"events\", [])` and iterates `for e in payload.get(\"events\", [])[:6]` — let me check whether it expects strings there. Line 211: `for e in payload.get(\"events\", [])[:6]:`. Let me check what it does with `e`. If fullscreen expects strings and notify expects dicts, there''s an inconsistency in shield-kitty itself. But I''m using notify (not fullscreen), so dicts is correct. Let me check line 205-215 to be sure I''m not breaking fullscreen.\n\nLet me look.","time":{"start":1790456348016,"end":1790456350776}},"time":1790456350777}');
