label,count,sample}]. The headline is\n  generated by the alert script, so passing one in was also wrong.\n- The unit ran the hook as root, and the log/db as root, while the installer\n  omitted sudo on the log. notify-send needs the USER session bus, so a\n  root-run hook delivers the alert to nobody. arpwatch now starts as root for\n  the AF_PACKET socket and drops to livings via -u, with both writable paths\n  owned by livings. The DB moved out of ~ so ProtectHome=read-only still holds.\n\nVerified: 7/7 on classification (flip-flop alerts, new host silent, own IP and\ngateway ignored, MAC case/dash normalisation, identical MAC not a flip,\nmalformed args exit 0), plus a live end-to-end delivery through the real\nnotify-send path -- no traceback, notification returned 0.\n\nNOT INSTALLED -- needs root:\n  sudo ~/Projects/zen-hardening/install-arpwatch-spoof.sh --dry-run\n  sudo ~/Projects/zen-hardening/install-arpwatch-spoof.sh\"\ngit log --oneline | head -1"},"metadata":{"output":""},"time":{"start":1790456374575}}},"time":1790456374596}');
