INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df8fb891001hX0lWmSePYHqIB','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',4062,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df8fac2f0014rIH43K70hPznE","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df8f9c57001x8UTMCHw6w8HbC","type":"reasoning","text":"My ExecStart flags are wrong for arpwatch 3.9. The usage line shows the real flags:\n\n```\narpwatch [-CdFNpqsvzZ][-D arpdir] [-f datafile] [-i interface]\n         [-P pidfile] [-w watcher@email] [-W watchee@email]\n         [-n net[/width]] [-xnet[/width]] [-r file]\n```\n\nSo in arpwatch 3.9 (the \"new\" arpwatch, not the original ones):\n- `-i interface` for interface, NOT a positional argument\n- `-f datafile` for the database, NOT `-c`\n- No `-a` flag! No `-u` flag! No `-c`!\n\nThe original arpwatch (original arpwatch by LBL) uses `-c file`, `-a prog`, `-u user`, and positional interface. But this is arpwatch 3.9 from the `extra` repo which is a different implementation (Intronics arpwatch), with flags: -C -d -F -N -p -q -s -v -z -Z -D arpdir -f datafile -i interface -P pidfile -w/-W email -n net -xnet -r file.\n\nCritically: **there is no `-a` exec hook option in this version.** So my whole exec-hook design doesn''t work with arpwatch 3.9.\n\nLet me verify by checking the actual man page now that arpwatch is installed.\n\nThis is a significant finding. Let me check the man page and figure out the correct integration.\n\nOptions for arpwatch 3.9:\n- It writes to a database file (`-f datafile`) in a specific format\n- `-r file` — \"read database from file\"?\n- There''s no exec hook. So I need a different integration: tail/poll the database file, or use a different tool.\n\nAlternatives:\n1. Poll the arpwatch database file and detect flip-flops myself\n2. Use a different tool entirely for spoof detection\n\nLet me check the man page for what''s available.\n\nLet me investigate properly.","time":{"start":1790457130032,"end":1790457133200}},"time":1790457133201}');
