INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df982317001Jxuc9HHclDJCu3','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',4694,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df96cf84001VWtZwRxMt2oQjz","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df96c10a001rhCUrc58JG5GHG","type":"reasoning","text":"We need produce exact Markdown structure, same language conversation English. Need summarize entire combined state, focus current arpwatch failure / ongoing fix. Need retain objectives etc from prior unless outdated. Need carefully capture all completed commits/files/tests, active current test debugging. Need not continue conversation. We need ensure factual corrections: prior says firewalld inactive but later active; sshd inactive. BDE fixed not installed, faillock prepared not deployed, fail2ban 86400 live etc. Arpwatch now installed partially, service in restart loop due invalid flags. Scanner has bug? Conversation ended mid-debug: scanner actually works standalone/with bash -x, tests had issue perhaps state/harness. Need state precisely. Need inspect conversation details.\n\nLet''s map chronology and relevant current state.\n\nOriginal objective broad restore stack and audit BDE. Conversation subsequently:\n- BDE audit complete, no install. Code fixed committed 359cc45:\n  - pam/modules/bde-auth dynamic target user via pwd, BDE_FAILMODE open, unavailable distinction, etc.\n  - hardlock installer remove pam_deny, dry run backups, sshd opt-in.\n  - bde-hardlock.pam remove pam_deny.\n  - tested no daemon open exit 0 closed 1; dry-run. Not installed.\n  - correction UID is actually 1000 so hardcoded path accidentally correct today, but getuid root issue.\n- Notifications already active.\n- Void seeding stated 161/161 and later seeding maybe still running. Summary prior says 161/163. More recent conversation assistant claimed 161/161 DEPS repos fetched, 0 failures, 3GB, seeder prints done but pgrep still running. Need carry as perhaps seeding effectively complete but last verification not confirmed? Since later work irrelevant. Current objective now local security, not necessarily void. User says \"lets continue and build as needed for local systems security\" shifts objective. We need include parallel void work perhaps active/blocked because system prompt says carry workstreams. Keep terse.\n\nFaillock:\n- only login user livings, root only uid0.\n- pam_faillock active in /etc/pam.d/system-auth, sddm-autologin. live config deny10 unlock30 audit=silent malformed, no admin_group.\n- shield-admin absent, enroll lock absent.\n- User selected \"Deploy admin exemption, skip permanent lock\", but no sudo execution by agent; prepared deploy script, not deployed.\n- modified /home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/faillock.conf:\n  - audit/silent bare flags\n  - group parsing docs fixed with cut field4.\n- new deploy-faillock-admin.sh ordered, --check, deploy, revert, fixed own group parser bug discovered.\n- commit 819c363.\n- unlock_time 30 remains, no permanent 0.\n- no actual deploy due sudo.\n- buildlog entry.\nPotential scripts: enroll-admin.sh references primary livings and lock file. recovery `sudo faillock --user livings --reset`.\n\nFail2ban:\n- bantime 86400 already live in /etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty.conf. Firewalld active, workstation zone exists, bans enforceable. Earlier prior conflict corrected.\n- recidive deliberately enabled by user. Repo updated enabled true commit c897508, functional lines match live. Preconditions /var/log/fail2ban.log exists root root 0600 34K, loglevel INFO, backend polling logpath, fail2ban-client -t success.\n- docs stale permanent claims fixed commit 89506fc: unban-self.sh and fail2ban-coverage.md, address update.\n- ignoreip 10/8 and machine 10.197.250.246/8, so 16.7M addresses exempt; unresolved. Narrowing dangerous due enterprise /8 gateway 10.128.128.128. Need explicit real subnet.\n- sshd inactive and no port 22, jail inert. acceptable.\n- kdeconnectd false alarm correction: user autostart app app-org.kde.kdeconnect.daemon@autostart.service PID, but workstation firewalld bound wlo1, queries 1716 tcp/udp, 5353 udp all no; blocked. No jail logs possible.\n- system spoofing uncovered initially.\n\nArpwatch build:\n- arpwatch package available then user installed, service failed due flags.\n- Initial files:\n  - arpwatch-spoof-alert.sh exec hook (wrong for arpwatch 3.9)\n  - arpwatch-spoof.service initially uses unsupported -q -u -c -a and positional interface. Installer.\n  - commit 3a65f5e.\n  - sudo HOME bug and session env bug fixed b39490a:\n    - installer resolves SUDO_USER real home, rewrites unit\n    - hook derives alert path from BASH_SOURCE, bootstraps D-Bus and Wayland, output logging.\n  - user ran commands, second install installed package and service; service in restart loop, restart counter 6, enabled, usage shows correct flags.\n- Root cause: Arch extra arpwatch 3.9 syntax only `[-CdFNpqsvzZ] [-D arpdir] [-f datafile] [-i interface] [-P pidfile] [-w watcher@email] [-W watchee@email] [-n net[/width]] [-xnet[/width]] [-r file]`; no -a, -u, -c; must -i wlo1.\n- agent decided rearchitecture:\n  - collector service with correct flags `-F -i wlo1 -f /var/lib/arpwatch/arp.dat -s -q -N -z`; -F foreground, -s no email, -q no syslog reports, -N no bogon, -z no 0.0.0.0. But data file must be empty and precreated.\n  - new scanner `arpwatch-spoof-scan.sh` reads datafile format MAC IP timestamp [hostname], detects same IP >1 distinct MAC, state dedupe, notifications, ignore loopback, 0/8, linklocal.\n  - services `arpwatch-spoof-scan.service` oneshot and timer every 2 min.\n  - Existing `arpwatch-spoof-alert.sh` obsolete for 3.9 and should likely be removed or clearly retired, but not yet done.\n  - installer not yet updated to install new scan service/timer/datafile permissions, and old installed service is broken.\n- Tests:\n  - first scanner test: spoof 10.0.0.3/4 alerts, loopback/0 ignored. Dedup persistent no re-alert. New genuine spoof alerts.\n  - six-test suite had 5 pass 1 fail: case-different same MAC falsely counted. Edited awk to distinct MAC set.\n  - second test suite initially bizarre failures because expected cumulative count assumptions and maybe state? But manual scanner with `bash -x` proves `current=''10.3.0.1 ...''`, in_ignore, newly, SPOOF. The scanner''s awk works. Need not say fully verified after fix. There is likely an AWK `next` subtlety: when duplicate MAC in existing list, `next` jumps next record, which is fine. For new mac, appends. Thus correct.\n  - However test suite command itself had a likely bug: `run()` uses `\"$S\"` executable and state path, no issue. First test count 0, second count 0, third expected 1 got 0 — but direct run later alerted. Why? Let''s inspect exact script after edit. In run function:\n```\nrun(){ rm -f state; BDE_ARP_DATAFILE=\"$2\" BDE_ARP_STATE=... \"$S\" >/dev/null 2>&1; }\n```\nWhy did 3 fail? Maybe because test''s `run 3 /tmp/arpT2/real.dat` but file was real.dat, and state path. Should alert. Yet direct run worked. It may be due function `a` reading count before file flushed? No. Or edit happened after suite? Conversation says edit then suite, yes.\nCould be `awk next` bug when duplicate? For two different MAC, should append. Hmm.\nBut direct xtrace demonstrates current and log. We can say current logic validated on direct test, full suite rerun still needed. The active service must be stopped while rework. We cannot issue commands, just summary.\n\nNeed include current state: service installed enabled and restart-looping. `arpwatch` package is now installed. The user supplied password and ran installer, so root state partially changed:\n- /usr/sbin/arpwatch exists.\n- /etc/systemd/system/arpwatch-spoof.service old broken unit installed enabled.\n- /var/lib/arpwatch likely created; /var/log/arpwatch-spoof.log created; old arpwatch failed before writing likely. We know service restart counter 6. Need mention active.\n- No valid scanner units installed yet, only repo files. New units were written to repo, not copied. Timer not installed.\n- old service still in restart loop at summary. Immediate next action: stop/disable it then fix/reinstall units and installer, test scanner and systemd verify. We need state whether agent did stop? No, only checked, told user root cause. It remains in loop. So active.\n\nNeed include Git status? Latest commits after b39490a not committed for new scanner/unit rewrite. Existing changes in working tree:\n- `arpwatch-spoof.service` overwritten\n- new untracked `arpwatch-spoof-scan.sh`, `.service`, `.timer`\n- likely installer not yet modified to new architecture\n- `arpwatch-spoof-alert.sh` remains in repo.\nNo commit for scanner rework. Need state exactly.\n- `arpwatch-spoof-scan.sh` chmod +x.\n- tests direct.\n\nCould there be uncommitted modifications in buildlog? no.\n\nNeed carry original BDE snapper concern? Conversation found snapper installed, snapper-cleanup.timer active root, no self-heal timer/cron; no exact `snapper rollback` found. Mention maybe BDE audit unresolved? Yet BDE code fixed and not installed. Outstanding snapper rollback handoff still not matched. But current objective local security. Important details include snapper-cleanup timer active and root config, no 5-min rollback timer found. We should mention if relevant.\n\nOriginal void-bin:\n- Need preserve parallel workstream in Active/Blocked/Next maybe one bullet. User shifted but developer says carry forward objectives. We can include in Objective one-two sentences maybe \"finish local hardening and preserve ongoing void-bin build; ...\" But current objective specifically local systems security. One/two brief sentences. We can state: \"Continue hardening this Garuda host—safe admin-only PAM behavior, 24h network bans, and ARP spoof detection—while retaining prior void-bin/Electron build work.\" Good.\n- Important details include sudo manual requirement; user can run. We should not overdo old details.\n- Completed source seed maybe 161/161 stated by assistant; conflict with prior 161/163. The later says \"Void-bin sources — seeded. 161/161 DEPS repos fetched ... seeder prints done but still running.\" The prior says 163 pinned entries and two remained. Later wins. But was it actually 161/161? likely \"ok=161\"; two entries perhaps not actual repos? It claims all. We can say latest observed 161 ok, zero failures; seeder still showed process alive despite done, final status not revalidated. electron build not started.\n- Great Vibes safety, Shield Kitty active, etc completed; maybe no longer relevant but developer says drop only finished and no longer needed. Can omit Great Vibes unless retained parallel work. But \"Important Details\" could mention not global font. Yet not needed to continue arpwatch. Desired summary should focus.\n\nNeed exact output structure. We can have robust bullets.\n\nLet''s design sections:\n\n## Objective\n- Continue local security hardening: make `livings` sole faillock admin exemption, enforce 24h fail2ban bans, add safe ARP spoof detection, without self-lockout or false enforcement.\n- Preserve/finish deferred `void-bin`/`electron34` source/build workstream.\n\n## Important Details\n- Host Garuda/Arch; user `livings` uid1000, only login-capable nonroot, root uid0. `sudo` manual password required; agents can build but user runs root commands.\n- user chose deploy admin exemption, skip permanent lock. Do not set unlock_time0; no other users/other machines.\n- Fail2ban: 86400 already; recidive deliberate; ignoreip issue unresolved due /8; no blind narrowing.\n- KDE Connect correction / firewall active.\n- Arpwatch 3.9 syntax exact; no exec hook. No auto-ban due MAC randomization / large DHCP /8.\n- Alert JSON schema events list dict.\n- Need session bus environment for system service.\n- BDE not installed, commit, etc perhaps.\n- `void-bin` seed / build state.\n- shield kitty notification active.\n\nCould be too many. But summary should be comprehensive.\n\nWork State Completed:\n- BDE code fixed commit 359cc45, not installed. Explain tests.\n- Faillock prepared commit 819c363, not deployed.\n- Fail2ban docs/repo update commits.\n- Firewalld active, ban action works.\n- arpwatch initial build commits 3a65f5e, b39490a; fixes, but architecture invalid due wrong arpwatch version. Since completed but superseded. Mention as historical code commits.\n- notifications.\n- KDE correction.\n- source seeding etc.\n- Maybe original Great Vibes.\n\nActive:\n- arpwatch service currently enabled but restart-looping due old unsupported flags. Need stop.\n- new scanner files uncommitted, installer not updated.\n- direct test works but full suite rerun.\n- ignoreip etc maybe active.\n- void build.\n\nBlocked:\n- root manual command needed to stop old service and deploy corrected units. But user can run.\n- Cannot validate actual recidive runtime because /var/log/fail2ban.log root 0600. Maybe not blocker.\n- Cannot safely narrow ignoreip without true broadcast subnet.\n- void electron build long.\n- other remotes/gh? Prior workstream maybe preserve. gh absent, three repos no remotes. But current summary perhaps include under blocked if retained. User didn''t ask, but developer says carry constraints. Include terse.\n\nNext Move:\n1. Stop old service: `sudo systemctl disable --now arpwatch-spoof.service` maybe also `sudo systemctl reset-failed` optional. Then finish scanner architecture:\n  - remove/replace unsupported exec-hook references\n  - update `arpwatch-spoof.service` correct flags and precreate `/var/lib/arpwatch/arp.dat` owned? likely root; scan service needs read. Need decide ownership. We can say update installer to create empty datafile and install collector+scan service+timer.\n  - ensure datafile readable by scan service. Current unit scan service has no User, so root by default. It can read. But perhaps better user. Yet not decided. Keep generic.\n  - test `arpwatch -?`, `fail` no; `systemd-analyze verify` after arpwatch installed; use synthetic full tests.\n  - commit.\n  - give user exact commands dry-run/install and verify.\n2. After stable, decide ignoreip with user-provided broadcast domain; then start electron build after seed final check.\nMaybe immediate next action should include command. Summary format allows.\n\nRelevant Files:\nList:\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/arpwatch-spoof.service`: current corrected-in-repo collector, uncommitted; installed /etc version is old broken.\n- scanner files.\n- old alert hook obsolete.\n- installer still old (still installs collector only perhaps) and needs update.\n- /etc/systemd/system/arpwatch-spoof.service live broken.\n- faillock etc.\n- fail2ban.\n- BDE.\n- buildlog.\n- void PKGBUILD and seed log.\nMaybe no need list every old.\n\nNeed be accurate on new service `arpwatch-spoof-scan.service` unit. It has no `User=`, so root. It includes `Environment=HOME=/home/livings`, bootstraps uid based EUID=0 -> rt `/run/user/0` if no XDG_RUNTIME_DIR. Wait! Important bug! The scanner''s bootstrap_session_env:\n```\nlocal uid=\"${EUID:-$UID}\" rt\nrt=\"${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-/run/user/$uid}\"\n```\nUnit has `Environment=HOME=/home/livings` but not `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` or DBUS. Running as root means EUID=0, so it tries /run/user/0/bus, which likely doesn''t exist. Thus notifications will fail. This architecture has a latent bug! We should include as active unresolved. The old alert hook had same issue when root unless it runs as livings (it did arpwatch drop to user). But new scanner service runs root with no User. It should run as `livings` or explicitly set `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/1000`, `DBUS...`, `WAYLAND...`, or derive target user. This needs fixing before deployment. Very important. The conversation ended just after test, not noticing. Summary should mention as active bug. But we are a summarizer, not continue. Need preserve current exact state. Could say \"new scan service currently has no `User=` and would derive `/run/user/0`; notification env still needs correction before deployment.\" This is derivable but not explicitly in conversation. Is it okay to include? We should summarize known context, not invent, but this is exact. Better to include under active \"must validate user/session environment\" based prior learning.\n\nAlso scanner in_ignore uses Python each IP/CIDR, okay. `count` log grammar `anomal$( [ \"$count\" = 1 ] && echo y || echo ies)` yields anomaly/anomalies okay.\n- data file accumulation: scanner sees all historical entries forever, so \"newly anomalous\" will alert once per condition; if state file is lost, alerts old anomalies all over again. On /8 may false positives. Need perhaps state. Not necessary summary.\n- The service collector with `-q` and `-s`: Need confirm -q maybe suppress reports; -s suppress email? likely. Man usage. Fine.\n- Old installer creates log owned livings, DB dir livings. Corrected collector root can write anyway. New scanner can read. The current datafile path changed from `arpwatch.dat` to `arp.dat`, but installer still `DB=/var/lib/arpwatch/arpwatch.dat`; it does not create `arp.dat`. This is critical! Need update installer. It currently:\n```\nDB=/var/lib/arpwatch/arpwatch.dat\n...\ninstall dir\ninstall log\ninstall old unit (repo now corrected collector path /var/lib/arpwatch/arp.dat)\n```\nIt never touches DB file, just directory. Man says empty arp.dat must be created before first run. So install likely fail due missing datafile or arpwatch maybe creates? Man says must. Need active blocker.\n- Also installer does not install scan service/timer, nor remove old alert unit, nor set scanner env correctly.\n- The service restart loop from old unit still installed. Repo service was overwritten but not reinstalled. Good.\n\nNeed reflect BDE fixed code has potential logic flaw? Let''s inspect bde-auth: It removed unused talk. `capture_live` calls daemon action capture then `verify_against_profile` loc