ser response? It''s okay.\n2. update and deploy then decide ignoreip / electron.\n\nRelevant files list exact.\n\nNeed ensure user chose \"Deploy admin exemption, skip permanent lock\" and assistant prepared commands but didn''t run. Mention no actual deployment yet. They did run arpwatch commands only.\n\n`deploy-faillock-admin.sh` default case: `--check`, deploy, --revert. Good.\n\n`faillock.conf` group parsing `cut -d: -f4`. Good.\n\n`enroll.lock` missing. Group missing. Good.\n\n`pam_faillock` active but user lockable. Good.\n\nBDE no other users and no guests. \"Permanent lock out other users\" skipped as no targets. Good.\n\nArpwatch collector''s correct flags and units not installed. We can describe.\n\n`arpwatch-spoof-alert.sh` is obsolete for installed version but still in repo; not used by corrected service. The scanner is intended replacement. In next move, remove it or leave compatibility? The current scanner does its own notification; no need old hook. Installer likely doesn''t reference old hook after unit update? It still has HOOK prereq and references it! Current installer still requires and installs old unit, and old unit no longer uses hook. Must update. Mention.\n\n`install-arpwatch-spoof.sh` still uses DB=arpwatch.dat and HOOK, so broken relative new architecture. It needs rewrite. Good.\n\nThe live `/etc/systemd/system/arpwatch-spoof.service` has old command and is enabled. Could give exact broken command:\n`/usr/sbin/arpwatch -q -u livings -c /var/lib/arpwatch/arpwatch.dat -a /home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/arpwatch-spoof-alert.sh wlo1`\nCorrect intended:\n`/usr/sbin/arpwatch -F -i wlo1 -f /var/lib/arpwatch/arp.dat -s -q -N -z`\nThis is crucial. Include.\n\nPotential service command lacks root user so root by default. Fine.\n\nThe user wants local security. Could mention no other machine audit. Good.\n\nDo we need include Windows Electron cross-build selected? Prior says selected but unstarted. Include as deferred maybe: \"A Windows Electron `.exe` cross-build remains selected.\" But if objective preserve. Next move after security. Good.\n\n`firewalld` currently active and workstation zone. Earlier prior says inactive, corrected. We should state active. `sshd` remains inactive.\n\n`shield-kitty-watch.service` active. `arpwatch` alert environment must use `/run/user/1000/bus`; known. New scanner service currently lacks this. Mention.\n\nOne concern: The conversation used buildlog `warn` invalid, later re-logged note. No need.\n\nPotential output length desired 5, summary can be moderately detailed. Need terse bullets. Exact Markdown.\n\nLet''s draft:\n\n## Objective\n- Harden local Garuda host with safe admin-only PAM behavior, 24-hour bans, working spoof detection; resume void-bin build later.\n- BDE no install unless explicitly re-audited.\n\nImportant:\n- Manual sudo.\n- network.\n- fail2ban.\n- BDE and users.\n- arpwatch semantics.\n- no auto-ban.\n- no machine access.\n- notifications.\n- git perhaps.\n\nWork completed bullets.\n\nFor arpwatch completed, careful not say whole thing complete. \"Initial artifacts and sudo/session fixes committed, but integration superseded by version mismatch.\" Good.\n\nTesting:\n- 7/7 old hook classification passed.\n- scanner direct synthetic test produces alert and dedupe; full suite needs rerun after distinct-MAC fix.\n- first scanner tests found same MAC case bug fixed, but subsequent batch test confusing; direct xtrace verified. State active.\n\nFail2ban:\n- live only default, sshd, recidive. `ignoreip` broad. There is no sudo jail? Mention perhaps not needed. `sshd` jail inert.\n- Firewalld active means action enforceable.\n- recidive config sync.\n- docs fixed.\n\nBDE:\n- commit 359. `BDE_FAILMODE` default open and no pam_deny. Not installed. Should note no `snapper rollback` implementation found; snapper cleanup timer active. Maybe Important.\n\nSeeding:\n- 161/161? Maybe state latest report, not fully validated. Completed source fetch? We could move seeding fetch to completed with caveat. \"Latest run reported 161 ok, 0 fail and 3.0G; process still appeared active.\" Active final verification. Electron build unstarted in Active/Blocked.\n\nGit remotes/gh maybe no longer current objective but carry. In Blocked:\n- `gh` absent; `zen-hardening`, `buildlog`, `shield-kitty` no remotes.\nCould mention if future push.\n\nNext:\n1. `sudo systemctl disable --now arpwatch-spoof.service` to stop loop.\n2. Finish files: delete/retire old hook, correct installer paths/datafile, install scanner services/timer, fix scan service user/session, tests, commit, give user deploy commands.\n3. Run `faillock` deployment? User chose. They need run `sudo ...`. Could be next after arpwatch. But next move has two items max. We can combine admin deployment and void in second? Template allows any numbered count but likely 2. We can have 3 if needed; template says next action if known. Use 3 perhaps. But expected exact structure not number count. Fine.\n- Item 1 stop.\n- Item 2 finalize and deploy arpwatch.\n- Item 3 deploy faillock then resume build. Better separate? Maybe 3.\nUser currently troubleshooting arpwatch, immediate.\n\nRelevant files include:\n- arpwatch files.\n- live unit.\n- faillock.\n- fail2ban.\n- bde.\n- seed.\n- shield kitty.\n- buildlog.\nMaybe 12 bullets.\n\nNeed not mention `/tmp/arpT2` transient test dirs? They likely still exist because cleanup not after new tests. Could include under active? They are temporary. No need, but if next agent wants inspect logs, `/tmp/arpT2/real.dat`, `/tmp/arpT2/scan.log` exist. Not important.\n\nOne question: The old service is currently restart-looping; perhaps systemd may still be in loop as summary. Yes.\n\n\"arpwatch package installed\" resolved blocker. Good.\n\nOne nuance: BDE service old could have been installed? No. `find no BDE units`. Code only. Good.\n\nOne nuance: `firewalld` active despite prior. Good.\n\nOne nuance: `sshd inactive` and no :22. Good.\n\nOne nuance: \"only human login account\" vs system accounts. Include.\n\nOne nuance: user asked \"all new lock mechanisms only enroll and recognize me as admin no other users on any other machines ... guests banned.\" We can say no other human accounts or remote machines. We skipped permanent ban and guest ban because no targets. Fail2ban remains IP bans.\n\nOne nuance: \"admin exemption not deployed\" because user chose but assistant couldn''t sudo. User did later run arpwatch sudo, could now run faillock. Good.\n\nPotential risk: `admin_group` absent live. Good.\n\nPotential exact `pam_faillock` recovery: `sudo faillock --user livings --reset`. Include Important.\n\nPotential permanent `unlock_time=0` not enabled. Good.\n\nPotential no need \"Great Vibes\" but maybe carry original workstream. We can include Completed: safe Great Vibes gating and Blood Build. But summary focus might need preserve all. System explicitly says carry forward objectives, constraints, user directives, decisions, and parallel workstreams. The original Great Vibes was completed, no need if finished and no longer needed. It says drop only what is finished and no longer needed. It is finished, so can drop. Shield notifications still relevant to alerts. Keep.\n\nVoid source is unfinished, carry.\n\nOriginal remote repos no remote, unfinished. Keep perhaps blocked.\n\nCould mention `firewalld` was manually enabled after prior? No.\n\nNow ensure no claims unsupported:\n- \"BDE patrol benign\" from conversation: hashes config and writes logs. Could state.\n- \"No snapper rollback found\" yes.\n- `snapper-cleanup.timer` live root config. Good.\n\nArpwatch direct test:\n- `arpwatch-spoof-scan.sh` with bash -x after synthetic data shows alert. It writes to temp log and count.py. Good.\n- 7 old hook tests pass after session fix.\n- Full scanner suite had one bug fixed but batch result unreliable; we can say \"needs clean full rerun\" active.\n\nPotential issue in corrected `arpwatch-spoof.service`: `ProtectSystem` not set, no issue. It doesn''t set `User`; root. It doesn''t precreate data. Good.\n- scan timer `Requires=arpwatch-spoof.service` can cause timer trigger to start collector; okay.\n- scan service `After`, not `Requires`; timer requires.\n- scanner''s `IGNORE_CIDRS` default includes fe80:: but data IPv4 only. harmless.\n- state write. Fine.\n- environment issue. Add.\n\nShould we say installed old unit exact command? It is known from repo at install time. Yes.\n\nLet''s craft with concise bullets, not paragraphs.\n\nNeed not output anything else. Use exact headings. Ensure all sections.\n\nLet''s formulate detailed yet terse.\n\nPotential final:\n\n## Objective\n- Complete local security hardening: make `livings` sole `pam_faillock` admin, retain exactly 24h network bans, and replace broken arpwatch with working spoof detection without self-lockout.\n- Later resume deferred `void-bin`/Windows Electron cross-build.\n\n## Important Details\n...\nMaybe 12 bullets, okay.\n\nWork Completed:\nBDE, faillock prep, fail2ban, arpwatch initial, seed, notifications.\n\nActive:\nArpwatch, faillock deployment, ignoreip, void.\n\nBlocked:\nsudo, subnet, recidive log, gh, build.\n\nNeed not say \"blocked\" for code that can be fixed. But root user needed.\n\nOne concern: The user has just run arpwatch install and service is broken. Immediate next move should perhaps tell them to stop. In summary, no direct commands to user? It''s okay, but next agent can. Include exact command in Next Move.\n\nLet''s include live state:\n- Installed `arpwatch` 3.9.\n- Installed and enabled old service in restart loop, `NRestarts=6`.\n- Package installation resolved old blocker.\n- Old unit not replaced with repo rewrite.\n\nInstaller rewrite:\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/install-arpwatch-spoof.sh` still uses `DB=/var/lib/arpwatch/arpwatch.dat`, requires old hook, installs only collector. It needs update to use `arp.dat`, create empty file, install scan service+timer, remove old hook dependency. Good.\n\nSession user:\n- scan service runs root by default and `bootstrap_session_env` would seek `/run/user/0`; should instead set `User=livings` with read access to data or explicit user1000 bus. This wasn''t explicitly caught, but crucial. Include under Active.\n- alert schema correct.\n\nPotential tests after install:\n`systemd-analyze verify /etc/systemd/system/...`; `fail2ban-client` etc. Not needed.\n\nNext:\n1. user command stop.\n2. code fixes/test/commit/install.\n3. faillock and void.\n\nRelevant files:\n- all.\n\nLet''s ensure no false statement \"only login-capable account\" root can login; write only non-root. User''s goal recognizes livings; root is emergency.\n\nLet''s mention `admin_group` is absent, group absent, lock absent. Good.\n\nRemote other machines inaccessible. Good.\n\nOne more thing: user asked all new lock mechanisms to lock other users permanently, then changed to only 1 day. We skip permanent user lock. Good.\n\nOne more thing: \"only build a 1 day lockout time for anything spoofing or remote access\" but arpwatch no auto-ban by design. User''s request may not fully satisfied. Need state clearly in Active/Important: spoof detector alerts only, not bans, due false positives. The user later said build local security broadly; assistant made design decision. A future agent should not claim 24h ban for spoofing. Keep.\n\nOne-day fail2ban only auth attempts and recidive. System spoofing not banned. Good.\n\nPotential source seed data:\n- latest seeder report 161 ok, 0 warn, 0 defer, 0 fail, 3.0G, but pgrep said running. Could say fetched state reported complete but final process state unresolved. This is contradictory. Put Active final verification. Maybe prior says 161/163 entries. We can preserve both: \"Seed log last showed 161 ok / 0 fail; assistant interpreted 161/161 as complete, but process still appeared alive and two-entry discrepancy from earlier handoff was not reconciled.\" This is precise but maybe too much. Good.\n\nNow 