INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df986042001WqpJJUlO57VqTW','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',4696,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0df98231d001GZrbjFlgLnXWp3","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0df96c10a001rhCUrc58JG5GHG","type":"text","text":"## Objective\n- Finish local host security: safely deploy `livings` as the sole `pam_faillock` admin exemption, retain 24-hour fail2ban bans, and replace the broken arpwatch integration with working spoof detection.\n- Resume the deferred `void-bin`/Windows Electron cross-build after security work stabilizes.\n\n## Important Details\n- Host is Garuda Linux/Arch; `livings` is uid 1000 and the only non-root login-capable human account. Root is the only uid-0 account.\n- Agent has no passwordless sudo; privileged commands must be run by the user.\n- Only this host is accessible; no other machines or human users exist here to lock or ban.\n- User chose: deploy the faillock admin exemption, but do not enable permanent `unlock_time = 0`.\n- Network is a large DHCP `/8`: host `10.197.250.246/8`, gateway `10.128.128.128`.\n- Fail2ban’s `ignoreip` includes all `10.0.0.0/8`, exempting 16,777,216 addresses. Do not narrow it without the real broadcast domain; guessing could ban unrelated hosts.\n- Firewalld is active, `workstation` exists, and `firewallcmd-rich-rules` can enforce bans.\n- `sshd` is inactive and nothing listens on port 22, so its jail is inert.\n- KDE Connect is a user-session autostart process, but firewalld blocks `1716/tcp`, `1716/udp`, and `5353/udp`; the earlier LAN-exposure claim was incorrect.\n- Installed `arpwatch` is version 3.9, whose valid syntax is:\n  `[-CdFNpqsvzZ] [-D arpdir] [-f datafile] [-i interface] ...`\n  It has no `-a`, `-u`, or `-c` options.\n- ARP spoof detection intentionally must not auto-ban: DHCP address reuse and per-SSID MAC randomization resemble spoofing and would cause harmful 24-hour bans.\n- Root scripts must resolve user paths through `SUDO_USER`, not `$HOME`; sudo changes `HOME` to `/root`.\n- System services need `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/1000` and `DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS=unix:path=/run/user/1000/bus` for Shield Kitty notifications.\n- Shield Kitty payload schema is `events: [{\"label\": ..., \"count\": ..., \"sample\": ...}]`; plain strings cause `AttributeError`.\n- BDE remains deliberately not installed. No `snapper rollback` path was found; only `snapper-cleanup.timer` with a `root` config is active.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Audited and fixed BDE hardlock; commit `359cc45`:\n  - Removed unconditional `pam_deny.so`.\n  - Added fail-open daemon handling and target-user socket resolution.\n  - Made `sshd` opt-in.\n  - Added installer backups and `--dry-run`.\n  - Verified no daemon gives exit 0 in open mode and exit 1 in closed mode.\n  - Nothing installed.\n- Prepared safe faillock deployment; commit `819c363`:\n  - Fixed malformed `audit = silent` to separate bare flags.\n  - Fixed group parsing with `cut -d: -f4`.\n  - Added `deploy-faillock-admin.sh` with `--check`, deploy, and `--revert`.\n  - Enforces backup → group creation → enrollment → database verification → config install → enrollment lock.\n  - Not deployed; `shield-admin` and `/etc/shield-kitty/enroll.lock` are still absent.\n- Confirmed fail2ban 24-hour policy is already live:\n  - `/etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty.conf` has `bantime = 86400`.\n  - User confirmed `recidive enabled = true` was deliberate.\n  - Repo updated to match live; commit `c897508`.\n  - `fail2ban-client -t` passed.\n- Corrected stale permanent-ban documentation; commit `89506fc`.\n- Built initial arpwatch alert artifacts; commit `3a65f5e`.\n- Fixed sudo `$HOME` and notification-session bugs; commit `b39490a`:\n  - Installer resolves `SUDO_USER`.\n  - Hook path derives from `BASH_SOURCE`.\n  - User bus and Wayland environment are reconstructed.\n  - Old hook classification tests passed 7/7.\n- Corrected KDE Connect exposure assessment and logged it.\n- Shield Kitty notifications remain enabled and active.\n- Latest seed report showed `161 ok`, `0 warn`, `0 DEFER`, `0 FAIL`, approximately `3.0G`; the seeder process still appeared alive despite printing completion.\n\n### Active\n- Live `/etc/systemd/system/arpwatch-spoof.service` is installed, enabled, and in a restart loop; last observed `NRestarts=6`.\n- Broken live command still uses unsupported flags:\n  `/usr/sbin/arpwatch -q -u livings -c /var/lib/arpwatch/arpwatch.dat -a /home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/arpwatch-spoof-alert.sh wlo1`\n- Repo collector unit has been rewritten toward:\n  `/usr/sbin/arpwatch -F -i wlo1 -f /var/lib/arpwatch/arp.dat -s -q -N -z`\n  but has not been committed or reinstalled.\n- New uncommitted scanner design:\n  - `arpwatch-spoof-scan.sh`\n  - `arpwatch-spoof-scan.service`\n  - `arpwatch-spoof-scan.timer`\n- Scanner detects one IP claimed by multiple distinct MACs and deduplicates alerts through a state file.\n- A direct synthetic scanner test successfully produced a spoof alert; a clean full regression suite still needs rerunning.\n- `install-arpwatch-spoof.sh` still references the obsolete hook, uses `arpwatch.dat`, does not precreate the required empty `arp.dat`, and does not install the scanner service/timer.\n- New scan service currently runs as root without a correct user-bus environment; it would derive `/run/user/0` unless fixed.\n- Faillock admin exemption remains prepared but not deployed.\n- Fail2ban same-network coverage remains unresolved because `10.0.0.0/8` is ignored.\n- `void-bin`/`electron34` compile remains unstarted.\n\n### Blocked\n- Stopping the broken service and replacing `/etc` units requires the user’s sudo password.\n- Live arpwatch collection and final notification delivery require privileged installation.\n- Fail2ban recidive runtime output cannot be inspected unprivileged because `/var/log/fail2ban.log` is `root:root 0600`.\n- Safe fail2ban `ignoreip` narrowing requires the actual network broadcast domain.\n- `gh` remains absent; `zen-hardening`, `buildlog`, and `shield-kitty` still lack remotes.\n- Full `void-bin` build remains a long Electron/Chromium compile.\n\n## Next Move\n1. Stop the restart loop: `sudo systemctl disable --now arpwatch-spoof.service`.\n2. Finish the arpwatch 3.9 migration: precreate `/var/lib/arpwatch/arp.dat`, install collector plus scanner service/timer, retire the obsolete hook dependency, set the scanner to `livings` or explicitly target `/run/user/1000`, run the full synthetic suite and `systemd-analyze verify`, commit, then provide dry-run/install commands.\n3. After arpwatch is stable, deploy with `sudo ~/Projects/zen-hardening/deploy-faillock-admin.sh`, verify with `sudo faillock --user livings`, and later resolve `ignoreip` only after obtaining the true broadcast domain.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/arpwatch-spoof.service`: corrected collector-unit draft, not yet committed or installed.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/arpwatch-spoof-scan.sh`: new datafile scanner, not yet committed.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/arpwatch-spoof-scan.service`: new scanner oneshot unit with unresolved user/session configuration.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/arpwatch-spoof-scan.timer`: new two-minute scan timer.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/arpwatch-spoof-alert.sh`: obsolete exec-hook implementation for arpwatch 3.9.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/install-arpwatch-spoof.sh`: still based on the obsolete architecture and needs rewrite.\n- `/etc/systemd/system/arpwatch-spoof.service`: live broken/restarting unit.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/deploy-faillock-admin.sh`: prepared safe faillock deployment.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/faillock.conf`: corrected admin-group and logging configuration.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/enroll-admin.sh`: manages `shield-admin` membership and enrollment lock.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/shield-kitty-fail2ban.local`: repo source matching live recidive state.\n- `/etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty.conf`: live 24-hour fail2ban configuration.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/bde-security-biometrics/pam/modules/bde-auth`: fixed BDE PAM helper.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/bde-security-biometrics/hardlock/install-hardlock.sh`: fixed but uninstalled BDE installer.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/shield-kitty/shield-kitty-alert.py`: notification implementation and payload schema.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/buildlog/logs/buildlog.md`: durable security audit journal.\n- `/home/livings/.cache/paru/seed.log`: latest Electron source-seeding status.\n- `/home/livings/.cache/paru/clone/electron34/PKGBUILD`: unstarted `void-bin` build definition.","time":{"start":1790457684765,"end":1790457700417}},"time":1790457700417}');
