INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0df9f15ea001k0ba8Ef814SSuc','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',10321,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0df9f0521001Bvq5ppYf1FZayg","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0df9eff63001xm5Me6jMcKkw2X","type":"text","text":"`cfc20b1` pushed.\n\nNow run these four, in order:\n\n```bash\n# 1. audit helpers (trailing-comma fix still unverified)\nsudo bash /home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/install-audit-readonly.sh\n\n# 2. Shield Kitty units — the reboot-persistence fix\nsudo bash /home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/install-shield-kitty-units.sh\n\n# 3. sudoers repair — classifies before it changes anything\nsudo bash /home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/fix-sudoers-permissions.sh\n```\n\nStep 3 prints the contents of anything it quarantines, so paste me that output.\n\n## Why I''m not just chmod-ing it\n\n`chmod 0440 /etc/sudoers.d/opencode` would silence the warning *and* make sudo start honouring the file. If an agent wrote `NOPASSWD` into it, that command would activate passwordless root and delete the evidence in the same step. So the script:\n\n- Strips group/other **write** bits first — a writable sudoers file is a live root escalation and outranks everything else\n- Activates only files whose entire content is `Defaults` lines (the stock `editor`, `insults`, `pwfeedback`)\n- Moves anything containing `NOPASSWD`, an `ALL=(...) ALL` grant, or anything unrecognised to `/root/sudoers-quarantine-<timestamp>/` at `0600`, out of `/etc/sudoers.d`\n- Deletes nothing — prints original contents and how to restore\n\nGiven your baseline explicitly avoids blanket `NOPASSWD`, I''d rather it end up quarantined and reviewable than active.\n\n## After those three\n\nNothing found so far should block your reboot. Then re-run `sudo bash ~/Projects/zen-hardening/bootstrap.sh` for a final end-state check, and confirm Shield Kitty came back with:\n\n```bash\nsystemctl --user is-active shield-kitty-watch.service evidence-seal.timer\n```\n\nTwo items still genuinely open, neither boot-related: **Tor Browser isn''t installed** (Tor runs with no client, so it provides no anonymity yet), and **`machine-id` is still unique** — I won''t change that without you deciding, since it breaks services that bind to it.","time":{"start":1790458135841,"end":1790458140138}},"time":1790458140138}');
