INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0dfa0f051001DX7GrSmoxPt493','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',10335,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0dfa0e654001mYCeAyXzOEa9nf","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0dfa0e0e8001KtKFwURcnKzF5C","type":"reasoning","text":"The user ran something and said \"0 checks failed\" — presumably the bootstrap. But which of the three commands did they run? They said \"0 checks failed\" which is the bootstrap output. But I asked for three commands. They may have only run the bootstrap.\n\nI need to verify the actual state, not assume. Especially:\n1. Did the audit helpers get installed? (verify)\n2. Did Shield Kitty units get installed? (verify)\n3. Did the sudoers fix run? (verify — check visudo -c is clean)\n\nAnd re-verify the security state after those changes.\n\nThe lesson all session: verify, don''t assume. \"0 checks failed\" has already lied once (the MAC).\n\nLet me check all of it.\n\nLet me check:\n- audit-nft works passwordless\n- shield-kitty units installed/enabled/active\n- visudo -c clean\n- the overall security state\n- MAC still randomized\n- firewall still strict\n\nLet me run comprehensive verification.","time":{"start":1790458259028,"end":1790458261585}},"time":1790458261585}');
