INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0dfa35b2000129GQaPGtEn76MX','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',5100,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0dfa33e4d001T286GawwsFR4OP","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0dfa338940014B87cOdNLm1TPj","type":"reasoning","text":"Confirmed. SIGHUP forces an immediate update. And note the default arpdir is `/usr/local/arpwatch` per FILES, but the -D description said `/usr/local/arpwatch` too (the chdir warning said /usr/arpwatch, so this build''s compiled default is /usr/arpwatch). The package ships ethercodes.dat in /var/lib/arpwatch, so we should pass `-D /var/lib/arpwatch` so it finds ethercodes.dat for vendor lookup. That''s a real improvement — currently arpwatch can''t find ethercodes.dat, so MAC vendor names won''t resolve in reports.\n\nNow let me implement the design change:\n1. Collector: add `-P /run/arpwatch-spoof.pid` and `-D /var/lib/arpwatch` (so ethercodes.dat is found)\n2. Scan unit: run as root, explicit livings bus env, ExecStartPre sends SIGHUP to force a fresh flush\n3. Timer stays 2 min — now actually meaningful\n\nLet me implement, verify the flags parse, then have the user test.\n\nLet me do the edits.\n\nFor the HUP, in the scan unit:\n```\nExecStartPre=/bin/sh -c ''kill -HUP \"$(cat /run/arpwatch-spoof.pid)\" 2>/dev/null || true''\n```\nBut the collector writes the pidfile; need to make sure arpwatch -P creates it. Yes.\n\nAlso, after HUP, arpwatch needs a moment to write. Add a short sleep:\n```\nExecStartPre=/bin/sh -c ''kill -HUP \"$(cat /run/arpwatch-spoof.pid)\" 2>/dev/null; sleep 1''\n```\n\nHmm, careful: with `set -e` not relevant in sh -c. If kill fails, sh returns nonzero? `kill ... 2>/dev/null; sleep 1` → exit status of sleep = 0. Good.\n\nBut if the pidfile doesn''t exist, `cat` fails, kill gets empty arg → error, but `;` continues to sleep. Fine.\n\nLet me also make sure the scan unit ordering: After=arpwatch-spoof.service, and Requires so it pulls the collector up.\n\nAlso: running the scan as root again — I need to be careful that the state file writes still work (root, fine) and that the alert uses the explicit bus env.\n\nLet me revert the User=livings in the scan unit and instead pass explicit env. Let me rewrite the unit.\n\nAlso update the installer: the state file ownership comment; and ARPWATCH_ARGS to include -P and -D.\n\nLet me implement all of it.\n\nLet me write the files.\n\nAlso: the parse-check probes with its own args; I should include -P and -D in the probe but with temp paths to avoid clobbering. Careful: -P /run/... as root would write the real pidfile. Let me use a temp pidfile in the probe.\n\nLet me restructure the probe to use temp -P and -D? -D must be a real dir with ethercodes.dat for vendor lookup, but the probe only checks flag parsing, and arpwatch chdir''s to it. If it doesn''t exist it just warns. For the probe I''ll use the real /var/lib/arpwatch (exists) and a temp pidfile.\n\nLet me implement.","time":{"start":1790458412621,"end":1790458420000}},"time":1790458420000}');
