INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0dfa3dd63001K5oa9UBdmBccS2','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',5209,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0dfa3d728001uWs3M5B1ZM293j","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0dfa3d1b5001ECyz8rI3EWpWdF","type":"reasoning","text":"Line 182: `[ -f \"$ALERT\" ]` — it requires ALERT to be a FILE, then runs `python3 \"$ALERT\"`. So it must be a Python script, not a bash script. My test used a bash script → python3 failed to parse it → but the error was captured into `out` and... `|| log \"alert delivery failed\"`. python3 on a bash script with `printf ''%s\\n'' \"$1\" >> ...` — actually `printf ''%s\\n'' \"$1\" >> /tmp/flow.alert` is not valid Python → SyntaxError → python3 exits nonzero → log \"alert delivery failed\".\n\nLet me check the log to confirm. Then re-test with a Python alert script.\n\nSo the contract is: BDE_ALERT must be a Python script. That''s fine — the real one is shield-kitty-alert.py. My test was wrong again.\n\nLet me re-test with a proper Python script.","time":{"start":1790458451752,"end":1790458453346}},"time":1790458453346}');
