INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0dfa42386001Zyd07i9BwyELMi','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',5245,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0dfa41c55001dJ6kOL6KCkeNDZ","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0dfa40d97001fjpoDI9Djz4ntO","type":"tool","callID":"call_function_vse16iap6x6b_1","tool":"bash","state":{"status":"running","input":{"command":"cd ~/Projects/buildlog\nbuildlog fix \"arp.dat stayed at 0 entries while arpwatch-spoof showed ''active (running)''. Root cause from SIGNALS in arpwatch(8): ''arpwatch updates arp.dat once every 15 minutes. The SIGHUP signal causes it to update immediately.'' So the 2-min scan timer re-read the same stale file 7x, and an empty datafile is indistinguishable from a healthy one in systemctl status. The 101-byte arp.dat- is arpwatch''s in-progress DB, not corruption. Fix: scan unit now SIGHUPs the collector (needs CAP_KILL against root) before reading, via a new -P /run/arpwatch-spoof.pid rather than pidof. Scan unit is root again BUT the session bus is now pinned to /run/user/1000 explicitly instead of derived from uid, which is what silently broke notifications before. Also added -D /var/lib/arpwatch: this build''s compiled-in arpdir /usr/arpwatch does not exist, so arpwatch never found ethercodes.dat (shipped in /var/lib/arpwatch) and MAC vendor names were silently missing from all reports. commit 706c458\" 2>&1 | tail -1"},"metadata":{"output":""},"time":{"start":1790458471302}}},"time":1790458471302}');
