INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0dfa6febc002I4XO2bbVrwyZYl','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',10629,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0dfa6ea5a001shUmf8Cnmdo7YS","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0dfa6e1710015ybd3h6ur3ejP1","type":"reasoning","text":"The user ran `sudo -l` and got \"Sorry, user livings may not run sudo on zero.\" — so the restore didn''t work, or pkexec didn''t run.\n\nI need to know whether the pkexec command succeeded. The user didn''t paste the pkexec output. They just ran `sudo -l`.\n\nSo either:\n1. pkexec didn''t run / failed / they cancelled the dialog\n2. pkexec ran but failed\n\nLet me ask for the pkexec output, or better, let me check the current state of /etc/sudoers.d — I can''t read it (permission denied on the dir).\n\nBut I can check whether the file exists via pkexec? No, that needs auth too.\n\nLet me think about what I can verify unprivileged:\n- `sudo -l` fails → no grant.\n- I can check if /etc/sudoers.d/10-installer exists? The dir is 0750 root:root, so I can''t stat files inside.\n\nActually `stat /etc/sudoers.d/10-installer` gave \"Permission denied\" earlier for opencode. So I can''t check.\n\nSo I need the user to run the pkexec command and paste output. Let me be very clear and simple — maybe break it into smaller steps so failure is diagnosable.\n\nLet me give a simpler, single-purpose pkexec command and ask for its output. Keep it dead simple to reduce the chance of quoting problems.\n\nSimplest possible:\n```\npkexec cp /root/sudoers-quarantine-20260926-143446/10-installer /etc/sudoers.d/10-installer\n```\nThat''s one simple command, no nested quoting. Then:\n```\npkexec chmod 0440 /etc/sudoers.d/10-installer\n```\nThen check.\n\nEven simpler and most robust — use `pkexec sh -c` with a here-doc? No, keep it minimal.\n\nLet me do it step by step with single commands to isolate any failure.\n\nStep 1: does the quarantine file exist? Use pkexec to check and report:\n```\npkexec ls -l /root/sudoers-quarantine-20260926-143446/\n```\nThat both tests pkexec AND shows the quarantine contents. Good first step — it verifies pkexec works at all.\n\nThen restore.\n\nLet me give that as step 1 and ask for output. That''s the right diagnostic: confirm pkexec works before attempting the fix.\n\nLet me keep it tight.","time":{"start":1790458653274,"end":1790458658492}},"time":1790458658492}');
