INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0dfb0de5d001zMRk3wGuY32WLY','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',5715,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0dfb0d70d001l8rWM1EF32PKC4","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0dfb0cee90013ufRk6nM9kvR49","type":"reasoning","text":"So delivery logs only appear if there''s output OR a nonzero rc. A successful `shield-kitty-alert.py` run that prints nothing and exits 0 produces NO log line. That''s by design (quiet on success) but it means **I cannot tell from the log whether the notification was delivered**. That''s a real observability gap — the same class of \"silently broken\" bug I''ve been fixing.\n\nGiven my whole session has been about silent failures (root bus, missing -q, etc.), I should add positive delivery confirmation. Let me check what shield-kitty-alert.py outputs on success — if it prints nothing, add a log line on success too.\n\nLet me test shield-kitty-alert.py directly to see.\n\nLet me run it and see stdout/rc.\n\nThat''s the decisive check: does the notifier work at all right now?\n\nLet me test.","time":{"start":1790459303693,"end":1790459305565}},"time":1790459305565}');
