d could never alert at all. State now holds only what is\nactually being reported.\n\nInstaller: the probe used two separate mktemp -u calls, so only the datafile''s\ndirectory was cleaned up -- under root, where the probe really runs, arpwatch\nwrote the pidfile and orphaned a directory per install. Now one mktemp -d\nshared by both paths (-u also races, since it only prints a name).\n\nInstaller: units hardcode /run/user/1000 for the session bus while the\ninstaller carefully resolved SUDO_USER for the home path, so it was user-aware\nin one place and hardcoded in another. Both are now derived and rewritten.\n\nVerified 16/16 including the two cases that were broken: DHCP reassignment\n(now silent) and un-ignoring a previously ignored address (now alerts). All\nscripts parse, all three units pass systemd-analyze verify, no temp-dir leak,\nidentity rewriting checked against a simulated second user, and the notify path\nconfirmed live via --test-notify.\"\ngit log --oneline | head -1"},"metadata":{"output":""},"time":{"start":1790459323179}}},"time":1790459323185}');
INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0dfb12333001VM7pjMhCsR231v','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',5772,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","part":{"id":"prt_0dfb10e5e001cc7908NILiL2Qm","sessionID":"ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk","messageID":"msg_0dfb1092d001ri7j7FO6OVk6at","type":"text","text":"Notification path confirmed working. Let me commit the audit fixes:","time":{"start":1790459317854,"end":1790459323187}},"time":1790459323187}');
