s zen-hardening, shield-kitty, forensics, buildlog. User chose \"Document relationship\", but has this been done? No. Active.\n   - canonical? User selected document relationship, not choose. Need state both `hermes-security-scripts` and lifsea exist, overlap/drift risk, documentation pending. Prior user asked private repos; all said private. Need not overdo.\n   - Agents still active. User authorized specific fixes. Need wait for quiet before final integration, push only files. Current zen-hardening repo has dirty modifications by agents plus our untracked/changed files. `/tmp/opencode/hss` has commits.\n12. Tor browser remains not installed. User selected not installed. Prior said maybe \"Tor browser not installed\" and active next. Still open.\n13. GitHub token shred: done, server revocation unconfirmed. SSH remote works. Need mention.\n14. Full reboot: user plans manually after audit. Current boot appears go. Need still not yet rebooted. Need final pre-reboot check after agents finish, update state. Boot test cannot actual without reboot. \"boot test ensure system boot\" read-only completed; manual reboot pending.\n15. Firewall zone semantics: latest table shows target default and final reject. Current summary should state strict. `kdeconnectd`, mDNS bound globally but blocked by firewall. Maybe network listener 1716, 5353 by design.\n16. fail2ban:\n   - two jails `recidive, sshd`, active.\n   - source current recidive true, not false as prior summary. Conversation wins.\n   - /var/log/fail2ban.log exists, so true appropriate.\n   - live config true. Bootstrap robustly toggles based on log.\n   - End-to-end ban test using 192.0.2.66 still not run. This is active from prior.\n   - `fail2ban-client` direct needs root, wrappers.\n   - no recent errors.\n17. systemd drop-in for PartOf firewalld still not created. Bootstrap works around by stop/restart; active from prior.\n18. set-home interface fixed now, contrary prior active. It discovers wlo1. Completed.\n19. bootstrap `bootstrap.sh` and identity script:\n   - `bootstrap.sh` syntax valid and ran 0 failures after MAC active. It now includes MAC hard check.\n   - Maybe after agent edits, need rerun due active work. But live state verified.\n   - `set-anon-identity.sh` modern detection uses `always`, older mode random. MAC succeeded.\n20. `recidive` bootstrap logic:\n   - source enabled true due deliberate request. bootstrap actively set false if log absent. Good.\n21. SDDM etc still open structural.\n22. machine-id, DMI, Ethernet MAC still open decisions.\n23. \"bootstrap session env for notify\" commit b39490a etc by other agent. Not necessarily.\n24. `arpwatch-spoof-alert.sh` uncommitted at one point; other agents active. Need avoid touching. New repos etc.\n\nNeed output exact structure only. \"Important Details\" should include critical constraints and facts. \"Completed\" can be many bullets but terse. \"Active\" current. \"Blocked\". \"Next Move\" immediate likely:\n1. Deploy updated audit-fail2ban wrapper (source parser fixed) and run root diagnostics. Perhaps `sudo bash .../install-audit-readonly.sh`, then `sudo audit-fail2ban`, `sudo audit-smart` (nvme-cli absent). But the user asked continue after recovery. The latest conversation ended at test parser issue, no response. We need summary for next agent, so immediate action should be fix wrapper test/deploy and finish remaining audit.\n2. Wait for other agents/repo activity quiet, reconcile/push latest files (including audit-fail2ban parser, RECOVER already pushed) and document lifsea relationship. Do not rerun `fix-sudoers-permissions.sh`.\n3. run final system audit/reverify no reboot blockers; perhaps install nvme-cli to get SMART? User asked full diagnostics. `nvme-cli` absent. We can use sysfs fallback or install package after sudo. Need decide immediate. We can mention active: NVMe SMART unavailable because `nvme: command not found`; install `nvme-cli` only with user approval or use `smartctl` if installed. But user asked full diagnostics, likely install is acceptable? Not yet. We can say next use `nvme smart-log` after installing `nvme-cli`, but avoid package change without user? User did say get everything working, root now restored. However no need now perhaps.\n4. end-to-end fail2ban test and systemd drop-in, Tor browser. But user''s immediate request is reboot readiness. Prior tasks remain.\n5. Before manual reboot: verify sudo, audit helpers, Shield Kitty, no lock, no failed, run bootstrap. Then user reboot and postboot test.\n6. After reboot check `systemctl --user ...`, firewall, Tor, MAC.\n\nNeed mention exact error and fix for `pkexec` account maybe not needed in current state but relevant caution: any future pkexec scripts should resolve `PKEXEC_UID`; `RECOVER-SUDO.sh` now does. Important detail.\n\nNeed perhaps mention current date? 2026-09-26 from logs. Not necessary.\n\nLet''s ensure \"same language as conversation\" English.\n\nNeed maybe not include markdown tables due terse bullets.\n\nWe need preserve all objectives from prior including remaining ecosystem work? The user asked summary combining objectives, so important details and active should carry unreviewed tools, ISO/emulator work. But current immediate objective is core stack/audit/reboot. The prior says continue remaining requested ecosystem only after core verified. We need retain them, perhaps one bullet in Active with list. But desired summary not overly huge? Yet user says carry everything not finished. Must include remaining tasks. Include major blockers.\n\nLet''s build detailed but terse.\n\nObjective:\n- Finish verified Garuda hardening/anonymity/rebuild stack, resolve audit/reboot blockers, push private repos; only then remaining Void/security/ISO/emulator tasks.\nOne or two sentences.\n\nImportant Details:\n- user env, shell, no blanket NOPASSWD.\n- design constraints firewalld, Tor, machine-id, SDDM, source recidive correction.\n- agent concurrency, repo canonical overlap.\n- verification