es and maybe not yet.\nCould mention `zen-hardening` active dirty and other agents, do not overwrite.\n\nBlocked:\n- root no longer blocked; interactive sudo works. Root audit wrappers work. Don''t say root blocked.\n- Tor browser package install now possible but pending user command? We could not install because no root. Now sudo restored, but still active.\n- machine ID decision.\n- SDDM.\n- transparent Tor.\n- secure home network.\n- ISO/emulator constraints.\n- `nvme-cli` absent.\n- \"Hermes separate no channel\" maybe constraint. They asked have Hermes deploy, but assistant cannot dispatch. We can state no direct Hermes channel; work direct.\n- `lifsea` agents still active.\n\nNext Move:\n1. Immediate: fix/deploy `audit-fail2ban` wrapper. Since source edit done but not installed. The raw test was empty because direct `sudo -n fail2ban-client` isn''t whitelisted; test should use `sudo -n audit-fail2ban` or parse captured known output. Need tell next agent exact issue: parser source fixed but test mistakenly called raw binary without password; use wrapper. Re-run installer `sudo bash .../install-audit-readonly.sh`, then `sudo -n /usr/local/sbin/audit-fail2ban`; ensure all helper probes.\n2. Wait for agents/repo quiet, inspect dirty and commit only owned files, push to hermes-security-scripts. Document relation to lifsea. Do not run fix-sudoers.\n3. Full final audit: `sudo audit-smart` after install nvme-cli or sysfs, memory, journal, boot. End-to-end f2b test, maybe add drop-in. Hmm immediate reboot request prioritized. Maybe before reboot run bootstrap check, verify sudo, units, no failures. User manually reboot. Postboot verify.\n4. Install Tor Browser after reboot? Could do before. But user wants reboot. Need order.\n5. Revoke token, remaining tasks later.\nCould include 5-6 steps, template says 1,2 but not limit. Fine.\n\nRelevant Files:\n- all important exact paths, plus commits/repos.\nNeed include `~/Projects/zen-hardening/install-audit-readonly.sh` curren