wrappers and sudoers, not wheel. Fine.\n- `fix-sudoers-permissions.sh` is dangerous though corrected to preserve password-required. It could still remove sole NOPASSWD that is the only current access (e.g. when no wheel rule). It is not to be used. Need redesign.\n- `RECOVER-SUDO` is safe; use pkexec if needed.\n- Quarantine directory still exists with 10-installer. Not active. Could leave.\n- `/etc/sudoers.d/opencode` is empty at 0440. Good.\n\nSystem:\n- The service units are in user config, not /etc despite installer. Current `systemctl --user` says enabled. Is `systemctl --global enable` necessary? The symlink likely in `~/.config/systemd/user/default.target.wants`. Linger yes. So survives.\n- Evidence service/timer active.\n- Shield Kitty watcher PID systemd cgroup. Good.\n- `device-blacklist` still not installed. Prior active? It was reviewed but not root-installed. Should mention as open maybe. User wants security tools. It is not in current conversation except handoff. Keep in active/relevant.\n- No browser.\n- machine ID, DMI.\n- Ethernet randomization.\n- btrfs snapshots root only.\n- `efivarfs` 70% but 57K free, okay.\n- memory pressure from agents. Need recheck after they finish.\n\n\"Failed to dispatch Hermes\": The user said \"have hermes deploy fleets\" but assistant explained no direct channel. The summary should state no direct channel to Hermes; continue direct or wait for agents. Good.\n\nLet''s decide exact format and detail level. Need not include prior \"Objective 21-layer encryption\" perhaps still relevant because no design. Add in Blocked/Active if preserving. The user asked remaining ecosystem after core. Include one bullet:\n- Remaining requested work: `void-bin` builds; review/install `bde-security-biometrics`, `lin-antimalware-tools`, `local-emergency-patrol`, `zen-healer`, `secure-tactical-systems`; `zen-healer` unsafe; ISO via `zen-suite` not installer; Xbox emulation blocked.\nThis retains.\n\nNeed maybe include `voidlit` theme active