INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0dfb2bf92001IuA6rxrcUeQ7k6','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',11231,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","part":{"id":"prt_0dfb2b0c7001sijwB7IuwD0kH7","sessionID":"ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g","messageID":"msg_0dfb2aab7001VCa62dqEuDyGxq","type":"reasoning","text":"Now I can see the truth:\n\n**RECOVER-SUDO.sh**: The `PKEXEC_UID` branch is FIRST and correct. The `SUDO_USER` references in my grep were in comments and in the echo. The logic is correct: pkexec → PKEXEC_UID, elif SUDO_USER, else USER. This is SAFE. My grep flagged comment lines and the `elif` as \"BUG\" incorrectly. So RECOVER-SUDO is fine.\n\n**install-arpwatch-spoof.sh**: This is a REAL bug of the same class. It handles `SUDO_USER` but NOT `PKEXEC_UID`. So if run via pkexec:\n- `SUDO_USER_NAME` is empty\n- `TARGET_HOME=\"$HOME\"` = `/root`\n- The hook path becomes `/root/Projects/zen-hardening/arpwatch-spoof-alert.sh` → doesn''t exist\n- It would report the hook as missing, or worse, write a unit with wrong paths\n\nThis is exactly the bug class I hit. And the unit files hardcode `/run/user/1000` — they \"resolve\" the uid via `stat -c %U \"$TARGET_HOME\"` = `root` → uid 0 → `/run/user/0`. So a pkexec run would install units pointing at `/run/user/0` and `/root/Projects/...`. Broken units.\n\nAlso: these scripts require root. If run as `sudo bash install-arpwatch-spoof.sh`, SUDO_USER is set correctly. If run via pkexec, it breaks. Since these installers are the kind of thing a desktop user double-clicks (pkexec is common from a file manager), this is a plausible path.\n\nSo: **install-arpwatch-spoof.sh has the real PKEXEC_UID bug.** Let me fix it.\n\n**install-audit-readonly.sh line 231** — let me check that one too. My grep said \"BUG bare $SUDO_USER\". Let me look.\n\nLet me check line 231 and also install-shield-kitty-units.sh line 35 (which said \"ok has fallback\").\n\nLet me read those.\n\nThen fix install-arpwatch-spoof.sh properly.\n\nLet me check install-audit-readonly.sh:231.","time":{"start":1790459424967,"end":1790459428754}},"time":1790459428754}');
