-----------------------------------------------------------\n\n    journalctl -b -p err --no-pager | tail -40\n    systemctl --failed\n\n  PASS:  systemctl --failed lists nothing\n        journal errors are the usual benign probe messages only\n\n  Known-benign, do NOT chase these:\n    - TDX / TDX-GS capability messages\n    - touchscreen / I2C probe messages\n    - ACPI capability warnings\n    - konsole \"PreviewJob ... does not exist\" for files in /etc/sudoers.d\n      (caused by that directory being mode 0750; harmless)\n    - systemd-coredump entries for alert.py --demo (these were test runs)\n    - one Xorg coredump at startup\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 8 -- STILL OUTSTANDING (not reboot related)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  a) Remove the temporary root audit surface. It is 7 passwordless wrappers,\n     created only for this audit, and should not outlive it:\n\n        sudo bash /home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/install-audit-readonly.sh --remove\n\n     Verified safe: removes only /etc/sudoers.d/audit-readonly and the seven\n     /usr/local/sbin/audit-* files. It never touches the %wheel rule.\n     After removing, `sudo -l` should show (ALL) ALL and nothing else.\n\n  b) Two commits are unpushed in /tmp/opencode/hss and exist ONLY on this disk:\n\n        d72d480  fix the pkexec/SUDO_USER identity-resolution bug (4 scripts)\n        5a7bf5d  add git-verified.sh\n\n     Local git is not a backup. Restoring push access needs a new SSH key,\n     which needs a browser session -- so do it before closing the browser.\n\n  c) torbrowser-launcher is installed and the tor daemon is active, so\n     anonymity is covered. The daemon alone was never sufficient -- it is a\n     SOCKS proxy with no client -- but the launcher is present now.\n\n  d) Deliberately not done, needs a decision, not a fix:\n        - /home has no snapshots (all 11 cover only the root subvolume)\n        - machine-id and DMI strings are still unique\n        - SDDM greeter has no automated brute-force protection (no remote\n          IP to ban; structural, not configurable)\n\n\n================================================================================\n  QUICK VERSION -- copy/paste this after logging back in\n================================================================================\n\n    uptime -s\n    systemctl --user is-active shield-kitty-watch.service evidence-seal.timer\n    systemctl --user show shield-kitty-watch.service -p ActiveEnterTimestamp --value\n    sudo visudo -c\n    systemctl is-active firewalld fail2ban tor\n    sudo nft list chain inet firewalld filter_INPUT | tail -3\n    hostname\n    cat /sys/class/net/wlo1/address\n    systemctl --failed\n\n  The single most important line is the third one: the activation timestamp\n  must be within ~30s of the boot time, not hours later.\n================================================================================\n","filePath":"/home/livings/Desktop/POST-REBOOT-CHECKLIST.txt"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","title":"home/livings/Desktop/POST-REBOOT-CHECKLIST.txt","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/livings/Desktop/POST-REBOOT-CHECKLIST.txt","exists":false,"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1790461010291,"end":1790461010296}}},"time":1790461010296}');
