INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0e98ebf35001O7612cUA7PTbpX','ses_f16732810ffehZhBAPc6TQNXa2',155,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f16732810ffehZhBAPc6TQNXa2","part":{"id":"prt_0e98e8dd0001LXgqj2AbOK925j","sessionID":"ses_f16732810ffehZhBAPc6TQNXa2","messageID":"msg_0e98e7a24001W6o3ydLZ9KVBBb","type":"reasoning","text":"So the user''s history shows earlier today they asked hermes:\n- \"check the past 4 months work of sessions under my UID Sin 1000\"\n- \"look at all past sessions from opencode and your terminals under the UID''s Living_sin Living_Sin Sin and livingsin\"\n- \"and then prepare a todo list and lets go over it\"\n\nNow they''re asking me (opencode): \"help hermes pull all of my user data from all of my usernames and UID on garuda rani systems going back 4 months under Living_Sin Living_sin sin and living_sin\"\n\nSo \"garuda rani systems\" - hmm. Garuda is the distro (Garuda Linux). \"Rani\" might be a machine name. Let me check the system hostname and whether there are other machines. Let''s check hostname, /etc/hosts, and whether there''s any reference to \"rani\" as a hostname.\n\nAlso check what UIDs exist locally: getent passwd for those usernames.\n\nThe task: help hermes pull all user data from all usernames and UIDs, going back 4 months. This is essentially a local audit: find sessions/data associated with usernames Living_Sin, Living_sin, sin, living_sin (and UID 1000?) over the past 4 months, and prepare a todo list.\n\nBut wait - \"garuda rani systems\" - maybe \"Rani\" is the hostname of this machine? Let me check hostname. Also check if there are multiple systems (fleet). Earlier history mentions \"fleet sessions\".\n\nLet me check hostname, getent passwd, and look for other hosts.","time":{"start":1790624828880,"end":1790624841524}},"time":1790624841524}');
