INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0e99160ed001LmJOwYG0P3BkNu','ses_f16732810ffehZhBAPc6TQNXa2',178,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f16732810ffehZhBAPc6TQNXa2","part":{"id":"prt_0e9911e02001fzNGB3OXMXZIBG","sessionID":"ses_f16732810ffehZhBAPc6TQNXa2","messageID":"msg_0e9910e39001WKbAQp17X4PM1H","type":"reasoning","text":"The user wants me to:\n1. Check on the Lia.CLI and older corrupted versions for memories and data\n2. Push all of the data to a private repo through hermes\n\nWait — but the original request context: \"help hermes pull all of my user data from all of my usernames and UID on garuda rani systems going back 4 months under Living_Sin Living_sin sin and living_sin\". Then this follow-up: check Lia.CLI and older corrupted versions for memories and data, then push all the data to a private repo through hermes.\n\nLet me think about what''s legitimate here. This is the user''s own machine (hostname zero, Garuda Linux, user livings with GECOS \"Living_Sin\", UID 1000). They want to collect their own session data/memories from their own tools (hermes, opencode, lia-cli) going back 4 months, check Lia.CLI and older corrupted versions for memories/data, and push to a private GitHub repo.\n\nConcerns: This is the user''s own data on their own machine. The MEMORY.md notes that pushing to GitHub currently doesn''t work (SSH key rejected, no gh token). Also the user''s USER.md preferences: they want scope choices, prefer staging irreversible work and stopping for confirmation, security work is \"report only\" unless authorized — but here they explicitly authorize pushing data to a private repo.\n\nPotential issue: pushing \"all of the data\" to a private repo — could include secrets. MEMORY.md says audit output includes `_secrets.json`. Pushing secrets to GitHub even private is risky. Standing convention in MEMORY.md: \"any security- or business-related work is pushed to GitHub as a PRIVATE repo by default, always.\"\n\nSo the plan:\n1. Explore Lia.CLI directory and find older/corrupted versions (maybe backups, .curator_backups, git history, old copies) for memories/data.\n2. Collect hermes memories, sessions, opencode sessions, terminal sessions from past 4 months under the usernames/UIDs.\n3. Organize into a directory (an export).\n4. Create a private repo and push through hermes (the hermes CLI has gitbus/sync? Let''s check hermes commands: config, heal, heartbeat, inbox, journal, ledger, send, services, sync, watch). \"push ... thru hermes\" — maybe hermes has a sync command that pushes to GitHub.\n\nBut first, there''s a known blocker: GitHub SSH key rejected / no token. MEMORY.md says as of 2026-09-26 no gh CLI/token and SSH key rejected. The history shows user said \"i should now be logged into the gh cli\" on 9/26 — need to verify current state.\n\nAlso, secrets: I should check for secrets in the data and probably exclude them or at least flag. The user''s USER.md says they prefer being told the actual missing capability.\n\nThis is a multi-step task. Let me set up todos and start exploring.\n\nLet me plan:\n1. Survey Lia.CLI: /home/livings/Projects/_inventory/lia-cli and /home/livings/Projects/lia-cli, find corrupted/older versions (maybe in .git history, backups, ~/.lia-cli).\n2. Survey hermes memories/sessions/cron/state.db for session data going back 4 months (since ~2026-05-28).\n3. Survey opencode sessions (~/.local/share/opencode? or ~/.config/opencode).\n4. Identify usernames/UIDs: only one local user (livings, UID 1000, GECOS Living_Sin). Old data from previous installs may reference other usernames (Living_sin, sin, living_sin) in files (e.g., /home/sin, /home/Living_Sin paths in old logs).\n5. Collect into an export folder, e.g., ~/Projects/_inventory/user-data-export-2026-09-28 or a new repo dir.\n6. Sanitize obvious secrets? The user said push all data. But pushing secrets to GitHub is bad practice. I should check and flag; per their preferences, security work is \"report only\" unless authorized... but they authorized pushing data. I''ll check for secrets and mention. Actually, the safest: gather, then report what''s there including any secrets files, and ask/flag before pushing secrets. But the user expects unrun/partial work stated plainly.\n\nLet me start exploring. Use parallel tool calls.\n\nFirst, find Lia.CLI locations and corrupted versions.","time":{"start":1790624996866,"end":1790625013996}},"time":1790625013997}');
