INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0e99240710017421QN2N2znbA1','ses_f16732810ffehZhBAPc6TQNXa2',251,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f16732810ffehZhBAPc6TQNXa2","part":{"id":"prt_0e99218d3001wlFA9UHIXtAMMH","sessionID":"ses_f16732810ffehZhBAPc6TQNXa2","messageID":"msg_0e992099f001ebeJ7zAU3OkUOf","type":"reasoning","text":"Good. Key data locations identified:\n- `~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db` (36MB) - opencode sessions\n- `~/.hermes/state.db` (15.7MB) - hermes sessions/memories\n- `~/.hermes/memories/` - MEMORY.md, USER.md\n- `~/.hermes/terminal-sessions/`\n- `~/.hermes/.hermes_history`\n- lia-cli data/memory + git history (older versions in _inventory clone)\n- `.curator_backups` blobs in ~/.hermes\n- fish history, konsole logs, recently-used\n\n\"older corrupted versions\" of Lia.CLI — the _inventory clone is behind (at 609f4bc) vs working (1e727cc). Also maybe there are other lia projects: lia-groq-bridge, living-sin-models/lia-sync.py, metals-alloy-engineering/lia_memory_bridge.py, nanite-systems/lia_nanite_bridge.py. And maybe older corrupted data in the hermes curator backups or the voynich memories/hermes-pending-memories.json.\n\nLet me check what \"corrupted\" means - maybe there are broken sqlite dbs or JSON. Let me check:\n1. lia-groq-bridge\n2. hermes-pending-memories.json\n3. .curator_backups blobs that mention living_sin\n4. Check git history in lia-cli for memory vault changes (the \"config memory updates\" commit 65bda31)\n\nAlso need to check whether there are old home dirs (e.g., /home/sin, /home/Living_Sin) from previous installs. Only /home/livings exists probably. Let''s check /home and also old data in /root? no, no root.\n\nAlso check `~/.hermes/vault`, `~/.hermes/pastes`, `~/.hermes/cron/output`, `~/.hermes/logs`.\n\nLet me also check \"garuda rani systems\" - still unexplained. Maybe \"Rani\" is the name of another machine. Search more broadly for \"rani\" in home excluding node_modules/venv/packs. Earlier search found matches only in venv/pygments and voynich corpus (cross-language.py). Maybe the voynich corpus mentions rani as a word. Possibly \"garuda rani\" is just how the user refers to their Garuda machine(s). Hostname is \"zero\". Let''s check if there are known hosts in ~/.ssh/known_hosts.\n\nLet me continue exploring in parallel batches.","time":{"start":1790625061075,"end":1790625071216}},"time":1790625071217}');
