INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0e9928adb0019nX5hJGlqYS3ji','ses_f16732810ffehZhBAPc6TQNXa2',277,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f16732810ffehZhBAPc6TQNXa2","part":{"id":"prt_0e9925f58001PmhTL9aH7x9fRO","sessionID":"ses_f16732810ffehZhBAPc6TQNXa2","messageID":"msg_0e9924d70001dA8ghyz4LTLO3E","type":"reasoning","text":"Good progress. Now I have a clear picture of data sources:\n\n1. **opencode.db** (~36MB): tables account, event, session, message, project, etc.\n2. **hermes state.db** (~15MB): sessions, messages, etc.\n3. **hermes memories**: MEMORY.md, USER.md, curator backups blobs, hermes-pending-memories.json (in voynich corpus data/memories — odd location)\n4. **Lia.CLI**: data/memory/lia-memory.vault.json, data/legal_report_*.json, git history (working repo ahead of inventory clone); lia-groq-bridge, living-sin-models/lia-sync.py, metals-alloy-engineering/lia_memory_bridge.py, nanite-systems/lia_nanite_bridge.py\n5. Terminal/shell: fish_history, konsole profiles, recently-used.xbel, hermes terminal-sessions, hermes .hermes_history, pastes\n6. blood-build-backup, sentinel, watchdog, etc.\n\n\"Older corrupted versions\" — maybe there are corrupted older lia versions in git history or in the inventory clones. Let me check git history for the memory vault across commits, and look for other lia copies. Also there might be a \"corrupted\" version somewhere — search for files with corrupted in name across the whole home (did earlier with maxdepth 5, found nothing except task-tracker.ts matches for \"corrupt\" in lia-cli src).\n\nLet me check task-tracker.ts corrupt reference, and search for other lia memory stores: e.g. `lia-memory.vault.json` copies elsewhere, `.vault` files, older lia dirs.\n\nAlso need to check the timeline: 4 months back = since 2026-05-28. Most files are from Sep 26 2026 (system rebuild). Data going back 4 months may exist in git history of repos (the inventory clones have full history), hermes state.db messages (created when?), opencode.db sessions.\n\nLet me check date ranges in opencode.db and hermes state.db.\n\nAlso \"garuda rani systems\" still unknown. Possibly the user''s phrase for their machines. I''ll note hostname \"zero\". Maybe \"Rani\" appears in konsole/Garuda.profile? Or in `~/.hermes/channel_directory.json`? Let me check that plus auth.json platform names.\n\nNext steps batch:\n1. Check DB date ranges and session counts.\n2. Find all lia memory/vault files.\n3. Check for corrupted lia versions (git fsck output was empty for first, then ===INV=== empty too — actually first fsck output showed nothing before ===INV===; both fine).\n4. Check gh CLI status and ssh -T github.","time":{"start":1790625079128,"end":1790625090267}},"time":1790625090267}');
