INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_0e99967a9001hwD70GSoWpRcCq','ses_f16732810ffehZhBAPc6TQNXa2',563,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_f16732810ffehZhBAPc6TQNXa2","part":{"id":"prt_0e998f9b1001VGY01H53S2gebk","sessionID":"ses_f16732810ffehZhBAPc6TQNXa2","messageID":"msg_0e998ed3c001Cqh4So4246zyX1","type":"reasoning","text":"- `_secrets.json` findings are mostly previews/truncated — previews like \"-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE K...\" (truncated) — looks like scanner metadata with short previews, not full secret values. There could be preview leaks (up to some chars). Risk moderate. I''ll include it — actually let me check max preview length... Sample previews are short. It''s the user''s own audit file, likely already needed. But policy: \"no secrets... ever pushed\" per sin-archive policy. To be safe I''ll include `_secrets.json` but if previews contain actual key material... Let me check the longest preview and whether any preview has >40 chars of key body.\n\n- `~/.config/gh/` has config.yml & hosts.yml (no token file — token in keyring). config.yml 1780 bytes might contain... gh config.yml is settings (not token). hosts.yml has oauth token? Actually hosts.yml historically stored token! In modern gh, token is in keyring, hosts.yml has just hostname + user + git_protocol. Let me check hosts.yml content (98 bytes — too small for token? A gho_ token is ~40+ chars, possible). Must check and withhold.\n\n- lia-cli working: only pyc modified; local master == origin/master? `log origin/master..HEAD` printed nothing → no unpushed commits. Good, inventory clone also up to date... wait earlier `hermes`/git showed inventory at 609f4bc while working at 1e727cc. The `git status -sb` for inventory shows? It printed only \" M lib/rlm/...\" for inventory? Actually output order: after `===`, first line `## master...origin/master` (lia-cli working status), then ` M lib/rlm/__pycache__...` — that''s inventory status line? Confusing. Let me recheck: command was: `git -C lia-cli log origin/master..HEAD --oneline` (no output), `git -C inventory status -sb | head -2` → `## master...origin/master` and ` M lib/...pyc`, then inventory log origin/master..HEAD → nothing. So inventory working tree has a modified pyc but HEAD == origin/master? But inventory HEAD was 609f4bc per earlier fsck/reflog while working HEAD 1e727cc... Both can''t equal origin/master. Unless origin/master moved: earlier `hermes sync` fetched hermes-cli, not lia-cli. Hmm, earlier inventory log showed top commit 609f4bc. And working top 1e727cc. For both `origin/master..HEAD` empty: inventory''s origin/master ref = 609f4bc (stale fetch), working''s origin/master = 1e727cc? That means GitHub already has 1e727cc — but working repo''s origin ref updated at its clone time (13:21) which was AFTER inventory''s (13:11)... but1e727cc was committed14:39 local — after both clones. So origin/master in working repo = whatever was fetched at 13:21 — can''t include 14:39 commit unless pushed and re-fetched. Contradiction → maybe they pushed lia-cli to GitHub after (gh works). So likely all lia-cli commits are already on GitHub. `git log origin/master..HEAD` empty for working → HEAD ≤ origin/master → GitHub has it. OK: everything''s pushed.\n\nSo inventory clone == GitHub full history; no unpushed lia data except working-tree artifacts (pyc, data/ files — data/memory & legal reports are they tracked? inventory has .gitignore maybe ignoring data. Check if data/ is tracked in lia-cli git — the vault from Jul 17 might be committed (commit 65bda31 \"config and memory updates\"). Let''s check `git log -- data/memory`.\n\nThe \"older corrupted versions\": in git history — kg_schema.py exists in inventory HEAD? Yes (file exists on disk at 609f4bc and status clean-ish aside pyc). Working repo doesn''t have it → deleted in later commits? Let me check `git log --diff-filter=D -- kg_schema.py` in working. Actually working repo status clean and file absent → deleted at some commit between. Fine — history preserved on GitHub.\n\nSo for lia, my export should include:\n- both checkouts'' data/ (vault, legal reports)\n- the corrupted older files (kg_schema.py etc.) — available in inventory clone / GitHub history; include copies + a note\n- voynich copies of lia-vault/hermes-pending-memories\n- git bundle of lia-cli full history (small, ensures preservation) — optional since already on GitHub; but \"push all data to a private repo\" suggests consolidating. A bundle of ~small repo is cheap. Let''s include `lia-cli-history.bundle`.\n- lia-groq-bridge etc.: already on GitHub; note in manifest (don''t duplicate).\n\nNow check: does `data/` get tracked in lia-cli git? And hosts.yml content. Then start assembling.","time":{"start":1790625511857,"end":1790625540007}},"time":1790625540008}');
