INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0deea575e001Jk7Wu63kUKJNB3','msg_0deea52ce001yLa47rm1FztIz4','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790446294878,1790446298691,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"28 public repos. But \"hermes blood build\" — I don''t see anything named hermes or blood. Let me also check private repos. The public API won''t show them. But I can probe with `git ls-remote` over SSH.\n\nLet me think about candidate names. \"hermes blood build\" — Hermes is a Greek god, associated with Hermes blood / \"hermes blood\" is an alchemical term. In game modding, there''s a known thing: \"Hermes\" blood texture in Skyrim? Actually, there''s a well-known Skyrim mod texture pack called \"Blood\" or \"Hermes\"... Hmm.\n\nWait — actually there IS a known thing. In Skyrim, \"Hermes\" ... no. Let me think about the \"Voynich\" repo, occult corpus, \"garuda-tools\"... The user seems to have repos with occult/kitbash themes.\n\nLet me probe for private repos by trying `git ls-remote` on plausible names. But guessing names blindly is a shot in the dark and could be slow/noisy.\n\nBetter approach: I can''t list private repos without an API token (the REST API doesn''t accept SSH auth). So to see private repos, I''d need a token — which brings us back to the thing I flagged.\n\nLet me be honest about that limit and check: is there a \"hermes\" or \"blood\" match in the public list? No. Closest: `voynich-occult-corpus`, `garuda-tools-fresh`.\n\nLet me try a handful of plausible private repo names via ls-remote — cheap and non-destructive. Let me try: hermes, hermes-blood, hermes-blood-build, blood, hermesbuild, etc.\n\nActually, let me be smart and just report findings + state the limitation, and ask them to confirm the name. But I can do a quick probe to be helpful. Let me probe ~12 candidate names in one loop.\n\nLet me do that.","time":{"start":1790446294878,"end":1790446298689}}');
