INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0deeb07500015pLginpXR6Npof','msg_0deeb033b001d6j0ukgVYq4PWz','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790446339920,1790446344092,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"Confirmed: the `Blood` icon theme does NOT exist. Available: Adwaita, BeautyLine, breeze, garuda, hicolor, etc.\n\nThe install script sets `Theme=Blood` in kdeglobals but never installs a Blood icon theme. So on Plasma, the icon theme will fail to resolve → icons go missing across the desktop.\n\nThe README says \"Blood icon theme inherits from BeautyLine + hicolor (safe fallback)\" — implying a Blood theme was supposed to exist somewhere. It doesn''t exist in this repo (no icons/ dir).\n\nYou are running Plasma (Wayland), so this will visibly break.\n\nFix options:\n1. Point Theme to an existing theme (BeautyLine or breeze-dark — dark fits the black/red theme).\n2. Create a Blood icon theme that inherits BeautyLine/hicolor (symlinks) so the name resolves.\n\nThe minimal correct fix that preserves the \"Blood\" name: create ~/.local/share/icons/Blood with index.theme inheriting BeautyLine, plus symlinked dirs. That way `Theme=Blood` resolves and you get BeautyLine''s icons.\n\nLet me ask the user which they prefer rather than guessing — actually, this is a real decision. But the safer, more faithful-to-intent default is #2 (make Blood resolve via inheritance, as the README describes). That matches the documented intent exactly: \"Blood icon theme inherits from BeautyLine + hicolor (safe fallback)\".\n\nLet me just do #2 since it matches the repo''s own documented design, and it''s non-destructive. Actually, let me reconsider — creating an icon theme dir is a write to their system. But it''s the documented intent and fixes a broken state. It''s in ~/.local/share/icons which is user-scoped and currently has no Blood.\n\nI think I should ask, briefly, since it''s a visual choice. But I can also just implement the documented design and tell them how to change it. Given \"rebuild my theme\" is the task and this is a bug in the install, implementing the documented inheritance is the right call.\n\nLet me do it — create the Blood theme inheriting BeautyLine with hicolor fallback.\n\nLet me check BeautyLine''s structure first.","time":{"start":1790446339920,"end":1790446344091}}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0deeb179d001b4mbIICGY8Pi59','msg_0deeb033b001d6j0ukgVYq4PWz','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790446344093,1790446345734,'{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed a genuine bug in the installer. You''re on **Plasma/Wayland**, and it set `Theme=Blood` in `kdeglobals` — but no `Blood` icon theme exists anywhere. The repo has no `icons/` directory, so Plasma will fail to resolve the name and you''ll get missing icons across the desktop. The README even hints at the fix (\"inherits from BeautyLine + hicolor\") but the theme was never shipped.","time":{"start":1790446344093,"end":1790446345732}}');
