INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0deec1e11001Os4HRPVjBsxFWE','msg_0deec1713001t15ZkBMu89AAYK','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790446411281,1790446411282,'{"type":"step-start"}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0deec1e13001tKS1cSqcjU4RJB','msg_0deec1713001t15ZkBMu89AAYK','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790446411283,1790446417006,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"The user is asking me to:\n1. Install the hermes blood build (already done last turn)\n2. \"Go back through my sessions on both you and hermes\" — sessions on opencode and on \"hermes\"\n3. Install, debug, error check everything before installation\n4. Ensure it works 100% and won''t brick/lock them out\n5. \"Prepare the fleet\"\n\nLet me think about what''s real here and what isn''t.\n\nThings I can actually verify:\n- The install already ran successfully last turn. I can re-verify.\n- I can audit the install script for destructive behavior, check for lockout risks (e.g., a bad GTK/konsolerc that makes the desktop unusable, font issues).\n- I can error-check the config files (valid TOML, valid colorscheme, valid JSON).\n\nThings I CANNOT do:\n- \"Go back through my sessions on both you and hermes\" — I have no access to opencode session history, and no access to anything called \"Hermes.\" There''s no \"Hermes\" tool here. `~/.hermes/` is just a directory the theme script writes a skin file into; it''s not a running agent with sessions I can read. Let me verify that — check if ~/.hermes exists and what''s in it.\n- \"Ensure it works 100%\" — I cannot guarantee this. That''s an unfulfillable claim. I should be honest.\n- \"Won''t brick my build or lock me out\" — I can assess concrete risks, which is legitimate.\n- \"Prepare the fleet\" — vague, unclear. I should ask.\n\nThe lockout risk is actually a REAL and important concern I should genuinely check: if the theme makes Konsole/Plasma unreadable, can they still log in / get a shell? Specifically:\n- Great Vibes is a cursive display font. Applied as the *global* KDE font (kdeglobals font=) at size 14, terminal text and UI text may become hard to read or cause layout issues. That''s a genuine usability/lockout-adjacent risk.\n- If konsolerc gets a bad profile, Konsole may fail to start → no terminal.\n- If the OpenCode theme JSON is malformed, opencode may fail to start.\n- gtk settings.ini errors could affect GTK apps.\n\nThese are real, checkable things. That''s the valuable work here.\n\nSo my plan: do a genuine pre-flight audit — validate each config file syntactically, assess lockout/brick risk concretely, and report. Be honest that I can''t do the session-history review or guarantee 100%.\n\nLet me investigate. Let me:\n1. Check ~/.hermes — what''s actually there\n2. Check opencode session storage location\n3. Validate all config files\n4. Check the font readability concern\n5. Check konsolerc for profile correctness\n\nLet me do this in parallel.\n\nLet me be careful not to over-claim. Let me gather facts first.","time":{"start":1790446411283,"end":1790446417005}}');
