INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0deec85cf001wiZm8KpfMFD2MU','msg_0deec7b39001hmbb1KGkFRL3bv','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790446437839,1790446440836,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"More findings — and these are significant:\n\n1. **`gtk-font-name=Great Vibes Bold,  14`** — \"Great Vibes Bold\" is NOT a real font family. Only \"Great Vibes\" exists. This will fall back to a default font. Also the double space. This is a real bug. Let me verify with fc-match.\n\n2. **`gtk-cursor-theme-name=Rage-Gothic`** — does this cursor theme exist? Need to check. GTK3 with a nonexistent cursor theme → falls back to default, usually harmless.\n\n3. **`gtk-icon-theme-name=Blood`** in GTK3 settings — my Blood theme is now created, so that resolves. Good. But note gtk-4.0 also has it.\n\n4. **`gtk-theme-name=Sweet-Dark`** — does Sweet GTK theme exist? Earlier icon list showed \"Sweet-cursors\" but I should check gtk themes. If missing, GTK apps fall back.\n\n5. **`gtk-decoration-layout=close,maximize,minimize:`** — trailing colon, harmless.\n\n6. **fish IS installed**, so Konsole profile is fine. Good — no lockout there.\n\n7. `blood.yaml` — it''s a config for a \"Hermes\" agent that doesn''t exist. Dead config, harmless.\n\nLet me verify the font and theme/cursor existence. These are the real \"will it actually work\" checks.\n\nLet me run fc-match for \"Great Vibes Bold\" and check for Sweet-Dark GTK theme and Rage-Gothic cursor.\n\nThis is the crux of the audit. Let me be thorough.\n\nNote: this is a lot of genuine issues. The user''s core ask — \"make sure it works 100% and won''t brick me\" — is actually well-founded, because there ARE real defects. I should deliver this honestly.\n\nLet me run the final checks.","time":{"start":1790446437839,"end":1790446440835}}');
