INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0deecd4b2001g1eAb52wW3hWqQ','msg_0deeccf1e001RnSE8kMCIheMnU','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790446458034,1790446458958,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"Both GTK configs now correctly resolve to Great Vibes. Previously they resolved to Noto Sans.\n\nNow let me give the honest report. I need to address:\n1. What I can''t do (Hermes sessions — don''t exist; \"100%\" guarantee; \"fleet\")\n2. What I found and fixed\n3. Lockout risk assessment\n\nLet me be concise but complete. This is a case where detail is warranted since it''s an audit report the user explicitly requested.\n\nLet me not commit anything (not asked). Let me mention the repo has uncommitted changes.\n\nLet me write the report.","time":{"start":1790446458034,"end":1790446458955}}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0deecd850001o1oMs1jM8QkRHE','msg_0deeccf1e001RnSE8kMCIheMnU','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790446458960,1790446463858,'{"type":"text","text":"Done. Report:\n\n## Two parts of your request I can''t do\n\n**\"Go back through my sessions on Hermes\"** — there are none. `~/.hermes/` contains exactly one file, `skins/blood.yaml`, which the installer itself wrote. No `hermes` binary on PATH, no process running. It''s a config directory for a tool that isn''t installed here. There''s no session history to review.\n\n**\"Works 100%\"** — I can''t promise that, and I''d be lying if I said so. What I did instead was verify each dependency against the actual filesystem. Below is what''s confirmed, not assumed.\n\n**\"Prepare the fleet\"** — undefined. Tell me what you mean and I''ll do it.\n\n## Real defects found\n\n| Defect | Evidence | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Blood` icon theme didn''t exist | `kdeglobals` set `Theme=Blood`, no such dir. Breaks **all** Plasma icons | **fixed** |\n| `gtk-font-name=Great Vibes Bold` | Not a real family — `fc-match` returned **Noto Sans**. All GTK apps ignored the theme''s font | **fixed** (now resolves to Great Vibes) |\n| Great Vibes has no Bold/Italic | Only `Regular` installed; alacritty requests both, fontconfig silently returns Regular | open — no bold/italic in terminal |\n| `Rage-Gothic` cursor missing | No such theme in `/usr/share/icons` | open — falls back to default |\n| Dancing Script installed, unused | Git log `f984a14` moved everything to Great Vibes; `install.sh:69` still ships it | open — harmless cruft |\n\n## Verified sound\n\nfish installed (so Konsole''s `Garuda` profile won''t die on spawn), konsole + alacritty TOML parse cleanly with correct colors under `primary`, `voidlit.json` is valid JSON, `konsolerc` → `Garuda.profile` → `BlackRed.colorscheme` chain is consistent, `Sweet-Dark` GTK theme exists, backup written to `~/.local/share/blood-build-backup/20260926_111207`.\n\n## Lockout risk: low\n\nNothing in this theme touches PAM, the display manager, autostart, or keyboard input. Every failure mode I found degrades to a fallback font or missing icon — cosmetic, not fatal. You cannot get locked out by this.\n\nOne honest caveat in the other direction: Great Vibes is a formal calligraphy script now set as the **global KDE UI font** at size 14. It won''t lock you out, but desktop UI text will be genuinely hard to read, and the README already concedes it''s variable-width. If that bothers you, `kdeglobals` is a one-line revert.\n\nRepo has uncommitted changes (`gtk/settings.ini`). I haven''t committed anything. Want me to commit the font fix plus an installer step that creates the `Blood` theme, so the next clone isn''t broken?","time":{"start":1790446458960,"end":1790446463857}}');
