INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0deee40390013RhgyWDGn8ca03','msg_0deee3591001v9pCVc2vtifc8v','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790446551097,1790446556984,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"Now I have the full picture, and it''s a significant finding.\n\n1. **opencode session history: exactly ONE session, from today.** No 3-week history, no 2-day-ago session. All 8 \"fleet\" matches in the DB are from *this* conversation — the user''s own message and my replies. There is no prior session.\n\n2. **BUT — \"fleet\" DOES exist, and it''s real, and it''s big.** In `~/.cache/paru/clone/hermes-agent/src/hermes-agent-2026.9.24/` there''s a full source tree for **hermes-agent 2026.9.24** with an extensive fleet subsystem:\n   - `hermes_cli/update_cmd_fleet.py`\n   - `update_cmd_fleet_checkout.py`\n   - `update_cmd_fleet_gatewayless.py`\n   - `update_fleet_scope.py`\n   - tests for fleet config migration, fleet matrix down state, self-restart pending, check fail-closed, checkout build stamp, home scope, incomplete warning\n   - desktop: `fleet-rail.ts`, `use-fleet-roster.ts`, `fleet-roster.ts`, `fleet-profile-rail.spec.ts`\n\nSo \"Hermes\" IS a real project — `hermes-agent` — and it has a \"fleet\" feature. It''s just not *installed* on this machine (no binary on PATH), and its source is sitting in a paru (AUR helper) build cache directory.\n\nThis completely changes the picture from my earlier turn where I said \"There is no Hermes agent.\" I need to correct that. Earlier I said `~/.hermes/` had only blood.yaml and no `hermes` binary — that was accurate about *those two checks*, but I concluded too broadly that Hermes doesn''t exist. It does exist as source in the paru cache. I should own that correction.\n\nAlso: this is an AUR build cache (`~/.cache/paru/clone/`), which means at some point they tried to build/install hermes-agent from the AUR and it may have FAILED (leaving only the clone cache, no installed package). That''s a very plausible explanation for \"rebuild everything that was broken\" — they were trying to install hermes-agent and it didn''t complete.\n\nLet me investigate this properly:\n- Is hermes-agent installed as a package? Check pacman.\n- What''s the state of that source tree — is it built?\n- What''s the date on it (2026.9.24, and the dir timestamps).\n- The `contributors/emails/hermes-fleet-fix@localhost` is interesting — suggests local modifications to fleet code.\n- `kevin@fleetsmarts.net` — embedded in the source.\n\nThis is the actual lead. Let me dig in.\n\nImportant: I should be careful about `~/.cache/paru` — that''s a build cache, safe to read. Let me not modify it.\n\nLet me check package status and the tree state.\n\nLet me also reconsider: \"rebuild everything that was broken\" — so likely hermes-agent install broke. Let me find out.\n\nLet me investigate.","time":{"start":1790446551097,"end":1790446556983}}');
