INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0deef79c0001nVV9xLKXuKzlBJ','msg_0deef74ee001lHssas3Br60dlm','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790446631360,1790446637217,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"**sudo requires a password.** I cannot provide it. So I cannot run the build to completion — `makepkg -si` / `paru -S` will prompt for a password and hang (or fail) in my non-interactive shell.\n\nI should NOT ask the user to paste their sudo password into chat (same problem as the token — and worse). \n\nOptions:\n1. The user runs the command themselves in their own terminal.\n2. The user configures NOPASSWD for paru/makepkg temporarily.\n3. I run the build *without* sudo up to the point of packaging (makepkg without -i), producing a .pkg.tar.zst, then the user installs it with sudo themselves. This is a clean approach! `makepkg -s --noconfirm` builds the package but doesn''t install. Then `sudo pacman -U file.pkg.tar.zst`.\n\nOption 3 is genuinely good: I can do all the heavy lifting (the 10-30 min build) without any password, and hand them a single sudo command to run.\n\nThat''s the right move. Let me do that.\n\nNote: the PKGBUILD''s package() installs to $pkgdir which is user-owned in the build dir, so no sudo needed for packaging. Only the final install needs root.\n\nLet me clean the broken staging dir first (the d--x--x--x one) — actually it needs chmod to remove. `rm -rf` on it — the dir is d--x--x--x so rm -rf may fail because can''t read inside. Let me chmod it first. But it''s owned by livings, so I can chmod it.\n\nLet me clean and run the build.\n\nAlso note: `makepkg -s` will need to install makedepends via pacman (npm, rsync) — but both are already installed (I verified rsync and npm are present). So -s shouldn''t need sudo. Actually `-s` uses sudo to install missing deps; if none missing, no prompt. Let me use `--nodeps` to be safe? No — better to check. All makedepends (npm, rsync) are installed, so no sudo call needed.\n\nLet me clean the broken pkg dir and start the build in the background since it''s long, logging to a file.\n\nLet me kick it off with nohup and a log file, then poll.\n\nLet me first fix the pkg dir perms and clean.\n\nLet me be careful: `rm -rf` on the staging dir. It''s a paru build artifact, safe to remove — a fresh build regenerates it. And it''s the likely source of the previous weirdness.\n\nLet me do it.\n\nGiven the build is long, let me run it in background with nohup and a log, then report progress. I''ll set a reasonable approach: start it, then poll.\n\nLet me go.","time":{"start":1790446631360,"end":1790446637216}}');
