INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df043322001hTx70heCzcrz71','msg_0df042dcd001zHG580sZGtdKo6','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790447989538,1790447992313,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"Still 28, all public. So `/user/repos` with `affiliation=owner` returns only 28 for this token. That means the fine-grained token does NOT have access to the other ~92 repos.\n\nWhy? Because I told the user to set \"Repository access: All repositories\" with \"Contents: Read-only\". But they may have:\n- Selected only specific repositories, OR\n- Not granted access to all repos\n\nA fine-grained token only sees repos you''ve explicitly granted it access to. If they picked \"Only select repositories\" or limited it, it''ll only see those.\n\nSo the token is scoped to fewer repos than expected — or the user actually has 28 repos owned and 120 total including repos where they''re a *collaborator/member* but not owner.\n\n`affiliation=owner` filters to owner only. Let me try without the affiliation filter, and also check `affiliation=collaborator,organization_member` to see the full picture.\n\nLet me test:\n1. `/user/repos` with no affiliation (default = owner,collaborator,organization_member)\n2. Check total\n\nThat''s the key test. Maybe the 92 are repos they collaborate on.\n\nLet me run it.\n\nThis is the right diagnostic. Let me do it.","time":{"start":1790447989538,"end":1790447992312}}');
