INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df0779ee0018c9CZlxkwqpzpJ','msg_0df07736d0013s00P9zRrRmxcJ','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790448204270,1790448208341,'{"type":"text","text":"Blood Build rebuilt and verified. All checks pass.\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| 9 config files installed | all present |\n| `alacritty.toml` | valid TOML |\n| `voidlit.json` | valid JSON |\n| `blood.yaml` | valid YAML |\n| GTK font resolves | `Great Vibes, 14` → **Great Vibes Regular** (was Noto Sans) |\n| `Blood` icon theme | resolves via `kdeglobals` |\n| Konsole chain | `konsolerc` → `Garuda.profile` → `BlackRed.colorscheme` ✓ |\n| fish present | yes, Garuda profile won''t fail |\n| KDE cache | rebuilt |\n\nBackup of your prior configs: `~/.local/share/blood-build-backup/20260926_114306`\n\nBoth bugs I found earlier are still fixed and survived the rebuild — the installer writes `gtk/settings.ini` from the repo source, and I corrected the source file, so re-running `install.sh` no longer reintroduces the broken `Great Vibes Bold` reference. The `Blood` icon theme lives in `~/.local/share/icons/` and isn''t touched by the installer, so it persists.\n\n**Log out and back in** to pick up the Plasma/KDE parts.\n\nThree things still open, and I want to be straight that the rebuild doesn''t cover any of them:\n\n1. **`install.sh` still has the icon-theme bug.** I patched your live system, but the script never creates the `Blood` theme it depends on. A fresh clone on another machine breaks the same way. Two commits would fix it properly: the `gtk/settings.ini` font fix (currently uncommitted in your working tree) and an installer step that builds the theme. Want me to write both?\n\n2. **Dancing Script is dead weight** — `install.sh:69` still ships it, though commits `f984a14`/`418e662` moved everything to Great Vibes. Cosmetic.\n\n3. **The token is still live** at `~/.config/gh/token.clean`. It''s read-only and we''ve used it for the inventory, so it''s not urgent — but say the word and I''ll shred it. The SSH key still gives you full git access.\n\nStill waiting on you for: `sudo pacman -U ~/.cache/paru/clone/hermes-agent/hermes-agent-0.21.5-1-x86_64.pkg.tar.zst`, and a lead on **supercode**.","time":{"start":1790448204270,"end":1790448208339}}');
