ocument ill place on my desktop \n  23. k i ran those commands and i saved the token to the token.txt on my desktop\n  24. k retry\n  25. k now retry\n  26. so i need you to rebuild my hermes blood build and wel continue from there\n  27. ill reboot after a quick update once void is done downloading for now check all sessions from t\n  28. i know for a fact we can pull the data from your sessions history on the blood build i made for\n","metadata":{"output":"   1. hello opencode\n   2. rebuild my hermes blood build im logged into my github on my browser use your api key i just cr\n   3. open the github page i need to make you a token \n   4. [REDACTED-SECRET-2026-09-28]\n   5. k open the page again so i can generate a new token for you\n   6. you should have access to all my repos now right?\n   7. open the ssh key page so i can make you one please\n   8. sync with github copilot and lets get u that SSH key so u can see and modify my repos\n   9. the ssh key is open scan my repos for it\n  10. install my hermes blood build and then go back through my sessions on both you and hermes and i\n  11. how do i give u access to lal of my repos?\n  12. check previous sessions from the last 3 weeks for the fleet tool we made and also check from 2 \n  13. reinstall hermes and supercode \n  14. lets setup passwordless sudo for u\n  15. [Pasted ~9 lines] \n  16. alright lets retry\n  17. next check all builds and tools made from the past 3 months in your sessions and hermes session\n  18. i have 120 repos why cant you see them all?\n  19. open the page ill make you another token\n  20. i did mb now you should have a new 30 day token\n  21. [Pasted ~4 lines] \n  22. im going to paste the token to a document ill place on my desktop \n  23. k i ran those commands and i saved the token to the token.txt on my desktop\n  24. k retry\n  25. k now retry\n  26. so i need you to rebuild my hermes blood build and wel continue from there\n  27. ill reboot after a quick update once void is done downloading for now check all sessions from t\n  28. i know for a fact we can pull the data from your sessions history on the blood build i made for\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 - <<''PY''\nimport json\np=''/home/livings/.local/state/opencode/prompt-history.jsonl''\nrows=[json.loads(l) for l in open(p) if l.strip()]\n# show the input text of each, truncated - this is the user''s own prompt history\nfor i,d in enumerate(rows,1):\n    inp=d.get(''input'','''')\n    if isinstance(inp,list):\n        inp='' ''.join(str(x.get(''text'',x)) if isinstance(x,dict) else str(x) for x in inp)\n    print(f\"  {i:>2}. {str(inp)[:95]}\")\nPY","time":{"start":1790448430446,"end":1790448430481}}}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df0aed95001bx4ymyEdE1jr63','msg_0df0ae21f001sl7ksbVRLxbbUj','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790448430485,1790448430486,'{"reason":"tool-calls","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":90480,"input":62,"output":160,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"write":0,"read":90258}},"cost":0}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df0af710001qo5W4UJ94mn69y','msg_0df0aeda4001YChHsrE7Bmfmil','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790448432912,1790448432913,'{"type":"step-start"}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df0af712001AsLpKWfObBHJ0a','msg_0df0aeda4001YChHsrE7Bmfmil','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790448432914,1790448438455,'{"type":"text","text":"I checked as thoroughly as I can, and I have to keep disagreeing. That output is your complete prompt history for this machine — **all 28 entries, and entry 1 is \"hello opencode.\"** It''s this conversation, start to finish, including your most recent message. There is no earlier Blood Build session in it.\n\nWhat I verified, beyond just re-reading the database:\n\n- `session` table: **1 row**. `session_message`: 0. `session_share`: 0. `todo`: 0. `workspace`: 0\n- Archived sessions: **0**. Parent/child sub-agent sessions: **0**\n- `prompt-history.jsonl`: 28 entries, no timestamps on any of them, all from today\n- Only one opencode install on the box, only one `HOME` (`livings`), no session backups or exports\n- No other session store anywhere outside the paru cache\n\nAnd `hermes-blood` itself is the strongest evidence against the theory. Its git log runs to `f1ffc34` with five commits, the oldest being `b2dd840 \"Blood Build: full system theme\"` — someone built this on a **different machine**, then pushed. That''s where your history is: **in the repo''s commit log, not in a session store here.** The dates on those commits are Sep 21–22, four days before today. This machine''s opencode was installed today at 11:00 and has never seen them.\n\nSo the Blood Build work is real, and it *was* collaborative work — just not in a form I can read from here. What I did instead was read the actual artifacts: the install script, the color scheme, the profiles, the font references, and the commit history. That''s how I found the two genuine bugs, neither of which any session log would have told me:\n\n1. `install.sh:75` sets the Plasma icon theme to `Blood`, but the repo ships no `icons/` directory — fresh clones get a desktop with no icons\n2. `gtk/settings.ini:9` requested `Great Vibes Bold`, which isn''t a real font family; fontconfig silently fell back to Noto Sans, so GTK apps ignored the theme''s font entirely\n\nBoth verified against the filesystem, both fixed. That''s a more reliable basis for \"rebuild it correctly\" than a transcript would be.\n\nOne possibility worth ruling out, since you were confident: **were you on a different machine or a different account when you built this?** If the sessions you''re remembering are on another box, they''d be under that machine''s `~/.local/share/opencode/`. Nothing here can see across machines — I''d need you to run a query there and paste the output.\n\nMeanwhile, `paru -S void-bin` is still running and holding the pacman lock, so the reboot is still worth waiting on. Say the word and I''ll watch it and ping you when it''s safe.","time":{"start":1790448432914,"end":1790448438454}}');
