INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df0bbfa1001qxVPw9s6FWndna','msg_0df0b96cc001512UPAR2QFGFom','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790448484257,1790448484259,'{"type":"step-start"}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df0bbfa4001jAKI8rH5NNGkcM','msg_0df0b96cc001512UPAR2QFGFom','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790448484261,1790448487518,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"That explains everything. The user rebuilt the machine. So the sessions are gone because the machine was wiped/rebuilt. That''s a genuine, coherent explanation — and it means my earlier \"no sessions exist\" was correct for this machine, but the history they''re remembering is on a machine that no longer exists (or was wiped).\n\nThis is a moment to be genuinely helpful and not rub in the disagreement. I was right about the facts but I was arguing with someone whose context I didn''t have. I should acknowledge that, and pivot to what''s actionable: recover what we can.\n\nKey insight: the Blood Build history IS recoverable — from the git repo, which survived because it was pushed to GitHub. That''s the actual recovery path. And the 120 repos mean most of their work survived.\n\nLet me check what''s recoverable and offer real value. Let me look at what the git history contains, and think about what other recovery avenues exist.\n\nLet me be concise but substantive. I should:\n1. Acknowledge the lockout explains it — and that I was arguing with incomplete context\n2. Note the irony/help: the git push is what saved the work\n3. Offer concrete recovery: full git history of hermes-blood, and audit the 120 repos\n4. Check on void-bin status since they''re waiting to reboot\n\nLet me do a quick check on the git history depth and void-bin status.","time":{"start":1790448484260,"end":1790448487517}}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df0bcc5f001cdn8o0UY7ASTp2','msg_0df0b96cc001512UPAR2QFGFom','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790448487520,1790448489641,'{"type":"text","text":"That explains it. You were right about the history existing — it just died with the machine, and I''ve been telling you to look in a directory that got wiped.\n\nI was arguing from incomplete context. My facts were right about *this* machine, but the conclusion I kept pressing — that you''d never built this with me — was wrong. Apologies for repeating it four times.\n\nThe good news is that the lockout didn''t lose the work, because you''d pushed it:","time":{"start":1790448487519,"end":1790448489641}}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df0bd099001P0ZIIplfoAZW3X','msg_0df0b96cc001512UPAR2QFGFom','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790448488601,1790448489660,'{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_function_ta6pbehmk716_1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd ~/Projects/hermes-blood\necho \"=== hermes-blood: full recoverable history ===\"\ngit log --pretty=''%h  %ad  %s'' --date=short | sed ''s/^/  /''\necho\necho \"=== total commits + contributors ===\"\necho \"  commits: $(git rev-list --count HEAD)\"\ngit shortlog -sn HEAD | sed ''s/^/  /''"},"output":"=== hermes-blood: full recoverable history ===\n  f1ffc34  2026-09-21  chore: tune gtk settings and install script\n  418e662  2026-08-21  fix: ensure all components use Great Vibes font\n  5dfbfab  2026-08-21  fix: remove stray ] from BlackRed.colorscheme Color7Intense and ForegroundIntense\n  f984a14  2026-08-20  restore: switch font from Dancing Script to Great Vibes everywhere\n  b2dd840  2026-08-18  Blood Build: full system theme (black bg, red text, Dancing Script font)\n  968b304  2026-08-18  Blood skin + cursive fonts\n\n=== total commits + contributors ===\n  commits: 6\n       3\tLiving_Sin\n       2\tintricos777-dot\n       1\tsin\n","metadata":{"output":"=== hermes-blood: full recoverable history ===\n  f1ffc34  2026-09-21  chore: tune gtk settings and install script\n  418e662  2026-08-21  fix: ensure all components use Great Vibes font\n  5dfbfab  2026-08-21  fix: remove stray ] from BlackRed.colorscheme Color7Intense and ForegroundIntense\n  f984a14  2026-08-20  restore: switch font from Dancing Script to Great Vibes everywhere\n  b2dd840  2026-08-18  Blood Build: full system theme (black bg, red text, Dancing Script font)\n  968b304  2026-08-18  Blood skin + cursive fonts\n\n=== total commits + contributors ===\n  commits: 6\n       3\tLiving_Sin\n       2\tintricos777-dot\n       1\tsin\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd ~/Projects/hermes-blood\necho \"=== hermes-blood: full recoverable history ===\"\ngit log --pretty=''%h  %ad  %s'' --date=short | sed ''s/^/  /''\necho\necho \"=== total commits + contributors ===\"\necho \"  commits: $(git rev-list --count HEAD)\"\ngit shortlog -sn HEAD | sed ''s/^/  /''","time":{"start":1790448489630,"end":1790448489660}}}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df0bd4a1001YyY9rO69GSbNt5','msg_0df0b96cc001512UPAR2QFGFom','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790448489634,1790448489717,'{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_function_ta6pbehmk716_2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"echo \"=== void-bin build status (you may be able to reboot) ===\"\npgrep -a paru 2>/dev/null | sed ''s/^/  /'' || echo \"  paru finished - lock released, safe to reboot\"\npacman -Q void-bin 2>&1 | head -1 | sed ''s/^/  /''"},"output":"=== void-bin build status (you may be able to reboot) ===\n  27643 paru -S void-bin\n  error: package ''void-bin'' was not found\n","metadata":{"output":"=== void-bin build status (you may be able to reboot) ===\n  27643 paru -S void-bin\n  error: package ''void-bin'' was not found\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"echo \"=== void-bin build status (you may be able to reboot) ===\"\npgrep -a paru 2>/dev/null | sed ''s/^/  /'' || echo \"  paru finished - lock released, safe to reboot\"\npacman -Q void-bin 2>&1 | head -1 | sed ''s/^/  /''","time":{"start":1790448489638,"end":1790448489716}}}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df0bd4f60011H0DdcC1ws2JmA','msg_0df0b96cc001512UPAR2QFGFom','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790448489718,1790448489718,'{"reason":"tool-calls","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":92228,"input":27,"output":299,"reasoning":282,"cache":{"write":0,"read":91620}},"cost":0}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df0bdc00001vwg9XeQB2doFfY','msg_0df0bd4ff001wCneeAU5woprHs','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790448491520,1790448491521,'{"type":"step-start"}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df0bdc02001hO5Ugw7hYpjQTw','msg_0df0bd4ff001wCneeAU5woprHs','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790448491522,1790448497528,'{"type":"text","text":"The commit history is intact and it''s better than a session log — six commits from **August 18 to September 21**, under three identities (`Living_Sin`, `intricos777-dot`, `sin`). That''s a month of work, and it survived because it was pushed. The rebuild cost you the transcripts, not the code.\n\nThis also explains the Blood Build evolution, which I can now read properly:\n\n- `968b304` Aug 18 — Blood skin + cursive fonts\n- `b2dd840` Aug 18 — full system theme, **Dancing Script**\n- `f984a14` Aug 20 — switch to **Great Vibes** everywhere\n- `418e662` Aug 21 — ensure *all* components use Great Vibes\n\nSo Dancing Script wasn''t cruft I wanted to delete. It was the original font, deliberately replaced. I should have read the history before calling it dead weight — the right cleanup is a deliberate decision by you, not my inference.\n\n**The lockout is worth understanding**, because it points at the theme itself. My earlier read was that nothing in Blood Build could prevent login — no PAM, no display manager, no keyboard config. But you got locked out, so something in that chain caused it. The most likely candidate is the one I flagged as a joke and then dropped:\n\n**Great Vibes as the global KDE UI font at size 14.** It''s a formal calligraphy script with very poor legibility and no bold or italic. If Plasma rendered its menus, dialogs, or — most damagingly — a password or lock-screen prompt in it, you could plausibly have been unable to read your way back in.\n\nTwo things I can do about that, and I''d suggest the first:\n\n1. **Audit the lockout path specifically.** Read the KDE lock screen, greeter, and SDDM/Plasma configs and check what font they''d actually use. If Great Vibes reaches the lock screen, that''s your lockout, and the fix is to scope the font to terminals and apps only, leaving system UI on a legible face.\n2. **Reconstruct the August sessions** from the git history — every commit, diff, and message is intact. Not a transcript, but the actual state changes.\n\nAlso: **`paru -S void-bin` is still running** (pid 27643) after all this time, and `void-bin` still isn''t installed. That looks stuck rather than slow. It''s holding the pacman lock, so rebooting now risks a half-written package database. I''d kill it and retry cleanly before you reboot:\n\n```bash\nkill 27643; sleep 3; sudo rm -f /var/lib/pacman/db.lck; sudo pacman -Syu\n```\n\nWhich do you want — the lockout font audit, or the August reconstruction?","time":{"start":1790448491522,"end":1790448497526}}');
