INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df0f9dd0001A8IAHBuCT2LvM6','msg_0df0f8b89001W2amrV9eAchkJ7','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790448737745,1790448737746,'{"type":"step-start"}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df0f9dd3001OCjUFYePPpgULk','msg_0df0f8b89001W2amrV9eAchkJ7','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790448737747,1790448742752,'{"type":"text","text":"Built `buildlog` at `~/Projects/buildlog`, on your shell-script conventions (`set -e`, `${BASH_SOURCE[0]}` dirs, `✅`-style output, README + install).\n\n**It solves the exact thing that bit you.** Session transcripts live in `~/.local/share/` and die with the machine. Code survives because you pushed it — but *decisions and fixes* never made it into commit messages. This logs those, in a git repo, so a rebuild costs you one `git clone`.\n\n```bash\nbuildlog build \"hermes-agent: makepkg started\"\nbuildlog fix   \"gtk font family -> Noto Sans fallback\"\nbuildlog env   # toolchain snapshot\nbuildlog push  # survive the next crash\n```\n\nI seeded it with this session''s real work — both Blood Build bugs, the Node 20→26 swap, the supercode 404s, the void-bin Chromium hang, and the lockout note. `buildlog env` also confirms your `hermes` at `0.21.5-1` and the toolchain.\n\n**One bug I hit and fixed while testing.** Fish ignores the `#!/bin/bash` shebang when you run a script directly, so `BASH_SOURCE` was empty and my `SCRIPT_DIR` resolved to your *current directory* — meaning it silently created a second log file wherever you happened to be standing. Only caught it because I tested in fish rather than bash. Now pinned to `$HOME/Projects/buildlog` with a fallback, verified from two different directories with no stray logs.\n\n**Not yet pushed** — no remote configured, so the log is local-only and would *not* survive a rebuild. That''s the whole point, so:\n\n```bash\ncd ~/Projects/buildlog\ngit remote add origin git@github.com:intricos777-dot/buildlog.git\nbuildlog push\n```\n\nThe repo doesn''t exist on GitHub yet; it''ll 404 until you create it (private, given your other tooling).\n\nTwo things I deliberately did **not** do:\n\n**Didn''t push or create the repo.** That''s a write to your account, and per your own standing instruction in this session I only commit when asked — you did say commit, and I committed locally, but pushing is a separate call.\n\n**Didn''t wire up `~/.local/bin` to bash.** Your `config.fish` already adds it at line 27, so `buildlog` works in your interactive shell. It fails in bash because bash has no `~/.local/bin` in `PATH`. Tell me if you want that added to `~/.bashrc`.\n\nTwo housekeeping items still stale from earlier:\n\n- **`paru` is still stuck** (pid 27643, 55+ min, 0 bytes progress) and holds the pacman lock. `kill 27643; sudo rm -f /var/lib/pacman/db.lck` before you reboot.\n- **The lockout font audit** is the one I''d still do. Your log now names the suspect — Great Vibes as the global KDE UI font — but nothing has verified it. If that''s what locked you out, the next reboot repeats it.","time":{"start":1790448737747,"end":1790448742751}}');
