v/null; then\n     25: pacman -S --noconfirm \"$cmd\" 2>/dev/null || true\n     35: pacstrap -c \"${WORKDIR}/chroot\" base linux linux-firmware mkinitcpio grub xorriso dosfstools mtools \n     42: rm -rf \"${ISO_DIR}\"\n     45: cp \"${WORKDIR}/chroot/boot/vmlinuz-linux\" \"${ISO_DIR}/boot/vmlinuz-zen\" 2>/dev/null || \\\n     47: cp \"${WORKDIR}/chroot/boot/initramfs-linux.img\" \"${ISO_DIR}/boot/initramfs-zen.img\" 2>/dev/null || \\\n     49: cp \"/boot/initramfs-linux-zen-fallback.img\" \"${ISO_DIR}/boot/initramfs-zen-fallback.img\" 2>/dev/null\n     54: cp -r \"${SCRIPT_DIR}/../zen-suite/zen-core\"/* \"${ISO_DIR}/zen-suite/\" 2>/dev/null || true\n     59: cp -r /home/sin/Projects/polsia/businesses/linux-zen-build/zen-suite/zen-core/* \"${ISO_DIR}/zen-suit\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /tmp/opencode\nT=$(cat ~/.config/gh/token.clean)\ncurl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer $T\" \"https://api.github.com/repos/intricos777-dot/zen-suite/contents/build-zen-suite-iso.sh\" 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys,base64,re\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\ns=base64.b64decode(d[''content'']).decode(''utf-8'',''replace'')\nprint(''  build-zen-suite-iso.sh lines:'',len(s.splitlines()))\nfor i,l in enumerate(s.splitlines(),1):\n    if re.search(r''\\brm\\s+-rf|mkfs|dd\\s+if=|wipefs|sgdisk|parted|shred|losetup|xorriso|mkisofs|>\\s*/dev/|curl.*\\|\\s*(ba)?sh'', l, re.I):\n        print(f''   {i:>4}: {l.strip()[:100]}'')\n\" 2>&1","time":{"start":1790449225160,"end":1790449225428}}}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df170ed7001OHcOs7mOXMvUrc','msg_0df1702020010gqXIuEH64FTBz','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790449225431,1790449225431,'{"reason":"tool-calls","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":131017,"input":38,"output":240,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"write":0,"read":130739}},"cost":0}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df17156d001yA6BqIqSGGb06c','msg_0df170ee50017CQCDA20I3s8wl','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790449227117,1790449227118,'{"type":"step-start"}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df171570001lYa8OzCMQGHUlg','msg_0df170ee50017CQCDA20I3s8wl','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790449227120,1790449233200,'{"type":"text","text":"These scripts build ISOs — they `pacstrap` a fresh chroot and run `grub-mkrescue` + `xorriso`. They don''t install to your disk. That''s the safe version of this task, and it''s genuinely doable.\n\nBut I''ve accumulated a lot of open items across these last few messages, and I want to lay them out plainly rather than keep saying yes to the newest one.\n\n**Blocking everything: `paru` is still running.** Over an hour, still on the Chromium clone, still holding the pacman lock. Every single install you''ve asked for — Steam, emulators, the zen suite, lin-antimalware, BDE — needs that cleared. One command from you:\n\n```bash\nkill 27643; sleep 3; sudo rm -f /var/lib/pacman/db.lck\n```\n\n**Ready to install, low risk, no lockout:**\n\n| Repo | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `lin-antimalware` | scanner, CLI, reports — no PAM, no sudo |\n| `business-health-monitor` | health scan + HTML report + daily cron |\n| `business-debug-wrappers` | debug wrappers |\n| `zen-suite` ISO build | builds an ISO via pacstrap; doesn''t touch your disk |\n\n**Needs your explicit go-ahead:**\n\n| Repo | Why |\n|---|---|\n| `zen-healer` | 7 `sudo` calls as a daemon, `snapper rollback`, `shell=True`. Hardcoded for user `sin`, you''re `livings`. |\n| `bde-security-biometrics` | **installs PAM modules.** Misconfiguration = no login, no password. |\n| `local-emergency-patrol` | unread; has `security/` and `deploy/` |\n\n**Premises that didn''t hold:**\n- No **21-layer encryption** repo exists in your 120. Your disk is already LUKS2 full-disk, working, and \"reinstalling\" it means reformatting and losing everything.\n- No **Kali arm**. You''re on Garuda, single-boot, one disk. If you thought Kali was here, it isn''t.\n- **Bold Great Vibes** isn''t possible, font ships Regular only.\n- **supercode** doesn''t exist on npm — both packages 404.\n\nTwo questions, and then I''ll move:\n\n1. **Do you have a Kali partition somewhere?** If the dual-boot existed before the rebuild, knowing what partition scheme you used matters before I build any ISO.\n2. **Which of the four low-risk installs should I start with** once the lock is clear? I''d do `lin-antimalware` and `business-health-monitor` first — they''re the tools that would''ve caught the problems you hit today.\n\nOne thing worth saying plainly: you mentioned being locked out of this device, and your rebuild history suggests a lot of infrastructure went with it. Before re-enabling a PAM-authenticated biometric daemon and a self-healing root daemon on a machine with no second recovery path, I''d want `zen-healer` reviewed line by line and the PAM module left uninstalled. I''m not refusing to help — I''ll do all of it, I just won''t batch the dangerous parts in with the safe ones.","time":{"start":1790449227120,"end":1790449233199}}');
