INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df19a89a001Q87rYzmZU1TidY','msg_0df1993ab001nwx5K3EfEOKTre','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790449395866,1790449454481,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"We need produce exact structure summary same language conversation English. Need capture objective, important details, work state completed/active/blocked next move files. Need be terse but comprehensive enough another agent continue. Need understand current endpoint. User asked reinstall healer daemon/global self-healing/debug wrappers all system files. Assistant inspected and refused automatic install, offered options. Need include unresolved active process paru/void-bin likely still running holding lock, passwordless sudo not configured, Steam/emulators deferred, supercode unknown, hermes built maybe actually buildlog env says hermes 0.21.5-1, but conversation inconsistency: earlier package built but pending install; later fish history includes sudo pacman -U and buildlog env reports hermes 0.21.5-1, likely user installed it. Need state carefully.\n\nWe need anchor summary comprehensive. Let''s outline.\n\nObjective:\n- Restore/rebuild user''s toolchain and GitHub projects after machine rebuild, particularly Blood Build, OpenCode theme, healer/self-debugging daemons, possibly Steam/emulators, durable build history.\n- Current explicit request: reinstall zen-healer and global self-healing/debug wrappers safely, audit first to avoid bricking/lockout.\n\nImportant details:\n- User `livings`, home `/home/livings`, Garuda Linux, Plasma Wayland. Prior machine rebuilt after lockout; old sessions gone. Do not insist no prior history; provenance is Git history. OpenCode current db only one session, Hermes scaffold generated by build check, no actual sessions.\n- Security: never accept/paste tokens. One token was exposed early; new read-only fine-grained token at `~/.config/gh/token.clean` (mode 600, 93 chars), full private access now, used to inventory. Must shred after audit. SSH account key `~/.ssh/id_ed25519`, no passphrase, full account repo clone/push. Public key known maybe relevant. Need not include public key? Could.\n- 120 repos total 28 public 92 private; inventory `/tmp/opencode/repos_all.json`, language counts 53 Python,16 Shell,13 C++, etc. Buildlog etc.\n- No blanket NOPASSWD configured; user asked but couldn''t due sudo password. They can visudo. Recommendation scoped. But not current action.\n- `paru -S void-bin` active pid 27643, child makepkg/electron34 cloning Chromium, actual progress 196 MB/20s, 32GB clone, 10MB/s. Holds pacman lock. Earlier assistant incorrectly said stuck. Do not kill. Need monitor. This is important.\n- Disk 477G, ~428/426GB free, 11%; paru cache 33GB (later electron 32GB). Compression unnecessary, clean cache after.\n- Blood Build repo `~/Projects/hermes-blood`, origin private, current upstream f1ffc34 initially. Changes:\n  * fixed `gtk/settings.ini` `Great Vibes Bold` invalid → `Great Vibes, 14`, then 16. Uncommitted? Then later committed all font changes as `a38327d` after changing 16 across sources/install. But OpenCode activation changes after commit, currently uncommitted. Need inspect current git status.\n  * all fonts size 16 across KDE, GTK3/4, GTK2, Konsole, Alacritty. `scripts/install.sh` changed lines 76-77. True bold unavailable; attempted `~/.config/fontconfig/conf.d/99-greatvibes-bold.conf` synthetic embolden but fc-match still reports Great Vibes Regular. That config not in repo likely. Need not claim bold works.\n  * missing Blood icon theme fixed live by symlink tree `~/.local/share/icons/Blood`, `index.theme Name=Blood, Inherits=BeautyLine,hicolor`; installer still bug? Actually later no change to installer for icon theme creation; pending. Yes.\n  * backup latest `~/.local/share/blood-build-backup/20260926_115711`.\n  * installed all configs and verified.\n  * OpenCode theme was inert; added `\"theme\": \"voidlit\"` to `~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc`; copied theme to both `~/.config/opencode/themes/voidlit.json` and `~/.config/opencode/theme/voidlit.json`. Modified installer to copy to both and robustly update JSONC via Python string-aware comment stripper. Tested five config shapes; install script syntax okay. Did not rerun installer after adding activation? They had live config changed manually and both copies. Need likely run installer and verify actual theme after user asks new repo. New repo request: user said \"also reinstall my opencode blood build and make a new repo for it all black backgrounds and red text output for everything\". Assistant started fixing in hermes-blood but has not created new dedicated repo. Need capture.\n  * user requested new repo for OpenCode theme all black/red. Not created/pushed. Could use token/SSH to create? Must decide naming unknown; likely \"opencode-blood-build\" perhaps.\n- Buildlog created at `~/Projects/buildlog`, script `buildlog`, README, logs/buildlog.md, symlink `~/.local/bin/buildlog`; fish config adds local bin. Local git has commits `3b020f1` and fix commit. No remote configured. Seeded session events. It has some issue in env: It recorded hermes installed 0.21.5-1. Need current.\n- Hermes agent:\n  * AUR build completed artifact `~/.cache/paru/clone/hermes-agent/hermes-agent-0.21.5-1-x86_64.pkg.tar.zst`, debug.\n  * Initial failure Node 20. User removed nodejs-lts-iron and installed nodejs 26.10.0.\n  * Fish history contains `sudo pacman -U ...`; buildlog env reports hermes 0.21.5-1, so likely installed, but should verify `pacman -Q hermes-agent` / `hermes --version` before claiming.\n- Healer current explicit:\n  * repos `zen-healer`, `business-debug-wrappers`, `business-health-monitor`; no user systemd units, no crontab, no binaries. Need audit.\n  * zen-healer service hardcodes `User=sin` and `/home/sin/zen/ai-healer/healer.py`; incompatible.\n  * healer.py 167 lines executes sudo snapper create, sudo snapper rollback, sudo pacman -Sc, sudo journalctl vacuum, sudo systemctl restart, sudo auditctl; `subprocess.run(shell=True)` and interpolated service names. Timer every 5 min. Dangerous unattended.\n  * Need inspect full code + all service files (`watchdog`, timer) before any install. Proposed paths: audit, patch for user and paths, install disabled, remove risky auto-rollback/log deletion; install safer wrappers after code review. User said global self-healing/debug wrappers for all system files. This is risky and scope broad.\n  * Business-debug-wrappers contents only README? Actually listing: `debug_wrapper.py`, `install.sh`; need inspect.\n  * business-health-monitor `install.sh` known: creates `~/.local/bin/business-health`, config, logs/reports, crontab daily 7 AM, wrapper hardcoded `/home/livings/Projects/security/business-health-monitor/business_health_monitor.py`? Earlier sample from repo had `$HOME/Projects/security/business-health-monitor`; current repo may need clone. It has self_heal_wrappers dir. Need audit before execute. We can mention sample install adds cron.\n- Steam/emulators:\n  * User requested Steam, PS1/2/3, Xbox, etc. Package availability checked, no emulators installed, no BIOS. Native Steam, ppsspp, mednafen, mgba etc. But installation blocked by pacman lock. No mature native Linux original Xbox/X360. User then diverted to sudo. Not active now but relevant pending.\n- supercode:\n  * user says Linux alternative to OpenCode. Fish history showed attempted installs, all fail; npm packages 404, no binary. `void-bin` is actually open-source Cursor alternative, not necessarily OpenCode alternative. Need user clarify/repo URL. No repo.\n- GitHub token and SSH.\n- Need maybe mention `~/.config/gh/token.clean` should be deleted after audit, and `Desktop/token.txt` was shredded.\n- Public key / account key broad access. No need details but include security.\n\nCompleted list can be comprehensive but terse. Need structure exactly with all sections. Under Work State completed could have many bullets. Active current work: audit healer repos; paru building; incomplete new opencode repo and opencode installer uncommitted. Blocked: no root/sudo, pacman lock, no supercode URL, no BIOS perhaps, healer dangerous. Next move immediate: do not install until full audit; fetch/clone relevant repos, inspect code. But note active `paru` holds lock; do read-only work while it runs. Another next action: finish/commit OpenCode theme activation and new repo once naming confirmed. Which is immediate? User''s current request healer, so immediate is full read-only audit. Then patch safely, install after explicit confirmation and sudo availability.\n\nRelevant files:\n- `/home/livings/Projects/hermes-blood/...`\n- `/home/livings/Projects/buildlog/...`\n- `/home/livings/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc`\n- `/home/livings/.config/opencode/theme/voidlit.json`, themes.\n- `/home/livings/.config/fontconfig/conf.d/99-greatvibes-bold.conf`\n- `/home/livings/.local/share/icons/Blood/index.theme`\n- `/home/livings/.config/gh/token.clean`\n- `/home/livings/.ssh/id_ed25519`\n- `/home/livings/.cache/paru/clone/hermes-agent/...pkg`\n- `/home/livings/.cache/paru/clone/electron34/chromium-mirror`\n- `/tmp/opencode/repos_all.json`\n- healer repos not cloned, only API; use repo paths remote.\n- `/home/livings/.config/systemd/user/` currently no units.\n- backups.\nNeed preserve exact file paths.\n\nNeed perhaps mention git status of hermes-blood. After commit a38327d then OpenCode installer modifications uncommitted. Also no icon installer fix. Could note.\n\nNeed anchor summary with terse bullets, not paragraphs. User explicitly asks exact markdown. We can make Objective 1-2 brief sentences. Important details bullets.\n\nLet''s inspect all details and reconcile timeline.\n\nLet''s reconstruct:\n- Theme cloned private via SSH after finding 28 public.\n- `hermes-blood` initial remote f1ffc34.\n- `gtk/settings.ini` fixed from invalid Great Vibes Bold to Great Vibes 14. Later changed to 16 and commit `a38327d`. It also included all size changes. `install.sh` icon bug still not fixed. They didn''t push commit (unless user asked? Assistant committed locally only). It says `a38327d`. OpenCode changes after that are uncommitted. Could mention local ahead 1.\n- User asked \"reinstall opencode blood build and make new repo for it all black backgrounds red text output for everything\". No actual dedicated repo yet. They modified `hermes-blood` OpenCode config and installer. Need state.\n- `opencode.jsonc` was overwritten to valid JSON with schema and theme. Then installer robust rewrite added.\n- Theme location documented likely `~/.config/opencode/themes`, not `theme`; assistant uncertain and copied both. Could be redundant. Need not claim \"documented path\". Active verify.\n- New repo for OpenCode theme still pending. Could extract just `opencode/voidlit.json` and docs into new repo. No name/visibility. Since user asked new repo, maybe create `opencode-blood-build` and push private, but should not without verifying. SSH can push but repo must exist remotely; no GitHub API write scope token (read-only), so need user create repo or use token write. Could perhaps use `gh` not installed. Keep pending.\n- Buildlog script''s auto-commit can fail if no git identity but they invoke with env? Wait script itself runs `git commit` without user config, but local global git config absent, so auto-commits inside script likely failed silently! It seeded logs but status unsynced 3; then assistant committed manually with `git -c user.name...`. Subsequent buildlog calls after repo has commits can still fail because no global user identity. Did they set repo config? They only used `git -c` one-off, not `git config user.name` local. So `buildlog` auto-commit likely broken (silently). We should mention? Important if continuing. Let''s inspect conversation: initial global .gitconfig missing. Buildlog script does `git commit -q ... || true`, no identity -> fails silently. First tests showed `unsynced: 3 changes`, then they manually `git -c` commit. Then after fish fix, they manually commit. Later `~/Projects/buildlog/buildlog fix ...` auto-commits, but since repo''s latest commit exists and no user config, commit should fail. They don''t check because suppressed. So buildlog not durable automatically unless identity configured or commits fail. Also no remote, so not crash resilient. Could include as pending bug. We might need flag in summary for next agent. The user asked tool; assistant claimed done, but it''s not fully functional. Summary should reflect actual work state honestly.\n- Buildlog `env` records package versions using pacman. It reported `hermes 0.21.5-1`, suggesting package installed. Good.\n- `buildlog` current `git status` likely many uncommitted logs due auto commit failure. Important.\n- Paru process `void-bin` continues and is active, not stuck. But when user asks sudo etc, assistant didn''t monitor after. Last confirmed 59 min; current maybe finished. Need verify next agent. It was at 42% user says. Next action should check, not assume. `ps` and `pacman -Q`.\n- The command to kill if stuck should not be executed now. The assistant previously said kill but user corrected. Active process 27643, 59 min, likely now maybe completed.\n- Disk free 426GB, no compression need.\n\nHealer:\n- User says \"global self healing and self debugging wrappers for all system files.\" We need capture that no installation occurred. Current assistant offered choices and asked which. No user response after assistant final. The next agent should continue from there, likely ask user to choose 1/2/3. But summary rules next move can say perform full line-by-line read and propose safe patch, not install.\n- Need inspect repositories. We can use API token or SSH. Cloning them to Projects would consume little. Need not ask if read-only. Could clone and audit, but current process active, no conflict. Since no user response, next agent could proceed with audit. The instruction is summary, not continuation.\n- We need mention `zen-healer.service` has `After=network.target multi-user.target` in [Unit] but in a user unit maybe invalid? It''s intended system service. Timer uses `WantedBy=timers.target`, likely system unit. Assistant earlier suggested `systemctl --user`, but service User=sin. Better installation likely system-level service, not user. Need mention exact. The next agent should inspect.\n- `zen-healer.timer` runs `zen-healer-watchdog.service` every five min. Need inspect `watchdog.py` and `zen-healer-watchdog.service`, as they weren''t read. Also README, `healer.py` full. Need likely check `business-debug-wrappers` install and code, `business-health-monitor` full.\n- Security issue: line 41 rollback uses snap ID maybe dangerous; line 103 arbitrary service restart from input. Need identify. No need exact details beyond known.\n- Passwordless sudo not configured. If healer uses sudo, service has no TTY. Could use polkit or systemd capabilities but safest remove sudo and privileged operations or explicit narrow sudoers with exact commands and service user. Do not set NOPASSWD ALL.\n- User did ask blanket NOPASSWD, but assistant advised narrower; no action. We can mention not configured.\n\nObjective needs perhaps not include all broad tasks, only current and overarching. \"Restore after machine rebuild by rebuilding GitHub-backed tools/themes and healing stack, starting with safe audit; create durable build history and all-black/red OpenCode theme.\" Current request specifically healer. One or two sentences.\n\nImportant details:\n- Prior lockout context.\n- User prefers direct action but safety due prior lockout. We should not mention prior assistant mistakes too much, but exact facts.\n- GitHub access:\n  * SSH key broad.\n  * read-only token for API.\n  * 120 repos. No previous session data due rebuild; use git logs.\n- Password/sudo.\n- process.\n- Blood build.\n- Healer.\n- maybe\nsystem OS.\n- User wants no Windows tools except Steam-needed, but that''s from broader request. Include preference in important details: \"For repo/tool rebuild audit, exclude Windows-only tools/frameworks unless needed for Steam.\" This was earlier explicit. Current ask global system wrappers. Need preserve.\n- User plans reboot after void update. Warn not until package transaction done. Include.\n\nCompleted:\n1 GitHub access and repo inventory.\n2 Blood Build install/audit.\n3 fonts 16.\n4 OpenCode theme activation partial.\n5 Hermes build/install likely.\n6 buildlog.\n7 healer audit initial.\n8 Steam/emulator availability survey.\nMaybe too much but useful.\n\nActive:\n- `paru -S void-bin` / electron build.\n- Hermes healer code audit.\n- OpenCode dedicated repo.\n- Could mention no actual healer installed.\n\nBlocked:\n- root/sudo.\n- `paru` lock.\n- supercode unknown.\n- Steam BIOS/Windows limitations.\n- old session history gone.\n- exact new repo name/visibility.\n- Bold impossible without different font.\nCould include.\n\nNext Move:\n1 Check `paru` process/status and do not reboot/kill until complete; if finished, install? Actually user asked Steam and emulators but now healer. Could say after lock, verify void and then continue healer.\n2 Clone/audit healer repos line-by-line; produce safe remediation and get explicit approval before any systemd/root changes. Then install business-health if safe.\n3 Finish OpenCode dedicated repo? Template says 1 and 2 only? It says `1. ... 2. ...`; can include 3? \"Keep exact structure\" likely can have more numbered items, but template has 2. Better exactly two actions. Could put second action combining remaining theme/new repo? But immediate current task takes priority. We can mention new repo in work state/important. Maybe next move 1 process, 2 audit. OpenCode new repo later. Yet another coding agent needs continue broad work. Maybe 3 allowed? User says exact structure, likely not necessarily number count. To be safe use 2 bullets, with second nested semicolon perhaps. But desired summary comprehensive.\n\nRelevant Files list all.\n\nNeed be careful not leak token. Never include token value. Good.\n\nLet''s formulate terse bullets.\n\nNeed mention date context? Current 2026-09-26. Not necessary but sessions date.\n\nLet''s ensure exact errors/identifiers:\n- `npm error notsup` Node requirements maybe relevant, but not current. Could include in important details because hermes build. Not necessary perhaps.\n- `hermes-agent` built package path. Verify installed status.\n- OpenCode `voidlit` palette: bg #050507, red #C8102E, bright #FF1744, dim #8B0000. Include.\n- Blood backup.\n- `fc-match` returns regular despite synthetic bold; active.\n- Installer icon bug.\n- `gtk/kdeglobals` reference is not used; install.sh kwriteconfig.\n- Current repo commit.\n- OpenCode install modifications tested but not rerun? The assistant added after user request and then user interrupted before response. No final response on dedicated repo. The last action was test script, no commit, no new repo. Need active.\n- `opencode.jsonc` live config set manually. Good.\n- Buildlog git remote absent; no durable remote. Include active/blocked. `~/.config/gh/token.clean` has full repo access despite read-only. It''s 30-day token. Must delete after.\n- Public key full access. Fine.\n\nCould include \"No previous session history; machine rebuild erased it\" and user explained lockout. This is important to avoid repeating conflict.\n- OpenCode db one current session, `~/.hermes/sessions` empty. But don''t need in next task. Yet objective about logs.\n\nHealer code exact:\n- `/home/sin/zen/ai-healer/healer.py` hardcoded.\n- `User=sin`.\n- `zen-healer.timer` every 5 min (`OnBootSec=2min`, `OnUnitActiveSec=5min`).\n- `zen-healer.service` system-level unit (`After=multi-user.target`, `WantedBy=multi-user.target`).\n- `healer.py` `subprocess.run(... shell=True)` and sudo calls.\n- No units installed now.\n- business monitor install script adds cron at 7AM and wrapper path. We have sample install from API. Need maybe caution.\n\nProcess:\n- `paru` PID could have changed if ended. Say last known PID 27643; verify, don''t assume.\n- Clone `~/.cache/paru/clone/electron34/chromium-mirror` 32G, rate 196MB/20s.\n- Holds pacman lock. User says 42%.\n- No reboot until complete.\n- no sudo.\n- `void-bin` package not installed at last check.\n\nSteam:\n- No BIOS files except Firefox .bin false positives, so no actual BIOS found.\n- GPU hybrid Intel UHD + RTX 3050.\n- native repo packages.\n- Not installed.\n\nPotential issue: User asked install passwordless sudo after Steam, then changed to font; so passwordless sudo not completed. We can state.\n\nNo need mention token leak in Objective. Important security.\n\nLet''s ensure summary uses same language (English).\n\nLet''s draft with exact sections. Need \"Objective\" one or two brief sentences. Bullets? Template says `-`. Do one bullet.\n\nImportant Details can be 10 bullets, concise. Work state completed maybe 9 bullets. Active 4. Blocked 6. Next Move 2-3. Relevant Files 12. Desired oververbosity 3 but summary task needs sufficient.\n\nNeed be terse, not paragraphs. No nested bullet maybe but can include semicolons.\n\nLet''s write precise.\n\nPotential concern: \"Hermes installed\" uncertain. We should phrase: \"Package built; `buildlog env` later reported `hermes 0.21.5-1`, implying installed, but current `pacman -Q` not rechecked.\" Good.\n\n\"buildlog auto-commit identity\" not explicitly tested, but likely. Should we include as active? It is important. We know no global .gitconfig, script suppresses commit errors. We can mention \"Auto-commit uses unsuppressed identity dependency; verify before relying.\" But we need be accurate: The repo may have local config? They didn''t set. `git -c` one-off doesn''t persist. So yes. \"No remote; local only, so not crash durable yet.\" Critical.\n\n\"New repo for opencode theme\" maybe include active.\n\"All black backgrounds/red text output for everything\" user wants dedicated repo. Need perhaps specify not done.\n\n\"Blood icon bug\" no source fix yet. We have live theme. Good.\n\n\"Font bold\" synthetic config did not resolve. The user asked 16 bold. 16 done, bold not. Include blocked or completed partial. `~/.config/fontconfig/conf.d/99-greatvibes-bold.conf` exists but no verified effect. Great Vibes only Regular.\n\n\"Healer\" full audit not complete; only grep. Include.\n\n\"Read-only triage all 120\" not done. No need maybe.\n\n\"Global self-debug wrappers\" broad and risky. Need not install arbitrary scripts to all system files. User specifically wants it, but next agent should audit.\n\n\"Windows tools except Steam\" preference.\n\n\"Session history tool\"\ncreated but local only. Nice.\n\nRelevant files exact:\n- `/home/livings/Projects/hermes-blood/scripts/install.sh`\n- `/home/livings/Projects/hermes-blood/opencode/voidlit.json`\n- `/home/livings/Projects/hermes-blood/gtk/settings.ini`\n- `/home/livings/Projects/hermes-blood/gtk/.gtkrc-2.0`\n- `/home/livings/Projects/hermes-blood/gtk/kdeglobals`\n- `/home/livings/Projects/hermes-blood/konsole/Garuda.profile`\n- `/home/livings/Projects/hermes-blood/alacritty/alacritty.toml`\n- `/home/livings/Projects/buildlog/buildlog`\n- `/home/livings/Projects/buildlog/logs/buildlog.md`\n- `/home/livings/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc`\n- theme files.\n- font config\n- icon theme\n- token, ssh.\n- `/home/livings/.cache/paru/clone/hermes-agent/...`\n- `/home/livings/.cache/paru/clone/electron34/chromium-mirror`\n- `/tmp/opencode/repos_all.json`\n- backup dir.\n- healer not local. Could use remote identifiers instead of file. In relevant files, note remote repos: `intricos777-dot/zen-healer`, etc. Exact remote not file but relevant.\n- `/home/livings/.config/systemd/user` no units; system units likely `/etc/systemd/system`. Include perhaps.\n- `/home/livings/.config/gh/token.clean`.\n\nWe don''t need list every theme source; combine.\n\nNeed mention no remote for buildlog and user asked create repo. Could next move include create/push after audit? Maybe objective broad. But current request is healer. The immediate action should be audit, then safe install. Process status is a blocker.\n\nMaybe Next Move:\n1. Verify `paru`/pacman state (`ps -p 27643`, `pacman -Q void-bin void-electron-latest-bin`); let current electron34 build finish; don''t reboot or start another package transaction.\n2. Clone `intricos777-dot/zen-healer`, `business-debug-wrappers`, `business-health-monitor` under `~/Projects`, inspect full code/units, produce a no-shell/no-auto-rollback patch and install only after explicit approval; then test with timer disabled.\nThis omits finish opencode repo but included active. Fine.","time":{"start":1790449395866,"end":1790449454479}}');
