INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df1a3909001fI2JE2vUiTYk8i','msg_0df1a306d0011TTk5eN5gLaaNw','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790449432842,1790449436419,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"The user pasted a terminal output showing a git clone failure. This looks like paru (AUR helper) trying to clone an electron34 chromium-mirror repo (huge, 37 GiB). The clone failed with early EOF.\n\nThe user hasn''t asked a question explicitly, just pasted output. I should respond concisely with help. Let me think about what''s actually going on.\n\nThis is a known issue: the `electron34` AUR package''s source is a chromium-mirror git repo of enormous size. The clone fails due to network interruption. Solutions:\n- Retry the clone manually with more robustness (git config http.postBuffer, increase lowSpeedLimit, use partial clone with --filter=blob:none)\n- Download the tarball/snapshot instead of git clone\n\nActually for electron34 AUR, sources include chromium-mirror? Let me check. The electron34 package PKGBUILD has sources like `electron-v${pkgver}-linux-x64.zip` from github releases. The chromium-mirror thing... maybe the user''s own PKGBUILD.\n\nI should ask/advise. Let me first check the environment — is paru available, what''s in the cache dir.\n\nLet me be helpful and investigate a bit.\n\nThe most useful practical advice: `git clone --filter=blob:none --depth 1` or retry. But the real fix: paru/git-clone failures of huge repos → use `GIT_HTTP_LOW_SPEED_LIMIT` / retry, or better: avoid the git source entirely.\n\nLet me look at what''s on disk to give a concrete answer.","time":{"start":1790449432841,"end":1790449436415}}');
