INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df1a5101001enqRmfq1UbNDfj','msg_0df1a49ec001wT7KDlikuFtYuB','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790449438977,1790449441430,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"The user wants me to fix the failed clone. Let me understand the situation first.\n\nThe `chromium-mirror` bare repo is being cloned into `/home/livings/.cache/paru/clone/electron34/chromium-mirror`. It''s 37 GiB and failed with early EOF. The directory doesn''t exist now (paru cleaned it up after failure).\n\nLet me look at the PKGBUILD to see how the source is declared, and understand whether we even need a full clone.\n\nKey insight: the electron34 PKGBUILD probably has a VCS source pointing at github.com/electron/chromium-mirror which is a giant repo. A better approach:\n1. Retry the clone with a resumable/robust method (`git clone --filter=blob:none` partial clone, or just retry until it works).\n2. Or clone the parent repo shallowly and only fetch the needed refs.\n\nLet me check the PKGBUILD source lines.\n\nActually, a smarter fix: for `electron34` in AUR, the VCS source is likely `git+https://github.com/electron/chromium-mirror.git` with a specific tag. The standard AUR helper clone does a full clone (not shallow), which is 37+ GB. We can avoid this.\n\nLet me first inspect the PKGBUILD.","time":{"start":1790449438977,"end":1790449441425}}');
