INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df244c46001IAWYsKXFzze3Eo','msg_0df2447f9001BLKs2ya3A4glOk','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790450093126,1790450102335,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"The checkout now works: HEAD → 5c0cb964bca15fcf41718d54f4b8d70d6b9079de, on branch `makepkg`, in 32s.\n\nAll three makepkg code paths verified. Let me now:\n1. Verify DEPS and key files exist in the worktree.\n2. Clean up the verify dir.\n3. Then tackle the next issue: the 164 `chromium-mirror_*` DEPS sources, which makepkg will full-mirror. That could be another huge chunk of data and is the next real wall.\n\nLet me check what the verify worktree contains and its size, then clean up.\n\nThen assess the DEPS repos. To assess without cloning, I can query the actual DEPS file in the chromium checkout for the git URLs, and then estimate sizes. Actually a cheaper approach: for each of the 164 sources, we can create a shallow fetch of just the required commit. That''s a script. I can write a helper that pre-seeds ALL 164 mirror dirs shallowly at their required commit, exactly the same trick.\n\nThat''s the scalable fix: a loop over all `git+URL#commit=XXX` sources, doing `git init --bare` + `fetch --depth 1 <commit>`. For commit-pinned sources, fetching a specific SHA requires the server to allow `uploadpack.allowReachableSHA1InWant` / `allowAnySHA1InWant`. GitHub supports fetching arbitrary commit SHAs? GitHub has `uploadpack.allowAnySHA1InWant` enabled? Actually GitHub supports `allowReachableSHA1InWant`... Hmm, for GitHub, fetching an arbitrary commit SHA is generally NOT supported unless it''s a ref tip. But googlesource.com DOES support fetching arbitrary SHAs (it has allowAnySHA1InWant enabled).\n\nBut actually — the DEPS commit SHAs are the current tips of those repos'' master branches, so fetching the default branch shallowly at depth 1 will include them. Let me verify: `third_party/angle#commit=ce13a00a...` — is that the tip of angle''s main? At the time the PKGBUILD was generated, yes.\n\nHmm, but not guaranteed. Safer: fetch the default branch with depth 1, then check if the commit exists; if not, deepen.\n\nThis is getting complex. Let me first measure the actual scale of the problem before engineering: how big are those 164 repos? I can query a few with `git ls-remote` (cheap) and estimate, or do a `git clone --mirror --depth 1` for each which is exactly the trick.\n\nActually, the pragmatic approach: pre-seed ALL git sources shallowly using a script. For `#commit=` sources, try `git fetch --depth 1 origin <sha>`; if that fails, fetch the default branch shallowly and deepen until the commit is present (or unshallow that repo).\n\nBut the user asked to \"fix that please\" and then chose \"fix the paru build here on Garuda\". The immediate crash is fixed. Let me report that, clean up, and then tackle the DEPS repos as the next step — measuring first.\n\nLet me be efficient: verify the worktree contents, clean up, and in parallel start measuring the DEPS repo sizes via a shallow-mirror dry run on a few of the biggest suspects.\n\nActually the most valuable next step: write the general pre-seed script and run it for all 165 sources. That both fixes the next wall and tells us the total size. Let me do it.\n\nBut first, let me confirm the PKGBUILD''s source list is what I think and extract the git sources programmatically. Also need to know the directory naming: makepkg''s `get_filename` for `name::git+url#fragment` → `name`. And `get_filepath` returns `$SRCDEST/$filename` if SRCDEST set, else... let me check. In makepkg, `get_filepath`:\n\n```bash\nget_filepath() {\n\tlocal netfile=$1\n\tif [[ -n $SRCDEST ]]; then\n\t\tprintf ''%s/%s'' \"$SRCDEST\" \"$netfile\"\n\telse\n\t\tprintf ''%s'' \"$netfile\"\n\tfi\n}\n```\nHmm, roughly — but for VCS sources `download_git` computes `dir=$(get_filepath \"$netfile\")` where netfile is `repo` (the filename) already... let me re-read.\n\n```bash\nlocal netfile=$1\nlocal dir=$(get_filepath \"$netfile\")\n[[ -z \"$dir\" ]] && dir=\"$SRCDEST/$(get_filename \"$netfile\")\"\nlocal repo=$(get_filename \"$netfile\")\n```\n\nSo `get_filepath` is called with the *netfile* (full source entry). Let me look at makepkg''s actual get_filepath in util/pkgbuild.sh.\n\nLet me check that, plus verify the worktree, plus clean up.\n\nLet me run these.","time":{"start":1790450093126,"end":1790450102334}}');
