resolve SCRIPT_DIR via $HOME, BASH_SOURCE is empty under fish shebang-less exec\n3b020f1 buildlog: durable build journal tool\n--- branches/stash ---\n* master\n--- ever-tracked agent-ish files ---\n","metadata":{"output":"=========== hermes-blood ===========\n2ae226a fix: install voidlit to opencode theme/ lookup path and activate it in opencode.jsonc\na38327d fonts: bump Great Vibes to 16pt across all components\nf1ffc34 chore: tune gtk settings and install script\n418e662 fix: ensure all components use Great Vibes font\n5dfbfab fix: remove stray ] from BlackRed.colorscheme Color7Intense and ForegroundIntense\nf984a14 restore: switch font from Dancing Script to Great Vibes everywhere\nb2dd840 Blood Build: full system theme (black bg, red text, Dancing Script font)\n968b304 Blood skin + cursive fonts\n--- branches/stash ---\n* main\n  remotes/origin/HEAD -> origin/main\n  remotes/origin/main\n--- ever-tracked agent-ish files ---\n=========== zen-hardening ===========\n2fe0d82 zen-hardening: sysctl, faillock and firewalld workstation hardening configs\n--- branches/stash ---\n* master\n--- ever-tracked agent-ish files ---\n=========== nyan-gfsf-alert ===========\nedb9cd5 nyan-gfsf-alert: pixel-art nyan cat intrusion alert (PyQt6, zenity/kdialog/terminal fallbacks)\n--- branches/stash ---\n* master\n--- ever-tracked agent-ish files ---\n=========== buildlog ===========\n2d83dd3 fix: resolve SCRIPT_DIR via $HOME, BASH_SOURCE is empty under fish shebang-less exec\n3b020f1 buildlog: durable build journal tool\n--- branches/stash ---\n* master\n--- ever-tracked agent-ish files ---\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"for r in hermes-blood zen-hardening nyan-gfsf-alert buildlog; do\n  d=~/Projects/$r\n  echo \"=========== $r ===========\"\n  git -C \"$d\" log --all --oneline 2>/dev/null | head -20\n  echo \"--- branches/stash ---\"\n  git -C \"$d\" branch -a 2>/dev/null; git -C \"$d\" stash list 2>/dev/null\n  echo \"--- ever-tracked agent-ish files ---\"\n  git -C \"$d\" log --all --diff-filter=D --name-only --pretty=format: 2>/dev/null | sort -u | grep -iE \"agent|hermes|daemon|service|\\.timer|\\.service|systemd|opencode\" | head -15\ndone","time":{"start":1790450282565,"end":1790450282616}}}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df273049001bVIGkOGAXEQAH3','msg_0df27046f001id49WMVVQojkz6','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790450282569,1790450282613,'{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_function_0iglphphk7v2_2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"echo \"=== buildlog README ===\"; cat ~/Projects/buildlog/README.md\necho; echo \"=== buildlog logs dir ===\"; ls -la ~/Projects/buildlog/logs/\necho; echo \"=== buildlog script ===\"; head -60 ~/Projects/buildlog/buildlog"},"output":"=== buildlog README ===\n# buildlog\n\nDurable build/audit journal. Solves one problem: **session transcripts die with the machine.**\n\nOpencode and hermes keep session history in `~/.local/share/` and `~/.hermes/` — wiped on rebuild.\nCode survives because it was pushed. This logs the *decisions and fixes* that never made it into a commit message.\n\n## Install\n\n```bash\nln -s ~/Projects/buildlog/buildlog ~/.local/bin/buildlog\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n```bash\nbuildlog build \"hermes-agent: makepkg started\"\nbuildlog ok    \"126MB pkg built\"\nbuildlog fail  \"void-bin: paru stuck cloning Chromium\"\nbuildlog fix   \"gtk/settings.ini: bad font family -> Noto Sans fallback\"\nbuildlog env   # snapshot toolchain versions\nbuildlog tail 40\nbuildlog push  # push to remote\n```\n\nEntries are markdown, one `## <timestamp> · <category>` section each, appended to `logs/buildlog.md`.\nEvery entry auto-commits, so `git log` is the audit trail.\n\n## Recovering after a rebuild\n\n```bash\ngit clone <remote> && cd buildlog && buildlog tail 100\n```\n\n\n=== buildlog logs dir ===\ntotal 4\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 livings livings   22 Sep 26 11:51 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 livings livings   70 Sep 26 11:51 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 livings livings 2595 Sep 26 11:58 buildlog.md\n\n=== buildlog script ===\n#!/bin/bash\n# buildlog — durable build/audit journal for crash recovery\n# Appends timestamped entries to a git repo so session context survives a rebuild.\n\nset -e\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$HOME/Projects/buildlog\"\n[ -d \"$SCRIPT_DIR\" ] || SCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]:-$0}\")\" && pwd)\"\nLOG_DIR=\"${BUILDLOG_DIR:-$SCRIPT_DIR/logs}\"\nENTRY_FILE=\"$LOG_DIR/buildlog.md\"\nSTATE_FILE=\"$LOG_DIR/.state\"\n\nmkdir -p \"$LOG_DIR\"\n\ncmd=\"${1:-help}\"\nshift || true\n\ntimestamp() { date ''+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S''; }\n\nensure_header() {\n    if [ ! -f \"$ENTRY_FILE\" ]; then\n        cat > \"$ENTRY_FILE\" << ''EOF''\n# Build Log\n\nDurable journal of builds, audits, and fixes. Survives system rebuilds.\n\nFormat: one `## <timestamp> · <category>` section per entry.\nEOF\n    fi\n}\n\nrecord() {\n    category=\"$1\"; shift\n    message=\"$*\"\n    ensure_header\n    printf ''\\n## %s · %s\\n\\n%s\\n'' \"$(timestamp)\" \"$category\" \"$message\" >> \"$ENTRY_FILE\"\n    if [ -d \"$SCRIPT_DIR/.git\" ]; then\n        git -C \"$SCRIPT_DIR\" add -A >/dev/null 2>&1 || true\n        git -C \"$SCRIPT_DIR\" commit -q -m \"$category: $message\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true\n    fi\n    printf ''  [✓] logged: %s\\n'' \"$message\"\n}\n\ncase \"$cmd\" in\n    build)\n        record \"build\" \"started: ${*:-unnamed}\"\n        ;;\n    ok)\n        record \"ok\" \"${*:-completed}\"\n        ;;\n    fail)\n        record \"FAIL\" \"${*:-unknown failure}\"\n        ;;\n    fix)\n        record \"fix\" \"${*:-no detail}\"\n        ;;\n    note)\n        record \"note\" \"${*:-no detail}\"\n        ;;\n    env)\n","metadata":{"output":"=== buildlog README ===\n# buildlog\n\nDurable build/audit journal. Solves one problem: **session transcripts die with the machine.**\n\nOpencode and hermes keep session history in `~/.local/share/` and `~/.hermes/` — wiped on rebuild.\nCode survives because it was pushed. This logs the *decisions and fixes* that never made it into a commit message.\n\n## Install\n\n```bash\nln -s ~/Projects/buildlog/buildlog ~/.local/bin/buildlog\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n```bash\nbuildlog build \"hermes-agent: makepkg started\"\nbuildlog ok    \"126MB pkg built\"\nbuildlog fail  \"void-bin: paru stuck cloning Chromium\"\nbuildlog fix   \"gtk/settings.ini: bad font family -> Noto Sans fallback\"\nbuildlog env   # snapshot toolchain versions\nbuildlog tail 40\nbuildlog push  # push to remote\n```\n\nEntries are markdown, one `## <timestamp> · <category>` section each, appended to `logs/buildlog.md`.\nEvery entry auto-commits, so `git log` is the audit trail.\n\n## Recovering after a rebuild\n\n```bash\ngit clone <remote> && cd buildlog && buildlog tail 100\n```\n\n\n=== buildlog logs dir ===\ntotal 4\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 livings livings   22 Sep 26 11:51 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 livings livings   70 Sep 26 11:51 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 livings livings 2595 Sep 26 11:58 buildlog.md\n\n=== buildlog script ===\n#!/bin/bash\n# buildlog — durable build/audit journal for crash recovery\n# Appends timestamped entries to a git repo so session context survives a rebuild.\n\nset -e\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$HOME/Projects/buildlog\"\n[ -d \"$SCRIPT_DIR\" ] || SCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]:-$0}\")\" && pwd)\"\nLOG_DIR=\"${BUILDLOG_DIR:-$SCRIPT_DIR/logs}\"\nENTRY_FILE=\"$LOG_DIR/buildlog.md\"\nSTATE_FILE=\"$LOG_DIR/.state\"\n\nmkdir -p \"$LOG_DIR\"\n\ncmd=\"${1:-help}\"\nshift || true\n\ntimestamp() { date ''+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S''; }\n\nensure_header() {\n    if [ ! -f \"$ENTRY_FILE\" ]; then\n        cat > \"$ENTRY_FILE\" << ''EOF''\n# Build Log\n\nDurable journal of builds, audits, and fixes. Survives system rebuilds.\n\nFormat: one `## <timestamp> · <category>` section per entry.\nEOF\n    fi\n}\n\nrecord() {\n    category=\"$1\"; shift\n    message=\"$*\"\n    ensure_header\n    printf ''\\n## %s · %s\\n\\n%s\\n'' \"$(timestamp)\" \"$category\" \"$message\" >> \"$ENTRY_FILE\"\n    if [ -d \"$SCRIPT_DIR/.git\" ]; then\n        git -C \"$SCRIPT_DIR\" add -A >/dev/null 2>&1 || true\n        git -C \"$SCRIPT_DIR\" commit -q -m \"$category: $message\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true\n    fi\n    printf ''  [✓] logged: %s\\n'' \"$message\"\n}\n\ncase \"$cmd\" in\n    build)\n        record \"build\" \"started: ${*:-unnamed}\"\n        ;;\n    ok)\n        record \"ok\" \"${*:-completed}\"\n        ;;\n    fail)\n        record \"FAIL\" \"${*:-unknown failure}\"\n        ;;\n    fix)\n        record \"fix\" \"${*:-no detail}\"\n        ;;\n    note)\n        record \"note\" \"${*:-no detail}\"\n        ;;\n    env)\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"echo \"=== buildlog README ===\"; cat ~/Projects/buildlog/README.md\necho; echo \"=== buildlog logs dir ===\"; ls -la ~/Projects/buildlog/logs/\necho; echo \"=== buildlog script ===\"; head -60 ~/Projects/buildlog/buildlog","time":{"start":1790450282579,"end":1790450282613}}}');
