INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df273a3f001Zjjh1KaoPdRMAy','msg_0df2730840012UkbUZ6ACpazeZ','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790450285119,1790450285137,'{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_function_2cu7a97vpl4l_1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/livings/Projects/buildlog/logs/buildlog.md"},"output":"<path>/home/livings/Projects/buildlog/logs/buildlog.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Build Log\n2: \n3: Durable journal of builds, audits, and fixes. Survives system rebuilds.\n4: \n5: Format: one `## <timestamp> · <category>` section per entry.\n6: \n7: ## 2026-09-26 11:51:45 · build\n8: \n9: started: hermes-blood: cloned via SSH, ran install.sh\n10: \n11: ## 2026-09-26 11:51:45 · fix\n12: \n13: gtk/settings.ini: ''Great Vibes Bold'' is not a real family -> fontconfig fell back to Noto Sans; changed to ''Great Vibes, 14''\n14: \n15: ## 2026-09-26 11:51:45 · fix\n16: \n17: install.sh:75 sets Plasma icon theme to Blood but repo ships no icons/ dir -> all desktop icons would vanish; created ~/.local/share/icons/Blood inheriting BeautyLine,hicolor\n18: \n19: ## 2026-09-26 11:51:45 · ok\n20: \n21: verified all 9 configs, valid TOML/JSON/YAML, konsole profile->colorscheme chain intact\n22: ## 2026-09-26 11:51:48 · env\n23: \n24: ```\n25: os        : Garuda Linux\n26: kernel    : 7.2.7-zen1-1-zen\n27: node      : v26.10.0\n28: python    : Python 3.14.7\n29: opencode  : 1.18.32-1\n30: hermes    : 0.21.5-1\n31: ```\n32: \n33: ## 2026-09-26 11:51:48 · FAIL\n34: \n35: supercode: 4 install attempts, all failed - npm @kirmad/supercode and supercode both 404 Not Found\n36: \n37: ## 2026-09-26 11:51:48 · FAIL\n38: \n39: void-bin: paru stuck 55min cloning all of Chromium (code.sh source redirects to chromium mirror); 0 bytes in 15s - AUR packaging bug\n40: \n41: ## 2026-09-26 11:51:48 · ok\n42: \n43: hermes-agent 0.21.5-1 built via makepkg (126MB pkg.tar.zst) after swapping nodejs-lts-iron 20 -> nodejs 26.10.0\n44: \n45: ## 2026-09-26 11:51:48 · note\n46: \n47: machine was rebuilt after a lockout; prior session history lost. 120 repos intact via git remote. Prime lockout suspect: Great Vibes as global KDE UI font (calligraphy, size 14, no bold/italic) reaching lock screen + dialogs\n48: \n49: ## 2026-09-26 11:57:30 · fix\n50: \n51: fonts: bumped Great Vibes 10/12/14 -> 16pt across all 6 locations (kdeglobals font/fixed, gtk-3.0, gtk-4.0, gtkrc-2.0, Garuda.profile, alacritty). Repo sources + install.sh updated so it survives re-install. Great Vibes has only a Regular weight; added fontconfig synthetic-embolden rule at ~/.config/fontconfig/conf.d/99-greatvibes-bold.conf\n52: \n53: ## 2026-09-26 11:58:35 · fix\n54: \n55: opencode: voidlit.json was installed but NEVER ACTIVATED - opencode.jsonc had no \"theme\" key, so the black/red theme was inert since first install. Fixed by adding theme:voidlit to opencode.jsonc, installing to ~/.config/opencode/theme/ as well as themes/, and adding an activation step to install.sh (string-aware comment stripper so URLs in $schema survive). Tested against 5 config shapes.\n56: \n57: ## 2026-09-26 11:58:35 · fix\n58: \n59: fonts: Great Vibes 10/12/14 -> 16pt across all 6 locations; repo sources + install.sh updated (commit a38327d). No true bold available - font ships Regular only.\n\n(End of file - total 59 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Build Log\n\nDurable journal of builds, audits, and fixes. Survives system rebuilds.\n\nFormat: one `## <timestamp> · <category>` section per entry.\n\n## 2026-09-26 11:51:45 · build\n\nstarted: hermes-blood: cloned via SSH, ran install.sh\n\n## 2026-09-26 11:51:45 · fix\n\ngtk/settings.ini: ''Great Vibes Bold'' is not a real family -> fontconfig fell back to Noto Sans; changed to ''Great Vibes, 14''\n\n## 2026-09-26 11:51:45 · fix\n\ninstall.sh:75 sets Plasma icon theme to Blood but repo ships no icons/ dir -> all desktop icons would vanish; created ~/.local/share/icons/Blood inheriting BeautyLine,hicolor\n\n## 2026-09-26 11:51:45 · ok\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/livings/Projects/buildlog/logs/buildlog.md","text":"# Build Log\n\nDurable journal of builds, audits, and fixes. Survives system rebuilds.\n\nFormat: one `## <timestamp> · <category>` section per entry.\n\n## 2026-09-26 11:51:45 · build\n\nstarted: hermes-blood: cloned via SSH, ran install.sh\n\n## 2026-09-26 11:51:45 · fix\n\ngtk/settings.ini: ''Great Vibes Bold'' is not a real family -> fontconfig fell back to Noto Sans; changed to ''Great Vibes, 14''\n\n## 2026-09-26 11:51:45 · fix\n\ninstall.sh:75 sets Plasma icon theme to Blood but repo ships no icons/ dir -> all desktop icons would vanish; created ~/.local/share/icons/Blood inheriting BeautyLine,hicolor\n\n## 2026-09-26 11:51:45 · ok\n\nverified all 9 configs, valid TOML/JSON/YAML, konsole profile->colorscheme chain intact\n## 2026-09-26 11:51:48 · env\n\n```\nos        : Garuda Linux\nkernel    : 7.2.7-zen1-1-zen\nnode      : v26.10.0\npython    : Python 3.14.7\nopencode  : 1.18.32-1\nhermes    : 0.21.5-1\n```\n\n## 2026-09-26 11:51:48 · FAIL\n\nsupercode: 4 install attempts, all failed - npm @kirmad/supercode and supercode both 404 Not Found\n\n## 2026-09-26 11:51:48 · FAIL\n\nvoid-bin: paru stuck 55min cloning all of Chromium (code.sh source redirects to chromium mirror); 0 bytes in 15s - AUR packaging bug\n\n## 2026-09-26 11:51:48 · ok\n\nhermes-agent 0.21.5-1 built via makepkg (126MB pkg.tar.zst) after swapping nodejs-lts-iron 20 -> nodejs 26.10.0\n\n## 2026-09-26 11:51:48 · note\n\nmachine was rebuilt after a lockout; prior session history lost. 120 repos intact via git remote. Prime lockout suspect: Great Vibes as global KDE UI font (calligraphy, size 14, no bold/italic) reaching lock screen + dialogs\n\n## 2026-09-26 11:57:30 · fix\n\nfonts: bumped Great Vibes 10/12/14 -> 16pt across all 6 locations (kdeglobals font/fixed, gtk-3.0, gtk-4.0, gtkrc-2.0, Garuda.profile, alacritty). Repo sources + install.sh updated so it survives re-install. Great Vibes has only a Regular weight; added fontconfig synthetic-embolden rule at ~/.config/fontconfig/conf.d/99-greatvibes-bold.conf\n\n## 2026-09-26 11:58:35 · fix\n\nopencode: voidlit.json was installed but NEVER ACTIVATED - opencode.jsonc had no \"theme\" key, so the black/red theme was inert since first install. Fixed by adding theme:voidlit to opencode.jsonc, installing to ~/.config/opencode/theme/ as well as themes/, and adding an activation step to install.sh (string-aware comment stripper so URLs in $schema survive). Tested against 5 config shapes.\n\n## 2026-09-26 11:58:35 · fix\n\nfonts: Great Vibes 10/12/14 -> 16pt across all 6 locations; repo sources + install.sh updated (commit a38327d). No true bold available - font ships Regular only.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":59,"totalLines":59,"truncated":false}},"title":"home/livings/Projects/buildlog/logs/buildlog.md","time":{"start":1790450285124,"end":1790450285136}}}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df273a53001365FMd9rWXymVV','msg_0df2730840012UkbUZ6ACpazeZ','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790450285139,1790450285139,'{"reason":"tool-calls","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":46557,"input":1163,"output":56,"reasoning":98,"cache":{"write":0,"read":45240}},"cost":0}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df273f73001q3yJVLgaUQTbOA','msg_0df273a5c00144YxdlQnvpdOse','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790450286451,1790450286452,'{"type":"step-start"}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df273f750014jXjrhzVjLYL95','msg_0df273a5c00144YxdlQnvpdOse','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790450286453,1790450296999,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"Now I have real evidence. Key findings:\n\n1. **Line 39**: `void-bin: paru stuck 55min cloning all of Chromium (code.sh source redirects to chromium mirror); 0 bytes in 15s - AUR packaging bug`\n\nSo `void-bin` is an AUR package whose `code.sh` source redirects to the chromium mirror. That''s why the user said \"it was a void install i need void\" — they meant the **`void-bin` AUR package**, not a Void Linux installation! Now the earlier confusion is fully resolved. My correction (\"this box is not Void\") was technically true but missed the actual intent: they wanted the `void-bin` AUR package built via paru.\n\nWait — but the chromium-mirror I pre-seeded is for `electron34`, not `void-bin`. The handoff line 35-38 says \"void-bin never installed. The chromium mirror is now pre-seeded as a 1.3 GB shallow bare mirror at ~/.cache/paru/clone/electron34/chromium-mirror (tag 132.0.6834.210, 1 ref) instead of the 37 GB full-history clone that died. Retry should work.\"\n\nHmm, so the handoff conflates: the pre-seeded mirror is in the `electron34` directory, but the package that needed it is `void-bin`. That''s a discrepancy! `void-bin` would have its own clone dir `~/.cache/paru/clone/void-bin/...`. So the pre-seed I did (in electron34/) does NOT help void-bin.\n\nLet me verify what void-bin''s sources actually are.\n\n2. **Line 47**: \"machine was rebuilt after a lockout; prior session history lost. 120 repos intact via git remote. Prime lockout suspect: Great Vibes as global KDE UI font (calligraphy, size 14, no bold/italic) reaching lock screen + dialogs\"\n\nThis is critical context. The user''s machine was REBUILT after a LOCKOUT, and the prime suspect was Great Vibes as the global KDE UI font. And the Blood Build theme **sets Great Vibes as the global KDE UI font** (kdeglobals General font + fixed). And line 51 says they bumped it 10/12/14 → 16pt to mitigate.\n\nSo: **reapplying the Blood Build theme = re-applying Great Vibes as the global UI font, which is the documented cause of a previous system lockout.** That''s a serious warning I must raise before \"reapplying.\"\n\n3. **Line 35**: `supercode: 4 install attempts, all failed - npm @kirmad/supercode and supercode both 404 Not Found`\n\nSo there was a \"supercode\" agent component that failed.\n\n4. There''s no mention of a \"global agent system\" as a distinct thing. The agents present: hermes (0.21.5), opencode (1.18.32), supercode (failed).\n\nSo \"rebuild the global agent system i had in place before\" most plausibly means: get hermes + opencode working again as the global agents. But there''s no recorded \"global agent system\" — and the one dangerous extra (the healer daemon with `sudo snapper rollback` timer) was explicitly \"deliberately not done.\"\n\nNow, what should I do? The user has now asked three times for vaguely-specified things, and I''ve been investigating. I have real, decision-relevant findings. I should:\n\n1. Report the key discoveries, especially:\n   - `void-bin` is an AUR package — that''s what \"void\" meant. My earlier correction was wrong in spirit. I should own that.\n   - The pre-seeded mirror is in the WRONG directory for void-bin (electron34/ vs void-bin/).\n   - **The Great Vibes lockout risk** — reapplying Blood Build re-applies the font that was blamed for a lockout.\n   - There''s no surviving spec for a \"global agent system\"; the only agents recorded are hermes + opencode (+ supercode which 404''d).\n   - Nothing is pushed to GitHub, so the \"120 repos intact via git remote\" claim needs checking — the handoff says nothing was pushed, so those remotes may be unreachable/unpushed. Actually \"120 repos intact via git remote\" suggests they HAVE remotes. But \"Nothing has been pushed to GitHub\" for these 4 repos. Contradiction worth noting.\n\n2. Ask the user what they actually want, with concrete options.\n\nLet me quickly check void-bin and the fontconfig/lockout state to be maximally useful. Let me verify:\n- Is there a void-bin in paru cache? What''s its PKGBUILD source?\n- Current KDE font setting (is Great Vibes currently applied?)\n\nLet me do that, then report + ask.\n\nI should be careful not to over-run. Let me do one focused batch.\n\nLet me check void-bin sources and current font state.\n\nThis is genuinely important: if the user re-runs install.sh, it sets Great Vibes as global UI font at 16pt, which is the documented lockout suspect. I must flag it. The user did already bump to 16pt and added a synthetic bold rule, so they were mitigating. Still worth flagging.\n\nLet me check.","time":{"start":1790450286453,"end":1790450296997}}');
