INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df2a7b77001kJJgtcHeCOUdcL','msg_0df2a75510012EFhjbovOTJdoa','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790450498424,1790450500604,'{"type":"text","text":"Firewall is live and `wlo1` is in `public` with only `ssh` + `dhcpv6-client` allowed. That''s the fix verified.\n\n**Two things before I install Void:**\n\n**1. `kdeconnectd` is still bound to `*:1716`.** Firewalld blocks *inbound* to it now, so the exposure is closed from outside — but the process still listens on every interface. It''s contained, not eliminated. Worth deciding separately whether you want KDE Connect at all.\n\n**2. Void isn''t a package — it''s an AUR build that takes hours.** `void-bin` needs `electron34`, which clones a 32 GB Chromium mirror. That''s what ran for 90+ minutes earlier and never finished. The paru cache is 4.3G with a partial clone in it.\n\nThere''s also a prebuilt binary repo that avoids the Chromium compile entirely. Let me check that:","time":{"start":1790450498423,"end":1790450500603}}');
