INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df2cbea6001Y4TfcjDhku7eOL','msg_0df2cb542001A8hKq6nptTtW7B','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790450646694,1790450646695,'{"type":"step-start"}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df2cbea8001T9V3fm3n7S7g8X','msg_0df2cb542001A8hKq6nptTtW7B','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790450646696,1790450650997,'{"type":"text","text":"Both done.\n\n## 1. Watcher service — running and verified end-to-end\n\n```\nActive: active (running)   Main PID: 186750   Memory: 9.2M\n```\n\nI injected a synthetic SSH brute-force and a faillock lockout into the journal; the watcher caught both and logged `ALERT: 2 event(s), severity=critical`. It fired the fullscreen pixel alert. **It works.**\n\nTwo bugs I hit and fixed:\n- **`log()` crash** — same multi-arg bug as before, at a second call site. I fixed the one instance earlier and missed this one. That was my error.\n- **`226/NAMESPACE`** — my own hardening directives (`ProtectSystem=strict`, `ProtectHome=read-only`) blocked the script from reading `~/Projects`. Replaced with directives that actually work: `ProtectKernelTunables`, `ProtectControlGroups`, `RestrictSUIDSGID`.\n\n## 2. Cache cleanup\n\n| Item | Reclaimed |\n|---|---|\n| paru build cache | **4.3G → 544K** |\n| pacman package cache | already clean — `paccache` found no candidates |\n| **paru cache total** | **4.3G freed** |\n\nDisk went 16G → let me confirm, but that''s the bulk of it.\n\n**On the 18 orphans — I''d leave them.** Total is 368 MB, and `electron39` is 280 MB of that. `paccache` already found nothing to prune, so the 3.8G figure was stale. Not worth the risk of removing packages on a machine where I can''t verify what depends on them.\n\n```bash\n# optional, 368MB, verify first:\nsudo pacman -Rns $(pacman -Qdtq)\n```\n\n---\n\nOne thing I should flag: **something outside this session committed to your repos.** `shield-kitty-watch.py` at 12:20 was authored by `Living_Sin <intricos777-dot@users.noreply.github.com>` — a rename of my files. It was a clean rename and the content was intact, so no harm, but you may want to check whether that''s you in another terminal.\n\n**Now ready for the full diagnostics sweep** you asked for. That''s the last outstanding item from your earlier message.","time":{"start":1790450646696,"end":1790450650995}}');
