ull 2>&1 || true export AI_AGENT=\"${AI_AGENT:-hermes-agent}\" HERMES_AGENT=\"${HERMES_AGENT:-true}\" export GIT_PAGER=\"${GIT_PAGER:-cat}\" PAGER=\"${PAGER:-cat}\" builtin cd -- /home/livings/Projects/shield-kitty || exit 126 eval ''sleep 90; echo done'' __hermes_ec=$? umask 077 __hermes_snap_tmp=$(mktemp /home/livings/.hermes/cache/scratch/hermes-snap-840a76504c3a.sh.tmp.XXXXXXXXXX) && { { ( unset ${!HERMES_SESSION_*} ${!HERMES_CRON_AUTO_DELIVER_*} ${!HERMES_BROWSER_CONTROL_*} AI_AGENT HERMES_AGENT HERMES_DELEGATED_CHILD_CONTEXT HERMES_CRON_SESSION HERMES_UI_SESSION_ID 2>/dev/null; export -p; ) || true; } > \"$__hermes_snap_tmp\" && mv -f \"$__hermes_snap_tmp\" /home/livings/.hermes/cache/scratch/hermes-snap-840a76504c3a.sh; } 2>/dev/null || rm -f \"$__hermes_snap_tmp\" 2>/dev/null || true printf ''\\n__HERMES_CWD_840a76504c3a__%s__HERMES_CWD_840a76504c3a__\\n'' \"$(pwd -P)\" exit $__hermes_ec\n","metadata":{"output":"=== files ===\ntotal 24\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 livings livings  126 Sep 26 12:24 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 livings livings  256 Sep 26 12:25 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 livings livings  144 Sep 26 12:25 .git\n-rw-r--r-- 1 livings livings   19 Sep 26 12:14 .gitignore\n-rwxr-xr-x 1 livings livings 7283 Sep 26 12:20 shield-kitty-alert.py\n-rwxr-xr-x 1 livings livings 9763 Sep 26 12:23 shield-kitty-watch.py\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 livings livings   52 Sep 26 12:25 systemd\n\n=== is a shield-kitty process running right now? ===\n 186750     143 /usr/bin/python3 /home/livings/Projects/nyan-gfsf-alert/shield-kitty-watch.py\n 188697      20 opencode run --session ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk HANDOFF FROM HERMES (status only, no action): the nyan GFSF tool is renamed to SHIELD KITTY. Repo moved ~/Projects/nyan-gfsf-alert -> ~/Projects/shield-kitty; scripts are now shield-kitty-alert.py and shield-kitty-watch.py; runtime state dir and log prefix follow; on-screen wordmark is SHIELD KITTY. Commits: edb9cd5 (initial), ffd58fc (rename), fe2a4b5 (rename details). Selftest re-verified after the rename: journal access True, 796 lines scanned, rules match, --demo exits 0. Also committed ~/Projects/zen-hardening (2fe0d82) and the pending hermes-blood install.sh fix (2ae226a). Full detail in /tmp/hermes-handoff.md - read it. Acknowledge only; do not install or change anything because of this message.\n 188735      17 /usr/bin/bash -c source /home/livings/.hermes/cache/scratch/hermes-snap-840a76504c3a.sh >/dev/null 2>&1 || true export AI_AGENT=\"${AI_AGENT:-hermes-agent}\" HERMES_AGENT=\"${HERMES_AGENT:-true}\" export GIT_PAGER=\"${GIT_PAGER:-cat}\" PAGER=\"${PAGER:-cat}\" builtin cd -- /home/livings/Projects/shield-kitty || exit 126 eval ''sleep 90; echo done'' __hermes_ec=$? umask 077 __hermes_snap_tmp=$(mktemp /home/livings/.hermes/cache/scratch/hermes-snap-840a76504c3a.sh.tmp.XXXXXXXXXX) && { { ( unset ${!HERMES_SESSION_*} ${!HERMES_CRON_AUTO_DELIVER_*} ${!HERMES_BROWSER_CONTROL_*} AI_AGENT HERMES_AGENT HERMES_DELEGATED_CHILD_CONTEXT HERMES_CRON_SESSION HERMES_UI_SESSION_ID 2>/dev/null; export -p; ) || true; } > \"$__hermes_snap_tmp\" && mv -f \"$__hermes_snap_tmp\" /home/livings/.hermes/cache/scratch/hermes-snap-840a76504c3a.sh; } 2>/dev/null || rm -f \"$__hermes_snap_tmp\" 2>/dev/null || true printf ''\\n__HERMES_CWD_840a76504c3a__%s__HERMES_CWD_840a76504c3a__\\n'' \"$(pwd -P)\" exit $__hermes_ec\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd ~/Projects/shield-kitty\necho \"=== files ===\"; ls -la\necho; echo \"=== is a shield-kitty process running right now? ===\"\nps -eo pid,etimes,cmd 2>/dev/null | grep -iE \"shield-kitty|nyan\" | grep -v grep || echo \"  none running\"","time":{"start":1790450755037,"end":1790450755083}}}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df2e6611001RXWtUcPvU7koKu','msg_0df2e4857001bMZjLKVzRpzgFG','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790450755089,1790450755090,'{"reason":"tool-calls","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":60545,"input":1691,"output":280,"reasoning":372,"cache":{"write":0,"read":58202}},"cost":0}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df2e68ac001L5uxZzL2IrbOnK','msg_0df298cf8001Q1UCZ05j01wGxl','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790450755756,1790450758342,'{"type":"text","text":"Two hard blockers found, plus one safety issue:\n\n- **`sudo` requires a password** → I cannot enable firewalld, install `gh`, or create GitHub repos.\n- **firewalld safety issue**: your `firewalld-workstation.conf` denies all inbound *except SSH*, but **`sshd` is inactive and nothing is listening on :22**. Enabling it as-is would deny all inbound with no SSH fallback.\n- `git` identity was only set in `nyan-gfsf-alert` (`Living_Sin <intricos777-dot@users.noreply.github.com>`); the other three repos can''t be committed at all, which is why buildlog''s auto-commit would silently no-op.\n\n`hermes-blood` is now pushed (`f1ffc34..2ae226a`). Restoring the identity so journaling works:","time":{"start":1790450755756,"end":1790450758341}}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df2e6d76001gNRPdf57o0TZMN','msg_0df2e661e001CmRi9v1dX6w11N','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790450756982,1790450756984,'{"type":"step-start"}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df2e6d790013Roj0fiwCL2tKD','msg_0df2e661e001CmRi9v1dX6w11N','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790450756986,1790450760666,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"MAJOR findings. The rename is **broken in production**:\n\n1. **The installed systemd unit still points at the OLD path:**\n   - `Documentation=file://%h/Projects/nyan-gfsf-alert/` → path no longer exists\n   - `ExecStart=/usr/bin/python3 %h/Projects/nyan-gfsf-alert/shield-kitty-watch.py` → **path no longer exists!**\n\n2. **The running process (PID 186750, running 143s) is the OLD in-memory process** started from the old path. It''s still running because it was started before the move. `Restart=on-failure` — if it dies, systemd will try to restart it from a path that **doesn''t exist**, and it''ll fail-loop.\n\n3. So: the service is `active` but running a zombie process from a deleted path. On next login (or if it restarts), it will break.\n\nThis is exactly the kind of thing that connects to the user''s request. But wait — the user asked \"lets also ensure shield kitty doesnt display against me.\"\n\nLet me now focus on the real request. The service is enabled+active. The user''s concern: SHIELD KITTY shouldn''t display alerts against them (false positives).\n\nLet me look at the watcher''s detection logic to understand what triggers the alert, and what \"against me\" means:\n- False positives: legitimate user activity being flagged as intrusion\n- Or: the alert displaying at all when there''s no threat\n\nLet me read shield-kitty-watch.py to understand the rules.\n\nAlso note: the handoff said \"Selftest re-verified after the rename: journal access True, 796 lines scanned, rules match, --demo exits 0.\" So it has a --demo mode.\n\nLet me read the watcher.\n\nAlso important: the unit file in the repo `~/Projects/shield-kitty/systemd/shield-kitty-watch.service` — does it have the corrected path? Let me check. The repo was updated (systemd dir has 52 bytes modified 12:25). The *installed* one at ~/.config/systemd/user/ is stale.\n\nLet me read both.\n\nLet me read the watch script to address false positives.\n\nThis is the substantive work. Let me read it.","time":{"start":1790450756985,"end":1790450760664}}');
