-speed USB device number 3 using xhci_hcd\n2026-09-26T10:48:05-07:00 living-asustufdashf15fx517zcfx517zc kernel: usb 3-7: Product: USB2.0 HD UVC WebCam\n2026-09-26T10:48:06-07:00 living-asustufdashf15fx517zcfx517zc kernel: usb 3-9: Product: C-Media(R) Audio\n\n=== own sudo failures in last 24h? ===\n0\n=== pam_unix auth failures (fires login_failure) in last 24h? ===\n0\n","exit":1,"truncated":false},"title":"cd ~/Projects/shield-kitty\necho \"=== what matches the usb_attach rule in the last 24h? ===\"\njournalctl --no-pager -q --since \"-24h\" 2>/dev/null | grep -icE \"usb .*(new high-speed USB device|Product:)\"\necho \"  ^ count of USB attach lines (each would show a fullscreen nyan cat)\"\necho\necho \"=== sample of them ===\"\njournalctl --no-pager -q --since \"-24h\" -o short-iso 2>/dev/null | grep -iE \"usb .*(new high-speed USB device|Product:)\" | tail -3 | cut -c1-140\necho\necho \"=== own sudo failures in last 24h? ===\"\njournalctl --no-pager -q --since \"-24h\" 2>/dev/null | grep -icE \"sudo:.*incorrect password\"\necho \"=== pam_unix auth failures (fires login_failure) in last 24h? ===\"\njournalctl --no-pager -q --since \"-24h\" 2>/dev/null | grep -cE \"pam_unix\\([^)]*:auth\\): authentication failure\"","time":{"start":1790450784156,"end":1790450784499}}}');
