INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df3286ac0014O1Wc6wWV6CUgO','msg_0df3280880012ibI5K7w7yFtfU','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790451025580,1790451029464,'{"type":"text","text":"All three tools resolve in your actual login shell. My earlier \"MISSING\" was a bad test on my part.\n\n## Full diagnostics — system is healthy\n\n| Area | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Failed units | **none** |\n| Disk | **13G / 477G (3%)** |\n| Updates | **0 pending** |\n| Package integrity | **0 altered files** (`pacman -Qkk` clean) |\n| Firewall | **active**, `wlo1` → public, only `ssh` + `dhcpv6-client` |\n| Hardening (live) | `kptr_restrict=1`, `perf_event_paranoid=3`, `suid_dumpable=0` |\n| Faillock | `deny=10`, `unlock_time=1800` — live |\n| Account | `livings P` — not locked |\n| Evidence chain | **INTACT** |\n| Watcher | active, caught both injected tests |\n| Hermes | 0.21.5-1 installed |\n| Toolchain | all three tools resolve in fish |\n\n**Orphans dropped from 18 to 1** — Hermes cleaned up during the session.\n\n## Two open items\n\n**1. `kdeconnectd` on `*:1716`.** Still listening on all interfaces. Firewalld blocks inbound, so it''s not reachable from outside — but the process is still there. You only have a Public network, so there''s no trusted zone to scope it to. **Do you want it, or should I disable it?**\n\n**2. Memory is tighter than earlier.** 595M free, 2.1G available (was 848M/3.0G), and 5.2G used with two `opencode` processes at ~750M each. No OOM, no swap pressure, but that''s what''s producing the `kwin: your system is too slow` messages. Not a fault — just headroom.\n\n## Uncommitted work\n\n`shield-kitty` has 3 uncommitted files, `buildlog` has 1. Hermes may be mid-edit on those. Want me to check what they are before committing over its work, or leave them alone?\n\n**Not done, still flagged:** Void (upstream source 404s — AUR build cannot succeed), the OpenCode dedicated repo, and the PAM/zen-healer items I''ve declined.","time":{"start":1790451025580,"end":1790451029463}}');
