telist VID PID|unban VID PID`. NOT INSTALLED — sudo needs your password.\n\n5. Commit 3845292 on top of your c9f7bc9 (evidence chain). Your commits are intact; I built on top of them. Earlier: edb9cd5, ffd58fc, fe2a4b5. zen-hardening 2fe0d82, hermes-blood 2ae226a.\n\n6. Fixed by testing, worth knowing about: a crash in is_banned that fired on EVERY device add once the blacklist was non-empty, header comments in the state files being parsed as ban records, and a sysfs lookup that never matched real devices (wrong root-hub filter).\n\nFull detail: /tmp/hermes-handoff.md. Acknowledge only.\""}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df36c84d001kMI25m7Q95ZzvW','msg_0df36b800001iedywPl7BLQHxz','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790451304525,1790451304526,'{"type":"step-start"}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df36c850001zO447dfqXTyg2Q','msg_0df36b800001iedywPl7BLQHxz','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790451304528,1790451306671,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"The handoff says my changes were built upon: \"Commit 3845292 on top of your c9f7bc9 (evidence chain). Your commits are intact; I built on top of them.\"\n\nBut wait — my commits? I never committed anything! I made edits but never ran `git commit`. The handoff claims a commit `c9f7bc9` that is mine. Let me verify this claim carefully — this is exactly the kind of falsifiable claim I should check.\n\nLet me verify:\n1. Does commit c9f7bc9 exist?\n2. Does it contain my changes (the USB regex fix / log_events)?\n3. Is the USB rule actually removed?\n4. Is the notification path real (notify-send)?\n5. Is the device-blacklist real?\n\nAnd critically: I have uncommitted changes potentially mixed in. Let me check git state.\n\nAlso important: the handoff says \"Your commits are intact; I built on top of them.\" But I never committed. So either Hermes committed on my behalf (taking my working-tree changes), or the claim is false.\n\nLet me verify empirically.\n\nAlso I should acknowledge only — no install/change. But verification (read-only) is fine and consistent with my established practice. Let me verify then acknowledge.\n\nLet me check the state.","time":{"start":1790451304528,"end":1790451306668}}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df36cf17001VFu3LI8cQvwg1a','msg_0df36c0d50017gfSBo9W8Y4Jrq','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790451306264,1790451306266,'{"type":"step-start"}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df36cf1b001zBCpgK7Pgc8JK7','msg_0df36c0d50017gfSBo9W8Y4Jrq','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790451306267,1790451311685,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"The user (via Hermes) is giving me a handoff status. They explicitly say: \"status only — do not install or change anything in response to this\" and \"Acknowledge only.\"\n\nSo I should acknowledge only. No tool calls, no changes. Just confirm receipt and acknowledge.\n\nBut — there''s one thing worth flagging. Item 4 describes a device-blacklist that does driver unbinding via udev, and it''s NOT INSTALLED. It''s pending sudo. That''s a genuinely risky component: it unbinds HID drivers. Even though Hermes says HID is exempted via INTERFACE class, and root hubs never blocked, the risk of unbinding input drivers on a machine with no second recovery path is real. I already have a track record of concern about exactly that class of thing (PAM, healer daemon).\n\nThe instruction is \"acknowledge only\" and \"do not install or change anything.\" Acknowledging is fine. Should I flag the concern? The instruction says acknowledge only — but flagging a risk I''m genuinely concerned about, without installing or changing anything, is arguably part of good acknowledgement. And my guidelines say to raise safety concerns when they matter.\n\nHowever, I should be careful: they said acknowledge only. I can acknowledge concisely AND note that item 4 is the one thing I''d want to look at before it''s installed, since it''s the exact class of thing (system-level, boot/login-adjacent, unattended) that burned this machine before. That''s one or two sentences, not a lecture. I shouldn''t relitigate the whole pattern again — I''ve made that argument repeatedly and the user has a right to run their own security stack.\n\nLet me be brief. Acknowledge the state accurately, confirm nothing changed, and note the one item I''d want reviewed before install. Keep it short — that''s what was asked.\n\nLet me also confirm what I know: they said my commits are intact. I should note the evidence chain service is running and the pending items I know about (admin_group not live, fail2ban installed-but-disabled, kdeconnectd listening).\n\nKeep it tight. Acknowledge only.","time":{"start":1790451306267,"end":1790451311682}}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df36d0b3001tsHVx7bDVP84rn','msg_0df36b800001iedywPl7BLQHxz','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790451306676,1790451307907,'{"type":"text","text":"Verifying the falsifiable claims before acknowledging — particularly \"your commits are intact,\" since I never actually ran `git commit`.","time":{"start":1790451306675,"end":1790451307906}}');
