INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df3d065b001zOhEbO2xQkZ3od','msg_0df3cfcdf001ykevYLEMknvrI3','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790451713627,1790451717312,'{"type":"text","text":"Now the push situation, which has a blocker you need to know about.\n\n**Secret scan: clean.** One hit, a fake test fixture in `lin-antimalware/tests/test_dredge.py` with a literal `abc` key body. No real credentials in any working tree or any repo''s full history.\n\n**SSH push auth works** — authenticated as `intricos777-dot`.\n\n## Can push immediately (3 repos, remotes exist)\n\n| Repo | Unpushed |\n|---|---|\n| `business-debug-wrappers` | 1 |\n| `business-health-monitor` | 1 |\n| `lin-antimalware` | 1 |\n\n## Blocked: 4 repos have no GitHub repo\n\n`buildlog`, `shield-kitty`, `shield-kitty-forensics`, `zen-hardening` — all return **HTTP 404**. They don''t exist on GitHub, and **my token is read-only**, so I can''t create them.\n\nThis is the one thing I can''t do for you. Options:\n\n1. **You create them** — four private repos on github.com, then I add remotes and push\n2. **You give me a write-scoped token** and I''ll create them via the API\n3. **Skip pushing those four** and only push the three that work\n\nGiven you said you can rebuild from scratch, option 1 or 2 serves you well — these four are the ones that *don''t* exist remotely, so they''re the ones a rebuild would actually lose.\n\n**Uncommitted before any push:**\n- `zen-hardening` — modified `faillock.conf`, plus `shield-kitty-fail2ban.local` and two `.bak` files. I''d exclude the `.bak` files via `.gitignore` unless you want them.\n- `buildlog` — modified `logs/buildlog.md`\n\nOne caution on `zen-hardening`: `faillock.conf` currently has `admin_group = wheel` in the project copy, but that''s **not** what''s live on the machine. Pushing it as-is would make the repo claim a config you haven''t applied.\n\nWant me to push the three ready repos now while you decide on the other four?","time":{"start":1790451713627,"end":1790451717311}}');
