INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df406594001jfUyF5lQS72meS','msg_0df3eac31001JqZnMkrKVwS6gR','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790451934612,1790451953046,'{"type":"text","text":"## Objective\n- Restore and audit the user’s post-rebuild Garuda Linux security/tool stack, apply reversible hardening, and complete system diagnostics without causing another authentication/boot lockout.\n- Finish Shield Kitty alerting/evidence enforcement and optionally install Void; keep PAM, root-daemon, and device-control changes reviewed and explicitly enabled.\n\n## Important Details\n- User is `livings` on Garuda Linux, Plasma/Wayland; member of `wheel`; sudo requires a password. Do not add blanket `NOPASSWD: ALL`.\n- Root filesystem is active LUKS2 on `nvme0n1p2`; no reformat or “21-layer encryption” reinstall is needed.\n- Firewalld is enabled/active; `wlo1` is in `public`; allowed services are `ssh` and `dhcpv6-client`. OpenSSH is installed but `sshd` is disabled and port 22 is not listening.\n- `kdeconnectd` listens on TCP/UDP `*:1716`; firewalld blocks inbound, but the bind address remains broad. mDNS also listens on UDP 5353.\n- `pam_faillock` is per-username and has no source-IP or permanent-ban semantics. `fail2ban` is required to ban attacking systems by IP.\n- `admin_group = wheel` is a real supported directive, but it exempts wheel members from normal faillock lockout; it does not prevent an attacker who guesses `livings` from inheriting admin rights.\n- Current live `/etc/security/faillock.conf` is `deny = 10`, `unlock_time = 30`, `audit = silent`; it does **not** contain `admin_group = wheel`.\n- Permanent fail2ban bans can self-lock a laptop user; current `wlo1` address `10.245.106.176` is covered by `10.0.0.0/8`, but future public-IP sessions would not be.\n- Hermes is the parallel agent making expected Shield Kitty renames/commits; this was confirmed by the user.\n- No scan can prove “no attack surfaces,” and dark-web scanning/authority reporting cannot be truthfully automated. Evidence is tamper-evident, not automatically legal proof.\n- Temporary GitHub API token remains at `/home/livings/.config/gh/token.clean`; shred after the repository audit.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Installed and verified `/etc/sysctl.d/99-hardening.conf`; 24 keys, 13 live changes including `kernel.kptr_restrict=1`, `kernel.perf_event_paranoid=3`, redirects disabled, and `fs.suid_dumpable=0`.\n- Installed firewalld workstation zone; firewalld is enabled and active.\n- Corrected `~/.config/environment.d/firefox.conf` to `MOZ_USE_XINPUT2=1`; backup is outside `environment.d` at `~/.config/environment.d-backups/firefox.conf.20260926_120708.bak`.\n- Installed and tested:\n  - `lin-antimalware` venv/CLI; scan works, no quarantine run.\n  - `business-health-monitor`; wrapper fixed, scan reports 0 critical/0 high, daily 07:00 user timer armed.\n  - `business-debug-wrappers`; wrapper path fixed and functional.\n- Fixed hardcoded installer paths:\n  - `/home/livings/Projects/lin-antimalware/start.sh`\n  - `/home/livings/Projects/business-health-monitor/install.sh`\n  - `/home/livings/Projects/business-debug-wrappers/install.sh`\n- Replaced unavailable cron scheduling with `business-health.timer`.\n- Built Shield Kitty at `/home/livings/Projects/shield-kitty`; watcher service is active, notifications are default, fullscreen is opt-in, USB rule removed, and debounce is 10 seconds/3 seconds critical.\n- Built `/home/livings/Projects/shield-kitty-forensics/evidence.py` with HMAC hash chain, hourly sealing, signed bundles, reports, and verification; watcher integration is active. Evidence chain last verified `INTACT`.\n- Authority transmission is intentionally manual; reports distinguish logged attempts from successful compromise.\n- Verified Hermes agent `0.21.5-1`, zero pending updates, zero altered package files, and disk around 13G/477G after purging 4.3G of paru clone cache.\n- Blood Build/OpenCode theme work remains installed: `\"theme\": \"voidlit\"` in `~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc`, with theme copies in both `~/.config/opencode/theme/voidlit.json` and `~/.config/opencode/themes/voidlit.json`.\n- Confirmed no Kali partition or dual-boot exists; machine is single-boot Garuda.\n\n### Active\n- Fail2ban 1.1.1 is installed and enabled but **failed/inactive** with:\n  - `Failed to access socket path: /var/run/fail2ban/fail2ban.sock. Is fail2ban running?`\n  - `Have not found any log file for ''recidive'' jail.`\n- Corrected project config `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/shield-kitty-fail2ban.local` now has `recidive enabled = false`, but it has not been installed under a `.conf` filename.\n- Existing `/etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty-fail2ban.local` is ignored because fail2ban auto-loads `jail.d/*.conf`; the stock recidive jail is what currently aborts startup.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/faillock.conf` contains `admin_group = wheel`, but it is not live; do not install silently because it conflicts with the anti-bruteforce goal.\n- Shield Kitty `device-blacklist/` is built but not installed; udev enforcement requires root and review.\n- `void-bin`/`void-electron-latest-bin` remain absent. The old paru process ended and its cache was purged; a fresh build is required. The prior 404 check used unrelated `void-oss/void-bin`; actual AUR remote is `https://aur.archlinux.org/void-bin`.\n- Not installed/reviewed: `bde-security-biometrics`, `lin-antimalware-tools`, `local-emergency-patrol`, `zen-healer`, `security-audit-2026`, and `secure-tactical-systems`.\n- `zen-healer` remains unsafe as written: hardcoded `sin`, privileged daemon, `shell=True`, service restarts, Snapper rollback, and journal deletion.\n- Full Zen/Kali/Arch request remains unresolved; `zen-suite` builds an ISO via `pacstrap`, not a disk installation, and no Kali partition exists.\n- KDE Connect enable/disable decision remains pending.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/buildlog` has one uncommitted change; dedicated OpenCode Blood Build repository and verified Great Vibes bold remain unfinished.\n- Steam/emulators remain absent; “supercode” remains unidentified.\n\n### Blocked\n- Root installation/configuration requires the user to authenticate sudo.\n- Faillock cannot permanently ban source systems; only fail2ban can do that.\n- No `21-layer encryption` repository or design specification was found; reformatting would destroy data.\n- Native Xbox/Xbox 360 emulation remains unavailable; console emulation requires legally dumped firmware.\n- “No attack surfaces” and complete clearnet/dark-web vulnerability coverage cannot be guaranteed.\n- Shield Kitty device enforcement and PAM/root-daemon installation require line-by-line review and explicit approval.\n\n## Next Move\n1. Install the corrected fail2ban config with a loadable extension and validate it:\n   ```bash\n   sudo install -m 0644 ~/Projects/zen-hardening/shield-kitty-fail2ban.local /etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty.conf\n   sudo fail2ban-client -t\n   sudo systemctl restart fail2ban\n   sudo fail2ban-client status\n   ```\n   After the first successful start creates `/var/log/fail2ban.log`, enable `recidive`, retest, and restart.\n2. Recheck live faillock values and require fresh confirmation before enabling `admin_group = wheel`; then rerun full diagnostics, including failed units, active jails/listeners, package integrity, updates, memory, disk, and evidence-chain verification.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/shield-kitty-fail2ban.local`: corrected fail2ban config; recidive disabled for bootstrap.\n- `/etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty-fail2ban.local`: ignored installed copy with the old recidive setting.\n- `/etc/fail2ban/jail.conf`: stock recidive jail causing current startup failure.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/faillock.conf`: project config containing `deny=10`, `unlock_time=30`, `audit=silent`, and `admin_group=wheel`.\n- `/etc/security/faillock.conf`: live config; currently lacks `admin_group`.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/faillock.conf.1800s.bak`: previous 1800-second configuration.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/faillock.conf.pre-admin.bak`: configuration before `admin_group`.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/99-hardening.conf`: reviewed sysctl hardening.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/firewalld-workstation.conf`: reviewed firewalld zone source.\n- `/etc/firewalld/zones/public.xml`: active firewalld zone.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/shield-kitty/shield-kitty-watch.py`: active journal watcher.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/shield-kitty/shield-kitty-alert.py`: notification/fullscreen alert renderer.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/shield-kitty/device-blacklist/`: unroot-installed udev enforcement.\n- `/home/livings/.config/systemd/user/shield-kitty-watch.service`: active watcher unit.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/shield-kitty-forensics/evidence.py`: evidence-chain/report generator.\n- `/home/livings/.config/systemd/user/evidence-seal.timer`: hourly sealing timer.\n- `/home/livings/.local/share/shield-kitty/evidence/chain.jsonl`: HMAC-chained event log.\n- `/home/livings/.config/shield-kitty/evidence.key`: mode-600 local HMAC key.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/lin-antimalware/start.sh`: repaired self-relative launcher.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/business-health-monitor/install.sh`: repaired wrapper and systemd timer installer.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/business-debug-wrappers/install.sh`: repaired wrapper installer.\n- `/home/livings/.config/systemd/user/business-health.timer`: daily 07:00 health scan.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/hermes-blood`: latest handoff commit `2ae226a`.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/hermes-blood/opencode/voidlit.json`: active black/red OpenCode theme source.\n- `/home/livings/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc`: live `\"voidlit\"` activation.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/buildlog`: local build journal; no Git remote.\n- `/tmp/hermes-handoff.md`: full Shield Kitty handoff details.\n- `/home/livings/.config/gh/token.clean`: temporary GitHub API credential to shred after audit.\n- `/tmp/opencode/repos_all.json`: cached 120-repository inventory.","time":{"start":1790451934612,"end":1790451953041}}');
