INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df40b9fc0014sfhkqA00WZ5IU','msg_0df40adcf001OWi93drlc2W5Qr','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790451956220,1790451958470,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"Let me continue. Next steps:\n1. `buildlog` — needs a home. `garuda-tools-fresh` is public (unsafe). Best private fit: `security-audit-2026` (private, has `logs/`) or `rocket-build-system`. Let me check rocket-build-system and decide.\n2. Verify fail2ban is actually running now (the user never confirmed the restart)\n3. Final verification of everything\n\nLet me do buildlog placement and check fail2ban state in parallel.\n\nLet me check rocket-build-system and security-audit-2026 logs/ dir.\n\nActually, let me reconsider buildlog. It''s a \"durable journal of builds, audits, and fixes. Survives system rebuilds.\" Its whole purpose is to survive rebuilds. It contains hostname and personal history.\n\nOptions:\n- `security-audit-2026` (private, has logs/, findings/, reports/, README) — the repo is about audits. buildlog records builds/audits/fixes. Reasonable.\n- `rocket-build-system` (private, Python) — build journal fits \"build system\"\n\nHonestly `security-audit-2026` with its `logs/` dir is the cleaner fit given buildlog explicitly logs audits. And it''s private.\n\nLet me check both quickly, then place it.\n\nLet me also verify fail2ban.","time":{"start":1790451956220,"end":1790451958468}}');
