INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df4107fa001fVUcGcHTV9uXzz','msg_0df41035a001cpiAFaNkJRVIY1','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790451976186,1790451979821,'{"type":"text","text":"Everything is backed up. All 7 repos are clean, and the four orphaned projects now live in repos that already exist.\n\n**Pushed:**\n\n| Where | What |\n|---|---|\n| `business-debug-wrappers` | `7301a28` |\n| `business-health-monitor` | `e1562d4` |\n| `lin-antimalware` | `4d304c3` |\n| `hermes-security-scripts` | `36e2e1b` — `zen-hardening` → `config/zen-hardening/`, `shield-kitty` → `scripts/shield-kitty/`, forensics → `scripts/shield-kitty/forensics/` |\n| `security-audit-2026` | `407fdf5` — `buildlog` → `logs/buildlog/` |\n\nI kept `.bak` files, venvs, and `__pycache__` out, and ran a credential scan on every staged tree and every repo''s full history before committing. Only hit was a fake test fixture.\n\n**One deliberate non-push:** `buildlog` has your hostname and personal build history in it, and its most natural thematic home — `garuda-tools-fresh` — is **public**. I put it in `security-audit-2026` (private) instead. Say the word if you want it elsewhere.\n\n**fail2ban is still down.** Your 12:40 test only validated the file — it never started the service. This is unchanged since 12:36:\n\n```\nSep 26 12:36:53  ERROR  Have not found any log file for ''recidive'' jail.\n```\n\nThe config is now correct, so this should clear on the first restart:\n\n```bash\nsudo systemctl restart fail2ban\nsystemctl is-active fail2ban\nsudo fail2ban-client status\n```\n\nThe token at `~/.config/gh/token.clean` is still needed for the API checks, so I''ve left it in place rather than shredding it — say when you''re done and I''ll clear it.","time":{"start":1790451976186,"end":1790451979820}}');
