INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df4dfafa001RHetU1rXksCSWr','msg_0df4df4fa001m22vZOgYe6TV8f','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790452824826,1790452832124,'{"type":"text","text":"System state confirmed. Stopping to report rather than plowing ahead, because the situation has changed materially.\n\n**The paru cache was wiped.** `~/.cache/paru/clone/` is now empty — all 6 repos gone, including the 377 MB `electron` tarball and the 1.3 GB shallow `chromium-mirror` I built and verified for you earlier. Disk went 16G → 13G. `/var/cache/pacman/pkg` is intact (943 packages, 3.9G), so system packages are fine; only the AUR build state is gone.\n\n**The systemd unit is already fixed** — not by me. `ExecStart` now points at `shield-kitty/`, PID 211116 runs from the correct path, cursor file is live. Another agent closed that one.\n\n**Status of your four selected items:**\n\n| Item | State |\n|---|---|\n| Close durability gap | Partial — `hermes-blood` pushed; other 3 repos still have no remote (needs `gh`, needs sudo) |\n| Reapply theme, skip KDE font | Not started |\n| Enable firewalld | Blocked — needs your sudo password; also `sshd` is inactive so the allow-SSH rule has no fallback |\n| Finish `void-bin` | Blocked — cache wiped, must redo the shallow mirror + ~165 DEPS repos + multi-hour Chromium compile |\n\nTwo things I want to flag before spending your bandwidth and hours again:\n\n1. **The `void-bin` path is long and previously failed once.** It needs `electron34`, which means rebuilding the 1.3 GB mirror, seeding ~165 more git sources, then a multi-hour Chromium compile. That is easily 4–8 hours of machine time. I can automate the shallow-seeding and run it in the background, but I''d rather you confirm before I start something that size again.\n\n2. **I can''t do most of the remaining items** — `firewalld`, `gh` install, and repo creation all need your sudo password. For those, the fastest path is for you to run them and paste the output.\n\nWhich do you want?","time":{"start":1790452824826,"end":1790452832123}}');
