INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df4f4c2c001spTRb2nWkbndYn','msg_0df4f4701001HzT1yaMPVhDCYj','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790452911148,1790452917256,'{"type":"text","text":"Both bugs fixed and validated. **Recovery — run this now:**\n\n```bash\nsudo cp ~/Projects/zen-hardening/firewalld-workstation.conf /etc/firewalld/zones/public.xml\nsudo firewall-offline-cmd --check-config\n```\n\nIf that prints `ok`, then:\n\n```bash\nsudo firewall-cmd --reload\n```\n\nThen confirm you''re actually protected again:\n\n```bash\nfirewall-cmd --state\nsudo nft list tables | grep -c firewalld\n```\n\nYou need `running` and a non-zero table count. Anything else means still unprotected.\n\n## What went wrong\n\nTwo separate defects in that zone file, both mine:\n\n1. **`disable=\"yes\"`** — not in the firewalld zone schema. The correct way to suppress an inherited service is `enable=\"no\"`. This is what produced `PARSE_ERROR`.\n2. **`--` inside XML comments** — illegal in XML. firewalld''s parser had been tolerating it, so this never surfaced until the parse error forced a stricter check.\n\nThe `PARSE_ERROR` also explains the first message: because the reload aborted, firewalld sat in `failed` state, which locks out `--permanent` edits until it''s restarted.\n\n## Why this went from \"cosmetic\" to urgent\n\nBefore your `cp`, `/etc/firewalld/zones/public.xml` was malformed but *tolerated* — firewalld was running with its rules loaded. Your `cp` replaced it with a schema-invalid file, the reload failed, and firewalld **unloaded its nft tables**. With zero tables, no zone filtering is happening on any interface.\n\nSo the honest status: the `ssh` hole I was closing was never the bigger risk. A malformed zone config that takes the firewall offline beats a closed port on a disabled daemon. You were more exposed in the last few minutes than at any point since the rebuild.\n\n## Where things stand\n\n- Firewall: **currently down**, fixable with the four commands above\n- Source file: fixed, schema-validated\n- Still unverified: fail2ban jail list, `set-anon-identity.sh` never run\n- `kdeconnectd` still blocked, `home-net` zone still deferred as you asked\n\nI''ll re-push the corrected zone file once your firewall is back up and the reload succeeds — I don''t want to push a config I haven''t seen pass `--check-config` against your live system again.","time":{"start":1790452911148,"end":1790452917255}}');
