INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df52e5360018XXvaw83zi1Jof','msg_0df52dcb00016Tz1ttaIbjcdNA','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790453146934,1790453151467,'{"type":"text","text":"Validated against firewalld 2.5.2''s own parser. Now the recovery sequence — your firewall is still down, so this is the priority:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Install the validated zone\nsudo cp ~/Projects/zen-hardening/workstation.xml /etc/firewalld/zones/workstation.xml\n\n# 2. Remove the broken public override\nsudo rm -f /etc/firewalld/zones/public.xml\n\n# 3. Validate\nsudo firewall-offline-cmd --check-config\n\n# 4. Load it (only if step 3 printed \"ok\")\nsudo firewall-cmd --reload\nsudo firewall-cmd --set-default-zone=workstation\n\n# 5. Bind the wifi connection\nsudo nmcli con mod \"USL - Public\" connection.zone workstation\nsudo nmcli con up \"USL - Public\"\n```\n\n**Verify you''re protected:**\n```bash\nfirewall-cmd --state\nsudo nft list tables | grep -c firewalld\nfirewall-cmd --zone=workstation --list-services\n```\n\nWant `running`, a non-zero table count, and `dhcpv6-client` as the only service.\n\nIf step 4 fails, get protected immediately with the built-in zone — no custom file needed:\n```bash\nsudo rm -f /etc/firewalld/zones/workstation.xml /etc/firewalld/zones/public.xml\nsudo firewall-cmd --reload\nsudo firewall-cmd --set-default-zone=public\n```\n\n## What I got wrong, plainly\n\nYou reported `Unexpected attribute enable`. I had already produced one wrong fix (`disable=` → `enable=`) without checking either, and guessed a third form (`remove-service`) that doesn''t exist in firewalld 2.5.2. Three wrong answers to a question I could have answered by reading the shipped schema first.\n\nThe actual constraint: **`<service>` accepts only `name`**, and there is no way to subtract an inherited service. Overriding the built-in `public` zone can never yield a truly empty allowlist, because your file gets *merged* with the built-in, not substituted for it.\n\nThe fix is structural, not a syntax tweak — a uniquely-named zone has no built-in twin, so it inherits nothing and starts empty.\n\nI''ve now validated this file against `zone_reader` from firewalld 2.5.2 itself, which is the same code path `--check-config` uses. It will pass. I won''t push it until you confirm the reload succeeded.","time":{"start":1790453146934,"end":1790453151466}}');
