 systemd[1]: Stopped Fail2Ban Service.\n  Sep 26 13:20:02 zero systemd[1]: Started Fail2Ban Service.\n  Sep 26 13:20:02 zero fail2ban-server[227197]: Server ready\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"echo \"═══ IS FAIL2BAN ACTUALLY UP NOW? ═══\"\nsystemctl is-active fail2ban | sed ''s/^/  service: /''\npgrep -a fail2ban-server 2>/dev/null | sed ''s/^/  /'' || echo \"  no process\"\necho\necho \"═══ SOCKET PRESENT? ═══\"\nls -la /run/fail2ban/ 2>&1 | grep -E \"sock|pid\" | sed ''s/^/  /''\necho\necho \"═══ ANY ERRORS SINCE RESTART? ═══\"\njournalctl -u fail2ban -S \"13:19\" --no-pager 2>&1 | grep -iE \"server ready|error|fail\" | tail -6 | sed ''s/^/  /''","time":{"start":1790454018166,"end":1790454018215}}}');
