INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df6048a0001tGHnvKsKo4DwG4','msg_0df6030c4001gvPMABHlw8SotU','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790454024352,1790454026575,'{"type":"text","text":"It''s up — `Server ready`, socket created at 13:20, zero errors. Your query landed in the same second the socket was being created.\n\nMy fault for repeating `systemctl restart` → immediate `status`. Three times now. Here''s the readiness gate that actually works, as a fish function so you stop retyping it:\n\n```fish\nfunction f2bready\n    while not sudo fail2ban-client status 2>/dev/null | grep -q \"Jail list\"\n        sleep 0.5\n    end\n    sudo fail2ban-client status\nend\n```\n\nThat waits for the **jail list**, not just the socket. `ping` alone was insufficient before, which is what caused the `recidive` NOK.\n\nTo see the current jails, just re-run the query now:\n\n```bash\nsudo fail2ban-client status\n```\n\nI expect **`sshd` only** — `recidive` should still be disabled since you haven''t done the sed step yet. Paste the output and I''ll confirm before you enable recidive.","time":{"start":1790454024352,"end":1790454026574}}');
