INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df65453b001TotpuybInOYn5s','msg_0df6535fb001jyuqDYGVnhKf4m','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790454351164,1790454354886,'{"type":"text","text":"Config is valid and the sed pattern matches exactly one line — no risk of hitting `sshd`.\n\n**Do the `sed` + restart, then tell me the jail count.** If it''s 2, I''ll push everything.\n\n## What happened, plainly\n\nYou didn''t break anything and it isn''t a new fault. I rewrote the config file with `recidive` set to `enabled = false` — deliberate, because that jail can''t start on a machine where fail2ban has never run, and the failure aborts *all* jails. But I didn''t warn you that copying my version over your live one would therefore switch recidive back off.\n\nThe result was a jail list going 2 → 1 after a perfectly clean restart. No errors in the log, nothing crashed. Just my file undoing your change.\n\nI''ve added a warning block at the top of the file and asserted the sed pattern matches exactly one line, so it can''t accidentally flip `sshd` instead.\n\n## Where the session landed\n\n| | Status |\n|---|---|\n| Firewall | `workstation` zone, all inbound denied except `dhcpv6-client` ✓ |\n| Hostname / `/etc/hosts` | `zero` ✓ |\n| `wlo1` MAC randomization | still unconfirmed |\n| fail2ban | 2 jails, `bantime=86400`, `zone=workstation` — pending re-enable |\n| Greeter protection | **none** — structural, not fixable by config |\n| Browser / Tor | not installed; SOCKS port unused |\n\nThe MAC randomization check and the end-to-end ban test are the two things still worth doing, plus pushing.","time":{"start":1790454351163,"end":1790454354885}}');
