INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df674952001pmbxeVNf2utPKL','msg_0df6740d6001EORrudWBp0Olbo','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790454483282,1790454483284,'{"type":"step-start"}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df674956001qbMcg7Q7vjqOFa','msg_0df6740d6001EORrudWBp0Olbo','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790454483286,1790454489528,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"The user is asking me to reinstall \"BDE patrols and notifications\". Let me think about what this is.\n\nFrom the earlier handoff:\n> ## Deliberately not done\n> - healer daemon / BDE patrols / antivirus / hardening daemons: not installed. The healer runs `sudo snapper rollback -c root` on a 5-minute timer with `shell=True` interpolation.\n\nSo \"BDE patrols\" was something explicitly noted as deliberately NOT installed, and the handoff flagged that the healer daemon is dangerous (runs `sudo snapper rollback -c root` on a 5-minute timer with `shell=True` interpolation).\n\nBDE = BitLocker Drive Encryption presumably (Windows), or \"BDE patrols\" might be some custom thing. Let me search for what BDE patrols actually is in the repos. I should investigate before acting.\n\nImportant: this is a request to install something that:\n1. Was explicitly \"deliberately not done\"\n2. The handoff flagged the healer as dangerous (auto-rollback root on a timer, with shell=True injection risk)\n\nAlso, critically: I already established that `sudo` requires a password. So I CANNOT install any of this — it needs root. That''s a hard blocker I must communicate.\n\nLet me first investigate what \"BDE patrols\" actually refers to, since I have no record of it. Let me search the repos, the buildlog, and the handoff file.\n\nLet me also note the seed just finished (161 ok). I should wrap that up too.\n\nLet me search for BDE.\n\nKey facts I need to establish:\n1. What is \"BDE patrols\"? Does it exist in any repo?\n2. What are \"notifications\" in this context — Shield Kitty notifications are already installed and running.\n3. Can I even do it? sudo needs a password → NO for anything root.\n\nLet me investigate. I should not fabricate a \"BDE patrol\" system. If there''s no record of it, I should say so rather than invent one — especially since inventing one would mean writing a daemon that runs sudo snapper rollback.\n\nLet me search.\n\nAlso I should be alert: this request has the shape of \"reinstall something dangerous that a prior agent deliberately didn''t install, and whose own documentation flags it as risky.\" I should be honest and careful. But I shouldn''t be preachy — I should just be factual.\n\nLet me search the filesystem for BDE references.\n\nLet me do the search and also confirm the seed result.\n\nI''ll run parallel searches.","time":{"start":1790454483286,"end":1790454489526}}');
