INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df6c40ed001hgAcgbH7t9NEeP','msg_0df6c39db001pUPoxwqblG6XMi','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790454808813,1790454808813,'{"type":"step-start"}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df6c40ee0017Bj6Vqg98ga75O','msg_0df6c39db001pUPoxwqblG6XMi','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790454808814,1790454814324,'{"type":"text","text":"Everything is consolidated into one private repo. `shield-kitty` and `shield-kitty-forensics` had no remote, but their full contents are now committed inside `hermes-security-scripts` — you asked earlier to fold them into existing repos, so they''re covered rather than duplicated.\n\n## Pushed\n\n`hermes-security-scripts` @ **`99fe7b3`** (private), 28 files across `config/zen-hardening/` and `scripts/shield-kitty/`. Earlier this session also pushed to `business-debug-wrappers`, `business-health-monitor`, `lin-antimalware`, and `security-audit-2026`. All private. Secret scan clean on every staged tree and full history.\n\n## What `bootstrap.sh` does on a fresh machine\n\n1. Packages: `fail2ban`, `firewalld`, `tor`; notes `torbrowser-launcher` as optional\n2. Installs `workstation.xml`, removes the broken `public.xml` override, restarts firewalld with the `PartOf=` workaround\n3. Installs fail2ban config, enables `recidive` only if `/var/log/fail2ban.log` exists, waits on the jail list rather than `ping`\n4. Runs the anonymisation script\n5. Prints live values and exits non-zero unless firewall is running **with nft tables loaded**, default zone is `workstation`, hostname is `zero`, and fail2ban is active\n\nRun `sudo bash ~/Projects/zen-hardening/bootstrap.sh --check` first to preview.\n\n## Bugs I found in my own work this turn\n\n- **`set-anon-identity.sh` never worked.** I used `802-11-wireless.mac-address-mode`, which doesn''t exist in NetworkManager 1.58. `nmcli` errored, `set -e` aborted the script, and it printed success anyway. Your `wlo1` has been broadcasting the real MAC `f4:a4:75:e8:00:b2` this whole time. Now detects the correct property and fails loudly.\n- **`bootstrap.sh` had an unterminated quote** on the `install` line, which cascaded into a bogus \"unexpected token\" error 12 lines later. Found by bisecting with `head -N | bash -n`.\n\n## Run these two, then we''re done\n\n```bash\nsudo bash /home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/bootstrap.sh --check\nsudo bash /home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/bootstrap.sh\n```\n\nThat applies the MAC fix and verifies the whole baseline end to end.\n\n## Still open\n\n- **No browser.** Tor bootstraps 100% but nothing uses it. `torbrowser-launcher` is the only thing that gives real anonymous browsing.\n- **Greeter has zero automated protection** — structural, documented in `fail2ban-coverage.md`, not fixable with config.\n- **`machine-id` still unique**; DMI still reports your hardware model.\n- **`~/.config/gh/token.clean`** still on disk. Say the word and I''ll shred it.","time":{"start":1790454808814,"end":1790454814323}}');
