INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df6ea8f3001HrhNgHx8DQzzvw','msg_0df6ea164001MfVQP66KhuecbU','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790454966515,1790454966516,'{"type":"step-start"}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df6ea8f6001g7jyY2LcTK00tC','msg_0df6ea164001MfVQP66KhuecbU','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790454966518,1790454971632,'{"type":"text","text":"Code fixed and committed, nothing installed. Here''s where everything stands.\n\n**BDE patrols — fixed, not installed.** The audit found a genuine lockout and I fixed it (commit `359cc45`):\n\n- `pam required pam_deny.so` removed from the stack. That line plus `bde-auth` exiting non-zero on *any* exception meant a stopped daemon or missing socket denied login, sudo, and sshd even with the right password.\n- `bde-auth` now distinguishes **denied** (exit 1, real mismatch) from **unavailable** (exit 2, no verdict), with `BDE_FAILMODE` defaulting to `open`. Verified: no daemon → exit 0; `BDE_FAILMODE=closed` → exit 1.\n- Socket path resolves the target user via `pwd` instead of `os.getuid()` — PAM runs as root, so `getuid()` is 0 and was the wrong answer.\n- `sshd` excluded unless `BDE_INCLUDE_SSHD=1`; installer gains `--dry-run`, takes `/etc/pam.d` backups, and refuses to run without an executable `bde-auth`. Dropped the BlackArch-only step.\n- `--dry-run` executed: hooks `login`, `sudo`, `su` only, modifies nothing.\n\nOne correction to my earlier reasoning: your uid *is* 1000, so the old hardcoded path was accidentally right today. The real defect is the root/`getuid()` logic, not the number.\n\n**Notifications — already done, no work needed.** `shield-kitty-watch.service` is enabled and active using `notify-send`, with fullscreen opt-in only. That was your actual request, and it was already satisfied.\n\n**Void-bin sources — seeded.** 161/161 DEPS repos fetched by direct SHA, **0 failures, 0 deferrals**, 3.0G total. The earlier run that stalled at 2-per-3-minutes was my own bug: unfetchable tag pins were falling back to `--depth 50` (331k objects for a `v20.19.1` node pin), and a `[A-Za-z0-9_.-]` character class was truncating names like `libc++_src` into `_src`. Both fixed and committed. The seeder shows as still running but has printed `done` — it''s finishing the last writes.\n\n**Still blocked on your sudo password:** enabling firewalld (note `sshd` is inactive, so the allow-SSH rule has no fallback), `gh` install for the 3 missing remotes, and installing BDE if you want it.\n\n**Outstanding:** the `electron34` compile hasn''t started — that''s the multi-hour part. Want me to kick it off, or hold?","time":{"start":1790454966518,"end":1790454971631}}');
