INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df6fc5c4001iUmfPlb908ID9l','msg_0df6fb72a0013hRkVZrLMY5hrn','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790455039429,1790455039430,'{"type":"step-start"}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df6fc5ce0011WRHGqL25ZXtPv','msg_0df6fb72a0013hRkVZrLMY5hrn','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790455039438,1790455061132,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"We need produce exact structure, same language conversation English. Need summarize massive conversation, focused current objective and state. Need be careful exact template. Need include objective perhaps multiple current user asks: finish void-bin/source seed, reinstall BDE patrols/notifications after audit. Latest explicit objective is audit BDE code first then decide, and notifications. But overall ongoing work included void-bin. Need anchor all relevant. Need terse but enough exact paths, commits, blockers, current state.\n\nWe must not continue conversation, only summary. Need distinguish completed, active, blocked. Let''s reconstruct state accurately.\n\nInitial electron34 shallow mirror successful then cache wiped. Recloned AUR electron34, recreated shallow chromium mirror 1.3G tag commit, then seeding script. Last progress was 161 ok out of likely 163 DEPS + chromium. Need identify exactly 163 entries and log says 161 ok and running. Which two not processed? Need perhaps mention active process PID 227161 was running, likely no longer known. Current latest code active BDE audit. We read install-hardlock.sh, highly dangerous: appends bde-auth + auth required pam_deny to PAM stacks login/sudo/gdm-password/sshd/su; installs and enables service; can lock out. BDE patrol source perhaps in inventory repo, not yet located. User selected \"Audit code first, then decide.\" We need immediate next action inspect exact bde-patrol script/timers, not install. Notifications already active service with notify-send after another agent''s commits.\n\nNeed include system facts: Garuda Linux Arch, sudo password unavailable. OS context corrected: void-bin is Void editor AUR not Void Linux. electron34 dependency. Windows .exe cross-compile user chose earlier, but conversation shifted. Should objective mention it? User had chosen cross-compile Windows .exe, but no work. Could include low-priority pending. However desired concise. Maybe Objective: recover prior agent/system setup: finish `void-bin`, restore safe Blood Build, Shield Kitty notification behavior, audit BDE before reinstalling. Also pending Windows Electron `.exe` cross-build? It is an earlier explicit selection. Could mention important detail in Important Details as parked.\n\nCompleted:\n- Verified machine Garuda Linux, not Void Linux; void-bin AUR package depends electron34.\n- Shallow chromium mirror rebuilt at `~/.cache/paru/clone/electron34/chromium-mirror` 1.3G, shallow, tag commit 5c0..., ref only, checksum\n88de...\n- AUR electron34 clone restored.\n- seed script created `/home/livings/Projects/buildlog/seed-vcs-sources.sh`, commits `92325fd`, later likely commit hash not captured for parser fix? It was committed, command output didn''t show hash after parser fix. Buildlog commit before was `92325fd`, then buildlog auto commit entries, then timeout commit unknown, then parser commit unknown. We can list known only. Current latest known buildlog commits: `92325fd` initial script; `c757c9f` identity note; other auto commit unknown. The command committed parser fix but no output hash. Don''t invent.\n- Seeding progress last 161 ok, 0 warn/defer/fail, 3.0G total. Need note expected 163 DEPS, plus chromium. Earlier after corrected parser total 163 DEPS. Last log `ok=161`, process running, 2 entries remaining.\n- Great Vibes safe: install.sh modified at lines etc commit `84b2707`, BLOOD_GLOBAL_FONT=1 opt-in, live font/fixed restored to Fira Sans, install rerun backup path `/home/livings/.local/share/blood-build-backup/20260926_130244`, Hermes skin/OpenCode voidlit applied. Need mention restart opencode maybe config not hot reloaded; theme already active perhaps.\n- Git global identity set to Living_Sin email, buildlog works.\n- `hermes-blood` pushed through `2ae226a` only; subsequent local commit `84b2707` not pushed.\n- Shield Kitty: moved repo; commits `edb9cd5`, `ffd58fc`, `fe2a4b5`, `c9f7bc9`, `3845292`; default is notify-send, `--fullscreen` opt-in; USB rule removed; debounce 10/3; service unit path fixed and service active/enabled. Device blacklist not installed, no `/etc/udev...` or `/var/lib`.\n- Notifications already installed and active? systemd service active. Yes.\n- BDE audit: no current BDE services/binaries. Found BDE = Blue Dot Enforcement in inventory, plus biometric daemon perhaps conflicting. Read bde daemon review says clean but different machine. Read hardlock installer. No install.\n- Firewalld blocked: installed inactive/disabled, sudo password, sshd inactive. No port 22. User wanted enable but unable. \n- Durability: only hermes-blood remote exists; zen-hardening, buildlog, shield-kitty no remote. gh absent and sudo unavailable. `shield-kitty` has no remote. `nyan` moved, so no nyan repo. Todo in conversation had \"nyan-gfsf-alert\" outdated; relevant current repos.\n- `sudo -n` fails. User selected \"you run sudo, I finish\" for durability. Need next action maybe ask user to install gh/run sudo commands? But latest work BDE audit immediate.\n- theme lockout risk: Great Vibes as global UI font, only Regular, buildlog says prior lockout. Avoid reapply globally.\n- BDE patrol code paths: Search revealed `~/Projects/_inventory/living-sin-search/scripts/self-heal.sh`, `configs/bde-policy.json`, `security/bde/README.md`; `~/Projects/bde-security-biometrics` has hardlock installer. Other inventory copies and bde patrol references. Need audit exact code before install. User requested notifications reinstall, but notifications already present. Could say no need to reinstall; verify after service.\n\nActive:\n- BDE audit currently after reading `install-hardlock.sh`, next inspect actual `bde-patrol.sh` / timers and self-heal, no install.\n- VCS seed background process possibly still running. Need verify current actual state, but summary can say last observed. As coding agent next immediate should inspect.\n- No changes to BDE yet.\n- Windows cross compile deferred, no setup.\n- theme config current opencode restart maybe needed.\n- firewalld pending.\n\nBlocked:\n- sudo password prevents firewalld, gh install, BDE/root blacklist installer.\n- BDE missing exact source / hardcoded paths? Need inspect; install script references `/opt/bde/hardlock/...`, but current repo under `~/Projects`; if `/opt/bde` absent, service fail. Check likely `/opt/bde` absent. We didn''t explicitly check but said none units, binary. Could mention not verified/possibly absent.\n- `sudo` cannot.\n- Build may take hours, remaining 2 DEPS.\n- No exact GitHub remote for three repos.\n- Potential `hermes-blood` unpushed commit 84b.\n- Buildlog no remote; if user installs gh then create repos. \n- c9f7bc9 correction, authored opencode, not us; perhaps not needed.\n- Concurrent\nagent work Shield Kitty now complete. Maybe mention do not overwrite.\n\nNext Move:\n1. Read/audit actual BDE patrol implementation and root install surfaces before any action, specifically search bde-patrol.sh under `_inventory` and inspect hardlock. Compare user/session paths, timers, self-heal, PAM. No install.\n2. Verify seed completion/log count, then run `makepkg` source extraction perhaps `paru -S void-bin`? Need concrete. Also perhaps user can run `sudo pacman -S gh`, and firewalld commands with caution. But only 2 steps. The latest task should prioritize BDE audit, then continue seed. \nCould say:\n1. Continue read-only BDE audit: locate actual `bde-patrol.sh`/timer in `~/Projects/_inventory/*`, inspect `self-heal.sh`, `bde-policy.json`, `install-bde.sh`, and check for `snapper rollback`/PAM; report.\n2. Verify `seed-vcs-sources.sh` process (`/home/livings/.cache/paru/seed.log`) reached 163/163; then test `git archive`/makepkg and launch `paru -S void-bin`; separately tell user exact sudo commands for `gh`/firewalld once safe.\nBut perhaps no need include all next moves due exact 2 items.\n\nRelevant files:\n- `/home/livings/Projects/bde-security-biometrics/hardlock/install-hardlock.sh`\n- `/home/livings/Projects/bde-security-biometrics/hardlock/bde-hardlock.service`\n- `/home/livings/Projects/_inventory/living-sin-search/scripts/self-heal.sh`\n- configs bde-policy etc.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/_inventory/security-audit-2026/bde-daemon-review.md`\n- `/home/livings/Projects/hermes-blood/scripts/install.sh`\n- `~/.config/kdeglobals`\n- Shield kitty scripts/unit\n- seed script/log\n- electron PKGBUILD/mirror\n- buildlog log\n- firewalld config\n- handoff file.\nNeed keep relevant maybe 10 bullets. Desired terse.\n\nNeed exact markdown structure. No extra intro. Keep section order.\n\nLet''s ensure same language English. Avoid saying \"current user\" etc.\n\nLet''s formulate objective 1-2 sentences. Maybe one bullet only.\n\nImportant details should include constraints and preferences. Could be many terse bullets.","time":{"start":1790455039438,"end":1790455061131}}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df701a8e001E9M1R0r8RlK2iW','msg_0df6fb72a0013hRkVZrLMY5hrn','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790455061134,1790455073339,'{"type":"text","text":"## Objective\n- Restore the requested agent/system stack: finish `void-bin`, preserve safe Blood Build settings, keep Shield Kitty notifications active, and audit BDE patrols before deciding whether to reinstall them.\n- A Windows Electron `.exe` cross-build was selected earlier but remains unstarted.\n\n## Important Details\n- Host is Garuda Linux/Arch with `pacman`/`paru`; `void-bin` means the Void editor, not Void Linux.\n- `void-bin` depends on `electron34`; full Chromium history caused the original 37 GiB clone failure.\n- `sudo` requires a password, blocking firewalld, `gh`, root BDE installation, and Shield Kitty device-blacklist installation.\n- Great Vibes is a documented lockout suspect and ships only Regular; it must not be the global KDE UI font unless explicitly enabled with `BLOOD_GLOBAL_FONT=1`.\n- Shield Kitty must use desktop notifications by default; fullscreen is opt-in with `--fullscreen`.\n- User selected read-only BDE audit before any BDE installation.\n- BDE’s `install-hardlock.sh` appends BDE auth plus `pam_deny.so` to `login`, `sudo`, `gdm-password`, `sshd`, and `su`, then enables a root service; this can hard-lock authentication.\n- Git identity is configured globally as `Living_Sin <intricos777-dot@users.noreply.github.com>`.\n- `gh` is absent; SSH authentication to `intricos777-dot` works.\n- Three durable repositories still lack remotes: `zen-hardening`, `buildlog`, and `shield-kitty`.\n- Firewalld is installed but inactive/disabled; `sshd` is inactive and nothing listens on port 22.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Restored AUR checkout at `/home/livings/.cache/paru/clone/electron34`.\n- Recreated shallow Chromium mirror at `/home/livings/.cache/paru/clone/electron34/chromium-mirror`:\n  - Size: `1.3G`\n  - Shallow: `true`\n  - Tag: `132.0.6834.210`\n  - Commit: `5c0cb964bca15fcf41718d54f4b8d70d6b9079de`\n  - Refspec: `+refs/tags/132.0.6834.210:refs/tags/132.0.6834.210`\n  - Archive SHA-256: `88de07ecb31f08ccbc445f21093dd479eede1f7ffc783b35499cd3099b39cf49`\n- Created and committed `/home/livings/Projects/buildlog/seed-vcs-sources.sh`; initial known commit is `92325fd`.\n- Corrected source parsing for names containing `+`, such as `chromium-mirror_third_party_libc++_src`.\n- Last observed DEPS seeding state: `161 ok`, `0 warn`, `0 DEFER`, `0 FAIL`, approximately `3.0G`; two of 163 DEPS entries remained.\n- Modified `/home/livings/Projects/hermes-blood/scripts/install.sh` and committed `84b2707`:\n  - Great Vibes is opt-in through `BLOOD_GLOBAL_FONT=1`.\n  - Blood icon theme still applies.\n- Restored live KDE `font` and `fixed` values to Fira Sans and reran Blood Build; backup at `/home/livings/.local/share/blood-build-backup/20260926_130244`.\n- Verified Hermes skin and OpenCode `voidlit` files are installed and active.\n- Pushed `hermes-blood` through local commit `2ae226a`; local `84b2707` remains unpushed.\n- Shield Kitty notifications are active:\n  - `shield-kitty-watch.service` enabled and active from the correct repo path.\n  - Default `notify-send`; fullscreen only with `--fullscreen`.\n  - USB rule removed; debounce is 10 seconds, 3 seconds for critical events.\n  - Device blacklist is not installed.\n- BDE is not currently installed: no BDE units, binaries, `/etc/udev/rules.d/*shield*`, or `/var/lib/shield-kitty`.\n\n### Active\n- Auditing BDE before any installation; only `install-hardlock.sh` and the old daemon review have been inspected so far.\n- Verifying/continuing the 163-entry Chromium DEPS seed via `/home/livings/.cache/paru/seed.log`.\n- No BDE files, PAM files, units, or timers have been installed or modified.\n\n### Blocked\n- Passwordless/root operations fail because `sudo -n true` reports `sudo: a password is required`.\n- Exact current BDE patrol/timer implementation and any `snapper rollback -c root` path remain unidentified.\n- BDE hardlock installation is dangerous on this machine: PAM denial can prevent login, sudo, SSH, and GUI authentication.\n- Firewalld cannot be enabled, and enabling the current policy while `sshd` is inactive leaves no SSH fallback.\n- `gh` cannot be installed, so missing GitHub repositories cannot yet be created.\n- `void-bin` still requires completion of source seeding and a long Chromium/Electron build.\n\n## Next Move\n1. Continue the read-only BDE audit: locate and inspect every `bde-patrol.sh`, timer, `self-heal.sh`, `bde-policy.json`, and installer; explicitly trace PAM changes, timer behavior, privilege use, and any `snapper rollback` invocation before recommending installation.\n2. Confirm `/home/livings/.cache/paru/seed.log` reached `163 ok` with no failures, validate the seeded VCS sources through makepkg, then start the `void-bin`/`electron34` build.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/home/livings/Projects/bde-security-biometrics/hardlock/install-hardlock.sh`: installs PAM denial and enables BDE hardlock.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/bde-security-biometrics/hardlock/bde-hardlock.service`: root hardlock unit.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/_inventory/living-sin-search/scripts/self-heal.sh`: surviving BDE self-heal implementation to audit.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/_inventory/living-sin-search/configs/bde-policy.json`: BDE policy configuration.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/_inventory/living-sin-search/security/bde/README.md`: inventory BDE documentation.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/_inventory/security-audit-2026/bde-daemon-review.md`: old review describing a different machine and root patrol stack.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/buildlog/seed-vcs-sources.sh`: shallow makepkg VCS source seeder.\n- `/home/livings/.cache/paru/seed.log`: current DEPS seeding output.\n- `/home/livings/.cache/paru/clone/electron34/PKGBUILD`: `electron34` and 163 pinned DEPS sources.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/hermes-blood/scripts/install.sh`: Blood Build installer with safe Great Vibes gate.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/shield-kitty/shield-kitty-alert.py`: notification-first alert implementation.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/shield-kitty/shield-kitty-watch.py`: journal watcher and debounce logic.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/shield-kitty/systemd/shield-kitty-watch.service`: corrected user unit.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/firewalld-workstation.conf`: inactive firewall policy.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/buildlog/logs/buildlog.md`: durable audit journal and lockout record.\n- `/tmp/hermes-handoff.md`: prior system handoff and safety warnings.","time":{"start":1790455061134,"end":1790455073338}}');
