other stale ''permanent'' claims remain ===\n./shield-kitty-fail2ban.local:6:# a source IP, host, or permanent state. It cannot \"lock out a system\" — it\n./shield-kitty-fail2ban.local:37:# 1 day (86400s), not -1. A permanent ban is not self-cancelling: on a\n./set-anon-identity.sh:49:# Without this, NetworkManager uses the permanent hardware MAC on every\n./set-anon-identity.sh:115:  echo \"       Your permanent hardware MAC may still be broadcasting.\" >&2\n./enroll-admin.sh:80:        echo \"REFUSED: enrolling $user would grant a permanent lockout exemption.\" >&2\n./set-home-trusted-zone.sh:86:if firewall-cmd --permanent --get-zones 2>/dev/null | grep -qx \"$ZONE\"; then\n./set-home-trusted-zone.sh:89:  firewall-cmd --permanent --new-zone=\"$ZONE\"\n./set-home-trusted-zone.sh:93:firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=\"$ZONE\" --set-target=default\n./set-home-trusted-zone.sh:94:firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=\"$ZONE\" --add-service=kdeconnectd\n./set-home-trusted-zone.sh:95:firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=\"$ZONE\" --add-service=mdns\n  (fail2ban-coverage.md excluded; checking it separately)\n67:All jails use `bantime = -1` — permanent, never expiring. `ignoreip` covers\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd ~/Projects/zen-hardening\nbash -n unban-self.sh && echo \"syntax OK\"\necho; echo \"=== confirm no other stale ''permanent'' claims remain ===\"\ngrep -rn \"bantime = -1\\|bantime=-1\\|permanent\" --include=\"*.sh\" --include=\"*.local\" --include=\"*.md\" . 2>/dev/null | grep -v \"^./fail2ban-coverage.md\" | head\necho \"  (fail2ban-coverage.md excluded; checking it separately)\"\ngrep -n \"bantime\" fail2ban-coverage.md 2>/dev/null | head","time":{"start":1790455797198,"end":1790455797214}}}');
