INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df7bc500001xMQnsjZ1RHr1y8','msg_0df7ba7f8001ic98PtpMVZGe1f','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790455825664,1790455825666,'{"type":"step-start"}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df7bc504001XFUUERLq3ELBSm','msg_0df7ba7f8001ic98PtpMVZGe1f','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790455825668,1790455830149,'{"type":"text","text":"Audit done. **The 1-day lockout you asked for is already live** — `bantime = 86400` on both jails, matching your repo, and firewalld is active with the `workstation` zone so bans are actually enforceable. I also found and fixed docs that would have misled you.\n\nBut two of your three requirements are **not** actually working, and one is impossible with the current tooling.\n\n**Remote access — largely uncovered, in three specific ways:**\n\n- **Your `ignoreip` exempts the entire network you''re on.** It includes `10.0.0.0/8`, and your address is `10.197.250.246/8`. That means **16,777,216 addresses are permanently exempt from banning** — fail2ban structurally cannot ban \"another system\" on your network. The 1-day ban only ever applies to hosts arriving from a public address.\n- **The `sshd` jail is inert.** `sshd` is inactive and nothing listens on 22, so it matches zero events. It exists as a placeholder, not a control.\n- **`kdeconnectd` is exposed and unmonitored.** It''s listening on `*:1716` (tcp+udp) — the *only* genuine LAN-reachable attack surface on this machine — and there is **no jail for it**. It handles remote control and file transfer, so it''s more relevant than sshd, which is off.\n\n**System spoofing — entirely uncovered, and fail2ban cannot do it.** There is no `arpwatch`, `suricata`, `zeek`, `tcpdump`, or `tpm2-tools`, and no spoofing logic in any repo. This isn''t a config gap I can close by editing a file: fail2ban parses auth logs for *repeated failures* and has no concept of ARP/DHCP spoofing, hostname collision, MAC impersonation, or a rogue device claiming to be your machine. Detecting those needs different tooling.\n\n**Fixed (commit `89506fc`):** `unban-self.sh` and `fail2ban-coverage.md` both claimed the policy was `bantime = -1` permanent. It isn''t — it''s 86400. That mattered in the worst direction: `unban-self.sh` is your emergency escape hatch, and its own header described a failure mode that doesn''t exist while omitting the real recovery advice. A ban now **expires by itself after a day**; you usually just wait. I also corrected a stale IP in the docs.\n\nNote the `recidive` jail is `enabled = true` live but `false` in your repo — the only config drift between them. Someone enabled it deliberately, which looks intentional given the documented bootstrap order.","time":{"start":1790455825668,"end":1790455830148}}');
