INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df801ca10011hZozm20vLhU8j','msg_0df801577001lVaCJzS6VdExoc','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790456110241,1790456114252,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"Very useful. Key findings:\n\n1. **`shield-kitty-watch.service` and `evidence-seal.timer` are `not-found`** — the units don''t exist! Earlier summary said they were active. So they were removed or never installed, or the units aren''t in /etc/systemd/system. This is a regression — need to check.\n\n2. **3 coredumps** — `systemd-coredump@...` three times. Need to investigate what crashed.\n\n3. **firewalld INVALID_ZONE: workstation** errors — but workstation now works. These are historical (from the broken period at 13:07-13:14). The most recent firewalld error was 13:09-13:14. Current state is fine. But I should confirm no recent errors after the last successful config.\n\n4. `watchdog-faucet-daemon` errors — a project `bch-faucet` with missing `.env`. Not security-critical, but a failed project service. It''s in user@1000.service context (59 errors). These are pre-existing project issues, likely one of the \"other instances\" work. Not boot-critical.\n\n5. `user@1000.service` has 59 errors — worth a look but these are user-session units (bch-faucet watchdog).\n\n6. wpa_supplicant 2 errors.\n\nLet me dig into:\n- coredumps (what crashed)\n- shield-kitty units missing\n- whether firewalld errors are historical (check timestamps vs now)\n- wpa_supplicant errors\n\nLet me check these.\n\nNote: the \"INVALID_ICMPTYPE: v6-neighbour-solicit\" errors — those are from an attempt to block ICMP types (the old broken public.xml which we removed). Historical.\n\nLet me investigate the coredumps and the missing units — those are real issues.\n\nAlso I notice the hostname in journal was `living-asustufdashf15fx517zcfx517zc` early in boot and `zero` later — that''s the rename taking effect. Fine.\n\nLet me check coredumps and shield-kitty.","time":{"start":1790456110241,"end":1790456114251}}');
