INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df80f507001uiBPWQp97R559b','msg_0df80ec95001csMQ20DExY04oc','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790456165639,1790456170266,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"dmesg returned nothing — likely restricted (kernel.dmesg_restrict=1, which we set). That''s our own hardening. I should note that: our sysctl `kernel.dmesg_restrict=1` means dmesg is now restricted, so I can''t read it unprivileged. That''s expected and correct, but it means these checks need root.\n\nFirewalld zone confirmed:\n- target: default\n- interfaces: lo wlo1\n- services: dhcpv6-client only\n- ports: none\n- protocols: icmp ipv6-icmp\n- icmp-blocks: NONE ✓\n- rich rules: none\n- forward: no, masquerade: no\n\nSo with `target: default`, firewalld''s default policy is reject for input. kdeconnectd (1716) and mDNS (5353) are NOT in the allow list → they will be dropped. Good. The listener binding doesn''t matter because the zone rejects by default.\n\nI should verify the actual nft rules to be certain (need root). Let me ask the user to run one root command to confirm, or note it.\n\nActually, earlier in the session we already confirmed `table inet firewalld` exists and the apply script verified. The zone has no ports/services for 1716/5353, target default → firewalld inserts a reject rule. I''m confident, but a direct nft check would be conclusive.\n\nLet me now check if agents are done, since I''ve done most of the read-only audit. Then compile findings and fix.\n\nRemaining audit items:\n- SMART (needs root)\n- dmesg (needs root, restricted by our own hardening — worth noting)\n- btrfs scrub status\n- user@1000 / bch-faucet — resolved (not installed)\n- Check SUID/world-writable for the audit\n- Check SSH daemon status\n- Check the `wpa_supplicant` errors\n\nLet me check agent status and a few last security items.\n\nLet me be mindful of scope. I have a good picture. Let me check agents + a couple more security items, then report and fix once agents are done.\n\nLet me check agents now.","time":{"start":1790456165639,"end":1790456170265}}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df81071b0016AsstUA3WFUlrZ','msg_0df80ec95001csMQ20DExY04oc','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790456170267,1790456172606,'{"type":"text","text":"Zone policy confirms the block: `target: default` with only `dhcpv6-client` and ICMP protocols allowed, so 1716 and 5353 are rejected despite being bound. Note `dmesg` is now unreadable — that''s our own `kernel.dmesg_restrict=1` working as intended, so those checks need root.\n\nChecking whether the agents have finished:","time":{"start":1790456170267,"end":1790456172605}}');
