INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df8673d7001VgOU3T7bp1xECZ','msg_0df866e2f001VIHINiQFcHLTCw','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790456525783,1790456525784,'{"type":"step-start"}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df8673d9001AAwGtbU786DCZf','msg_0df866e2f001VIHINiQFcHLTCw','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790456525785,1790456529264,'{"type":"text","text":"Fixed (`b39490a`). Your error exposed **two** bugs, and the second one is the dangerous kind.\n\n**Bug 1 — the one you hit.** `sudo` resets `$HOME` to `/root`, so `$HOME/Projects/...` resolved to `/root/Projects/...`. The installer now resolves the real home from `SUDO_USER` via `getent`, and rewrites the unit''s hardcoded path plus an explicit `Environment=HOME` at install time.\n\n**Bug 2 — would have been silent, and it''s worse.** Your error message made me check the hook itself, and it had the same class of failure. The hook runs as a child of arpwatch, which systemd starts as root and which drops privileges with `-u`. **`-u` changes the uid but not the environment** — so the hook inherited no `DISPLAY`, no `WAYLAND_DISPLAY`, and no `DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS`. Every spoof notification would have failed, while the log line still appeared normally. It would have looked like it was working.\n\nI confirmed this is real rather than theoretical: `notify-send` with a bare environment fails with `Cannot autolaunch D-Bus without X11 $DISPLAY`, while the same call with the session reconstructed exits `0`. The hook now rebuilds the session from your user bus socket (`/run/user/1000/bus`) and picks up the Wayland socket if present.\n\nI also made the alert script path derive from `BASH_SOURCE` instead of `$HOME` — it''s a sibling directory of the hook''s parent, so it''s independent of who runs it and can''t break this way again.\n\n**One more fix while I was in there:** the notifier''s output was being redirected into the log file. When the log wasn''t writable, the redirect itself failed and the real delivery error vanished — readable only at the moment you needed it. It''s now captured and routed through a `log()` that falls back to stderr.\n\n**Verified:** 7/7 classification tests still pass, and the installer dry-run now completes under a simulated `env -i HOME=/root SUDO_USER=livings`.\n\nPlease re-run both commands. The dry-run should now get past step 1 and print `home: /home/livings (from SUDO_USER=livings)`.","time":{"start":1790456525785,"end":1790456529263}}');
