INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df8c5649001uuG1LhJ7zrdMPp','msg_0df8c4a25001TDjsfHzVG4ddqR','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790456911433,1790456914089,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"A NEW repo appeared: `lifsea-security-suite` — committed 2 minutes ago. Agents are creating new projects. This is a moving target.\n\nzen-hardening last commit 6 minutes ago. buildlog 6 min. lifsea-security-suite 2 min.\n\nThe agents are clearly still doing work. Waiting indefinitely may not be productive. The user said wait for repo activity to go quiet. But new repos keep appearing — the agents are actively building.\n\nI should report this: a new repo appeared during the wait, so agents are still creating work, not finishing. I should ask whether to continue waiting or proceed.\n\nBut I don''t want to ping-pong questions. Let me give a clear status and a recommendation.\n\nImportant: zen-hardening was committed 6 min ago (b39490a). Let me check the recidive state now — that tells me if the regression is still there or was fixed.\n\nLet me check the current state of zen-hardening''s fail2ban config and git log. That''s read-only and informative.\n\nLet me also note memory pressure is likely worse with more agents.\n\nLet me report and ask for a decision, since this is genuinely the user''s call — but I should be decisive with a recommendation.\n\nLet me first gather the read-only facts on zen-hardening recidive so my report is concrete.\n\nLet me check.","time":{"start":1790456911433,"end":1790456914087}}');
