n  76:backend = systemd\n  81:# matches nothing today. It is here so that if sshd is ever enabled, bans\n  83:[sshd]\n  84:enabled  = true\n  89:bantime  = 86400\n  94:[recidive]\n  95:# ENABLED as of 2026-09-26 — enabled deliberately on this machine, not drift.\n  107:#   1. deploy this file with ''enabled = false''\n  109:#   3. sudo sed -i ''s/^enabled  = false/enabled  = true/'' \\\n  118:#   backend/logpath        polling + the file above, since the systemd journal\n  120:enabled  = true\n  124:# contain it. Needs a non-systemd backend override.\n  125:backend = polling\n  126:logpath  = /var/log/fail2ban.log\n  129:bantime  = 86400\n","metadata":{"output":"═══ zen-hardening recent commits ═══\n  b39490a fix: resolve paths via SUDO_USER, bootstrap session env for notify\n  3a65f5e security: add ARP spoof detection via arpwatch, notifying via Shield Kitty\n  29355eb feat(zen): rebuild sentinel, watchman and bchn-monitor\n  c897508 fail2ban: recidive enabled=true in repo, matching live by request\n  89506fc docs: correct stale permanent-ban claims to the actual 86400\n  819c363 faillock: add ordered deploy script, fix malformed audit/silent flags\n  207f22e chore: ignore __pycache__\n  6aa717a zen-hardening: unban-self escape hatch, and honest fail2ban coverage doc\n\n  dirty files: 2\n     M arpwatch-spoof-alert.sh\n    ?? install-audit-readonly.sh\n\n═══ THE RECIDIVE REGRESSION — current state of source config ═══\n  41:# wifi, or airports, so bantime is finite by design.\n  44:# recidive ships with enabled=false so a first-ever install cannot abort\n  48:#   sudo sed -i ''s/^enabled  = false/enabled  = true/'' \\\n  54:[DEFAULT]\n  67:zone = workstation\n  69:bantime = 86400\n  73:# backend=auto tries only pyinotify/polling — it does NOT include systemd,\n  74:# so a journalctl logpath was silently ignored. This system is journald-only:\n  75:# no syslog-ng, no rsyslog, no /var/log/auth.log. systemd backend required.\n  76:backend = systemd\n  81:# matches nothing today. It is here so that if sshd is ever enabled, bans\n  83:[sshd]\n  84:enabled  = true\n  89:bantime  = 86400\n  94:[recidive]\n  95:# ENABLED as of 2026-09-26 — enabled deliberately on this machine, not drift.\n  107:#   1. deploy this file with ''enabled = false''\n  109:#   3. sudo sed -i ''s/^enabled  = false/enabled  = true/'' \\\n  118:#   backend/logpath        polling + the file above, since the systemd journal\n  120:enabled  = true\n  124:# contain it. Needs a non-systemd backend override.\n  125:backend = polling\n  126:logpath  = /var/log/fail2ban.log\n  129:bantime  = 86400\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd ~/Projects/zen-hardening\necho \"═══ zen-hardening recent commits ═══\"\ngit log --oneline -8 | sed ''s/^/  /''\necho\necho \"  dirty files: $(git status --porcelain | wc -l)\"\ngit status --porcelain | head -12 | sed ''s/^/    /''\necho\necho \"═══ THE RECIDIVE REGRESSION — current state of source config ═══\"\ngrep -nE ''^\\[|enabled|bantime|backend|logpath|^zone'' shield-kitty-fail2ban.local 2>/dev/null | sed ''s/^/  /''","time":{"start":1790456915016,"end":1790456915038}}}');
