INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df9187c0001AfwKrTqMOEv8v3','msg_0df917ab4001SPfjaPCI0sTdXd','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790457251776,1790457253418,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"The awk works correctly in isolation! It outputs `10.3.0.1 aa:bb:cc:00:00:0b,cc:dd:ee:00:00:0c`.\n\nSo the awk is fine. The problem must be in the script — the `current` variable construction, or the heredoc/quoting inside the script broke the awk.\n\nWait — the script has the awk inside `$( ... )`. Let me check: inside `$( )` with single quotes inside, it should be fine.\n\nHmm, but the test showed 0 alerts. Let me check whether the script file actually has the updated awk. Maybe my edit didn''t apply as expected, or the script is reading a different DATAFILE.\n\nActually — the test harness: `run(){ rm -f \"/tmp/arpT2/st_$1\"; BDE_ARP_DATAFILE=\"$2\" BDE_ARP_STATE=\"...\" \"$S\" >/dev/null 2>&1; }`. And I exported BDE_ARP_DATAFILE globally too, but run() overrides it per-call. Should be fine.\n\nLet me run the script directly with debugging to see what happens.\n\nLet me check the script content and run it verbosely.","time":{"start":1790457251776,"end":1790457253417}}');
