 it cannot drift again. commit fc71393\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd ~/Projects/buildlog\nbuildlog fix \"arpwatch-spoof STILL failed after the 3.9 rewrite: the culprit was -q. arpwatch(8) lists -q in the synopsis [-CdFNpqsvzZ] and describes it in OPTIONS, but the 3.9 binary rejects it and prints usage, exit 1. Tested every synopsis letter: -C -d -F -N -p -s -v -z -Z all accepted, -q is the sole exception, so the man page is wrong. arpwatch prints usage BEFORE opening the raw socket, so bad flags are detectable unprivileged -- added a parse-check to the installer reading ARPWATCH_ARGS shared with the unit, so it cannot drift again. commit fc71393\" 2>&1 | tail -1","time":{"start":1790457474638,"end":1790457474657}}}');
