red commit 819c363, not deployed.\n- Fail2ban docs/repo update commits.\n- Firewalld active, ban action works.\n- arpwatch initial build commits 3a65f5e, b39490a; fixes, but architecture invalid due wrong arpwatch version. Since completed but superseded. Mention as historical code commits.\n- notifications.\n- KDE correction.\n- source seeding etc.\n- Maybe original Great Vibes.\n\nActive:\n- arpwatch service currently enabled but restart-looping due old unsupported flags. Need stop.\n- new scanner files uncommitted, installer not updated.\n- direct test works but full suite rerun.\n- ignoreip etc maybe active.\n- void build.\n\nBlocked:\n- root manual command needed to stop old service and deploy corrected units. But user can run.\n- Cannot validate actual recidive runtime because /var/log/fail2ban.log root 0600. Maybe not blocker.\n- Cannot safely narrow ignoreip without true broadcast subnet.\n- void electron build long.\n- other remotes/gh? Prior workstream maybe preserve. gh absent, three repos no remotes. But current summary perhaps include under blocked if retained. User didn''t ask, but developer says carry constraints. Include terse.\n\nNext Move:\n1. Stop old service: `sudo systemctl disable --now arpwatch-spoof.service` maybe also `sudo systemctl reset-failed` optional. Then finish scanner architecture:\n  - remove/replace unsupported exec-hook references\n  - update `arpwatch-spoof.service` correct flags and precreate `/var/lib/arpwatch/arp.dat` owned? likely root; scan service needs read. Need decide ownership. We can say update installer to create empty datafile and install collector+scan service+timer.\n  - ensure datafile readable by scan service. Current unit scan service has no User, so root by default. It can read. But perhaps better user. Yet not decided. Keep generic.\n  - test `arpwatch -?`, `fail` no; `systemd-analyze verify` after arpwatch installed; use synthetic full tests.\n  - commit.\n  - give user exact commands dry-run/install and verify.\n2. After stable, decide ignoreip with user-provided broadcast domain; then start electron build after seed final check.\nMaybe immediate next action should include command. Summary format allows.\n\nRelevant Files:\nList:\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/arpwatch-spoof.service`: current corrected-in-repo collector, uncommitted; installed /etc version is old broken.\n- scanner files.\n- old alert hook obsolete.\n- installer still old (still installs collector only perhaps) and needs update.\n- /etc/systemd/system/arpwatch-spoof.service live broken.\n- faillock etc.\n- fail2ban.\n- BDE.\n- buildlog.\n- void PKGBUILD and seed log.\nMaybe no need list every old.\n\nNeed be accurate on new service `arpwatch-spoof-scan.service` unit. It has no `User=`, so root. It includes `Environment=HOME=/home/livings`, bootstraps uid based EUID=0 -> rt `/run/user/0` if no XDG_RUNTIME_DIR. Wait! Important bug! The scanner''s bootstrap_session_env:\n```\nlocal uid=\"${EUID:-$UID}\" rt\nrt=\"${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-/run/user/$uid}\"\n```\nUnit has `Environment=HOME=/home/livings` but not `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` or DBUS. Running as root means EUID=0, so it tries /run/user/0/bus, which likely doesn''t exist. Thus notifications will fail. This architecture has a latent bug! We should include as active unresolved. The old alert hook had same issue when root unless it runs as livings (it did arpwatch drop to user). But new scanner service runs root with no User. It should run as `livings` or explicitly set `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/1000`, `DBUS...`, `WAYLAND...`, or derive target user. This needs fixing before deployment. Very important. The conversation ended just after test, not noticing. Summary should mention as active bug. But we are a summarizer, not continue. Need preserve current exact state. Could say \"new scan service currently has no `User=` and would derive `/run/user/0`; notification env still needs correction before deployment.\" This is derivable but not explicitly in conversation. Is it okay to include? We should summarize known context, not invent, but this is exact. Better to include under active \"must validate user/session environment\" based prior learning.\n\nAlso scanner in_ignore uses Python each IP/CIDR, okay. `count` log grammar `anomal$( [ \"$count\" = 1 ] && echo y || echo ies)` yields anomaly/anomalies okay.\n- data file accumulation: scanner sees all historical entries forever, so \"newly anomalous\" will alert once per condition; if state file is lost, alerts old anomalies all over again. On /8 may false positives. Need perhaps state. Not necessary summary.\n- The service collector with `-q` and `-s`: Need confirm -q maybe suppress reports; -s suppress email? likely. Man usage. Fine.\n- Old installer creates log owned livings, DB dir livings. Corrected collector root can write anyway. New scanner can read. The current datafile path changed from `arpwatch.dat` to `arp.dat`, but installer still `DB=/var/lib/arpwatch/arpwatch.dat`; it does not create `arp.dat`. This is critical! Need update installer. It currently:\n```\nDB=/var/lib/arpwatch/arpwatch.dat\n...\ninstall dir\ninstall log\ninstall old unit (repo now corrected collector path /var/lib/arpwatch/arp.dat)\n```\nIt never touches DB file, just directory. Man says empty arp.dat must be created before first run. So install likely fail due missing datafile or arpwatch maybe creates? Man says must. Need active blocker.\n- Also installer does not install scan service/timer, nor remove old alert unit, nor set scanner env correctly.\n- The service restart loop from old unit still installed. Repo service was overwritten but not reinstalled. Good.\n\nNeed reflect BDE fixed code has potential logic flaw? Let''s inspect bde-auth: It removed unused talk. `capture_live` calls daemon action capture then `verify_against_profile` locally. talk unused. Exit 2 constant never used because unavailable maps to exit 0/1. But fine. Installer says failmode open but PAM `default=ignore`; on