d mention BDE notification layer already installed. no root.\n\nThe user gave commands and got error; currently service restart loop. The next agent should probably fix files before asking user to rerun. We must summarize that.\n\nLet''s formulate in terse bullets but enough detail.\n\nPotential structure:\n\n## Objective\n- Finish local host security: replace broken arpwatch integration, safely deploy `livings`-only faillock exemption, and preserve 24h bans without self-lockout.\n- Resume `void-bin`/Electron build after final source-seed verification.\n\n## Important Details\n- Garuda Linux/Arch, `livings` uid1000 only nonroot login; root uid0; only this host accessible. `sudo` password manually.\n- Current network 10.197.250.246/8, gateway 10.128.128.128, DHCP enterprise /8.\n- Fail2ban 86400; ignoreip 10/8 means no same-network ban. Do not guess subnet.\n- KDE Connect is autostart, blocked by firewall.\n- arpwatch 3.9 no hook and exact command. No auto-ban due random MAC.\n- Shield Kitty events schema etc.\n- BDE remains not installed.\n\nMaybe mention sudo HOME behavior in Important Details: scripts resolve `SUDO_USER`; don''t use `$HOME` in root installers. That''s important. Add.\n\nWork Completed:\n- BDE.\n- faillock prepared.\n- fail2ban.\n- arpwatch initial and tests.\n- Seed.\n\nActive:\n- live failure and repo rework.\n- service is restart loop.\n- scanner direct test.\n- faillock deploy.\n- ignoreip.\n- void.\n\nBlocked:\n- user sudo required.\n- cannot read fail2ban log (root 0600) to confirm recidive runtime.\n- unknown subnet.\n- gh / remotes maybe.\n- arpwatch live requires root; cannot run from agent.\n- electron build not started.\nMaybe service failure is not \"blocked\" because fixable.\n\nNext Move:\n1. stop loop and finalize. Include exact command and file tasks. But Next Move should not assume user response? It''s okay.\n2. update and deploy then decide ignoreip / electron.\n\nRelevant files list exact.\n\nNeed ensure user chose \"Deploy admin