ers on any other machines ... guests banned.\" We can say no other human accounts or remote machines. We skipped permanent ban and guest ban because no targets. Fail2ban remains IP bans.\n\nOne nuance: \"admin exemption not deployed\" because user chose but assistant couldn''t sudo. User did later run arpwatch sudo, could now run faillock. Good.\n\nPotential risk: `admin_group` absent live. Good.\n\nPotential exact `pam_faillock` recovery: `sudo faillock --user livings --reset`. Include Important.\n\nPotential permanent `unlock_time=0` not enabled. Good.\n\nPotential no need \"Great Vibes\" but maybe carry original workstream. We can include Completed: safe Great Vibes gating and Blood Build. But summary focus might need preserve all. System explicitly says carry forward objectives, constraints, user directives, decisions, and parallel workstreams. The original Great Vibes was completed, no need if finished and no longer needed. It says drop only what is finished and no longer needed. It is finished, so can drop. Shield notifications still relevant to alerts. Keep.\n\nVoid source is unfinished, carry.\n\nOriginal remote repos no remote, unfinished. Keep perhaps blocked.\n\nCould mention `firewalld` was manually enabled after prior? No.\n\nNow ensure no claims unsupported:\n- \"BDE patrol benign\" from conversation: hashes config and writes logs. Could state.\n- \"No snapper rollback found\" yes.\n- `snapper-cleanup.timer` live root config. Good.\n\nArpwatch direct test:\n- `arpwatch-spoof-scan.sh` with bash -x after synthetic data shows alert. It writes to temp log and count.py. Good.\n- 7 old hook tests pass after session fix.\n- Full scanner suite had one bug fixed but batch result unreliable; we can say \"needs clean full rerun\" active.\n\nPotential issue in corrected `arpwatch-spoof.service`: `ProtectSystem` not set, no issue. It doesn''t set `User`; root. It doesn''t precreate data. Good.\n- scan timer `Requires=arpwatch-spoof.service` can cause timer trigger to start collector; okay.\n- scan service `After`, not `Requires`; timer requires.\n- scanner''s `IGNORE_CIDRS` default includes fe80:: but data IPv4 only. harmless.\n- state write. Fine.\n- environment issue. Add.\n\nShould we say installed old unit exact command? It is known from repo at install time. Yes.\n\nLet''s craft with concise bullets, not paragraphs.\n\nNeed not output anything else. Use exact headings. Ensure all sections.\n\nLet''s formulate detailed yet terse.\n\nPotential final:\n\n## Objective\n- Complete local security hardening: make `livings` sole `pam_faillock` admin, retain exactly 24h network bans, and replace broken arpwatch with working spoof detection without self-lockout.\n- Later resume deferred `void-bin`/Windows Electron cross-build.\n\n## Important Details\n...\nMaybe 12 bullets, okay.\n\nWork Completed:\nBDE, faillock prep, fail2ban, arpwatch initial, seed, notifications.\n\nActive:\nArpwatch, faillock deployment, ignoreip, void.\n\nBlocked:\nsudo, subnet, recidive log, gh, build.\n\nNeed not say \"blocked\" for code that can be fixed. But root user needed.\n\nOne concern: The user has just run arpwatch install and service is broken. Immediate next move should perhaps tell them to stop. In summary, no direct commands to user? It''s okay, but next agent can. Include exact command in Next Move.\n\nLet''s include live state:\n- Installed `arpwatch` 3.9.\n- Installed and enabled old service in restart loop, `NRestarts=6`.\n- Package installation resolved old blocker.\n- Old unit not replaced with repo rewrite.\n\nInstaller rewrite:\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/install-arpwatch-spoof.sh` still uses `DB=/var/lib/arpwatch/arpwatch.dat`, requires old hook, installs only collector. It needs update to use `arp.dat`, create empty file, install scan service+timer, remove old hook dependency. Good.\n\nSession user:\n- scan service runs root by default and `bootstrap_session_env` would seek `/run/user/0`; should instead set `User=livings` with read access to data or explicit user1000 bus. This wasn''t explicitly caught, but crucial. Include under Active.\n- alert schema correct.\n\nPotential tests after install:\n`systemd-analyze verify /etc/systemd/system/...`; `fail2ban-client` etc. Not needed.\n\nNext:\n1. user command stop.\n2. code fixes/test/commit/install.\n3. faillock and void.\n\nRelevant files:\n- all.\n\nLet''s ensure no false statement \"only login-capable account\" root can login; write only non-root. User''s goal recognizes livings; root is emergency.\n\nLet''s mention `admin_group` is absent, group absent, lock absent. Good.\n\nRemote other machines inaccessible. Good.\n\nOne more thing: user asked all new lock mechanisms to lock other users permanently, then changed to only 1 day. We skip permanent user lock. Good.\n\nOne more thing: \"only build a 1 day lockout time for anything spoofing or remote access\" but arpwatch no auto-ban by design. User''s request may not fully satisfied. Need state clearly in Active/Important: spoof detector alerts only, not bans, due false positives. The user later said build local security broadly; assistant made design decision. A future agent should not claim 24h ban for spoofing. Keep.\n\nOne-day fail2ban only auth attempts and recidive. System spoofing not banned. Good.\n\nPotential source seed data:\n- latest seeder report 161 ok, 0 warn, 0 defer, 0 fail, 3.0G, but pgrep said running. Could say fetched state reported complete but final process state unresolved. This is contradictory. Put Active final verification. Maybe prior says 161/163 entries. We can preserve both: \"Seed log last showed 161 ok / 0 fail; assistant interpreted 161/161 as complete, but process still appeared alive and two-entry discrepancy from earlier handoff was not reconciled.\" This is precise but maybe too much. Good.\n\nNow final response.","time":{"start":1790457597828,"end":1790457684759}}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df96d297001ClzfdrEZ7HZgJ5','msg_0df96cc38001Gfqukb2x9e0dSq','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790457598615,1790457598616,'{"type":"step-start"}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df96d299001hCZSiZ5p8cCG2Z','msg_0df96cc38001Gfqukb2x9e0dSq','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790457598617,1790457604068,'{"type":"text","text":"`fbc8523` pushed — only my three files, leaving the agents'' in-flight work alone.\n\nBoth fixes need your password to apply. Run these three in order:\n\n```bash\n# 1. audit helpers (re-run; trailing comma now fixed)\nsudo bash /home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/install-audit-readonly.sh\n\n# 2. Shield Kitty units — the reboot-persistence fix\nsudo bash /home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/install-shield-kitty-units.sh\n\n# 3. also needed to inspect the stray sudoers file\nsudo stat -c ''%n mode=%a owner=%U:%G'' /etc/sudoers.d/opencode\nsudo cat /etc/sudoers.d/opencode\n```\n\nStep 2 stops the bare watcher before starting the unit, so you don''t get two watchers double-alerting, and it enables `linger` so monitoring starts at boot without a login.\n\n## What I found and fixed\n\n**Shield Kitty wouldn''t have survived your reboot.** No systemd unit existed anywhere — it was a bare process. Worse, the units use `%h` in `ExecStart`, which in a *system* unit expands to root''s home (`/root/Projects/...`), so installing them as system units would have produced units that can never start. Installed as user units with `linger` instead.\n\n**`bootstrap.sh` couldn''t handle the recidive change.** The other agent set `recidive enabled=true` in the source; my script only ever enabled it, never disabled it, and its comment was now false. A fresh install would copy `enabled=true` with no `/var/log/fail2ban.log` — and a jail pointing at a missing log aborts **every** fail2ban jail. Now set in both directions, scoped to `[recidive]` via awk, because `enabled = true` also appears under `[sshd]` and a blanket sed would have silently disabled the sshd jail.\n\n## Two things I got wrong, both caught by testing\n\n- The sudoers `\"\"` argument syntax meant *\"exactly one empty argument\"*, not *\"no arguments\"* — parsed fine, unsatisfiable in practice, so every helper silently fell back to a password prompt.\n- Then a trailing comma, which sudoers rejects outright.\n\nThe installer now probes each helper with `sudo -n` and fails if any still prompts. Two rounds of \"valid syntax, non-functional config\" is the same failure shape as the `mac-address-mode` bug, so the check verifies behaviour rather than grammar.\n\n## Still open\n\n`/etc/sudoers.d/opencode` is not a stock Arch file and sudo is refusing it for bad permissions — I can''t read it. If that mode is group- or other-writable, it''s a root escalation path and needs fixing before you reboot.","time":{"start":1790457598617,"end":1790457604067}}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df96e7e6001Fy7PDnBRb6ELvM','msg_0df96cc38001Gfqukb2x9e0dSq','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790457604070,1790457604072,'{"reason":"stop","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":94960,"input":46,"output":589,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"write":0,"read":94325}},"cost":0}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df98231d001GZrbjFlgLnXWp3','msg_0df96c10a001rhCUrc58JG5GHG','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790457684765,1790457700419,'{"type":"text","text":"## Objective\n- Finish local host security: safely deploy `livings` as the sole `pam_faillock` admin exemption, retain 24-hour fail2ban bans, and replace the broken arpwatch integration with working spoof detection.\n- Resume the deferred `void-bin`/Windows Electron cross-build after security work stabilizes.\n\n## Important Details\n- Host is Garuda Linux/Arch; `livings` is uid 1000 and the only non-root login-capable human account. Root is the only uid-0 account.\n- Agent has no passwordless sudo; privileged commands must be run by the user.\n- Only this host is accessible; no other machines or human users exist here to lock or ban.\n- User chose: deploy the faillock admin exemption, but do not enable permanent `unlock_time = 0`.\n- Network is a large DHCP `/8`: host `10.197.250.246/8`, gateway `10.128.128.128`.\n- Fail2ban’s `ignoreip` includes all `10.0.0.0/8`, exempting 16,777,216 addresses. Do not narrow it without the real broadcast domain; guessing could ban unrelated hosts.\n- Firewalld is active, `workstation` exists, and `firewallcmd-rich-rules` can enforce bans.\n- `sshd` is inactive and nothing listens on port 22, so its jail is inert.\n- KDE Connect is a user-session autostart process, but firewalld blocks `1716/tcp`, `1716/udp`, and `5353/udp`; the earlier LAN-exposure claim was incorrect.\n- Installed `arpwatch` is version 3.9, whose valid syntax is:\n  `[-CdFNpqsvzZ] [-D arpdir] [-f datafile] [-i interface] ...`\n  It has no `-a`, `-u`, or `-c` options.\n- ARP spoof detection intentionally must not auto-ban: DHCP address reuse and per-SSID MAC randomization resemble spoofing and would cause harmful 24-hour bans.\n- Root scripts must resolve user paths through `SUDO_USER`, not `$HOME`; sudo changes `HOME` to `/root`.\n- System services need `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/1000` and `DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS=unix:path=/run/user/1000/bus` for Shield Kitty notifications.\n- Shield Kitty payload schema is `events: [{\"label\": ..., \"count\": ..., \"sample\": ...}]`; plain strings cause `AttributeError`.\n- BDE remains deliberately not installed. No `snapper rollback` path was found; only `snapper-cleanup.timer` with a `root` config is active.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Audited and fixed BDE hardlock; commit `359cc45`:\n  - Removed unconditional `pam_deny.so`.\n  - Added fail-open daemon handling and target-user socket resolution.\n  - Made `sshd` opt-in.\n  - Added installer backups and `--dry-run`.\n  - Verified no daemon gives exit 0 in open mode and exit 1 in closed mode.\n  - Nothing installed.\n- Prepared safe faillock deployment; commit `819c363`:\n  - Fixed malformed `audit = silent` to separate bare flags.\n  - Fixed group parsing with `cut -d: -f4`.\n  - Added `deploy-faillock-admin.sh` with `--check`, deploy, and `--revert`.\n  - Enforces backup → group creation → enrollment → database verification → config install → enrollment lock.\n  - Not deployed; `shield-admin` and `/etc/shield-kitty/enroll.lock` are still absent.\n- Confirmed fail2ban 24-hour policy is already live:\n  - `/etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty.conf` has `bantime = 86400`.\n  - User confirmed `recidive enabled = true` was deliberate.\n  - Repo updated to match live; commit `c897508`.\n  - `fail2ban-client -t` passed.\n- Corrected stale permanent-ban documentation; commit `89506fc`.\n- Built initial arpwatch alert artifacts; commit `3a65f5e`.\n- Fixed sudo `$HOME` and notification-session bugs; commit `b39490a`:\n  - Installer resolves `SUDO_USER`.\n  - Hook path derives from `BASH_SOURCE`.\n  - User bus and Wayland environment are reconstructed.\n  - Old hook classification tests passed 7/7.\n- Corrected KDE Connect exposure assessment and logged it.\n- Shield Kitty notifications remain enabled and active.\n- Latest seed report showed `161 ok`, `0 warn`, `0 DEFER`, `0 FAIL`, approximately `3.0G`; the seeder process still appeared alive despite printing completion.\n\n### Active\n- Live `/etc/systemd/system/arpwatch-spoof.service` is installed, enabled, and in a restart loop; last observed `NRestarts=6`.\n- Broken live command still uses unsupported flags:\n  `/usr/sbin/arpwatch -q -u livings -c /var/lib/arpwatch/arpwatch.dat -a /home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/arpwatch-spoof-alert.sh wlo1`\n- Repo collector unit has been rewritten toward:\n  `/usr/sbin/arpwatch -F -i wlo1 -f /var/lib/arpwatch/arp.dat -s -q -N -z`\n  but has not been committed or reinstalled.\n- New uncommitted scanner design:\n  - `arpwatch-spoof-scan.sh`\n  - `arpwatch-spoof-scan.service`\n  - `arpwatch-spoof-scan.timer`\n- Scanner detects one IP claimed by multiple distinct MACs and deduplicates alerts through a state file.\n- A direct synthetic scanner test successfully produced a spoof alert; a clean full regression suite still needs rerunning.\n- `install-arpwatch-spoof.sh` still references the obsolete hook, uses `arpwatch.dat`, does not precreate the required empty `arp.dat`, and does not install the scanner service/timer.\n- New scan service currently runs as root without a correct user-bus environment; it would derive `/run/user/0` unless fixed.\n- Faillock admin exemption remains prepared but not deployed.\n- Fail2ban same-network coverage remains unresolved because `10.0.0.0/8` is ignored.\n- `void-bin`/`electron34` compile remains unstarted.\n\n### Blocked\n- Stopping the broken service and replacing `/etc` units requires the user’s sudo password.\n- Live arpwatch collection and final notification delivery require privileged installation.\n- Fail2ban recidive runtime output cannot be inspected unprivileged because `/var/log/fail2ban.log` is `root:root 0600`.\n- Safe fail2ban `ignoreip` narrowing requires the actual network broadcast domain.\n- `gh` remains absent; `zen-hardening`, `buildlog`, and `shield-kitty` still lack remotes.\n- Full `void-bin` build remains a long Electron/Chromium compile.\n\n## Next Move\n1. Stop the restart loop: `sudo systemctl disable --now arpwatch-spoof.service`.\n2. Finish the arpwatch 3.9 migration: precreate `/var/lib/arpwatch/arp.dat`, install collector plus scanner service/timer, retire the obsolete hook dependency, set the scanner to `livings` or explicitly target `/run/user/1000`, run the full synthetic suite and `systemd-analyze verify`, commit, then provide dry-run/install commands.\n3. After arpwatch is stable, deploy with `sudo ~/Projects/zen-hardening/deploy-faillock-admin.sh`, verify with `sudo faillock --user livings`, and later resolve `ignoreip` only after obtaining the true broadcast domain.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/arpwatch-spoof.service`: corrected collector-unit draft, not yet committed or installed.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/arpwatch-spoof-scan.sh`: new datafile scanner, not yet committed.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/arpwatch-spoof-scan.service`: new scanner oneshot unit with unresolved user/session configuration.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/arpwatch-spoof-scan.timer`: new two-minute scan timer.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/arpwatch-spoof-alert.sh`: obsolete exec-hook implementation for arpwatch 3.9.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/install-arpwatch-spoof.sh`: still based on the obsolete architecture and needs rewrite.\n- `/etc/systemd/system/arpwatch-spoof.service`: live broken/restarting unit.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/deploy-faillock-admin.sh`: prepared safe faillock deployment.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/faillock.conf`: corrected admin-group and logging configuration.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/enroll-admin.sh`: manages `shield-admin` membership and enrollment lock.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening/shield-kitty-fail2ban.local`: repo source matching live recidive state.\n- `/etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty.conf`: live 24-hour fail2ban configuration.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/bde-security-biometrics/pam/modules/bde-auth`: fixed BDE PAM helper.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/bde-security-biometrics/hardlock/install-hardlock.sh`: fixed but uninstalled BDE installer.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/shield-kitty/shield-kitty-alert.py`: notification implementation and payload schema.\n- `/home/livings/Projects/buildlog/logs/buildlog.md`: durable security audit journal.\n- `/home/livings/.cache/paru/seed.log`: latest Electron source-seeding status.\n- `/home/livings/.cache/paru/clone/electron34/PKGBUILD`: unstarted `void-bin` build definition.","time":{"start":1790457684765,"end":1790457700417}}');
