INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0df98f3e9001Vg9NZWbxF0kLbf','msg_0df98ea76001ZuBZLBUr6HYh66','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790457738217,1790457741594,'{"type":"text","text":"It wasn''t stuck on installing arpwatch — it was stuck on **my parse-check from last commit**, which I added to prevent the `-q` class of bug. That check runs `arpwatch <flags>` in the foreground, and under sudo it works fine, opens the raw socket, and never returns. `-F` is precisely what keeps it in the foreground, so the installer blocked on a perfectly healthy arpwatch.\n\nI only ever tested that check unprivileged, where arpwatch fails on the socket and exits instantly — the one case that returns. As root it hangs forever. My test coverage was exactly inverted from the case that matters.\n\nFixed in `54050ec` with `timeout 3`, where exit 124 (\"still running\") is treated as **success** — it''s the positive proof the flags parsed. The reliable signal is the *absence* of a usage message, which works under both root and unprivileged. The probe also writes to a temp datafile now so it can''t disturb the live one. All three paths tested; full dry-run completes in 0.05s.\n\nDo these two, in order:\n\n```\nsudo pkill -f \"arpwatch -F -i wlo1\"\n```\n\n```\nsudo ~/Projects/zen-hardening/install-arpwatch-spoof.sh\n```\n\nThe probe line will now read slightly differently under sudo, which is expected:\n\n```\nflags parse OK: arpwatch -F -i wlo1 -f /var/lib/arpwatch/arp.dat -s -N -z (still running when the probe timed out)\n```\n\nThat 3-second pause is the probe working correctly. Then:\n\n```\nsystemctl status arpwatch-spoof --no-pager\n```\n\n```\nsystemctl list-timers arpwatch-spoof-scan.timer --no-pager\n```\n\nOne note on the `pkill`: the service is currently in a restart loop, so it will respawn. `pkill` won''t stop that — let the installer''s `systemctl enable --now` take over, and if the old loop is still racing it, `sudo systemctl stop arpwatch-spoof` first, then run the installer.","time":{"start":1790457738217,"end":1790457741592}}');
