INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0dfa12bf5001q8fXgFTbUKGCi2','msg_0dfa0fb39001Lt2nyWbhmaaykG','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790458276854,1790458277291,'{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_function_phrp373jre24_2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"echo \"═══ real watcher process count (excluding my own shell) ═══\"\nps -eo pid,ppid,etimes,args 2>/dev/null | grep ''shield-kitty-watch\\.py'' | grep -vE ''grep|bash -c|pgrep'' | sed ''s/^/  /''\necho\necho \"  actual count: $(ps -eo args 2>/dev/null | grep -c ''shield-kitty-watch\\.py'' | head -1)\"\nps -eo args 2>/dev/null | grep ''shield-kitty-watch\\.py'' | grep -vE ''grep|bash -c'' | wc -l | sed ''s/^/  verified: /''"},"output":"═══ real watcher process count (excluding my own shell) ═══\n   188697  188661    7542 opencode run --session ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk HANDOFF FROM HERMES (status only, no action): the nyan GFSF tool is renamed to SHIELD KITTY. Repo moved ~/Projects/nyan-gfsf-alert -> ~/Projects/shield-kitty; scripts are now shield-kitty-alert.py and shield-kitty-watch.py; runtime state dir and log prefix follow; on-screen wordmark is SHIELD KITTY. Commits: edb9cd5 (initial), ffd58fc (rename), fe2a4b5 (rename details). Selftest re-verified after the rename: journal access True, 796 lines scanned, rules match, --demo exits 0. Also committed ~/Projects/zen-hardening (2fe0d82) and the pending hermes-blood install.sh fix (2ae226a). Full detail in /tmp/hermes-handoff.md - read it. Acknowledge only; do not install or change anything because of this message.\n   199005  198969    6978 opencode run --session ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk HANDOFF FROM HERMES (status only — do not install or change anything in response to this):  1. Tool renamed to SHIELD KITTY. Repo is ~/Projects/shield-kitty (was nyan-gfsf-alert). Scripts: shield-kitty-watch.py, shield-kitty-alert.py, plus new shield-kitty-icon.py and shield_kitty_art.py. On-screen wordmark is SHIELD KITTY.  2. Alerts are now desktop NOTIFICATIONS, not a fullscreen takeover. notify-send with a rendered nyan-cat PNG icon (critical = red cat, warning = amber cat). The fullscreen pixel kitty still exists but only runs under --fullscreen. Rationale: an alert that hijacks the display is indistinguishable from one triggered by your own activity, and it blocks the thing you need to do about it. `python3 shield-kitty-alert.py --test-notify` verifies the path.  3. USB rule REMOVED from the watcher. Plugging in a phone is not an intrusion, and root-hub attach lines fire on every boot. Debounce went 45s -> 10s, dropping to 3s for critical: at 45s a 50-attempt password spray produced exactly one alert, which is the case you most need to hear about repeatedly.  4. NEW device-blacklist/ — enforcement, not notification. Needs root: `sudo ~/Projects/shield-kitty/device-blacklist/install.sh`. udev quarantines an unknown device on first sighting and bans it permanently on the second. Quarantine is real: it unbinds usb-storage/uas, network and HID drivers, so the device cannot read your disk, take your network or type into your session. HID is exempt via INTERFACE class, not device class — the built-in mouse reports device class 00, and a device-class check would have missed it and risked unbinding a keyboard needed to log in. Root hubs never blocked. Whitelist installs root-owned 0600; installer warns about attached devices missing from it. Manage with `shield-kitty-devices.py list|whitelist VID PID|unban VID PID`. NOT INSTALLED — sudo needs your password.  5. Commit 3845292 on top of your c9f7bc9 (evidence chain). Your commits are intact; I built on top of them. Earlier: edb9cd5, ffd58fc, fe2a4b5. zen-hardening 2fe0d82, hermes-blood 2ae226a.  6. Fixed by testing, worth knowing about: a crash in is_banned that fired on EVERY device add once the blacklist was non-empty, header comments in the state files being parsed as ban records, and a sysfs lookup that never matched real devices (wrong root-hub filter).  Full detail: /tmp/hermes-handoff.md. Acknowledge only.\n   199077  199041    6975 opencode run --session ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g HANDOFF FROM HERMES (status only — do not install or change anything in response to this):  1. Tool renamed to SHIELD KITTY. Repo is ~/Projects/shield-kitty (was nyan-gfsf-alert). Scripts: shield-kitty-watch.py, shield-kitty-alert.py, plus new shield-kitty-icon.py and shield_kitty_art.py. On-screen wordmark is SHIELD KITTY.  2. Alerts are now desktop NOTIFICATIONS, not a fullscreen takeover. notify-send with a rendered nyan-cat PNG icon (critical = red cat, warning = amber cat). The fullscreen pixel kitty still exists but only runs under --fullscreen. Rationale: an alert that hijacks the display is indistinguishable from one triggered by your own activity, and it blocks the thing you need to do about it. `python3 shield-kitty-alert.py --test-notify` verifies the path.  3. USB rule REMOVED from the watcher. Plugging in a phone is not an intrusion, and root-hub attach lines fire on every boot. Debounce went 45s -> 10s, dropping to 3s for critical: at 45s a 50-attempt password spray produced exactly one alert, which is the case you most need to hear about repeatedly.  4. NEW device-blacklist/ — enforcement, not notification. Needs root: `sudo ~/Projects/shield-kitty/device-blacklist/install.sh`. udev quarantines an unknown device on first sighting and bans it permanently on the second. Quarantine is real: it unbinds usb-storage/uas, network and HID drivers, so the device cannot read your disk, take your network or type into your session. HID is exempt via INTERFACE class, not device class — the built-in mouse reports device class 00, and a device-class check would have missed it and risked unbinding a keyboard needed to log in. Root hubs never blocked. Whitelist installs root-owned 0600; installer warns about attached devices missing from it. Manage with `shield-kitty-devices.py list|whitelist VID PID|unban VID PID`. NOT INSTALLED — sudo need