INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0dfad2027001AMmGbOhuI0iddk','msg_0dfad1920001UXXtM2VdCGVyKL','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790459060264,1790459061748,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"26 pass, 1 \"fail\" — but the corruption_errs check is my grep pattern being wrong. Earlier the output showed:\n\n```\n[/dev/mapper/luks-...].corruption_errs  0\n```\n\nMy grep was `''corruption_errs    0''` with 4 spaces. The actual output has 2 spaces: `corruption_errs  0`. So the grep failed due to whitespace.\n\nThat''s a false negative in MY check, not a real problem. Let me verify with a whitespace-insensitive check.\n\nLet me confirm.\n\nThen give the GO.\n\nLet me fix the check and re-verify.\n\nNote the device stats earlier clearly showed corruption_errs 0, write_io_errs 0, etc. So it''s fine.\n\nLet me do the corrected check.","time":{"start":1790459060263,"end":1790459061747}}');
