INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0dfae5ac6001PpRG401hyjCNwt','msg_0dfae5303001p7qfiCgDGQ81x2','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790459140806,1790459145621,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"`torbrowser-launcher` 0.3.9-1 comes from `extra` — the official Arch repo — and is signature-validated. So `sudo pacman -S torbrowser-launcher` is legitimate and safe.\n\nNote: chaotic-aur is also enabled, which is a third-party repo. That''s a mild supply-chain consideration worth mentioning, but chaotic-aur is widely used and signed.\n\nNow let me:\n1. Give the Tor Browser install command\n2. Explain the token revocation (web UI only)\n\nLet me be concise and give clear instructions.\n\nFor the token: the user must revoke it themselves in a browser. Steps:\n- https://github.com/settings/tokens (classic) or\n- https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens (fine-grained)\n\nThey should delete it. Since they need Tor Browser or a browser — they have no browser installed except... nothing? Earlier: no browser installed (firefox not installed). So they''d need a browser to reach GitHub settings!\n\nWait — firefox is NOT installed. And no other browser? Let me check what browsers exist. That''s a practical blocker for revoking the token.\n\nLet me check for any browser.\n\nIf no browser, they can''t easily reach GitHub settings. Options:\n- Install a browser (they''re about to install Tor Browser — but using Tor to revoke a token is fine actually, though logging into GitHub over Tor is discouraged by GitHub)\n- Use a text-mode approach? Not practical.\n- Install firefox from official repos, revoke, then optionally remove.\n\nActually: GitHub explicitly warns against logging in over Tor. So revoking via Tor Browser is not ideal. Better: install Firefox/Chromium from official repos, revoke the token, then decide what to keep.\n\nLet me check what browsers are available.\n\nLet me check.\n\nThis is an important practical detail — the \"just revoke it\" advice is unusable if they have no browser.\n\nLet me check available browsers.","time":{"start":1790459140806,"end":1790459145619}}');
