INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0dfb05483001MBTGaPwjZ0axAv','msg_0dfb04e210017YCwWH9ujTG1qu','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790459270275,1790459272287,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"Now the /run/user/1000 hardcoding. The installer resolves TARGET_HOME from SUDO_USER but leaves /run/user/1000 in the scan unit. Let me make the installer derive the target UID and rewrite both.\n\nLet me add TARGET_UID and rewrite the sed to also handle /run/user/1000.\n\nLet me look at the sed line and TARGET_USER resolution.\n\nLine 27-34 area:\n```\nSUDO_USER_NAME=\"${SUDO_USER:-}\"\nif [ -n \"$SUDO_USER_NAME\" ]; then\n    TARGET_HOME=\"$(getent passwd \"$SUDO_USER_NAME\" | cut -d: -f6)\"\nelse\n    TARGET_HOME=\"$HOME\"\nfi\n```\n\nLet me add TARGET_USER and TARGET_UID. If SUDO_USER_NAME is empty, fall back to the owner of TARGET_HOME (stat -c %U).\n\nThen the sed: replace /run/user/1000 → /run/user/$TARGET_UID.\n\nLet me implement.\n\nLet me read the exact block first.","time":{"start":1790459270275,"end":1790459272285}}');
