SUDO.sh: non-destructive sudo recovery\n","metadata":{"output":"  [✓] pushed\n  47601c0 Add README: verified baseline, and the relationship to lifsea-security-suite\n  2333dd8 Fix audit-fail2ban jail list parsing\n  983bfea Add RECOVER-SUDO.sh: non-destructive sudo recovery\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /tmp/opencode/hss\ngrep -rInE \"(gh[pousr]_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}|AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}|BEGIN [A-Z ]*PRIVATE KEY)\" README.md config/ scripts/ 2>/dev/null | grep -v ''fake\\|fixture'' | head -3 || true\ngit add README.md\ngit -c user.name=opencode -c user.email=opencode@localhost commit -q -m \"Add README: verified baseline, and the relationship to lifsea-security-suite\n\nRecords what ''verified'' means in this repo and, more usefully, the list\nof settings that were accepted silently, reported success, and did\nsomething other than what was asked. Each is now a regression check in\nthe scripts. The instruction to carry: verify behaviour, not\nconfiguration, and treat ''[ok]'' as evidence of nothing.\n\nDocuments the overlap with lifsea-security-suite, which imports\nbuildlog, zen-hardening, shield-kitty and shield-kitty-forensics as a\nsecond copy with no automated relationship. This repo is the one wired\nto the live system; lifsea was imported at upstream b39490a and does not\ncontain the later fixes. They will drift until one is declared\ncanonical, which is recorded as an open decision rather than silently\npicked here.\n\nAlso states what is deliberately not covered: SDDM greeter brute force,\nmachine-id and DMI, anonymous browsing (Tor with no client is not\nanonymity), and Ethernet MACs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\" 2>&1 | sed ''s/^/  /''\ngit push -q origin HEAD 2>&1 | sed ''s/^/  /'' && echo \"  [✓] pushed\" || echo \"  [✗] failed\"\ngit log --oneline -3 | sed ''s/^/  /''","time":{"start":1790459308400,"end":1790459310077}}}');
