INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0dfb0ef2c001falBGEiLkFpujf','msg_0dfb0e4c0001eKkQe64GULrxPC','ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk',1790459309868,1790459311176,'{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_function_22ghax5xkhah_1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"echo \"=== all shield-kitty units ===\"\nsystemctl list-unit-files --no-pager 2>/dev/null | grep -i \"shield\\|kitty\" | sed ''s/^/  /''\necho\necho \"=== running kitty/script processes ===\"\npgrep -af \"kitty|shield\" 2>/dev/null | head -5 | sed ''s/^/  /'' || echo \"  none\"\necho\necho \"=== what does the alert script target? ===\"\ngrep -nE \"sock|path|shield_kitty|kitty @|on @\" ~/Projects/shield-kitty/shield-kitty-alert.py 2>/dev/null | head -8 | sed ''s/^/  /''"},"output":"=== all shield-kitty units ===\n\n=== running kitty/script processes ===\n  188697 opencode run --session ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk HANDOFF FROM HERMES (status only, no action): the nyan GFSF tool is renamed to SHIELD KITTY. Repo moved ~/Projects/nyan-gfsf-alert -> ~/Projects/shield-kitty; scripts are now shield-kitty-alert.py and shield-kitty-watch.py; runtime state dir and log prefix follow; on-screen wordmark is SHIELD KITTY. Commits: edb9cd5 (initial), ffd58fc (rename), fe2a4b5 (rename details). Selftest re-verified after the rename: journal access True, 796 lines scanned, rules match, --demo exits 0. Also committed ~/Projects/zen-hardening (2fe0d82) and the pending hermes-blood install.sh fix (2ae226a). Full detail in /tmp/hermes-handoff.md - read it. Acknowledge only; do not install or change anything because of this message.\n  199005 opencode run --session ses_f20e5cfc2ffeSFa4odnoYLiUOk HANDOFF FROM HERMES (status only — do not install or change anything in response to this):  1. Tool renamed to SHIELD KITTY. Repo is ~/Projects/shield-kitty (was nyan-gfsf-alert). Scripts: shield-kitty-watch.py, shield-kitty-alert.py, plus new shield-kitty-icon.py and shield_kitty_art.py. On-screen wordmark is SHIELD KITTY.  2. Alerts are now desktop NOTIFICATIONS, not a fullscreen takeover. notify-send with a rendered nyan-cat PNG icon (critical = red cat, warning = amber cat). The fullscreen pixel kitty still exists but only runs under --fullscreen. Rationale: an alert that hijacks the display is indistinguishable from one triggered by your own activity, and it blocks the thing you need to do about it. `python3 shield-kitty-alert.py --test-notify` verifies the path.  3. USB rule REMOVED from the watcher. Plugging in a phone is not an intrusion, and root-hub attach lines fire on every boot. Debounce went 45s -> 10s, dropping to 3s for critical: at 45s a 50-attempt password spray produced exactly one alert, which is the case you most need to hear about repeatedly.  4. NEW device-blacklist/ — enforcement, not notification. Needs root: `sudo ~/Projects/shield-kitty/device-blacklist/install.sh`. udev quarantines an unknown device on first sighting and bans it permanently on the second. Quarantine is real: it unbinds usb-storage/uas, network and HID drivers, so the device cannot read your disk, take your network or type into your session. HID is exempt via INTERFACE class, not device class — the built-in mouse reports device class 00, and a device-class check would have missed it and risked unbinding a keyboard needed to log in. Root hubs never blocked. Whitelist installs root-owned 0600; installer warns about attached devices missing from it. Manage with `shield-kitty-devices.py list|whitelist VID PID|unban VID PID`. NOT INSTALLED — sudo needs your password.  5. Commit 3845292 on top of your c9f7bc9 (evidence chain). Your commits are intact; I built on top of them. Earlier: edb9cd5, ffd58fc, fe2a4b5. zen-hardening 2fe0d82, hermes-blood 2ae226a.  6. Fixed by testing, worth knowing about: a crash in is_banned that fired on EVERY device add once the blacklist was non-empty, header comments in the state files being parsed as ban records, and a sysfs lookup that never matched real devices (wrong root-hub filter).  Full detail: /tmp/hermes-handoff.md. Acknowledge only.\n  199077 opencode run --session ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g HANDOFF FROM HERMES (status only — do not install or change anything in response to this):  1. Tool renamed to SHIELD KITTY. Repo is ~/Projects/shield-kitty (was nyan-gfsf-alert). Scripts: shield-kitty-watch.py, shield-kitty-alert.py, plus new shield-kitty-icon.py and shield_kitty_art.py. On-screen wordmark is SHIELD KITTY.  2. Alerts are now desktop NOTIFICATIONS, not a fullscreen takeover. notify-send with a rendered nyan-cat PNG icon (critical = red cat, warning = amber cat). The fullscreen pixel kitty still exists but only runs under --fullscreen. Rationale: an alert that hijacks the display is indistinguishable from one triggered by your own activity, and it blocks the thing you need to do about it. `python3 shield-kitty-alert.py --test-notify` verifies the path.  3. USB rule REMOVED from the watcher. Plugging in a phone is not an intrusion, and root-hub attach lines fire on every boot. Debounce went 45s -> 10s, dropping to 3s for critical: at 45s a 50-attempt password spray produced exactly one alert, which is the case you most need to hear about repeatedly.  4. NEW device-blacklist/ — enforcement, not notification. Needs root: `sudo ~/Projects/shield-kitty/device-blacklist/install.sh`. udev quarantines an unknown device on first sighting and bans it permanently on the second. Quarantine is real: it unbinds usb-storage/uas, network and HID drivers, so the device cannot read your disk, take your network or type into your session. HID is exempt via INTERFACE class, not device class — the built-in mouse reports device class 00, and a device-class check would have missed it and risked unbinding a keyboard needed to log in. Root hubs never blocked. Whitelist installs root-owned 0600; installer warns about attached devices missing from it. Manage with `shield-kitty-devices.py list|whitelist VID PID|unban VID PID`. NOT INSTALLED — s