INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0dfb1232b001ktZgzJqLa2y6J3','msg_0dfb119ee001exia2qbr2XX89K','ses_f211dfcd4ffevS1Yoddwab036g',1790459323179,1790459389335,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"We need produce exact markdown structure, same language conversation English. Need combine prior + recent, corrected. Must be terse but comprehensive enough another coding agent continue. Need carefully infer current state at conversation end. We need not continue conversation. Need include objective, details, completed, active, blocked, next, files.\n\nWe need parse all developments and contradictions. We need ensure current exact state as latest. Conversation extends huge. Need consolidate.\n\nLet''s outline chronology/current facts:\n\nInitial prior:\n- identity, firewall, fail2ban, Tor, bootstrap, GitHub etc.\nRecent:\n1. Found MAC bugs and fixed:\n   - NM 1.58 property 802-11-wireless.mac-address-randomization, values default/never/always. set script auto-detects modern vs old; modern uses always. Initially 1=never wrong.\n   - Applied user, setting always; reconnect resulted MAC ea:bd:c8:4d:53:a8 locally administered; connection activated.\n   - DHCP hostname suppression -1.\n2. Tor healthy active bootstrap 100, SOCKS loopback. No browser.\n3. Built bootstrap.sh, fixed syntax unclosed quote. set MAC robust. Pushed hermes-security-scripts private.\n4. bootstrap initially missed MAC verification. Added hard check setting always and locally administered live MAC, plus interface discovery in set-home trusted zone replacing wlo0. Pushed commit 505c4f6.\n5. token.clean shredded with 3 random + zero on btrfs, verified gone; SSH push works. Reminder token server revocation perhaps not confirmed. The prior says shred active; now done. Need mention server-side revocation still not confirmed/open.\n6. Shield Kitty persistence:\n   - Audit found no systemd units, bare process. Script install-shield-kitty-units.sh. It recognizes units with %h require user units. But current actual system: units ended up in /home/livings/.config/systemd/user (not /etc), active enabled linger yes; systemd owns PID via cgroup, evidence timer active. So persistence fixed, likely by another agent or user, no need re-run install script. We should state actual verified.\n7. Full audit:\n   - agent work still active, but user authorized fixing two issues now. We fixed bootstrap recidive:\n     * another agent commit c897508 intentionally changed source recidive true. Prior stale. Conversation current says source and live both enabled true and log exists. bootstrap now handles both directions scoped only [recidive].\n   - pushed fbc8523 with bootstrap, install audit, install shield units.\n   - later fix sudoers scripts cfc20b1 then 02f1bf3, RECOVER 983bfea.\n8. Audit:\n   - boot readiness:\n     * fstab okay, LUKS Btrfs subvol root/home/root/srv/cache/log/tmp, tmpfs /tmp, ESP UUID F54B-53CA.\n     * initramfs names linux-zen, dracut 111, current kernel 7.2.7-zen1-1-zen, image fresh.\n     * no pacman lock, 0 pending, no ignored, no .pacnew/pacsave, no failed units or jobs, boot 49.552s, graphical userspace 2.818.\n     * ESP mounted, fsck passed.\n     * storage 476.64 GiB, 16.67 GiB used, 456.86 free; btrfs scrub no errors, device stats zero.\n     * memory was pressure due agents, 5.3/7.4 and zram 2.9; no OOM. Need recheck after agents finish maybe.\n     * kernel benign messages only, no faults.\n     * dmesg restricted by sysctl, audit wrapper root.\n   - listeners 1716,5353 all bind but firewall confirmed nft final reject, so blocked.\n   - no pending.\n   - btrfs snapshots root subvol only (top level 256 @), no @home snapshot listed; token likely not in listed snapshots. But not necessarily needed.\n   - coredumps 3 test alert.py --demo, Xorg boot; benign.\n   - bch faucet errors but not installed/no boot.\n9. Audit helper mechanism:\n   - install-audit-readonly.sh with 7 root-owned wrappers:\n     audit-nft, btrfs, smart, dmesg, firewall, fail2ban, journal-err.\n   - Initially bugs:\n     * `\"\"` means exactly one empty arg and no match; removed.\n     * trailing comma syntax; fixed.\n     * whole tree visudo -c polluted by unrelated bad perms; fixed to `visudo -cf` own file.\n   - Now successfully installed via RECOVER-SUDO.sh, `/etc/sudoers.d/audit-readonly` valid, all helpers work passwordless.\n   - install-smart reports nvme-cli not installed; SMART unavailable. We might mention blocked.\n   - audit-fail2ban wrapper bug parsing comma list; source install-audit-readonly fixed but installed wrapper not yet updated. Latest test weird: `sudo -n fail2ban-client` direct gives raw empty? Wait audit-fail2ban did work as root and showed list. In test after edit, command `sudo -n fail2ban-client status` is not whitelisted! It should prompt/error; redirect 2>/dev/null means raw empty. The test of new parser against real output failed because direct binary isn''t NOPASSWD, not because parser. The source edit itself likely correct. Installed `/usr/local/sbin/audit-fail2ban` still old and shows `recidive,` bug. Need re-run installer to deploy updated wrapper after? But install-audit script when run via sudo may now work; or RECOVER-SUDO doesn''t rewrite helpers if existing. Need use sudo installer or pkexec? It needs user password sudo now restored. So next action perhaps re-run `sudo bash install-audit-readonly.sh` to update audit-fail2ban then verify `sudo audit-fail2ban`. But we must be careful installer may have safety issues? It now per-file validation and functional probes. Fine.\n10. Sudo lockout disaster:\n   - `fix-sudoers-permissions.sh` quarantined `/etc/sudoers.d/10-installer` (`%wheel ALL=(ALL) ALL`) due overbroad classifier. Then audit installer removed itself due visudo whole-tree.\n   - User locked out. `opencode` was empty and was set 0440. Stock editor/insults/pwfeedback fixed 0440.\n   - Corrected classifier treats password-required ALL as safe, only NOPASSWD quarantine; push 02f1bf3.\n   - Wrote RECOVER-SUDO.sh. First pkexec run failed safe due account root because uses SUDO_USER/USER; fixed using PKEXEC_UID, push 983bfea.\n   - Second pkexec run succeeded. Restored 10-installer, all files 0440, visudo clean, account wheel, audit helper valid. Current sudo works password-required; audit wrappers NOPASSWD. Need maybe user still hasn''t run `sudo -l` after success but output proves config and behavioral textual; earlier assistant said can verify. We know final state. Need note no need recovery.\n   - The quarantine directory remains `/root/sudoers-quarantine-20260926-143446` with copy 10-installer. It''s okay. The dangerous file not active. We should possibly remove quarantine later? It is root-only and no sudoers effect. No need.\n   - `fix-sudoers-permissions.sh` source corrected but not necessary to run again. Could perhaps remove it from repo or redesign further to never lock out. It still has risk: recognizes NOPASSWD, quarantines, could quarantine sole grant if NOPASSWD. It has no invoker safety. We should not run again; user asked all current issues. Need active: harden or remove/fix script with a preflight ensuring invoking user''s sudo before/after. Maybe no need unless in next move. Conversation''s last assistant says \"fix scripts separately\", corrected classifier, but deeper safety still needed. Include active.\n11. Git repos and commits:\n   - hermes-security-scripts private commits:\n     99fe7b3 initial bootstrap\n     79ecc5e MAC flags fix\n     505c4f6 MAC verification/interface\n     fbc8523 persistence fixes\n     cfc20b1 sudoers safe repair\n     02f1bf3 classifier/visudo fixes\n     983bfea recovery.\n   - Maybe commit latest audit-fail2ban parser not yet pushed. Source changed in ~/Projects/zen-hardening, likely dirty. Need include active.\n   - `lifsea-security-suite` second consolidation created by agents, imports zen-hardening, shield-kitty, forensics, buildlog. User chose \"Document relationship\", but has this been done? No. Active.\n   - canonical? User selected document relationship, not choose. Need state both `hermes-security-scripts` and lifsea exist, overlap/drift risk, documentation pending. Prior user asked private repos; all said private. Need not overdo.\n   - Agents still active. User authorized specific fixes. Need wait for quiet before final integration, push only files. Current zen-hardening repo has dirty modifications by agents plus our untracked/changed files. `/tmp/opencode/hss` has commits.\n12. Tor browser remains not installed. User selected not installed. Prior said maybe \"Tor browser not installed\" and active next. Still open.\n13. GitHub token shred: done, server revocation unconfirmed. SSH remote works. Need mention.\n14. Full reboot: user plans manually after audit. Current boot appears go. Need still not yet rebooted. Need final pre-reboot check after agents finish, update state. Boot test cannot actual without reboot. \"boot test ensure system boot\" read-only completed; manual reboot pending.\n15. Firewall zone semantics: latest table shows target default and final reject. Current summary should state strict. `kdeconnectd`, mDNS bound globally but blocked by firewall. Maybe network listener 1716, 5353 by design.\n16. fail2ban:\n   - two jails `recidive, sshd`, active.\n   - source current recidive true, not false as prior summary. Conversation wins.\n   - /var/log/fail2ban.log exists, so true appropriate.\n   - live config true. Bootstrap robustly toggles based on log.\n   - End-to-end ban test using 192.0.2.66 still not run. This is active from prior.\n   - `fail2ban-client` direct needs root, wrappers.\n   - no recent errors.\n17. systemd drop-in for PartOf firewalld still not created. Bootstrap works around by stop/restart; active from prior.\n18. set-home interface fixed now, contrary prior active. It discovers wlo1. Completed.\n19. bootstrap `bootstrap.sh` and identity script:\n   - `bootstrap.sh` syntax valid and ran 0 failures after MAC active. It now includes MAC hard check.\n   - Maybe after agent edits, need rerun due active work. But live state verified.\n   - `set-anon-identity.sh` modern detection uses `always`, older mode random. MAC succeeded.\n20. `recidive` bootstrap logic:\n   - source enabled true due deliberate request. bootstrap actively set false if log absent. Good.\n21. SDDM etc still open structural.\n22. machine-id, DMI, Ethernet MAC still open decisions.\n23. \"bootstrap session env for notify\" commit b39490a etc by other agent. Not necessarily.\n24. `arpwatch-spoof-alert.sh` uncommitted at one point; other agents active. Need avoid touching. New repos etc.\n\nNeed output exact structure only. \"Important Details\" should include critical constraints and facts. \"Completed\" can be many bullets but terse. \"Active\" current. \"Blocked\". \"Next Move\" immediate likely:\n1. Deploy updated audit-fail2ban wrapper (source parser fixed) and run root diagnostics. Perhaps `sudo bash .../install-audit-readonly.sh`, then `sudo audit-fail2ban`, `sudo audit-smart` (nvme-cli absent). But the user asked continue after recovery. The latest conversation ended at test parser issue, no response. We need summary for next agent, so immediate action should be fix wrapper test/deploy and finish remaining audit.\n2. Wait for other agents/repo activity quiet, reconcile/push latest files (including audit-fail2ban parser, RECOVER already pushed) and document lifsea relationship. Do not rerun `fix-sudoers-permissions.sh`.\n3. run final system audit/reverify no reboot blockers; perhaps install nvme-cli to get SMART? User asked full diagnostics. `nvme-cli` absent. We can use sysfs fallback or install package after sudo. Need decide immediate. We can mention active: NVMe SMART unavailable because `nvme: command not found`; install `nvme-cli` only with user approval or use `smartctl` if installed. But user asked full diagnostics, likely install is acceptable? Not yet. We can say next use `nvme smart-log` after installing `nvme-cli`, but avoid package change without user? User did say get everything working, root now restored. However no need now perhaps.\n4. end-to-end fail2ban test and systemd drop-in, Tor browser. But user''s immediate request is reboot readiness. Prior tasks remain.\n5. Before manual reboot: verify sudo, audit helpers, Shield Kitty, no lock, no failed, run bootstrap. Then user reboot and postboot test.\n6. After reboot check `systemctl --user ...`, firewall, Tor, MAC.\n\nNeed mention exact error and fix for `pkexec` account maybe not needed in current state but relevant caution: any future pkexec scripts should resolve `PKEXEC_UID`; `RECOVER-SUDO.sh` now does. Important detail.\n\nNeed perhaps mention current date? 2026-09-26 from logs. Not necessary.\n\nLet''s ensure \"same language as conversation\" English.\n\nNeed maybe not include markdown tables due terse bullets.\n\nWe need preserve all objectives from prior including remaining ecosystem work? The user asked summary combining objectives, so important details and active should carry unreviewed tools, ISO/emulator work. But current immediate objective is core stack/audit/reboot. The prior says continue remaining requested ecosystem only after core verified. We need retain them, perhaps one bullet in Active with list. But desired summary not overly huge? Yet user says carry everything not finished. Must include remaining tasks. Include major blockers.\n\nLet''s build detailed but terse.\n\nObjective:\n- Finish verified Garuda hardening/anonymity/rebuild stack, resolve audit/reboot blockers, push private repos; only then remaining Void/security/ISO/emulator tasks.\nOne or two sentences.\n\nImportant Details:\n- user env, shell, no blanket NOPASSWD.\n- design constraints firewalld, Tor, machine-id, SDDM, source recidive correction.\n- agent concurrency, repo canonical overlap.\n- verification philosophy due bugs.\n- current sudo recovery state.\n- maybe sudoers scripts hazard.\n- root wrappers are temporary, remove after audit.\n- Tor browser not installed.\n- user will reboot manually only after final go/no-go.\nCould be many.\n\nCompleted:\nDetailed bullets:\nIdentity:\n- hostname zero, DHCP suppressed.\n- MAC ea... always, NM property fixed.\nFirewall:\n- strict state, nft final reject, wlo1, etc.\nFail2ban:\n- 2 jails, source/live recidive true due log, bootstrap robust.\n- maybe unban, f2bready.\nTor:\n- active loopback, but no browser belongs active/open.\nSystemd Shield Kitty:\n- user units actual path, active enabled linger, cgroup, evidence timer.\nBootstrap/scripts:\n- bootstrap, set identity, set home fixed, installer.\nGit:\n- private repo commit latest, token shred, SSH push.\nSystem audit:\n- boot/storage/kernel/firewall.\nSudo recovery:\n- current restored, files 0440, audit wrappers.\nAudit helper:\n- 7 wrappers.\n- installer script bugs fixed, but installed fail2ban wrapper old parser.\nCould mark \"audit helpers installed; audit-nft/btrfs/dmesg/firewall/fail2ban works\" yes.\n- root-only results.\n\nNeed ensure not claim `nvme health` completed because unavailable. Put blocked.\n- no package updates, no failed units, etc.\n- 14 snapshots root subvol. Maybe not needed.\n- no btrfs errors.\n- btrfs snapshots mean shredded token maybe safe? We can''t guarantee. Server revocation still needed.\n- MAC locally administered maybe bit check says ea; yes.\n\nActive:\n- Finish full diagnostics: install/use nvme-cli, recheck memory after agents, maybe SMART.\n- Deploy audit-fail2ban parser source to installed wrapper and re-run.\n- wait agents quiet and reconcile repos, document lifsea.\n- final pre-reboot and postboot.\n- end-to-end fail2ban test.\n- fail2ban systemd drop-in.\n- Tor Browser.\n- security decisions.\n- remaining ecosystem.\n- hardening sudoers repair script before reuse / remove quarantine maybe.\n- push latest source parser changes and maybe not yet.\nCould mention `zen-hardening` active dirty and other agents, do not overwrite.\n\nBlocked:\n- root no longer blocked; interactive sudo works. Root audit wrappers work. Don''t say root blocked.\n- Tor browser package install now possible but pending user command? We could not install because no root. Now sudo restored, but still active.\n- machine ID decision.\n- SDDM.\n- transparent Tor.\n- secure home network.\n- ISO/emulator constraints.\n- `nvme-cli` absent.\n- \"Hermes separate no channel\" maybe constraint. They asked have Hermes deploy, but assistant cannot dispatch. We can state no direct Hermes channel; work direct.\n- `lifsea` agents still active.\n\nNext Move:\n1. Immediate: fix/deploy `audit-fail2ban` wrapper. Since source edit done but not installed. The raw test was empty because direct `sudo -n fail2ban-client` isn''t whitelisted; test should use `sudo -n audit-fail2ban` or parse captured known output. Need tell next agent exact issue: parser source fixed but test mistakenly called raw binary without password; use wrapper. Re-run installer `sudo bash .../install-audit-readonly.sh`, then `sudo -n /usr/local/sbin/audit-fail2ban`; ensure all helper probes.\n2. Wait for agents/repo quiet, inspect dirty and commit only owned files, push to hermes-security-scripts. Document relation to lifsea. Do not run fix-sudoers.\n3. Full final audit: `sudo audit-smart` after install nvme-cli or sysfs, memory, journal, boot. End-to-end f2b test, maybe add drop-in. Hmm immediate reboot request prioritized. Maybe before reboot run bootstrap check, verify sudo, units, no failures. User manually reboot. Postboot verify.\n4. Install Tor Browser after reboot? Could do before. But user wants reboot. Need order.\n5. Revoke token, remaining tasks later.\nCould include 5-6 steps, template says 1,2 but not limit. Fine.\n\nRelevant Files:\n- all important exact paths, plus commits/repos.\nNeed include `~/Projects/zen-hardening/install-audit-readonly.sh` currently updated parser but uncommitted in source? yes.\n- `RECOVER-SUDO.sh`\n- `fix-sudoers-permissions.sh` corrected but do not run until safety guard.\n- `install-shield-kitty-units.sh` perhaps current units are home path.\n- `bootstrap.sh`\n- `set-anon-identity.sh`\n- `set-home-trusted-zone.sh`\n- `workstation.xml`\n- `shield-kitty-fail2ban.local`\n- `~/.config/systemd/user` units\n- `evidence files`.\n- `/etc/sudoers.d/10-installer`, `audit-readonly`, etc.\n- audit wrappers.\n- repos.\n- `token.clean` gone.\n- btrfs snapshot location.\n- `/tmp/hermes-handoff.md`.\nCould be a lot but requested preserve exact file paths.\n\nNeed account for prior `faillock.conf` etc if not completed? They remain relevant. We should keep in Relevant Files and Active maybe full diagnostics. The prior says source faillock has admin_group wheel; don''t install silently. We should carry that important detail perhaps. It wasn''t discussed recently. Include in Important Details: PAM local sudo protection is faillock deny=10; `faillock.conf` source has `admin_group=wheel` and requires review. SDDM no fail2ban. Good.\n\nNeed carry business tools installed etc? Completed. Could include one bullet.\n- `lin-antimalware`, business health/debug installed and pushed. Fine.\n\nNeed reconcile commit IDs. Initial prior says `business-debug-wrappers @7301a28`, then conversation assistant said earlier pushed 54d0964, 2b6ad46, 6419b99, 4346767 etc. Most recent in conversation:\n  - hermes 505c4f6, fbc8523, cfc20b1, 02f1bf3, 983bfea. We should say latest pushed `983bfea` (but `audit-fail2ban` source edit is uncommitted after). Good.\n  - business-debug @54d0964, business-health @2b6ad46, lin-antimalware @c266365? Current repo activity final says lin-antimalware c266365. Earlier pushed commit 6419b99 but agents later c266365. We can avoid exact if uncertain or mention private repos with latest observed.\n  - security-audit @407fdf5 from prior, buildlog latest 2f82326 imported. Maybe not central.\n  - hermes repo at latest 983bfea. It also contains commit fbc etc.\n  - `lifsea-security-suite` commit ec32f41. Need include.\n- \"private repos\" user requested