e sole NOPASSWD that is the only current access (e.g. when no wheel rule). It is not to be used. Need redesign.\n- `RECOVER-SUDO` is safe; use pkexec if needed.\n- Quarantine directory still exists with 10-installer. Not active. Could leave.\n- `/etc/sudoers.d/opencode` is empty at 0440. Good.\n\nSystem:\n- The service units are in user config, not /etc despite installer. Current `systemctl --user` says enabled. Is `systemctl --global enable` necessary? The symlink likely in `~/.config/systemd/user/default.target.wants`. Linger yes. So survives.\n- Evidence service/timer active.\n- Shield Kitty watcher PID systemd cgroup. Good.\n- `device-blacklist` still not installed. Prior active? It was reviewed but not root-installed. Should mention as open maybe. User wants security tools. It is not in current conversation except handoff. Keep in active/relevant.\n- No browser.\n- machine ID, DMI.\n- Ethernet randomization.\n- btrfs snapshots root only.\n- `efivarfs` 70% but 57K free, okay.\n- memory pressure from agents. Need recheck after they finish.\n\n\"Failed to dispatch Hermes\": The user said \"have hermes deploy fleets\" but assistant explained no direct channel. The summary should state no direct channel to Hermes; continue direct or wait for agents. Good.\n\nLet''s decide exact format and detail level. Need not include prior \"Objective 21-layer encryption\" perhaps still relevant because no design. Add in Blocked/Active if preserving. The user asked remaining ecosystem after core. Include one bullet:\n- Remaining requested work: `void-bin` builds; review/install `bde-security-biometrics`, `lin-antimalware-tools`, `local-emergency-patrol`, `zen-healer`, `secure-tactical-systems`; `zen-healer` unsafe; ISO via `zen-suite` not installer; Xbox emulation blocked.\nThis retains.\n\nNeed maybe include `voidlit` theme active as completed. Not central but carry. Could one bullet.\n\nLet''s ensure no stale claims:\n- \"Source fail2ban intentionally ships recidive false\" must be corrected. Current source true. In Important Details state current source and live true; bootstrap handles absent log by false.\n- \"Shield Kitty units missing\" corrected complete.\n- \"MAC current f4\" corrected ea.\n- \"set-home hardcodes wlo0\" corrected dynamic.\n- \"root blocked\" resolved.\n- \"token.clean\" gone.\n- \"audit helper not installed\" resolved.\n- \"sudo broken\" resolved.\n- \"agents still active\" likely still; include last observed.\n- \"recidive source commit by request\" yes.\n- \"lifsea relationship docs pending\" yes.\n- \"bootstrap 0 checks\" now includes MAC check and passed after reconnect.\n- \"opencode file empty\" yes.\n- \"10-installer quarantined\" restored, but copy remains quarantine.\n- \"all files 0440\" output. Good.\n- `audit-fail2ban` wrapper installed version old. Source fixed.\n- \"nvme CLI not installed\" yes.\n- \"full audit not complete\" active.\n\nLet''s formulate.\n\nPotential output:\n\n## Objective\n- Complete and independently verify...\n- Finish core before reboot, then remaining...\n\nImportant Details bullets:\n- environment.\n- no blanket NOPASSWD; audit wrappers temporary exact.\n- current recovery facts and script hazards.\n- verification rule.\n- agent concurrency and repos.\n- security design constraints.\n- source recidive state.\n- Tor browser etc.\n- user will manually reboot.\n\nCompleted bullets maybe 20.\n\nLet''s be terse but comprehensive. We can combine.\n\nCompleted:\n1. Identity.\n2. Firewall.\n3. Fail2ban.\n4. Tor.\n5. Bootstrap.\n6. Shield Kitty.\n7. Tools/business.\n8. Git.\n9. Token.\n10. Boot audit.\n11. Storage.\n12. Kernel.\n13. Network exposure.\n14. Sudo recovery.\n15. Audit helper installation.\nMaybe 15 is okay.\n\nFor sudo recovery, exact:\n- `/etc/sudoers.d/10-installer` restored to `%wheel ALL=(ALL) ALL`, 0440.\n- `livings` in wheel. `visudo -c` clean.\n- audit-readonly 0440 valid, wrappers passwordless.\n- editor/insults/opencode/pwfeedback 0440.\n- opencode empty.\n- No need to run `fix-sudoers`.\nNeed mention latest test output: `audit helpers work without a password`. Good.\n\nAudit helper:\n- 7 wrappers. `audit-nft` confirmed final reject; btrfs no errors; dmesg benign; f2b jails. The installed f2b wrapper bug doesn''t undermine jail status. The source parser fixed but not deployed.\n- `audit-smart` command absent.\n- `audit-journal-err` not yet final.\n\nBoot:\n- current kernel and dracut.\n- no pacman lock etc.\n- systemd boot times.\n- no failed units at time.\n- `fstab` and ESP.\n- no reboot yet.\n- maybe no queued jobs.\n\nStorage:\n- 14 snapshots, no errors. Token snapshots? Could mention root-only, not home. But not necessary.\n- dmesg restricted expected.\n- data profile 75% allocated, not urgent. Could put in active/important.\n- memory pressure due agents. active.\n\nFirewall:\n- `policy accept` but final explicit reject. Explain enough.\n- mDNS/KDE Connect globally bound but blocked.\n\nFail2ban:\n- jails exact. SSH filter.\n- `bantime=86400`.\n- no ban test.\n\nTor:\n- active and bootstrap 100. No browser active.\n\nBusiness tools:\n- maybe not relevant to current. Include one bullet.\n\nGit:\n- latest pushed commit 983bfea. But source edit to audit-fail2ban is after and uncommitted. Explicit.\n- `lifsea` at ec32f41 and overlap. Document pending.\n\nActive:\n- Audit final.\n- source wrapper.\n- agent quiet.\n- fail2ban ban test and drop-in.\n- Tor browser.\n- machine id decisions.\n- device blacklist.\n- remaining ecosystem.\n- maybe token revoke.\n\nBlocked:\n- nvme-cli absent.\n- polkit no longer blocked.\n- user reboot not performed.\n- SDDM structural, home network, transparent Tor, machine ID decision.\n- ISO/emulator legal constraints.\n- direct Hermes channel.\nMaybe not every prior blocked needs list if active/decision. But template requires.\n\nNext Move:\n1. `sudo bash install-audit-readonly.sh` deploy parser, run wrapper. But this script also rewrites all helpers. It should work now. Then `sudo audit-fail2ban`; `sudo audit-journal-err`; `sudo audit-smart` after nvme-cli. However installing `nvme-cli` requires pacman; user asked diagnostics. Suggest `sudo pacman -S --needed nvme-cli`, but should not automatically run due potential package install. Since user authorized full audit, maybe next agent can. Yet no direct user confirmation after sudo restored. The prior said root installation requires interactive. We can say run via user.\n2. Wait for agents quiet, check dirty, commit only our files. Push latest. Document lifsea.\n3. Run end-to-end fail2ban test and add systemd drop-in.\n4. Pre-reboot final:\n   - `sudo bash bootstrap.sh --check`? Note root. Then normal.\n   - `sudo -l`\n   - `sudo audit-firewall`, `audit-fail2ban`\n   - check units.\n   - no lock etc.\n5. user reboot and postboot verify.\n6. then Tor Browser and token revoke etc.\nNeed \"immediate concrete action\" not questions.\n\nRelevant Files:\n- list. Need include exact paths and purpose.\nCould be 20 bullets. Keep terse.\n\nLet''s consider if output should mention the prior \"Source recidive false\" conflict. We state corrected. Good.\n\nNeed include repository path `/tmp/opencode/hss` and remote. `~/Projects/zen-hardening` local. The script changes are staged/committed in `/tmp/opencode/hss` but source repo dirty. Relevant.\n\nNeed mention commit `983bfea` latest pushed. There were later source edits not pushed. Good.\n- `fbc8523` contains install shield units and bootstrap recidive robust. `02f1bf3` corrected sudoers scripts. `983bfea` recovery. Not need all IDs, but useful exact. Could list latest chain in one bullet.\n- Private repo remote `git@github.com:intricos777-dot/hermes-security-scripts.git`.\n- `lifsea-security-suite` local `~/Projects/lifsea-security-suite`.\n- `security-audit-2026`.\n\nNeed maybe mention audit helper removal command. In Important:\n- temporary wrappers; remove after audit with `sudo bash ... --remove`; preserving wheel rule. Good.\n- Do not use direct NOPASSWD binaries.\n\nPotential concern: The user asked \"full system audit\" and the assistant made many destructive mistakes. Summary should clearly state current safe state. Good.\n\nLet''s ensure exact command to verify normal sudo: `sudo -l | tail -3`, but after recovery output only configuration. User likely should run. Next move.\n- `sudo audit-nft` should be NOPASSWD due sudoers wrapper. The user could run but assistant already did.\n- `sudo -n /usr/local/sbin/audit-nft` works.\n\nLet''s perhaps mention audit helper installed `sudoers` file uses `livings ALL=(root) NOPASSWD:` exact paths. Is that a concern? It''s narrow, accepted. Could include in Important. No need exact full line? Maybe yes:\n`livings ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/audit-nft, ...`.\nBut summary can say exact wrappers.\n\nNeed include `RECOVER-SUDO.sh` no longer needed. If future pkexec, it resolves `PKEXEC_UID`. Good.\n- `fix-sudoers-permissions.sh` should not run until redesigned. Put in Active or Important. It currently recognizes safe wheel rule, but can still quarantine NOPASSWD. If user is relying only on NOPASSWD it could lock out. It did exactly that compounded. So do not use.\n- The audit installer can still remove its own sudoers file on syntax invalid, but wheel rule now restored, so won''t lock out. Good.\n\nNeed mention no actual reboot yet. Put Completed/Active? \"Manual reboot has not occurred.\" Active.\n\nLet''s evaluate prior remaining tasks:\n- Post-rebuild bootstrap exists but Tor Browser not included (only optional note). Active.\n- systemd drop-in not made.\n- end-to-end fail2ban test not run.\n- package integrity? We did no pacman -Qkk, perhaps not in conversation. The user asked full audit; we didn''t run package integrity. Active: `pacman -Qkk`/systemctl? We should include. The assistant marked full system audit completed but no `pacman -Qkk`, no SMART, no journal after. So another coding agent should continue.\n- pending updates 0.\n- `nvme-cli` missing.\n- memory recheck.\n- SUID/world-writable not done.\n- no `pacman -Qkk` output. Need include active: remaining full audit components: package integrity, SUID/world-writable, final journal. The conversation said \"full system audit completed\" in todo, but tasks not all run. Be honest. The user explicitly requested full. Add active.\n- \"GPU\" diagnostics not done. Prior says full diagnostics includes GPU. The conversation did not inspect GPU beyond Xorg coredump. Add active if necessary: `journalctl -b -u`/kernel GPU. But could be low priority.\n- Boot chain is strong.\n\nNeed maybe mention \"coredumps were alert.py --demo test runs, plus Xorg startup; no current service crash\". Good.\n- `bch-faucet` unit not found, so missing .env not boot issue. Could omit.\n\nCould \"Blocked\" include `dmesg` restricted? No wrapper works.\n- Root audit is no longer blocked.\n- `nvme-cli` absent is not blocker if install.\n- no actual boot test until reboot; user requested ensure. It''s pending.\n\nLet''s draft structure with terse bullets.\n\nNeed ensure exactly no paragraphs outside bullets. Header sections. Fine.\n\nLet''s produce final in English.","time":{"start":1790459323179,"end":1790459389330}}');
