purpose state mutators that happen to\n  # have a read mode:\n  #\n\n═══ does it touch anything outside its own surface? ═══\n  files it removes:\n    59:  rm -f \"$SUDOERS_FILE\"\n    60:  for h in \"${HELPERS[@]}\"; do rm -f \"/usr/local/sbin/$h\"; done\n    257:  rm -f \"$SUDOERS_FILE\"\n\n  does any remove reference 10-installer or the wheel rule?\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /home/livings/Projects/zen-hardening\necho \"═══ what --remove actually deletes ═══\"\nsed -n ''/--remove/,/^fi/p'' install-audit-readonly.sh | head -12 | sed ''s/^/  /''\necho\necho \"═══ does it touch anything outside its own surface? ═══\"\necho \"  files it removes:\"\ngrep -n ''rm -f'' install-audit-readonly.sh | sed ''s/^/    /''\necho\necho \"  does any remove reference 10-installer or the wheel rule?\"\ngrep -n ''10-installer\\|%wheel'' install-audit-readonly.sh | sed ''s/^/    /'' || echo \"    no — the wheel rule is never touched by this script\"","time":{"start":1790459719052,"end":1790459719072}}}');
