h stub notifiers (silent rc=0, and rc=1 with stderr). commit 10ca689\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd ~/Projects/buildlog\nbuildlog fix \"alert delivery was unlogged on success: notify-send is silent, and the code only logged on output or non-zero rc, so an empty log meant either ''delivered'' or ''dropped''. That is the same ambiguity that hid the root-session-bus bug, where notifications failed while all status checks reported healthy. Both the datafile scanner and the hook test path now branch explicitly: ''alert delivered ok for <ip>'' or ''alert DELIVERY FAILED for <ip> (rc=N): <output>''. Verified both branches with stub notifiers (silent rc=0, and rc=1 with stderr). commit 10ca689\" 2>&1 | tail -1","time":{"start":1790459764801,"end":1790459764825}}}');
