INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0e9974f5e001XOAlMnKQPe3n2D','msg_0e9973283001yi7zFaEsaTxI3o','ses_f16732810ffehZhBAPc6TQNXa2',1790625402719,1790625428961,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"Very important: **`sin-archive-2026` MANIFEST** says:\n- Operated by: **sin** (host **sin-asustufdashf15fx517zcfx517zc**, Ubuntu/Garuda Arch, kernel 7.2.6-zen2-1-zen)\n- Policy: **no secrets, keys, wallets, or copyrighted media are ever pushed here.**\n\nSo the old machine was host `sin-asustufdashf15fx517zcfx517zc`, username `sin`. Current machine: host `zero`, user `livings` (GECOS Living_Sin). \"garuda rani systems\" — maybe still just how the user refers to their Garuda machines. Hmm \"rani\"... The old host string \"sin-asustufdashf15fx...\" — Garuda auto-hostname format is `<user>-<machine-id>` e.g., \"livings-zero\"? Garuda sets hostname as username-... Actually Garuda/Arch installers sometimes set hostname to `<username>-<product>`. \"Rani\" could be another host. Let me grep git logs for \"rani\" word-boundary across inventory (excluding junk). Try `grep -riw \"rani\"` on select files (MANIFESTs, md files) — quick targeted search.\n\nAlso the config: hermes REPO_DIR = ~/github-intricos777/hermes-cli (override HERMES_REPO_DIR env, or config.yaml repo_dir). config.yaml shown earlier had no repo_dir → REPO_DIR = /home/livings/github-intricos777/hermes-cli. Does that exist? Earlier `ls /home/livings` showed no `github-intricos777` dir! But `hermes sync` pulled/pushed successfully... maybe config.yaml DOES have repo_dir — the config.yaml I read had model/web/browser etc. — that was `~/.hermes/config.yaml`. Wait, `config_path()` = REPO_DIR/config.yaml, i.e., `~/github-intricos777/hermes-cli/config.yaml`. And `~/.hermes/config.yaml` is a different file (hermes-agent config). So hermes.CLI''s config lives in REPO_DIR. But REPO_DIR doesn''t exist under home... yet `hermes sync` worked (pulled from GitHub). Hmm, earlier ls showed home contents: no github-intricos777. Let me check again — maybe it exists but wasn''t in listing? The listing showed: .bash*, .bde-daemon, .cache, .config, Desktop, Documents, Downloads, .firedragon, .gitconfig, .gtkrc, .hermes, .icons, .lia-cli, .local, Music, .npm, .pki, .projects..., .python_history, .rustup, .ssh, .steam, .steampath, .steampid, Templates, .var, Videos, workspace. No github-intricos777. And no `workspace` contents explored.\n\nBut `hermes sync` output: \"pull: From https://github.com/intricos777-dot/hermes-cli ... [new branch] main -> origin/main\" and \"push: no changes to sync\". If REPO_DIR didn''t exist, gitbus.pull would `git init` in nonexistent dir → `_run` with cwd nonexistent would raise GitBusError... Actually subprocess with nonexistent cwd raises FileNotFoundError → caught? Only TimeoutExpired is caught. Hmm but it worked. Maybe `HERMES_REPO_DIR` env or config.yaml at REPO_DIR... chicken-egg. Or maybe REPO_DIR exists. Let me just check.\n\nWait — where did hermes CLI run from? `python3 /home/livings/Projects/_inventory/hermes-cli/hermes sync` — REPO_DIR = ~/github-intricos777/hermes-cli. Let me check if it exists (hidden? no). Check now.\n\nAlso `workspace` dir in home — check it.\n\nNext: assemble export. Let me also check `.bash_history`? Not present (only .bash_logout/.bash_profile/.bashrc). fish_history has 383 lines starting2026-09-26 (when: 1790444803 ≈ Sep 26 2026). So shell history only from rebuild date.\n\n4-month-old data on this machine: git histories (inventory clones, full history), voynich memories (Sep 3 lia-vault), data/memory (Jul 17), legal reports (Jul 21), sin-archive (Sep 24), buildlog, Desktop. Plus hermes-pending-memories.json (timestamps 1790024548 ≈ Sep 21 2026).\n\nWait1790024548 → let''s compute: 1790024548 s ≈ 2026-09-21. Yes.\n\nWhere''s data from before Sep 21? The system was rebuilt Sep 26 but previous system (user sin) existed until ~Sep 24-26. Data from the old system on this disk? The old home was `/home/sin` — deleted/reinstalled? `/home` only has `livings`. So old machine''s home is GONE (this is a fresh install on same or new disk). Old data surviving:\n- GitHub (120 private repos, full history) — already on GitHub.\n- sin-archive-2026 (already on GitHub).\n- Maybe backups: check /mnt, /media, external drives? Check `df -h` and mount.\n- `.hermes/.curator_backups/blobs` — from Sep 26.\n- konsole logs? only from Sep 26.\n\nSo \"4 months of sessions\" largely doesn''t exist locally except through git histories and whatever hermes/opencode captured since rebuild. I should also check `workspace/` and `Documents` etc.\n\nAlso maybe old session logs exist inside repos like `later-work`, `buildlog/logs/buildlog.md`, `hermes-self-evolve`, or `code-theft-evidence`. And `~/.hermes/kanban.db`, `shared-state.db` — from Sep 26.\n\nLet me check mounts/workspace and whether any archive of old home exists (e.g., tarballs). Then assemble.\n\nAlso — user asked earlier (in history) hermes to do this; hermes may have already produced a todo list. Check `~/.hermes/cron/executions.db` or journal for \"todo\" from this morning? The history ends at \"and then prepare a todo list and lets go over it\" (12:43 today). Maybe hermes created a todo list in kanban.db or state. Let me check kanban.db quickly and any recent Desktop/notes files.\n\nBatch:\n1. df -h / mount; ls /mnt /media; ls workspace\n2. check REPO_DIR ~/github-intricos777\n3. kanban.db tables/recent\n4. grep -riw rani in inventory md files (limited)","time":{"start":1790625402719,"end":1790625428958}}');
