INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_0e99989ce001CHUsNR94AZvUPh','msg_0e999733d001cuSMm1sHnGfGzk','ses_f16732810ffehZhBAPc6TQNXa2',1790625548751,1790625578244,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"- hosts.yml: no token. Safe (but config only).\n- `_secrets.json` previews max 27 chars — truncated, no full secrets. Safe to include.\n- lia data/ IS tracked in git (vault + legal reports committed at 39f544b). The commit f0f6235 deleted kg_schema.py, keygen key.txt, main.py, __init__.py (the \"older corrupted versions\") — those exist only in GitHub history now (and in inventory clone). \n\nEverything''s on GitHub already for lia-cli. Good.\n\nNow assemble. Directory: `/home/livings/Projects/sin-user-data-4mo/` — hmm, better: `user-data-archive` . Repo name: `user-data-archive-2026-09` (private). Let''s go with dir `/home/livings/Projects/user-data-archive-2026-09/` and repo `user-data-archive-2026-09`.\n\nContents plan:\n\n```\nREADME.md                      — manifest, scope, sources, withheld list, identities\nIDENTITY.md                    — usernames/UIDs/hosts evidence\nhermes/\n  memories/{MEMORY.md,USER.md}\n  .hermes_history\n  SOUL.md\n  config.yaml                  (agent config)\n  state.db.sql                 (sqlite dump: sessions+messages)\n  kanban.db.sql, shared-state.db.sql, cron/executions.db.sql\n  logs/ (agent.log, errors.log, gateway*.log; process-results/? check size — du didn''t show process-results... earlier du listed logs 1.4M total including process-results? The du output showed only 4 lines because process-results maybe inside logs (yes logs/1.4M covers it) — wait it printed .curator_backups 2.0M, logs 1.4M, kanban, shared-state, executions, opencode/log 2.9M. process-results missing → it''s under logs (included).\n  pastes/\n  terminal-sessions/\n  curator_backups/blobs/ (2MB)\n  runtime/active_sessions.json channel_directory.json, gateway_state.json, gateway-starts.log\nopencode/\n  opencode.db.sql (dump) or raw copy? dump is text; plus log/ (2.9M)\n  opencode-config/ (~/.config/opencode: jsonc, bak, tui.json — exclude node_modules/themes? themes are small, include)\nlia/\n  working/data/ (vault + legal reports)\n  inventory-older/ (kg_schema.py, main.py, __init__.py, keygen key.txt, lia-memory.vault.json, legal reports) — \"older corrupted versions\"\n  lia-cli.bundle (full git history)\n  voynich-memories/ (lia-vault.json, hermes-pending-memories.json)\n  CORRUPTION-NOTE.md — the verify findings + hermes message excerpt\nshell-terminal/\n  fish_history\n  konsole/ (Garuda.profile, BlackRed.colorscheme, konsolerc?)\n  recently-used.xbel + .bak\n  bash/.bashrc/.bash_profile/.bash_logout\ndesktop/NEXT-REBOOT-READ-ME.txt\naudit/{_verify.json,_clone_results.json,_secrets.json}\ngit-history-4mo.md (per-repo commits since 2026-05-28 across _inventory)\n```\n\nExclusions (state at end): auth.json (hermes+opencode), vault.key+vault.json.enc, nous_auth.json, .ssh, gh config/hosts, live DB WALs (use dumps instead), node_modules, browser profiles.\n\nWait — should I include raw state.db too? A .dump is safer & diffable. opencode.db dump might be large (36MB db, mostly indexes/fts) — dump maybe 10-30MB. Fine.\n\nAlso hermes `.curator_backups/blobs` — include.\n\nAlso include `~/.hermes/cron/ticker_*`? trivial, skip? include small stuff, why not — keep it simple: skip.\n\nAlso `~/.hermes/cron/ticker_*`? trivial, skip? include small stuff, why not — keep it simple: skip.\n\ngit-history-4mo: loop over `_inventory/*/` git repos and `Projects/*` repos, run `git log --since=2026-05-28 --all --pretty=format:''%h|%ad|%an|%s'' --date=short` append section. 120+ repos — could be slow-ish but fine locally. Timeout guard.\n\nSteps:\n1. mkdir structure2. copy files\n3. sqlite dumps\n4. git bundle for lia-cli (and maybe hermes-cli? hermes-cli source already on GitHub; skip)\n5. generate git-history-4mo.md\n6. README/IDENTITY\n7. git init, add, commit? Leave final commit+push to hermes per user request: \"push all of the data to a private repo thru hermes\". I''ll do: gh repo create --private, set remote, then run hermes sync with temp HERMES_REPO_DIR config so hermes performs commit+push.\n\nHmm — one wrinkle: gitbus.pull() runs first: repo has no .git? I''ll git init myself. Then pull adds origin remote (already added), fetch origin main — repo on GitHub empty (no branches) → fetch fails (\"unborn remote; continuing locally\"), then commit_and_push: dirty → add -A, commit, push HEAD:main. Works.\n\nActually if `gh repo create --private --source . --push`? That pushes immediately — but then hermes has nothing to do. User wants push thru hermes. So: create repo WITHOUT push (`gh repo create NAME --private --description ...` no source), add remote, then hermes sync commits+pushes.\n\nRemote auth: credential helper gh → works.\n\nIdentity for hermes commit: `_git_identity(repo_dir)` — checks repo config or global? Look: `_run(repo_dir, [\"config\",\"user.name\"])` presumably — global user.name = Living_Sin exists → uses that? It said \"Ensure identity exists (per-repo...)\" with fallback Hermes.CLI. Either fine.\n\nAlso user''s request \"check on the Lia.CLI and the older corrupted versions for memories and data\" → report findings: vault contents (test entries Jul 17; Sep 3 voynich copy with replika entry), corrupted kg_schema.py (owlready2 truncated), deleted-in-history stubs, and that hermes previously flagged it. Also legal reports (empty scans). And confirm nothing else (lia-groq-bridge etc. already on GitHub).\n\nWait — also check: are there memories in lia-cli `src/` store (ConversationStore) — config.ts defines store path (maybe `~/.lia-cli/history.jsonl` per hermes config paths: `lia_history`: ~/.lia-cli/history.jsonl). `.lia-cli/` only had `inbox/`. No history.jsonl. Also `.lia-cli/inbox/token`? inbox dir empty (total 0 earlier? `drwxr-xr-x 2 ... inbox` with10 bytes = empty). Check inbox/token existence — 0600 token file → withhold if present.\n\nAlso check supervisor tasks data: `data/supervisor/tasks.json` gitignored — does it exist? And `tasks/` dir in lia-cli (active-plan.json?). Include those (user data).\n\nLet me start assembling. First check lia tasks/supervisor files + .lia-cli/inbox.","time":{"start":1790625548751,"end":1790625578238}}');
